TURATH_CHUNK(44,[{"num":8800,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ شِهَابٍ قال: لَمَّا رَجَعَ كُلُّ الْمُشْرِكِينَ إِلَى مَكَّةَ أقبل عُمَيْرُ بْنُ وَهْبٍ حَتَّى جَلَسَ إِلَى صَفْوَانَ بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ فِي الْحِجَرِ، فَقَالَ صَفْوَانُ: قَبَّحَ اللَّهُ الْعَيْشَ بَعْدَ قَتْلَى بَدْرٍ، قَالَ: أَجَلْ، وَاللَّهِ مَا فِي الْعَيْشِ خَيْرٌ بَعْدَهُمْ، ولو لا دِينٌ عَلِيٍّ لاَ أَجِدُ لَهُ قَضَاءً، وَعِيَالٌ لا أَدَعُ لَهُمْ شَيْئًا، لَرَحَلْتُ إِلَى مُحَمَّدٍ فَقَتَلْتُهُ إِنْ مَلَأْتَ عَيْنِي مِنْهُ، فَإِنَّ لِي عِنْدَهُ عِلَّةً أَعْتَلُ بِهَا عَلَيْهِ، أَقُولُ: قَدِمْتُ مِنْ أَجْلِ ابْنِي هَذَا الأَسِيرِ. قَالَ: فَفَرِحَ صَفْوَانُ، وَقَالَ لَهُ: عَلَيَّ دِينُكَ، وَعِيَالُكَ أُسْوَةُ عِيَالِي فِي النَّفَقَةِ، لاَ يَسَعُنِي شَيْءٌ وأعجز عَنْهُمْ. فَاتَّفَقَا، وَحَمَلَهُ صَفْوَانُ وَجَهَّزَهُ، وَأَمَرَ بِسَيْفِ عُمَيْرٍ فَصَقَلَ وَسَمِّ، وَقَالَ عُمَيْرٌ لِصَفْوَانَ: اكْتُمْ خَبَرِي أَيّامًا.","وَقَدِمَ عُمَيْرٌ الْمَدِينَةَ، فَنَزَلَ بباب الْمَسْجِدِ، وَعَقَلَ رَاحِلَتَهُ، وَأَخَذَ السَّيْفَ، وَعَمَدَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَنَظَرَ إِلَيْهِ عُمَرُ وَهُوَ فِي نَفَرٍ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، ففزغ، وَدَخَلَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا نبي اللَّهِ لاَ تَأْمَنْهُ عَلَى شَيْءٍ، فَقَالَ: أَدْخِلْهُ عَلِيَّ فَخَرَجَ عُمَرُ، فَأَمَرَ أَصْحَابَهُ أَنْ يَدْخُلُوا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَيَحْتَرِسُوا مِنْ عُمَيْرٍ، وَأَقْبَلَ عُمَرُ وَعُمَيْرٌ حَتَّى دَخَلَا عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَعَ عُمَيْرِ سَيْفِهِ. قال رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِعُمَرَ : تَأَخَّرَ عَنْهُ فَلَمَّا دَنَا منه عُمَيْرٌ قَالَ: أنعم صَبَاحًا. وَهِيَ تَحِيَّةُ أهل الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَدْ أَكْرَمْنَا اللَّهُ عز وجل عَنْ تَحِيَّتِكَ، وَجَعَلَ تَحِيَّتَنَا تَحِيَّةَ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، وهي السَّلامُ فَقَالَ عُمَيْرٌ: إِنَّ عَهْدَكَ بِهَا لِحَدِيثٍ فَقَالَ له: مَا أُقَدِّمُكَ يَا عُمَيْرُ؟ قَالَ: قَدِمْتُ عَلَى أَسِيرِي عِنْدَكُمْ تُفَادُونَا فِي أَسْرَانَا فَإِنَّكُمُ الْعَشِيرَةُ وَالأَهْلُ. فَقَالَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: مَا بَالُ السَّيْفِ فِي عُنُقِكَ؟!، فَقَالَ: قَبَحَهَا اللَّهُ مِنْ سُيُوفٍ، فهل أَغْنْتَ عَنَّا شَيْئًا؟ إِنَّمَا نَسِيتُهُ فِي عُنُقِي حِينَ نَزَلَتْ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اصْدُقْنِي مَا أُقْدَمُكَ؟ قَالَ: مَا قَدِمْتُ إِلا فِي طَلَبِ أُسِيرِي قَالَ: فَمَاذَا شَرَطْتَ لِصَفْوَانَ فِي الْحِجْرِ؟ فَفَزِعَ عُمَيْرٌ، وَقَالَ: مَاذَا شَرَطْتَ لَهُ؟! قَالَ: تَحَمَّلْتُ لَهُ بِقَتْلِي عَلَى أَنْ يَعُولَ أَوْلاَدَكَ، وَيَقْضِيَ دَيْنَكَ، وَاللَّهِ حَائِلٌ بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ ذَلِكَ فَقَالَ عُمَيْرٌ: أَشْهَدُ أَنَّكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، وَأَشْهَدُ أَنْ لا إِلَهَ إِلا اللَّهُ، كُنَّا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ نُكَذِّبُكَ بِالْوَحْيِ، وَبِمَا يَأْتِيكَ مِنْ السَّمَاءُ، وَإِنَّ هَذَا الْحَدِيثَ كَانَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ صَفْوَانَ فِي الْحَجَرِ كَمَا قُلْتُ، لَمْ يَطَّلِعْ عَلَيْهِ أَحَدٌ، فَأَخْبَرَكَ اللَّهُ بِهِ، فَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي سَاقَنِي هَذَا الْمَسَاقَ، فَفَرَّحَ بِهِ الْمُسْلِمُونَ، وَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اجْلِسْ يَا عُمَيْرُ نؤانسك، وَقَالَ لأَصْحَابِهِ: عَلِّمُوا أَخَاكُمُ الْقُرْآنَ وَأَطْلَقَ لَهُ أَسِيرُهُ.","فَقَالَ عُمَيْرٌ: ائْذَنْ لِي يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَأُلْحِقَ بِقُرَيْشٍ، فَأَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَإِلَى الإِسْلامِ، لَعَلَّ اللَّهَ أَنْ يَهْدِيَهُمْ، فَأَذِنَ لَهُ، فَلَحِقَ بِمَكَّةَ.","وَجَعَلَ صَفْوَانُ يَقُولُ لِقُرَيْشٍ: أَبْشِرُوا بِفَتْحٍ يُنْسِيكُمْ وَقْعَةَ بَدْرٍ، وَجَعَلَ يَسْأَلُ كُلَّ رَاكِبٍ قَدِمَ مِنَ الْمَدِينَةِ: هَلْ كَانَ بِهَا مِنْ حَدَثٍ؟ حَتَّى قَدِمَ عليه رَجُلٌ فَقَالَ له: قَدْ أَسْلَمَ عُمَيْرٌ، فَلَعَنَهُ الْمُشْرِكُونَ. وَقَالَ صَفْوَانُ: لِلَّهِ عَلَيَّ أن لا أُكَلِّمُهُ أَبَدًا، وَلاَ أَنْفَعُهُ بِشَيْءٍ، ثُمَّ قَدِمَ عُمَيْرٌ فَدَعَاهُمْ إِلَى الإِسْلاَمِ وَنَصَحَهُمْ بِجَهْدِهِ، فَأَسْلَمَ بِسَبَبِهِ بَشَرٌ كَثِيرٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه موسى بن عقبة في مغازيه عن ابن شهاب هكذا مرسلا كما في الإصابة (7/531-533). ورواه الطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 119) من طريق محمد بن سهل بن عسكر، عن عبد الرزاق، أنا جعفر بن سليمان، عن أبي عمران الجوني، لا أعلمه إلا عن أنس بن مالك فذكر نحوه مختصرا. ورواه ابن منده من طريق أبي الأزهر، عن عبد الرزاق بإسناده، وقال: \"غريب لا نعرفه عن أبي عمران إلا من هذا الوجه\" كما قال الحافظ في الإصابة، ثم أشار إلى رواية الطبراني.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"انتقام قريش لقتلى بدر بالتآمر على النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah in his Maghāzī as in al-Iṣābah (7/531-533), and by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr (17/63).","chapter_en":"Quraysh Seeking Revenge for Those Killed at Badr by Plotting against the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بدر","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Battle of Badr","part_no":48,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":53,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Shihāb narrated: When the defeated remnants of the polytheists returned to Makkah, ʿUmayr ibn Wahb came and sat with Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah in al-Ḥijr. Ṣafwān said, “May Allah make life ugly after those killed at Badr.” He said, “Yes. By Allah, there is no good in life after them. Were it not for a debt upon me that I cannot repay, and dependents whom I would leave with nothing, I would travel to Muhammad and kill him if my eyes could fill with sight of him. I have an excuse with him by which I can approach him: I will say, ‘I came because of this son of mine who is a prisoner.’” Ṣafwān rejoiced and said to him, “Your debt is upon me, and your dependents will be like my dependents in maintenance. I will not be able to provide anything for mine while being unable to provide for them.” They agreed. Ṣafwān mounted him, prepared him, and ordered that a sword of Ḥimyar be polished and poisoned. ʿUmayr said to Ṣafwān, “Conceal my news for some days.” ʿUmayr came to Madinah, dismounted at the door of the mosque, tied his mount, took the sword, and headed toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar saw him while he was among a group of the Anṣār, became alarmed, and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, “O Prophet of Allah, do not trust him with anything.” He said, “Bring him in to me.” ʿUmar went out and ordered his companions to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and guard against ʿUmayr.","ʿUmar and ʿUmayr came forward until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while ʿUmayr had his sword. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar, “Step back from him.” When ʿUmayr drew near, he said, “May your morning be pleasant.” This was the greeting of the people of Jāhiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has honored us above your greeting, and has made our greeting the greeting of the people of Paradise, and it is salām.” ʿUmayr said, “Your time with it is recent.” He said to him, “What brought you, O ʿUmayr?” He said, “I came because of my prisoner who is with you, so deal kindly with us concerning our prisoners, for you are kin and family.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What is the matter with the sword around your neck?” He said, “May Allah make these swords ugly. Did they benefit us at all? I only forgot it around my neck when I dismounted.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Tell me the truth: what brought you?” He said, “I came only to seek my prisoner.” He said, “Then what did you stipulate with Ṣafwān in al-Ḥijr?” ʿUmayr was startled and said, “What did I stipulate with him?” He said, “You undertook to kill me for him on condition that he support your children and pay off your debt. Allah will come between you and that.” ʿUmayr said, “I testify that you are the Messenger of Allah, and I testify that there is no god but Allah. O Messenger of Allah, we used to deny you regarding revelation and what came to you from heaven. This conversation was between me and Ṣafwān in al-Ḥijr exactly as you said; no one knew of it, and Allah informed you of it. Praise be to Allah who brought me to this path.” The Muslims rejoiced over him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Sit, O ʿUmayr, so we may keep you company.” He said to his Companions, “Teach your brother the Qur’an.” And he released his prisoner for him. ʿUmayr said, “Permit me, O Messenger of Allah, to return to Quraysh and call them to Allah and to Islam, perhaps Allah will guide them.” He permitted him, and he returned to Makkah. Ṣafwān had been saying to Quraysh, “Rejoice in a victory that will make you forget the event of Badr.” He kept asking every rider who came from Madinah, “Has anything happened there?” until a man came to him and said, “ʿUmayr has accepted Islam.” The polytheists cursed him. Ṣafwān said, “It is upon me before Allah that I will never speak to him and will never benefit him with anything.” Then ʿUmayr came and called them to Islam and advised them with all his effort, and many people accepted Islam because of him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",376],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه موسى بن عقبة في مغازيه كما في الإصابة (7/531-533)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/63)."},{"num":8801,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: لَمَّا أَصَابَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قُرَيْشًا يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ، وَقَدِمَ الْمَدِينَةَ جَمَعَ الْيَهُودَ فِي سُوقِ بَنِي قَيْنُقَاعَ فَقَالَ: يَا مَعْشَرَ يَهُودَ أَسْلِمُوا قَبْلَ أَنْ يُصِيبَكُمْ مِثْلُ مَا أَصَابَ قُرَيْشًا. قَالُوا يَا مُحَمَّدُ لاَ يَغُرَّنَّكَ مِنْ نَفْسِكَ أَنَّكَ قَتَلْتَ نَفَرًا مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ كَانُوا أَغْمَارًا لاَ يَعْرِفُونَ الْقِتَالَ، إِنَّكَ لَوْ قَاتَلْتَنَا لَعَرَفْتَ أَنَّا نَحْنُ النَّاسُ، وَأَنَّكَ لَمْ تَلْقَ مِثْلَنَا. فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ فِي ذَلِكَ { قُلْ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا سَتُغْلَبُونَ } قَرَأَ مُصَرِّفٌ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: ﴿فِئَةٌ تُقَاتِلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ﴾ [سورة آل عمران: 13] } بِبَدْرٍ، { وَأُخْرَى كَافِرَةٌ }."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3001) عن مصرف بن عمرو الإيامي، حدثنا يونس –يعني ابن بكير – قال: حدثنا محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني محمد بن أبي محمد مولى زيد بن ثابت، عن سعيد بن جبير وعكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني قينقاع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3001).","chapter_en":"The Battle of Banū Qaynuqāʿ","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ defeated Quraysh on the Day of Badr and returned to Madinah, he gathered the Jews in the market of Banū Qaynuqāʿ and said, “O assembly of Jews, accept Islam before there strikes you the like of what struck Quraysh.” They said, “O Muhammad, do not be deceived by yourself because you killed a group of Quraysh who were inexperienced and did not know fighting. If you fought us, you would know that we are truly the people, and that you have not met the like of us.” So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning that: “Say to those who disbelieve: You will be overcome,” up to His saying: “One group fighting in the path of Allah and another disbelieving” [Āl ʿImrān: 12-13], regarding Badr."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الواقدي: إنها كانت في يوم السبت النصف من شوال سنة اثنتين من الهجرة."],"en":["Al-Wāqidī said: It occurred on Saturday, in the middle of Shawwāl, in the second year after the Hijrah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3001)."},{"num":8802,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ الأَنْصَارِيِّ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزْوَةِ أَنْمَارٍ يُصَلِّي عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ، مُتَوَجِّهًا قِبَلَ الْمَشْرِقِ مُتَطَوِّعًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4140) عن آدم، حدثنا ابن أبي ذئب، حدثنا عثمان بن عبد الله بن سُراقة، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب غزوة ذي أمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4140).","chapter_en":"The Battle of Dhū Amr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated: I saw the Prophet ﷺ in the Battle of Anmār praying voluntary prayer on his mount while facing toward the east."]},"intro":{"ar":["فلما رجع رسول الله ﷺ من غزوة السويق أقام بالمدينة بقية ذي الحجة، أو قريبًا منها، ثم غزا نجدًا، يريد غطفان، وهي غزوة ذي أمر، ويقال أيضًا: غزوة أنمار. واستعمل على المدينة عثمان بن عفان فيما قال ابن هشام. قال ابن إسحاق: فأقام بنجد صفرًا كله أو قريبًا من ذلك، ثم رجع إلى المدينة ولم يلق كيدًا، فلبث بها شهر ربيع الأول كله، أو إلا قليلًا منه. سيرة ابن هشام (٢/٤٦).","وفي طبقات ابن سعد (٢/٣٤): أن جمعًا من بني ثعلبة ومحارب بذي أمر قد تجمعوا يريدون أن يصيبوا من أطراف رسول الله ﷺ، جمعهم رجل منهم يقال له: دعثور بن الحارث من بني محارب، فندب رسول الله ﷺ المسلمين، وخرج لاثنتي عشرة ليلة مضت من شهر ربيع الأول في أربعمائة وخمسين رجلًا، ومعهم أفراس. فلما سمعوا مسير رسول الله ﷺ هربوا إلى رؤوس الجبال، ولم يلق رسول الله ﷺ أحدًا، إلا أنه ينظر إليهم في رؤوس الجبال.","وقال الحافظ ابن حجر في الفتح (٧/٤٢٩): يشبه أن تكون غزوة أنمار غزوة محارب وثعلبة؛ لأن ديار بني أنمار تقرب من ديار بني ثعلبة."],"en":["When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Battle of al-Sawīq, he remained in Madinah for the rest of Dhū al-Ḥijjah, or close to it. Then he campaigned in Najd, intending Ghaṭafān. This was the Battle of Dhū Amr, and it is also called the Battle of Anmār. According to Ibn Hishām, he appointed ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān over Madinah. Ibn Isḥāq said: He remained in Najd for all of Ṣafar, or close to that. Then he returned to Madinah without encountering any plot, and he stayed there for all of Rabīʿ al-Awwal, or almost all of it. Sīrat Ibn Hishām (2/46).","In Ṭabaqāt Ibn Saʿd (2/34): A group from Banū Thaʿlabah and Muḥārib at Dhū Amr had gathered, intending to strike the outskirts of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A man among them called Duʿthūr ibn al-Ḥārith from Banū Muḥārib had gathered them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned the Muslims and went out twelve nights into Rabīʿ al-Awwal with four hundred and fifty men, along with horses. When they heard of the march of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they fled to the mountaintops. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not meet anyone, except that he saw them on the mountaintops.","Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar said in al-Fatḥ (7/429): It seems that the Battle of Anmār was the Battle of Muḥārib and Thaʿlabah, because the dwellings of Banū Anmār are near the dwellings of Banū Thaʿlabah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",386],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4140)."},{"num":8803,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عبدالله الأنصاري أَنَّهُ قَالَ: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزْوَةِ بَنِي أَنْمَارٍ، قَالَ جَابِرٌ: فَبَيْنَا أَنَا نَازِلٌ تَحْتَ شَجَرَةٍ إِذَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أقبل فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ هَلُمَّ إِلَى الظِّلِّ، قَالَ: فَنَزَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقُمْتُ إِلَى غِرَارَةٍ لَنَا، فَالْتَمَسْتُ فِيهَا شَيْئًا، فَوَجَدْتُ فِيهَا جِرْوَ قثاءفكسرته، ثُمَّ قَرَّبْتُهُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَقَالَ: مِنْ أَيْنَ لَكُمْ هَذَا؟ قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ: خَرَجْنَا بِهِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مِنَ الْمَدِينَةِ. قَالَ جَابِرٌ: وَعِنْدَنَا صَاحِبٌ لَنَا نُجَهِّزُهُ يَذْهَبُ يَرْعَى ظَهْرَنَا، قَالَ: فَجَهَّزْتُهُ، ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ يَذْهَبُ فِي الظَّهْرِ وَعَلَيْهِ بُرْدَانِ لَهُ قَدْ خَلِقَا قَالَ: فَنَظَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَيْهِ فَقَالَ: أَمَا لَهُ ثَوْبَانِ غَيْرُ هَذَيْنِ؟ فَقُلْتُ: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لَهُ ثَوْبَانِ فِي الْعَيْبَةِ، كَسَوْتُهُ إِيَّاهُمَا، قَالَ: فَادْعُهُ، فَمُرْهُ فَلْيَلْبَسْهُمَا. قَالَ: فَدَعَوْتُهُ فَلَبِسَهُمَا، ثُمَّ وَلَّى يَذْهَبُ قَالَ: فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : مَا لَهُ ضَرَبَ اللهُ عُنُقَهُ، أَلَيْسَ هَذَا خَيْرًا لَهُ؟ قَالَ: فَسَمِعَهُ الرَّجُلُ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: فَقُتِلَ الرَّجُلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في اللباس (1) عن زيد بن أسلم، عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره. ومن طريقه رواه ابن حبان (5418)، والبزار (كشف الأستار 2963)، والحاكم (4/183) وقال: صحيح على شرط مسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب غزوة ذي أمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Mālik (1), Ibn Ḥibbān (5418), al-Bazzār, Kashf al-Astār (2963), and al-Ḥākim (4/183).","chapter_en":"The Battle of Dhū Amr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Battle of Banū Anmār. Jābir said: While I was resting beneath a tree, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, come to the shade.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted. I went to a sack of ours and searched in it for something. I found in it a small cucumber, broke it, and brought it near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “Where did you get this?” I said, “We brought it with us from Madinah, O Messenger of Allah.” Jābir said: We had a companion with us whom we had prepared to go and graze our riding animals. I prepared him, and he turned away to go to the riding animals, wearing two old worn cloaks of his. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him and said, “Does he not have two garments other than these?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He has two garments in the chest; I clothed him with them.” He said, “Call him and tell him to wear them.” I called him, and he wore them. Then he turned away to go. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What is the matter with him? May Allah strike his neck. Is this not better for him?” The man heard him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, in the path of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “In the path of Allah.” He said: The man was then killed in the path of Allah."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His phrase “jarw qiththāʾ”: “jarw” here means small cucumbers. “Al-ʿaybah” is like a chest in which clothes are placed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",387],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (1)، وابن حبان (5418)، والبزار، كشف الأستار (2963)، والحاكم (4/183)."},{"num":8804,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يَقُولُ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ لِكَعْبِ بْنِ الأَشْرَفِ؟ فَإِنَّهُ قَدْ آذَى اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ. فَقَامَ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ مَسْلَمَةَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَتُحِبُّ أَنْ أَقْتُلَهُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَأْذَنْ لِي أَنْ أَقُولَ شَيْئًا. قَالَ: قُلْ. فَأَتَاهُ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ مَسْلَمَةَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ هَذَا الرَّجُلَ قَدْ سَأَلَنَا صَدَقَةً، وَإِنَّهُ قَدْ عَنَّانَا، وَإِنِّي قَدْ أَتَيْتُكَ أَسْتَسْلِفُكَ. قَالَ: وَأَيْضًا وَاللَّهِ لَتَمَلُّنَّهُ، قَالَ: إِنَّا قَدِ اتَّبَعْنَاهُ، فَلاَ نُحِبُّ أَنْ نَدَعَهُ حَتَّى نَنْظُرَ إِلَى أَىِّ شَىْءٍ يَصِيرُ شَأْنُهُ، وَقَدْ أَرَدْنَا أَنْ تُسْلِفَنَا وَسْقًا، أَوْ وَسْقَيْنِ ـ وَحَدَّثَنَا عَمْرٌو غَيْرَ مَرَّةٍ، فَلَمْ يَذْكُرْ وَسْقًا أَوْ وَسْقَيْنِ، أَوْ: فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: فِيهِ وَسْقًا أَوْ وَسْقَيْنِ؟ فَقَالَ: أُرَى فِيهِ وَسْقًا أَوْ وَسْقَيْنِ ـ فَقَالَ: نَعَمِ، ارْهَنُونِي. قَالُوا: أَىَّ شَىْءٍ تُرِيدُ؟ قَالَ: فَارْهَنُونِي نِسَاءَكُمْ. قَالُوا كَيْفَ نَرْهَنُكَ نِسَاءَنَا وَأَنْتَ أَجْمَلُ الْعَرَبِ، قَالَ: فَارْهَنُونِي أَبْنَاءَكُمْ. قَالُوا كَيْفَ نَرْهَنُكَ أَبْنَاءَنَا، فَيُسَبُّ أَحَدُهُمْ، فَيُقَالُ: رُهِنَ بِوَسْقٍ أَوْ وَسْقَيْنِ. هَذَا عَارٌ عَلَيْنَا، وَلَكِنَّا نَرْهَنُكَ اللأْمَةَ ـ قَالَ سُفْيَانُ: يَعْنِي السِّلاَحَ ـ فَوَاعَدَهُ أَنْ يَأْتِيَهُ، فَجَاءَهُ لَيْلاً وَمَعَهُ أَبُو نَائِلَةَ، وَهْوَ أَخُو كَعْبٍ مِنَ الرَّضَاعَةِ، فَدَعَاهُمْ إِلَى الْحِصْنِ، فَنَزَلَ إِلَيْهِمْ، فَقَالَتْ لَهُ امْرَأَتُهُ: أَيْنَ تَخْرُجُ هَذِهِ السَّاعَةَ؟ فَقَالَ: إِنَّمَا هُوَ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ مَسْلَمَةَ، وَأَخِي أَبُو نَائِلَةَ، ـ وَقَالَ غَيْرُ عَمْرٍو، قَالَتْ: أَسْمَعُ صَوْتًا كَأَنَّهُ يَقْطُرُ مِنْهُ الدَّمُ. قَالَ: إِنَّمَا هُوَ أَخِي مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ مَسْلَمَةَ وَرَضِيعِي أَبُو نَائِلَةَ، ـ إِنَّ الْكَرِيمَ لَوْ دُعِيَ إِلَى طَعْنَةٍ بِلَيْلٍ لأَجَابَ، قَالَ: وَيُدْخِلُ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ مَسْلَمَةَ مَعَهُ رَجُلَيْنِ ـ قِيلَ لِسُفْيَانَ: سَمَّاهُمْ عَمْرٌو؟ قَالَ: سَمَّى بَعْضَهُمْ قَالَ عَمْرٌو: جَاءَ مَعَهُ بِرَجُلَيْنِ، وَقَالَ غَيْرُ عَمْرٍو: أَبُو عَبْسِ بْنُ جَبْرٍ، وَالْحَارِثُ بْنُ أَوْسٍ وَعَبَّادُ بْنُ بِشْرٍ، قَالَ عَمْرٌو: وَجَاءَ مَعَهُ بِرَجُلَيْنِ، ـ فَقَالَ: إِذَا مَا جَاءَ فَإِنِّي قَائِلٌ بِشَعَرِهِ فَأَشَمُّهُ، فَإِذَا رَأَيْتُمُونِي اسْتَمْكَنْتُ مِنْ رَأْسِهِ فَدُونَكُمْ فَاضْرِبُوهُ. وَقَالَ مَرَّةً: ثُمَّ أُشِمُّكُمْ. فَنَزَلَ إِلَيْهِمْ مُتَوَشِّحًا وَهْوَ يَنْفَحُ مِنْهُ رِيحُ الطِّيبِ، فَقَالَ: مَا رَأَيْتُ كَالْيَوْمِ رِيحًا ـ أَىْ أَطْيَبَ، ـ وَقَالَ غَيْرُ عَمْرٍو: قَالَ: عِنْدِي أَعْطَرُ نِسَاءِ الْعَرَبِ وَأَكْمَلُ الْعَرَبِ، قَالَ عَمْرٌو: فَقَالَ: أَتَأْذَنُ لِي أَنْ أَشَمَّ رَأْسَكَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، فَشَمَّهُ، ثُمَّ أَشَمَّ أَصْحَابَهُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَتَأْذَنُ لِي؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. فَلَمَّا اسْتَمْكَنَ مِنْهُ، قَالَ: دُونَكُمْ. فَقَتَلُوهُ، ثُمَّ أَتَوُا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخْبَرُوهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4037) ومسلم في الجهاد (1801) كلاهما من حديث سفيان، قال عمرو: سمعت جابر بن عبد الله يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قتل كعب بن الأشرف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4037) and Muslim (1801).","chapter_en":"The Killing of Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who will deal with Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf? He has harmed Allah and His Messenger.” Muḥammad ibn Maslamah stood and said, “O Messenger of Allah, would you like me to kill him?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then permit me to say something.” He said, “Say it.” Muḥammad ibn Maslamah came to him and said, “This man has asked us for charity, and he has burdened us. I have come to you seeking a loan.” He said, “And more than that, by Allah, you will grow tired of him.” He said, “We have followed him, and we do not wish to leave him until we see where his matter will end. We want you to lend us a wasq or two.” ʿAmr narrated to us more than once and did not mention “a wasq or two,” or I said to him, “Does it contain ‘a wasq or two’?” He said, “I think it contains ‘a wasq or two.’” He said, “Yes, give me collateral.” They said, “What do you want?” He said, “Pledge your women to me.” They said, “How can we pledge our women to you when you are the most handsome of the Arabs?” He said, “Then pledge your sons to me.” They said, “How can we pledge our sons to you, then one of them would be insulted and it would be said: He was pledged for a wasq or two? This would be shame upon us. But we will pledge our weapons to you.” Sufyān said: Meaning weapons. He made an appointment to come to him. He came to him at night with Abū Nāʾilah, who was Kaʿb’s brother through nursing. He called them to the fortress, and Kaʿb came down to them. His wife said to him, “Where are you going out at this hour?” He said, “It is only Muḥammad ibn Maslamah and my brother Abū Nāʾilah.” Someone other than ʿAmr said: She said, “I hear a voice as if blood is dripping from it.” He said, “It is only my brother Muḥammad ibn Maslamah and my foster brother Abū Nāʾilah. If a noble man were called to a stab at night, he would answer.” Muḥammad ibn Maslamah entered with two men. It was said to Sufyān: Did ʿAmr name them? He said: He named some of them. ʿAmr said: Two men came with him. Someone other than ʿAmr said: Abū ʿAbs ibn Jabr, al-Ḥārith ibn Aws, and ʿAbbād ibn Bishr. ʿAmr said: Two men came with him. He said, “When he comes, I will take hold of his hair and smell it. When you see that I have gained control of his head, then strike him.” And he said once: “Then I will let you smell it.” Kaʿb came down to them wearing his garment, and the scent of perfume was coming from him. He said, “I have never smelled a scent better than today’s.” Someone other than ʿAmr said: He said, “I have the most fragrant and most perfect women of the Arabs.” ʿAmr said: He said, “Do you permit me to smell your head?” He said, “Yes.” He smelled it, then let his companions smell it. Then he said, “Do you permit me?” He said, “Yes.” When he had gained control of him, he said, “Now!” So they killed him. Then they came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His killing was in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the third year, as Ibn Saʿd said in al-Ṭabaqāt (2/31)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",390],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4037)، ومسلم (1801)."},{"num":8805,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: مَشَى مَعَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، إِلَى بَقِيعِ الْغَرْقَدِ، ثُمَّ وَجَّهَهُمْ وَقَالَ: انْطَلِقُوا عَلَى اسْمِ اللَّهِ، وَقَالَ: اللهُمَّ أَعِنْهُمْ - يَعْنِي النَّفَرَ الَّذِينَ وَجَّهَهُمْ إِلَى كَعْبِ بْنِ الْأَشْرَفِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (2391) والطبراني (11/222) والبزار (كشف الأستار (1802،1801) والحاكم (2480) كلهم من حديث محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني ثور بن يزيد، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قتل كعب بن الأشرف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (2391), al-Ṭabarānī (11/222), al-Bazzār, Kashf al-Astār (1801, 1802), and al-Ḥākim (2480).","chapter_en":"The Killing of Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked with them to Baqīʿ al-Gharqad, then sent them forth and said, “Go in the name of Allah.” And he said, “O Allah, help them.” Meaning the group he sent to Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",391],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (2391)، والطبراني (11/222)، والبزار، كشف الأستار (1801، 1802)، والحاكم (2480)."},{"num":8806,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ كَعْبِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، - وَكَانَ أَحَدَ الثَّلاَثَةِ الَّذِينَ تِيبَ عَلَيْهِمْ، - وَكَانَ كَعْبُ بْنُ الأَشْرَفِ يَهْجُو النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَيُحَرِّضُ عَلَيْهِ كُفَّارَ قُرَيْشٍ، وَكَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ قَدِمَ الْمَدِينَةَ، وَأَهْلُهَا أَخْلاَطٌ، مِنْهُمُ الْمُسْلِمُونَ، وَالْمُشْرِكُونَ يَعْبُدُونَ الأَوْثَانَ. وَالْيَهُودُ، وَكَانُوا يُؤْذُونَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابَهُ، فَأَمَرَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ نَبِيَّهُ بِالصَّبْرِ وَالْعَفْوِ فَفِيهِمْ أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ: ﴿وَلَتَسْمَعُنَّ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ﴾ [سورة آل عمران: 186] } الآيَةَ فَلَمَّا أَبَى كَعْبُ بْنُ الأَشْرَفِ أَنْ يَنْزِعَ عَنْ أَذَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَعْدَ بْنَ مُعَاذٍ أَنْ يَبْعَثَ رَهْطًا يَقْتُلُونَهُ. فَبَعَثَ مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ مَسْلَمَةَ وَذَكَرَ قِصَّةَ قَتْلِهِ، فَلَمَّا قَتَلُوهُ فَزِعَتِ الْيَهُودُ وَالْمُشْرِكُونَ، فَغَدَوْا عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالُوا: طُرِقَ صَاحِبُنَا فَقُتِلَ. فَذَكَرَ لَهُمُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الَّذِي كَانَ يَقُولُ، وَدَعَاهُمُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى أَنْ يَكْتُبَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهُمْ كِتَابًا يَنْتَهُونَ إِلَى مَا فِيهِ، فَكَتَبَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ عَامَّةً صَحِيفَةً."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3000) عن محمد بن يحيى بن فارس، أن الحكم بن نافع حدثهم قال: أخبرنا شعيب، عن الزهري، عن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن كعب فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قتل كعب بن الأشرف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3000).","chapter_en":"The Killing of Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated from his father, who was one of the three whose repentance was accepted: Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf used to satirize the Prophet ﷺ and incite the disbelievers of Quraysh against him. When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, its people were mixed: among them were Muslims, polytheists who worshiped idols, and Jews. They used to harm the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded His Prophet to be patient and pardon. Concerning them Allah revealed: “And you will surely hear from those who were given the Scripture before you…” [Āl ʿImrān: 186]. When Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf refused to stop harming the Prophet ﷺ, the Prophet ﷺ ordered Saʿd ibn Muʿādh to send a group to kill him. So he sent Muḥammad ibn Maslamah, and he mentioned the story of his killing. When they killed him, the Jews and polytheists were terrified, and they came to the Prophet ﷺ in the morning and said, “Our companion was attacked at night and killed.” The Prophet ﷺ mentioned to them what he used to say, and the Prophet ﷺ called them to write a document between him and them to which they would adhere. So the Prophet ﷺ wrote a document between himself, them, and the Muslims in general."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His phrase “from his father” means his grandfather, because his grandfather Kaʿb ibn Mālik was one of the three."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",392],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3000)."},{"num":8807,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: بَعَثَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَهْطًا إِلَى أَبِي رَافِعٍ، فَدَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عَتِيكٍ بَيْتَهُ لَيْلاً وَهْوَ نَائِمٌ فَقَتَلَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4038) عن إسحاق بن نصر، حدثنا يحيى بن آدم، حدثنا ابن أبي زائدة، عن أبيه، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء بن عازب فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قتل أبي رافع عبد الله بن أبي الحقيق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4038).","chapter_en":"The Killing of Abū Rāfiʿ ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Ḥuqayq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a group to Abū Rāfiʿ. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAtīk entered his house at night while he was sleeping and killed him."]},"intro":{"ar":["ويقال: سلام بن أبي الحقيق، كان بخيبر، ويقال: في حصن له بأرض الحجاز. وقال الزهري: هو بعد كعب بن الأشرف."],"en":["It is also said: Sallām ibn Abī al-Ḥuqayq. He was at Khaybar, and it is said: in a fortress of his in the land of the Ḥijāz. Al-Zuhrī said: This was after Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",394],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4038)."},{"num":8808,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ، قَالَ: بَعَثَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى أَبِي رَافِعٍ الْيَهُودِيِّ رِجَالاً مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، فَأَمَّرَ عَلَيْهِمْ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عَتِيكٍ، وَكَانَ أَبُو رَافِعٍ يُؤْذِي رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَيُعِينُ عَلَيْهِ، وَكَانَ فِي حِصْنٍ لَهُ بِأَرْضِ الْحِجَازِ، فَلَمَّا دَنَوْا مِنْهُ، وَقَدْ غَرَبَتِ الشَّمْسُ، وَرَاحَ النَّاسُ بِسَرْحِهِمْ، فَقَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ لأَصْحَابِهِ: اجْلِسُوا مَكَانَكُمْ، فَإِنِّي مُنْطَلِقٌ، وَمُتَلَطِّفٌ لِلْبَوَّابِ، لَعَلِّي أَنْ أَدْخُلَ. فَأَقْبَلَ حَتَّى دَنَا مِنَ الْبَابِ، ثُمَّ تَقَنَّعَ بِثَوْبِهِ كَأَنَّهُ يَقْضِي حَاجَةً، وَقَدْ دَخَلَ النَّاسُ، فَهَتَفَ بِهِ الْبَوَّابُ، يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ: إِنْ كُنْتَ تُرِيدُ أَنْ تَدْخُلَ فَادْخُلْ، فَإِنِّي أُرِيدُ أَنْ أُغْلِقَ الْبَابَ. فَدَخَلْتُ فَكَمَنْتُ، فَلَمَّا دَخَلَ النَّاسُ أَغْلَقَ الْبَابَ، ثُمَّ عَلَّقَ الأَغَالِيقَ عَلَى وَتَدٍ، قَالَ: فَقُمْتُ إِلَى الأَقَالِيدِ، فَأَخَذْتُهَا، فَفَتَحْتُ الْبَابَ، وَكَانَ أَبُو رَافِعٍ يُسْمَرُ عِنْدَهُ، وَكَانَ فِي عَلاَلِيَّ لَهُ، فَلَمَّا ذَهَبَ عَنْهُ أَهْلُ سَمَرِهِ، صَعِدْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَجَعَلْتُ كُلَّمَا فَتَحْتُ بَابًا أَغْلَقْتُ عَلَىَّ مِنْ دَاخِلٍ، قُلْتُ: إِنِ الْقَوْمُ نَذِرُوا بِي لَمْ يَخْلُصُوا إِلَىَّ حَتَّى أَقْتُلَهُ. فَانْتَهَيْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَإِذَا هُوَ فِي بَيْتٍ مُظْلِمٍ وَسْطَ عِيَالِهِ، لاَ أَدْرِي أَيْنَ هُوَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا أَبَا رَافِعٍ. قَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ فَأَهْوَيْتُ نَحْوَ الصَّوْتِ، فَأَضْرِبُهُ ضَرْبَةً بِالسَّيْفِ، وَأَنَا دَهِشٌ، فَمَا أَغْنَيْتُ شَيْئًا، وَصَاحَ، فَخَرَجْتُ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ، فَأَمْكُثُ غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍ، ثُمَّ دَخَلْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَقُلْتُ: مَا هَذَا الصَّوْتُ يَا أَبَا رَافِعٍ. فَقَالَ: لأُمِّكَ الْوَيْلُ، إِنَّ رَجُلاً فِي الْبَيْتِ ضَرَبَنِي قَبْلُ بِالسَّيْفِ، قَالَ: فَأَضْرِبُهُ ضَرْبَةً أَثْخَنَتْهُ وَلَمْ أَقْتُلْهُ، ثُمَّ وَضَعْتُ ظُبَةَ السَّيْفِ فِي بَطْنِهِ حَتَّى أَخَذَ فِي ظَهْرِهِ، فَعَرَفْتُ أَنِّي قَتَلْتُهُ، فَجَعَلْتُ أَفْتَحُ الأَبْوَابَ بَابًا بَابًا، حَتَّى انْتَهَيْتُ إِلَى دَرَجَةٍ لَهُ، فَوَضَعْتُ رِجْلِي، وَأَنَا أُرَى أَنِّي قَدِ انْتَهَيْتُ إِلَى الأَرْضِ، فَوَقَعْتُ فِي لَيْلَةٍ مُقْمِرَةٍ، فَانْكَسَرَتْ سَاقِي، فَعَصَبْتُهَا بِعِمَامَةٍ، ثُمَّ انْطَلَقْتُ حَتَّى جَلَسْتُ عَلَى الْبَابِ، فَقُلْتُ: لاَ أَخْرُجُ اللَّيْلَةَ حَتَّى أَعْلَمَ: أَقَتَلْتُهُ؟ فَلَمَّا صَاحَ الدِّيكُ قَامَ النَّاعِي عَلَى السُّورِ، فَقَالَ: أَنْعَى أَبَا رَافِعٍ تَاجِرَ أَهْلِ الْحِجَازِ. فَانْطَلَقْتُ إِلَى أَصْحَابِي فَقُلْتُ: النَّجَاءَ، فَقَدْ قَتَلَ اللَّهُ أَبَا رَافِعٍ. فَانْتَهَيْتُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَحَدَّثْتُهُ فَقَالَ: ابْسُطْ رِجْلَكَ. فَبَسَطْتُ رِجْلِي، فَمَسَحَهَا، فَكَأَنَّهَا لَمْ أَشْتَكِهَا قَطُّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4039) عن يوسف بن موسى، حدثنا عبيد الله بن موسى، عن إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء فذكره. صلى الله عليه وسلم","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قتل أبي رافع عبد الله بن أبي الحقيق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4039).","chapter_en":"The Killing of Abū Rāfiʿ ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Ḥuqayq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent some men from the Anṣār to Abū Rāfiʿ the Jew and appointed ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAtīk over them. Abū Rāfiʿ used to harm the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and support others against him, and he had a fortress in the land of the Ḥijāz. When they came near him, the sun had set and the people had returned with their livestock. ʿAbdullāh said to his companions, “Sit in your place. I am going and will act gently with the gatekeeper; perhaps I will be able to enter.” He came forward until he drew near to the gate, then covered himself with his garment as if relieving himself, while the people had entered. The gatekeeper called out to him, “O ʿAbdullāh, if you want to enter, then enter, for I intend to close the gate.” So I entered and hid. When the people had entered, he closed the gate and hung the keys on a peg. He said: I went to the keys, took them, and opened the gate. Abū Rāfiʿ used to have people sit with him at night, and he was in an upper chamber of his. When those who had spent the evening with him left, I climbed up to him, and every time I opened a door, I locked it behind me from the inside. I said: If the people become aware of me, they will not reach me until I have killed him. I reached him, and he was in a dark room among his family. I did not know where he was in the room, so I said, “O Abū Rāfiʿ.” He said, “Who is this?” I moved toward the voice and struck him with the sword while I was startled, but I did not do anything effective. He cried out, so I left the room and stayed not far away. Then I entered upon him again and said, “What is that sound, O Abū Rāfiʿ?” He said, “May your mother be bereaved; a man in the house struck me with a sword just now.” He said: I struck him with a blow that wounded him severely but did not kill him. Then I placed the tip of the sword in his belly until it reached his back, and I knew that I had killed him. I began opening the doors one by one until I reached a stairway of his. I placed my foot down, thinking I had reached the ground, but I fell on a moonlit night and broke my leg. I tied it with a turban, then went and sat at the gate. I said: I will not leave tonight until I know whether I killed him. When the rooster crowed, the announcer of death stood on the wall and said, “I announce the death of Abū Rāfiʿ, the merchant of the people of the Ḥijāz.” I went to my companions and said, “Escape, for Allah has killed Abū Rāfiʿ.” I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. He said, “Stretch out your leg.” I stretched out my leg, and he wiped it, and it was as though I had never complained of it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",395],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4039)."},{"num":8809,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ كَعْبِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ رضي الله عنه قَالَ: عَهِدَ إِلَيْنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  ونحن بخيبر أن لا نَقْتُلَ صَبِيًّا وَلَا امْرَأَةً."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه ( المطالب العالية- 1959) عن روح بن عبادة، حدثنا محمد بن أبي حفصة، عن الزهري، عن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن كعب بن مالك أو عبد الله بن كعب – وكان قائد كعب بن مالك – عن كعب بن مالك فذكره، قال الحافظ في المطالب: هذا إسناد صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قتل أبي رافع عبد الله بن أبي الحقيق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Isḥāq ibn Rāhwayh, al-Maṭālib al-ʿĀliyah (1959).","chapter_en":"The Killing of Abū Rāfiʿ ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Ḥuqayq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع الأحداث التي بين غزوة بدر وبين غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of Events between the Battle of Badr and the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed us, while we were at Khaybar, not to kill a child or a woman."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",396],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7906],"tks":"صحيح: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه، المطالب العالية (1959)."},{"num":8810,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ كَأَنِّي فِي دِرْعٍ حَصِينَةٍ، وَرَأَيْتُ بَقَرًا مُنَحَّرَةً، فَأَوَّلْتُ أَنَّ الدِّرْعَ الْحَصِينَةَ الْمَدِينَةُ، وَأَنَّ الْبَقَرَ نَفَرٌ، وَاللهِ خَيْرٌ.","قَالَ: فَقَالَ لِأَصْحَابِهِ: لَوْ أَنَّا أَقَمْنَا بِالْمَدِينَةِ، فَإِنْ دَخَلُوا عَلَيْنَا فِيهَا، قَاتَلْنَاهُمْ فَقَالَوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَاللَّهِ مَا دُخِلَ عَلَيْنَا فِيهَا فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، فَكَيْفَ يُدْخَلُ عَلَيْنَا فِيهَا فِي الْإِسْلَامِ؟! قَالَ عَفَّانُ فِي حَدِيثِهِ: فَقَالَ: شَأْنَكُمْ إِذًا قَالَ: فَلَبِسَ لَأْمَتَهُ، قَالَ: فَقَالَتِ الْأَنْصَارُ: رَدَدْنَا عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَأْيَهُ، فجاؤوا، فَقَالَوا: يَا رسول اللَّهِ! شَأْنَكَ إِذًا، فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ لَيْسَ لِنَبِيٍّ إِذَا لَبِسَ لَأْمَتَهُ أَنْ يَضَعَهَا حَتَّى يُقَاتِلَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (14787)، والنسائي في الكبرى (7600) كلاهما من طريق حماد بن سلمة، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر فذكره. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب مشاورة النبي ﷺ للخروج من المدينة لمواجهة العدو والدفاع عن أهل المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (14787) and al-Nasā’ī in al-Kubrā (7600).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Consulting about Leaving Madinah to Face the Enemy and Defend the People of Madinah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I saw as if I were inside a fortified coat of armor, and I saw cattle being slaughtered. I interpreted the fortified armor as Madinah, and the cattle as—by Allah, good.” He said: He said to his Companions, “If we remain in Madinah, then if they enter upon us there, we will fight them.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, they never entered upon us there in Jāhiliyyah, so how could they enter upon us there in Islam?” ʿAffān said in his narration: He said, “Then it is your affair.” He put on his armor. The Anṣār then said, “We have rejected the opinion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” They came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, then do as you wish.” He said, “It is not for a prophet, once he has put on his armor, to take it off until he fights.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",398],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (14787)، والنسائي في الكبرى (7600)."},{"num":8811,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى، ـ أُرَاهُ ـ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ فِي الْمَنَامِ، أَنِّي أُهَاجِرُ مِنْ مَكَّةَ إِلَى أَرْضٍ بِهَا نَخْلٌ، فَذَهَبَ وَهَلِي إِلَى أَنَّهَا الْيَمَامَةُ، أَوْ هَجَرُ، فَإِذَا هِيَ الْمَدِينَةُ يَثْرِبُ، وَرَأَيْتُ فِي رُؤْيَاىَ هَذِهِ أَنِّي هَزَزْتُ سَيْفًا فَانْقَطَعَ صَدْرُهُ، فَإِذَا هُوَ مَا أُصِيبَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، ثُمَّ هَزَزْتُهُ بِأُخْرَى فَعَادَ أَحْسَنَ مَا كَانَ، فَإِذَا هُوَ مَا جَاءَ اللَّهُ بِهِ مِنَ الْفَتْحِ وَاجْتِمَاعِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، وَرَأَيْتُ فِيهَا بَقَرًا، وَاللَّهُ خَيْرٌ، فَإِذَا هُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، وَإِذَا الْخَيْرُ مَا جَاءَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الْخَيْرِ، وَثَوَابِ الصِّدْقِ الَّذِي آتَانَا اللَّهُ بَعْدَ يَوْمِ بَدْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3622) ومسلم في كتاب الرؤيا (2272) كلاهما من حديث حماد بن أسامة أبي أسامة، عن بريد بن عبد الله بن أبي بردة، عن جده أبي بردة، عن أبي موسى فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب مشاورة النبي ﷺ للخروج من المدينة لمواجهة العدو والدفاع عن أهل المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3622) and Muslim (2272).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Consulting about Leaving Madinah to Face the Enemy and Defend the People of Madinah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I saw in a dream that I was emigrating from Makkah to a land filled with date palms. At first I thought it was al-Yamāmah or Hajar, but it turned out to be Madinah, Yathrib. In that same dream I shook my sword, and its blade broke. I interpreted that as what befell the believers on the Day of Uḥud. Then I shook it again, and it returned even better than before. I interpreted that as the victory Allah granted and the reunion of the believers. I also saw cattle—and Allah is the source of all good. They represented the believers on the Day of Uḥud, while the good referred to the goodness Allah later brought and the reward for truthfulness that He granted us after Badr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",399],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3622)، ومسلم (2272)."},{"num":8812,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، قَالَ: تَنَفَّلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَيْفَهُ ذَا الْفَقَارِ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: وَهُوَ الَّذِي رَأَى فِيهِ الرُّؤْيَا يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، وَذَلِكَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا جَاءَهُ الْمُشْرِكُونَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ كَانَ رَأْيُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يُقِيمَ بِالْمَدِينَةِ يُقَاتِلُهُمْ فِيهَا فَقَالَ لَهُ نَاسٌ: لَمْ يَكُونُوا شَهِدُوا بَدْرًا أَتَخْرُجُ بِنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَيْهِمْ نُقَاتِلْهُمْ بِأُحُدٍ، وَرَجَوْا أَنْ يُصِيبُوا مِنَ الْفَضِيلَةِ مَا أَصَابَ أَهْلُ بَدْرٍ، فَمَا زَالُوا بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى لَبِسَ أَدَاتَهُ فَنَدِمُوا وَقَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَقِمْ فَالرَّأْيُ رَأْيُكَ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا يَنْبَغِي لِنَبِيٍّ أَنْ يَضَعَ أَدَاتَهُ بَعْدَ أَنْ لَبِسَهَا، حَتَّى يَحْكُمَ اللَّهُ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَ عَدُوِّهِ قَالَ: وَكَانَ مِمَّا قَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَئِذٍ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَلْبَسَ الْأَدَاةَ: إِنِّي رَأَيْتُ أَنِّي فِي دِرْعٍ حَصِينَةٍ، فَأَوَّلْتُهَا الْمَدِينَةَ، وَأَنِّي مُرْدِفٌ كَبْشًا، فَأَوَّلْتُهُ كَبْشَ الْكَتِيبَةِ، وَرَأَيْتُ أَنَّ سَيْفِي ذَا الْفَقَارِ، فُلَّ فَأَوَّلْتُهُ فَلًّا فِيكُمْ، وَرَأَيْتُ بَقَرًا تُذْبَحُ، فَبَقَرٌ، وَاللَّهِ خَيْرٌ، فَبَقَرٌ وَاللَّهِ خَيْرٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (2588) عن أبي العباس محمد بن يعقوب، أنبأنا محمد بن عبد الله بن عبد الحكم، أنبأنا ابن وهب، أخبرني ابن الزناد، عن أبيه، عن عبيد الله بن عبد الله بن عتبة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب مشاورة النبي ﷺ للخروج من المدينة لمواجهة العدو والدفاع عن أهل المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ḥākim (2588), and in abbreviated form by al-Tirmidhī (1561), Ibn Mājah (2808), and Aḥmad (2445).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Consulting about Leaving Madinah to Face the Enemy and Defend the People of Madinah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ awarded himself the sword Dhū al-Fiqār on the Day of Badr. Ibn ʿAbbās said: This was the sword concerning which he saw the dream before Uḥud. When the polytheists came for the Battle of Uḥud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ preferred to remain inside Madinah and fight them there. But some people who had not witnessed Badr said: “O Messenger of Allah, take us out to meet them at Uḥud so that we may attain the virtue attained by the people of Badr.” They continued urging the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he put on his armor. Then they regretted it and said: “O Messenger of Allah, remain here, for the decision is yours.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “It is not appropriate for a prophet to remove his armor after putting it on until Allah judges between him and his enemy.” He also said: “I saw myself inside a fortified coat of armor, and I interpreted it as Madinah. I saw that I had a ram riding behind me, and I interpreted it as the commander of the army. I saw that my sword Dhū al-Fiqār had a notch in it, and I interpreted it as a calamity that would befall you. I also saw cattle being slaughtered—and the cattle, by Allah, are good.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",400],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (2588)، ورواه الترمذي (1561)، وابن ماجه (2808)، وأحمد (2445) مختصرا."},{"num":8813,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الزُّبَيْرِ بْنِ الْعَوَّامِ، قَالَ: كَانَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دِرْعَانِ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، فَنَهَضَ إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ فَلَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ، فَأَقْعَدَ طَلْحَةَ تَحْتَهُ، فَصَعِدَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْهِ، حَتَّى اسْتَوَى عَلَى الصَّخْرَةِ، فَقَالَ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: أَوْجَبَ طَلْحَةُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3738،1692) وأحمد (1417) وابن حبان (6979) والحاكم (5602) والبيهقي (6/370 ، 9/46) من طرق عن محمد بن إسحاق (وهو في سيرته كما في سيرة ابن هشام 2/86) قال: حدثني يحيى بن عباد بن عبد الله بن الزبير، عن أبيه، عن جده عبد الله بن الزبير، عن الزبير بن العوام فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لبس النبي ﷺ الدرعين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1692, 3738), Aḥmad (1417), Ibn Ḥibbān (6979), and al-Ḥākim (5602).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Wearing Two Coats of Armor","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated: The Prophet ﷺ wore two coats of armor on the Day of Uḥud. When he attempted to climb a large rock, he was unable to do so. Ṭalḥah sat beneath him, allowing the Prophet ﷺ to step upon him until he reached the top of the rock. Al-Zubayr said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Ṭalḥah has secured Paradise.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The statement “Ṭalḥah has secured Paradise” means that he performed a deed deserving Paradise."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",402],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7937,9616,9934],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1692، 3738)، وأحمد (1417)، وابن حبان (6979)، والحاكم (5602)."},{"num":8814,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ السَّائِبِ بْنِ يَزِيدَ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ظَاهَرَ بَيْنَ دِرْعَيْنِ يَوْمَ أُحُد."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (15722) والشافعي في الأم (505) وسعيد بن منصور (2858) كلهم عن سفيان بن عيينة، عن يزيد بن خصيفة، عن السائب بن يزيد فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لبس النبي ﷺ الدرعين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (15722), al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm (4/252), and Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr (2858).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Wearing Two Coats of Armor","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Sā’ib ibn Yazīd narrated: The Prophet ﷺ wore two coats of armor together on the Day of Uḥud."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",403],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (15722)، والشافعي في الأم (505)، وسعيد بن منصور (2858)."},{"num":8815,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَخَذَ سَيْفًا يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ فَقَالَ: مَنْ يَأْخُذُ مِنِّي هَذَا؟ فَبَسَطُوا أَيْدِيَهُمْ كُلُّ إِنْسَانٍ مِنْهُمْ يَقُولُ: أَنَا، أَنَا. قَالَ: فَمَنْ يَأْخُذُهُ بِحَقِّهِ؟ قَالَ: فَأَحْجَمَ الْقَوْمُ، فَقَالَ سِمَاكُ بْنُ خَرَشَةَ أَبُو دُجَانَةَ: أَنَا آخُذُهُ بِحَقِّهِ. قَالَ: فَأَخَذَهُ فَفَلَقَ بِهِ هَامَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الفضائل (2470) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا عفان، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، حدثنا ثابت، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اختيار النبي ﷺ أبا دجانة لمنحه السيف ليقاتل به المشركين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2470).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Choosing Abū Dujānah to Receive the Sword","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a sword on the Day of Uḥud and said: “Who will take this sword from me with its due right?” Many stretched out their hands, each saying: “I will! I will!” He then asked: “Who will take it with its due right?” The people hesitated. Then Simāk ibn Kharashah, Abū Dujānah, said: “I will take it with its due right.” He took it and split open the heads of the polytheists with it."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Abū Dujānah was a courageous warrior. Whenever he tied on his distinctive red headband, people knew he was entering fierce combat. After receiving the Prophet’s ﷺ sword, he put on that red headband and strode proudly between the battle lines."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",405],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10331],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2470)."},{"num":8816,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: جَاءَ عَلِيٌّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ بِسَيْفِهِ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، قَدِ انْحَنَى، فَقَالَ لِفَاطِمَةَ: رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا: هَاكِي السَّيْفَ حُمَيْدًا، فَإِنَّهَا قَدْ شَفَتْنِي، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَئِنْ كُنْتَ أَجَدْتَ الضَّرْبَ بِسَيْفِكَ لَقَدْ أَجَادَهُ سَهْلُ بْنُ حُنَيْفٍ، وَأَبُو دُجَانَةَ، وَعَاصِمُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ الْأَفْلَحُ، وَالْحَارِثُ بْنُ الصِّمَّةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الحاكم (4309) وعنه البيهقي في الدلائل (894) عن محمد بن عبد الله الصغار، ثنا أبو الحسن علي بن محمد الثقفي بالكوفة، ثنا منجاب بن الحارث التميمي، قال: زعم سفيان بن عيينة، عن عمرو بن دينار، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أحسن القتال يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ḥākim (4309) and al-Bayhaqī in Dalā’il al-Nubuwwah (3/283–284).","chapter_en":"Those Who Excelled in Fighting at Uḥud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: ʿAlī came carrying his sword on the Day of Uḥud after it had become bent. He said to Fāṭimah: “Take this sword with praise, for it has satisfied me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you have fought well with your sword, then Sahl ibn Ḥunayf, Abū Dujānah, ʿĀṣim ibn Thābit al-Aflaḥ, and al-Ḥārith ibn al-Ṣimmah have also fought excellently.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",406],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الحاكم (4309)، والبيهقي في دلائل النبوة (894)."},{"num":8817,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي عُقْبَةَ، - وَكَانَ مَوْلًى مِنْ أَهْلِ فَارِسَ - قَالَ: شَهِدْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أُحُدًا فَضَرَبْتُ رَجُلاً مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ فَقُلْتُ: خُذْهَا مِنِّي وَأَنَا الْغُلاَمُ الْفَارِسِيُّ فَالْتَفَتَ إِلَىَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: فَهَلاَّ قُلْتَ خُذْهَا مِنِّي وَأَنَا الْغُلاَمُ الأَنْصَارِيُّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (5123)، وابن ماجه (2784)، وأحمد (22515) كلهم من طريق الحسين بن محمد، حدثنا جرير بن حازم، عن محمد بن إسحاق، عن داود بن حصين، عن عبد الرحمن بن أبى عقبة، عن أبي عقبة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من أحسن القتال يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (5123), Ibn Mājah (2784), and Aḥmad (22515).","chapter_en":"Those Who Excelled in Fighting at Uḥud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū ʿUqbah, a freedman of Persian origin, said: I fought with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Uḥud. I struck one of the polytheists and said: “Take that from me—I am the Persian youth!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward me and said: “Why did you not say: ‘Take that from me—I am the Anṣārī youth’?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",407],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (5123)، وابن ماجه (2784)، وأحمد (22515)."},{"num":8818,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ هُزِمَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ، فَصَرَخَ إِبْلِيسُ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ أَىْ عِبَادَ اللَّهِ أُخْرَاكُمْ. فَرَجَعَتْ أُولاَهُمْ، فَاجْتَلَدَتْ هِيَ وَأُخْرَاهُمْ، فَبَصُرَ حُذَيْفَةُ فَإِذَا هُوَ بِأَبِيهِ الْيَمَانِ، فَقَالَ: أَىْ عِبَادَ اللَّهِ أَبِي أَبِي. قَالَ: قَالَتْ: فَوَاللَّهِ مَا احْتَجَزُوا حَتَّى قَتَلُوهُ، فَقَالَ حُذَيْفَةُ: يَغْفِرُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ. قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: فَوَاللَّهِ مَا زَالَتْ فِي حُذَيْفَةَ بَقِيَّةُ خَيْرٍ حَتَّى لَحِقَ بِاللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4065) عن عبيد الله بن سعيد، حدثنا أبو أسامة، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب هزيمة المشركين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4065).","chapter_en":"The Initial Defeat of the Polytheists at Uḥud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated: When the Day of Uḥud came, the polytheists were initially defeated. Then Iblīs—may Allah curse him—shouted: “O servants of Allah, those behind you!” So the front ranks of the Muslims turned back toward those behind them, and they began fighting one another. Ḥudhayfah then saw that one of those being attacked was his own father, al-Yamān. He cried out: “O servants of Allah! My father! My father!” But, by Allah, they did not stop until they killed him. Ḥudhayfah then said: “May Allah forgive you.” ʿUrwah said: By Allah, there remained in Ḥudhayfah a remnant of goodness until he met Allah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",408],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4065)."},{"num":8819,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الزُّبَيْرِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: وَاللَّهِ إِنِّي لَأَنْظُرُ يَوْمَئِذٍ إِلَى خَدَمِ النِّسَاءِ، مُشَمِّرَاتٍ يَسْعَيْنَ حِينَ انْهَزَمَ الْقَوْمُ، وَمَا أَرَى دُونَ أَخْذِهِنَّ شَيْئًا، وَإِنَّا لَنَحْسَبُهُمْ قَتْلَى مَا يَرْجِعُ إِلَيْنَا مِنْهُمْ أَحَدٌ، وَلَقَدْ أُصِيبَ أَصْحَابُ اللِّوَاءِ، وَصَبَرُوا عِنْدَهُ حَتَّى صَارَ إِلَى عبد له حَبَشِيٍّ، يُقَالُ لَهُ صَوَابٌ ثُمَّ قُتِلَ صَوَابٌ فَطُرِحَ اللِّوَاءُ فَمَا يَقْرَبُهُ أَحَدٌ مِنْ خلق الله تعالى، حَتَّى وَثَبَتْ إِلَيْهِ عَمْرَةُ بِنْتُ عَلْقَمَةَ الحارثية، فَرَفَعَتْهُ لَهُمْ، وَثَابَ إِلَيْهِ النَّاسُ.","قَالَ الزُّبَيْرُ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ: فَوَاللَّهِ إِنَّا لَكَذَلِكَ قَدْ عَلَوْنَاهُمْ وَظَهَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ، إِذْ خَالَفَتِ الرُّمَاةُ عَنْ أَمْرِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَقْبَلُوا إِلَى الْعَسْكَرِ حِينَ رَأَوْهُ مُخْتَلًّا قَدْ أَجْهَضْنَاهُمْ عَنْهُ، فَرَغَبُوا إلى الْغَنَائِمِ، وَتَرَكُوا عَهْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ، فَجَعَلُوا يَأْخُذُونَ الْأَمْتِعَةَ، فأتَتْنا الْخَيْلُ مِنْ خَلْفِنَا، فَحَطَّمَتْنَا، وَكَرَّ النَّاسُ مُنْهَزِمِينَ، فَصَرَخَ صَارِخٌ يَرَوْنَ أَنَّهُ الشَّيْطَانُ: إِلَّا إِنَّ مُحَمَّدًا قد قتل. فأعظم النَّاسُ، وَرَكِبَ بَعْضُهُمْ بَعْضًا، فَصَارُوا أَثْلَاثًا: ثُلُثًا جريحًا، وثلثًا مَقْتُولًا، وَثُلُثًا مُنْهَزِمًا ، قَدْ بَلَغَتِ الْحَرْبُ، وَقَدْ كَانَتِ الرُّمَاةُ اخْتَلَفُوا فِيمَا بَيْنَهُمْ، فَقَالَتْ طَائِفَةٌ رَأَوُا النَّاسَ وَقَعُوا فِي الْغَنَائِمِ، وَقَدْ هَزَمَ الله تعالى الْمُشْرِكِينِ، وَأَخَذَ الْمُسْلِمُونَ الْغَنَائِمَ: فَمَاذَا تَنْتَظِرُونَ؟ وَقَالَتْ طَائِفَةٌ: قَدْ تَقَدَّمَ إِلَيْكُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَهَاكُمْ أَنْ تُفَارِقُوا مَكَانَكُمْ إِنْ كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِ أوْ لَهُ، فَتَنَازَعُوا فِي ذَلِكَ، ثُمَّ إِنَّ الطَّائِفَةَ الْأُولَى مِنَ الرُّمَاةِ أَبَتْ إِلَّا أَنْ تَلْحَقَ بِالْعَسْكَرِ، فَتَفَرَّقَ الْقَوْمُ، وَتَرَكُوا مَكَانَهُمْ، فَعِنْدَ ذَلِكَ حَمَلَتْ خَيْلُ الْمُشْرِكِينَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه إسحاق في \"مسنده\" عن وهب بن جرير بن حازم، حدثنا أبي قال: سمعت محمد بن إسحاق يقول: حدثني يحيى بن عباد، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن الزبير، عن الزبير فذكره. \"المطالب العالية\" (4260) وهو عند ابن إسحاق في سيرته (507) مختصراً، وأخرجه الحاكم (3/27) من طريق يونس بن بكير، عن ابن إسحاق مختصراً.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب هزيمة المشركين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ishaq in his Musnad, as cited in al-Matalib al-ʿAliyah (4260).","chapter_en":"The Initial Defeat of the Polytheists at Uḥud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Zubayr said: “By Allah, that day I could see the women’s anklets as they ran with their garments raised after the enemy had been routed. I saw nothing standing between us and capturing them. We thought that the enemy had been killed and that none of them would ever return to us. The standard-bearers had been struck down, [but they remained steadfast around the standard until it passed to an Abyssinian slave of theirs named Sawab. Then Sawab was killed and the standard fell]. No one among Allah Most High’s creation would approach it until ʿAmrah bint ʿAlqamah al-Harithiyyah sprang toward it, raised it for them, and the people rallied around it.","“By Allah, we remained in that condition, having gained the upper hand over them and defeated them, when the archers disobeyed the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They went down toward the camp when they saw it left exposed after we had driven the enemy away from it. They desired the spoils and abandoned their covenant with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and began taking the belongings. The cavalry then came upon us from behind and crushed our ranks. The people turned back in flight, and someone—whom they believed to be Satan—shouted, ‘Muhammad has been killed!’ The people were struck with tremendous alarm and trampled over one another. They became three groups: one-third wounded, one-third killed, and one-third fleeing. The battle had reached its height. “The archers had disagreed among themselves. One group, seeing the people collecting the spoils after Allah Most High had defeated the polytheists and the Muslims had taken the booty, said, ‘What are you waiting for?’ Another group said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave you explicit instructions and forbade you from leaving your position, whether the battle went against him or in his favor.’ They disputed over this. Then the first group of archers insisted on joining the army, so the men dispersed and abandoned their position. It was then that the cavalry of the polytheists charged.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",409],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه إسحاق في «مسنده» كما في «المطالب العالية» (4260)."},{"num":8820,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يُحَدِّثُ قَالَ: جَعَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الرَّجَّالَةِ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ ـ وَكَانُوا خَمْسِينَ رَجُلاً ـ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ جُبَيْرٍ فَقَالَ: إِنْ رَأَيْتُمُونَا تَخْطَفُنَا الطَّيْرُ، فَلاَ تَبْرَحُوا مَكَانَكُمْ هَذَا حَتَّى أُرْسِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ، وَإِنْ رَأَيْتُمُونَا هَزَمْنَا الْقَوْمَ وَأَوْطَأْنَاهُمْ فَلاَ تَبْرَحُوا حَتَّى أُرْسِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ، فَهَزَمُوهُمْ. قَالَ: فَأَنَا وَاللَّهِ رَأَيْتُ النِّسَاءَ يَشْتَدِدْنَ قَدْ بَدَتْ خَلاَخِلُهُنَّ وَأَسْوُقُهُنَّ، رَافِعَاتٍ ثِيَابَهُنَّ، فَقَالَ أَصْحَابُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ جُبَيْرٍ: الْغَنِيمَةَ ـ أَىْ قَوْمِ ـ الْغَنِيمَةَ، ظَهَرَ أَصْحَابُكُمْ فَمَا تَنْتَظِرُونَ؟ فَقَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ جُبَيْرٍ: أَنَسِيتُمْ مَا قَالَ لَكُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالُوا: وَاللَّهِ لَنَأْتِيَنَّ النَّاسَ فَلَنُصِيبَنَّ مِنَ الْغَنِيمَةِ. فَلَمَّا أَتَوْهُمْ صُرِفَتْ وُجُوهُهُمْ، فَأَقْبَلُوا مُنْهَزِمِينَ، فَذَاكَ إِذْ يَدْعُوهُمُ الرَّسُولُ فِي أُخْرَاهُمْ، فَلَمْ يَبْقَ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ غَيْرُ اثْنَىْ عَشَرَ رَجُلاً، فَأَصَابُوا مِنَّا سَبْعِينَ، وَكَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابُهُ أَصَابَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ أَرْبَعِينَ وَمِائَةً سَبْعِينَ أَسِيرًا وَسَبْعِينَ قَتِيلاً، فَقَالَ أَبُو سُفْيَانَ: أَفِي الْقَوْمِ مُحَمَّدٌ؟ ثَلاَثَ مَرَّاتٍ، فَنَهَاهُمُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يُجِيبُوهُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَفِي الْقَوْمِ ابْنُ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ؟ ثَلاَثَ مَرَّاتٍ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَفِي الْقَوْمِ ابْنُ الْخَطَّابِ؟ ثَلاَثَ مَرَّاتٍ، ثُمَّ رَجَعَ إِلَى أَصْحَابِهِ فَقَالَ: أَمَّا هَؤُلاَءِ فَقَدْ قُتِلُوا. فَمَا مَلَكَ عُمَرُ نَفْسَهُ فَقَالَ: كَذَبْتَ وَاللَّهِ يَا عَدُوَّ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ الَّذِينَ عَدَدْتَ لأَحْيَاءٌ كُلُّهُمْ، وَقَدْ بَقِيَ لَكَ مَا يَسُوؤُكَ. قَالَ: يَوْمٌ بِيَوْمِ بَدْرٍ، وَالْحَرْبُ سِجَالٌ، إِنَّكُمْ سَتَجِدُونَ فِي الْقَوْمِ مُثْلَةً لَمْ آمُرْ بِهَا وَلَمْ تَسُؤْنِي، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ يَرْتَجِزُ: أُعْلُ هُبَلْ، أُعْلُ هُبَلْ. قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَلاَ تُجِيبُوا لَهُ. قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، مَا نَقُولُ؟ قَالَ: قُولُوا: اللَّهُ أَعْلَى وَأَجَلُّ. قَالَ: إِنَّ لَنَا الْعُزَّى وَلاَ عُزَّى لَكُمْ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَلاَ تُجِيبُوا لَهُ. قَالَ: قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، مَا نَقُولُ؟ قَالَ: قُولُوا: اللَّهُ مَوْلاَنَا وَلاَ مَوْلَى لَكُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (3039) عن عمرو بن خالد، حدثنا زهير، حدثنا أبو إسحاق (هو السبيعي) قال: سمعت البراء بن عازب يحدّث فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ترك الرماة الجبل الذي عيّنهم عليه رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3039).","chapter_en":"The Archers Abandoning the Mountain upon Which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ Had Stationed Them","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Baraʾ ibn ʿAzib reported that on the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ appointed ʿAbdullah ibn Jubayr as commander over the infantry, who numbered fifty men. He said: “Even if you see birds snatching us away, do not leave this position until I send for you. And if you see us defeat and trample the enemy, do not leave until I send for you.” The Muslims defeated them. Al-Baraʾ said: “By Allah, I saw the women running swiftly with their garments raised, their anklets and lower legs exposed. The men under Ibn Jubayr said, ‘The spoils, people! The spoils! Your companions have prevailed, so what are you waiting for?’ ʿAbdullah ibn Jubayr said, ‘Have you forgotten what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told you?’ They replied, ‘By Allah, we will go to the people and obtain a share of the spoils.’ “When they reached them, the tide was turned against them, and they began fleeing. That was when the Messenger was calling to them from behind. Only twelve men remained with the Prophet ﷺ. The enemy killed seventy of us, whereas the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions had inflicted one hundred and forty casualties upon the polytheists at Badr: seventy captives and seventy killed. “Abū Sufyan then called three times, ‘Is Muhammad among the people?’ The Prophet ﷺ forbade them from answering him. He then asked three times, ‘Is the son of Abū Quhafah among the people?’ Then he asked three times, ‘Is the son of al-Khattab among the people?’ He returned to his companions and said, ‘These men have been killed.’ “ʿUmar could no longer restrain himself and said, ‘You have lied, by Allah, enemy of Allah! All those whom you named are alive, and there still remains for you that which will distress you.’ Abū Sufyan said, ‘A day in return for the day of Badr; war has its alternating fortunes. You will find mutilation among your dead. I did not order it, but it did not displease me.’ “He then began chanting, ‘Rise high, Hubal! Rise high, Hubal!’ The Prophet ﷺ said, ‘Will you not answer him?’ They asked, ‘Messenger of Allah, what should we say?’ He said, ‘Say: Allah is higher and more majestic.’ Abū Sufyan said, ‘We have al-ʿUzza, whereas you have no ʿUzza.’ The Prophet ﷺ said, ‘Will you not answer him?’ They asked, ‘Messenger of Allah, what should we say?’ He said, ‘Say: Allah is our Protector, and you have no protector.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",410],"full":1,"rep":[7898],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3039)."},{"num":8821,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: مَا نَصَرَ اللَّهِ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى فِي مَوْطِنٍ، كَمَا نَصَرَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ. قَالَ: فَأَنْكَرْنَا ذَلِكَ، فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ مَنِ انْكَرَ ذَلِكَ كِتَابُ اللَّهِ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ يَقُولُ فِي يَوْمِ أُحُدٍ: ﴿وَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمِ اللهُ وَعْدَهُ إِذْ تَحُسُّونَهُمْ بِإِذْنِهِ﴾ [آل عِمْرَانَ: ١٥٢]- يَقُولُ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: وَالْحَسُّ: الْقَتْلُ - ﴿حَتَّى إِذَا فَشِلْتُمْ﴾ [آل عِمْرَانَ: ١٥٢]- إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: - ﴿وَلَقَدْ عَفَا عَنْكُمْ وَاللهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ﴾ [آل عِمْرَانَ: ١٥٢]، وَإِنَّمَا عَنَى بِهَذَا الرُّمَاةَ، وَذَلِكَ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَقَامَهُمْ فِي مَوْضِعٍ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: احْمُوا ظُهُورَنَا، فَإِنْ رَأَيْتُمُونَا نُقْتَلُ، فَلا تَنْصُرُونَا، وَإِنْ رَأَيْتُمُونَا قَدْ غَنِمْنَا فَلا تُشْرِكُونَا فَلَمَّا غَنِمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَبَاحُوا عَسْكَرَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، أَكَبَّ الرُّمَاةُ جَمِيعًا، فَدَخَلُوا فِي الْعَسْكَرِ يَنْهَبُونَ، وَقَدِ الْتَقَتْ صُفُوفُ أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَهُمْ هَكَذَا، - وَشَبَّكَ بَيْنَ أَصَابِعِ يَدَيْهِ - وَالْتَبَسُوا، فَلَمَّا أَخَلَّ الرُّمَاةُ تِلْكَ الْخَلَّةَ الَّتِي كَانُوا فِيهَا، دَخَلَتِ الْخَيْلُ مِنْ ذَلِكَ الْمَوْضِعِ عَلَى أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَضَرَبَ بَعْضُهُمْ بَعْضًا، وَالْتَبَسُوا، وَقُتِلَ مِنَ المُسْلِمِينَ نَاسٌ كَثِيرٌ، وَقَدْ كَانَ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابِهِ أَوَّلُ النَّهَارِ، حَتَّى قُتِلَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ لِوَاءِ الْمُشْرِكِينَ سَبْعَةٌ، أَوْ تِسْعَةٌ، وَجَالَ الْمُسْلِمُونَ جَوْلَةً نَحْوَ الْجَبَلِ، وَلَمْ يَبْلُغُوا حَيْثُ يَقُولُ النَّاسُ الْغَارَ، إِنَّمَا كَانُوا تَحْتَ الْمِهْرَاسِ، وَصَاحَ الشَّيْطَانُ: قُتِلَ مُحَمَّدٌ، فَلَمْ يُشَكَّ فِيهِ أَنَّهُ حَقٌّ، فَمَا زِلْنَا كَذَلِكَ مَا نَشُكُّ أَنَّهُ قَدْ قُتِلَ، حَتَّى طَلَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَ السَّعْدَيْنِ نَعْرِفُهُ بِتَكَفُّئِهِ إِذَا مَشَى، قَالَ: فَفَرِحْنَا حَتَّى كَأَنَّهُ لَمْ يُصِبْنَا مَا أَصَابَنَا، قَالَ: فَرَقِيَ نَحْوَنَا، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: اشْتَدَّ غَضَبُ اللَّهِ عَلَى قَوْمٍ دَمَّوْا وَجْهَ رَسُولِهِ قَالَ: وَيَقُولُ مَرَّةً أُخْرَى: اللهُمَّ إِنَّهُ لَيْسَ لَهُمِ أنْ يَعْلُونَا حَتَّى انْتَهَى إِلَيْنَا. فَمَكَثَ سَاعَةً، فَإِذَا أَبُو سُفْيَانَ يَصِيحُ فِي أَسْفَلِ الْجَبَلِ: اعْلُ هُبَلُ - مَرَّتَيْنِ، يَعْنِي آلِهَتَهُ - أَيْنَ ابْنُ أَبِي كَبْشَةَ؟ أَيْنَ ابْنُ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ؟ أَيْنَ ابْنُ الْخَطَّابِ؟ فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَلا أُجِيبُهُ؟ قَالَ: بَلَى فَلَمَّا قَالَ: اعْلُ هُبَلُ، قَالَ عُمَرُ: اللهُ أَعْلَى وَأَجَلُّ. قَالَ: فَقَالَ أَبُو سُفْيَانَ: يَا ابْنَ الْخَطَّابِ، إِنَّهُ قَدِ انْعَمَتْ عَيْنُهَا، فَعَادِ عَنْهَا، أَوْ فَعَالِ عَنْهَا، فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ ابْنُ أَبِي كَبْشَةَ؟ أَيْنَ ابْنُ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ؟ أَيْنَ ابْنُ الْخَطَّابِ؟ فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: هَذَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَهَذَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَهَا أَنَا ذَا عُمَرُ. قَالَ: فَقَالَ أَبُو سُفْيَانَ: يَوْمٌ بِيَوْمِ بَدْرٍ، الْأَيَّامُ دُوَلٌ، وَإِنَّ الْحَرْبَ سِجَالٌ. قَالَ: فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: لَا سَوَاءً، قَتْلانَا فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَقَتْلاكُمْ فِي النَّارِ. قَالَ: إِنَّكُمْ لَتَزْعُمُونَ ذَلِكَ، لَقَدْ خِبْنَا إِذَنْ وَخَسِرْنَا. ثُمَّ قَالَ أَبُو سُفْيَانَ: أَمَا إِنَّكُمْ سَوْفَ تَجِدُونَ فِي قَتْلاكُمْ مَثْلَى، وَلَمْ يَكُنْ ذَاكَ عَنْ رَأْيِ سَرَاتِنَا. قَالَ: ثُمَّ أَدْرَكَتْهُ حَمِيَّةُ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ: أَمَا إِنَّهُ قَدْ كَانَ ذَاكَ، وَلَمْ نَكْرَهْهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (2609) والطبراني في الكبير (10731) والحاكم (3163) كلهم من طريق سليمان بن داود، أخبرنا عبد الرحمن بن أبي الزناد، عن أبيه، عن عبيد الله، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.قال الحاكم: صحيح الإسناد.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ترك الرماة الجبل الذي عيّنهم عليه رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (2609), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabir (10731), and al-Ḥākim (3163).","chapter_en":"The Archers Abandoning the Mountain upon Which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ Had Stationed Them","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbas said: “Allah, Blessed and Exalted, did not grant victory at any place as He granted victory on the day of Uhud.” We found that difficult to accept, so Ibn ʿAbbas said: “The Book of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will judge between me and whoever rejects this. Allah Almighty says concerning the day of Uhud: ‘Allah certainly fulfilled His promise to you when you were killing them by His permission.’ “Ibn ʿAbbas said that al-hass means killing. Allah then says: ‘Until, when you lost courage…’ through His saying: ‘He has already pardoned you, and Allah is the Possessor of bounty toward the believers.’ [Ali ʿImran: 152] “This referred specifically to the archers. The Prophet ﷺ stationed them in a particular position and said, ‘Protect our rear. If you see us being killed, do not come to our aid; and if you see us taking spoils, do not join us.’ “When the Prophet ﷺ gained the spoils and the camp of the polytheists was laid open, all the archers rushed down and entered the camp to plunder it. The ranks of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had become intermingled like this”—and he interlaced the fingers of his hands—“and they became confused. When the archers abandoned the opening where they had been stationed, the cavalry entered through that position and attacked the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. They struck one another, became confused, and many Muslims were killed. “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions had held the advantage at the beginning of the day, to the point that seven or nine of the polytheists’ standard-bearers were killed. The Muslims then recoiled toward the mountain. They did not reach the cave, as people claim; rather, they were beneath al-Mihras. Satan cried out, ‘Muhammad has been killed!’ No one doubted that it was true. We continued in that condition, having no doubt that he had been killed, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared between the two Saʿds. We recognized him by the swaying motion of his walk. “We rejoiced as though nothing of what had befallen us had happened. He climbed toward us, saying, ‘The wrath of Allah has become severe against a people who bloodied the face of His Messenger.’ On another occasion, he said, ‘O Allah, it is not for them to rise above us,’ until he reached us. “After some time, Abū Sufyan began shouting from the foot of the mountain, ‘Rise high, Hubal! Rise high, Hubal!’—referring to his deity—‘Where is the son of Abū Kabshah? Where is the son of Abū Quhafah? Where is the son of al-Khattab?’ “ʿUmar said, ‘Messenger of Allah, may I answer him?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ When Abū Sufyan said, ‘Rise high, Hubal,’ ʿUmar replied, ‘Allah is higher and more majestic.’ Abū Sufyan said, ‘Son of al-Khattab, you have certainly gladdened its eye, so leave it—or refrain from it.’ He then asked, ‘Where is the son of Abū Kabshah? Where is the son of Abū Quhafah? Where is the son of al-Khattab?’ “ʿUmar replied, ‘Here is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, here is Abū Bakr, and here I am, ʿUmar.’ “Abū Sufyan said, ‘A day in return for the day of Badr. Days alternate, and war has its changing fortunes.’ ʿUmar replied, ‘They are not equal. Our dead are in Paradise, whereas your dead are in the Fire.’ Abū Sufyan said, ‘If that is what you claim, then we have indeed failed and lost.’ “Abū Sufyan then said, ‘You will find mutilation among your dead, but it was not done by the decision of our leaders.’ Then the zeal of the Age of Ignorance overtook him, and he said, ‘It did happen, and we did not dislike it.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",411],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (2609)، والطبراني في «الكبير» (10731)، والحاكم (3163)."},{"num":8822,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَقُولُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ: اللَّهُمَّ! إِنَّكَ إِنْ تَشَأْ، لَا تُعْبَدْ فِي الْأَرْضِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد والسير (23:1743) عن حجاج بن الشاعر، حدثنا عبد الصمد، حدثنا حماد، عن ثابت، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"دعاء رسول الله ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (23:1743). Al-Nawawi said: “What is well known in the books of prophetic biography and military campaigns is that he said it on the day of Badr, while this narration states that he said it on the day of Uhud. There is no contradiction between the two, for he said it on both days. Allah knows best.”","chapter_en":"The Supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik reported that on the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: “O Allah! If You so will, You will not be worshipped upon the earth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",412],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7878,10069],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (23: 1743). قال النووي: «المشهور في كتب السير والمغازي أنه قال يوم بدر، وجاء في هذه الرواية أنه قال يوم أحد، ولا معارضة بينهما، فقاله في اليومين، والله أعلم»."},{"num":8823,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ قَتَادَةَ، حَدَّثَنَا أَنَسٌ، أَنَّ أَبَا طَلْحَةَ، قَالَ: غَشِيَنَا النُّعَاسُ، وَنَحْنُ فِي مَصَافِّنَا يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، ـ قَالَ: ـ فَجَعَلَ سَيْفِي يَسْقُطُ مِنْ يَدِي، وَآخُذُهُ، وَيَسْقُطُ وَآخُذُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4562) عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم بن عبدالرحمن أبي يعقوب، حدثنا حسين بن محمد، حدثنا شيبان، عن قتادة، حدثنا أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب وقوع النعاس يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4562).","chapter_en":"The Occurrence of Drowsiness on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that Abū Talhah said: “Drowsiness overcame us while we were standing in our battle lines on the day of Uhud. My sword kept falling from my hand; I would pick it up, then it would fall again, and I would pick it up.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Tirmidhi (3007) also narrated through another route from Abū Talhah that he said: “I raised my head on the day of Uhud and began looking around. There was not a single one of them that day who was not swaying beneath his leather shield because of drowsiness.” That is the meaning of the statement of Allah Almighty:","“Then, after the distress, He sent down upon you a sense of security—a drowsiness.” [Ali ʿImran: 154]"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: ﴿ثُمَّ أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ الْغَمِّ أَمَنَةً نُعَاسًا يَغْشَىٰ طَائِفَةً مِنْكُمْ وَطَائِفَةٌ قَدْ أَهَمَّتْهُمْ أَنْفُسُهُمْ يَظُنُّونَ بِاللَّهِ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ ظَنَّ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ﴾ [آل عمران: ١٥٤]."],"en":["Allah Most High says:","“Then, after the distress, He sent down upon you a sense of security—a drowsiness that overcame a group of you—while another group was concerned only about themselves, thinking of Allah what was untrue—the thought of ignorance.” [Ali ʿImran: 154]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",414],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4562)."},{"num":8824,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، أَنَّ أَبَا طَلْحَةَ، قَالَ: غُشِينَا وَنَحْنُ فِي مَصَافِّنَا يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، حَدَّثَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ فِيمَنْ غَشِيَهُ النُّعَاسُ يَوْمَئِذٍ، قَالَ: فَجَعَلَ سَيْفِي يَسْقُطُ مِنْ يَدِي وَآخُذُهُ، وَيَسْقُطُ مِنْ يَدِي وَآخُذُهُ. وَالطَّائِفَةُ الأُخْرَى الْمُنَافِقُونَ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ هَمٌّ إِلاَّ أَنْفُسُهُمْ، أَجْبَنُ قَوْمٍ وَأَرْعَبُهُ وَأَخْذَلُهُ لِلْحَقِّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3008) عن يوسف بن حماد، قال: حدثنا عبد الأعلى بن عبد الأعلى، عن سعيد، عن قتادة، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب وقوع النعاس يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (3008), who said: “Good authentic.”","chapter_en":"The Occurrence of Drowsiness on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that Abū Talhah said: “Drowsiness overcame us while we were in our battle lines on the day of Uhud.” He related that he was among those overcome by drowsiness that day, saying: “My sword kept falling from my hand and I would pick it up; then it would fall from my hand and I would pick it up again. The other group were the hypocrites, whose only concern was themselves—the most cowardly of people, the most panic-stricken, and the most forsaking of the truth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",415],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3008)، وقال: حسن صحيح."},{"num":8825,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الزُّبَيْرِ بْنِ الْعَوَّامِ، قَالَ: لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنِي مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ حِينَ اشْتَدَّ عَلَيْنَا الْخَوْفُ، وَأُرْسِلَ عَلَيْنَا النَّوْمُ، فَمَا مِنَّا أَحَدٌ إِلَّا وذقنه، أَوْ قَالَ: ذَقَنُهُ فِي صَدْرِهِ، فَوَاللَّهِ إِنِّي لَأَسْمَعُ كَالْحُلْمِ قَوْلَ مُعَتِّبِ بْنِ قُشَيْرٍ: لَوْ كَانَ لَنَا مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ ما قتلنا هاهنا فَحَفِظْتُهَا، فأنزل الله عز وجل فِي ذَلِكَ: ﴿ثُمَّ أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدَ الْغَمِّ أَمَنَةً نُعَاسًا﴾، إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: ﴿مَا قُتِلْنَا ههنا﴾ لِقَوْلِ مُعَتِّبِ بْنِ قُشَيْرٍ قَالَ: ﴿لَوْ كُنْتُمْ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ﴾، حَتَّى بَلَغَ ﴿وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُورِ﴾ [سورة آل عمران: ١٥٤]."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه في \"مسنده\" عن يحيى بن آدم، حدثنا ابن أبي زائدة، عن محمد بن إسحاق، عن يحيى بن عباد، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن الزبير، عن أبيه، فذكره. المطالب العالية (4260)","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب وقوع النعاس يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ishaq ibn Rahawayh in his Musnad, as cited in al-Matalib al-ʿAliyah (4260).","chapter_en":"The Occurrence of Drowsiness on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Zubayr said: “I remember being with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud when fear became intense upon us and sleep was sent over us. Every one of us had his chin—or he said, his chin—upon his chest. By Allah, I could hear, as though in a dream, Muʿattib ibn Qushayr saying: ‘If we had possessed any authority in this matter, we would not have been killed here.’ “I memorized those words, and Allah Almighty revealed concerning them: ‘Then, after the distress, He sent down upon you a sense of security—a drowsiness,’ through His saying, ‘We would not have been killed here,’ because of the words of Muʿattib ibn Qushayr. He then said: ‘Say: Even if you had remained in your homes,’ until He reached: ‘And Allah knows well what is within the breasts.’” [Ali ʿImran: 154]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه في «مسنده» كما في «المطالب العالية» (4260)."},{"num":8826,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُثْمَانَ بْنِ مَوْهَبٍ، قَالَ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ فَرَأَى قَوْمًا جُلُوسًا فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَؤُلاَءِ الْقُعُودُ؟ قَالُوا: هَؤُلاَءِ قُرَيْشٌ. قَالَ: مَنِ الشَّيْخُ؟ قَالُوا: ابْنُ عُمَرَ. فَأَتَاهُ فَقَالَ: إِنِّي سَائِلُكَ عَنْ شَىْءٍ أَتُحَدِّثُنِي، قَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ بِحُرْمَةِ هَذَا الْبَيْتِ، أَتَعْلَمُ أَنَّ عُثْمَانَ بْنَ عَفَّانَ فَرَّ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَتَعْلَمُهُ تَغَيَّبَ عَنْ بَدْرٍ فَلَمْ يَشْهَدْهَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَتَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ تَخَلَّفَ عَنْ بَيْعَةِ الرُّضْوَانِ فَلَمْ يَشْهَدْهَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَكَبَّرَ. قَالَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: تَعَالَ لأُخْبِرَكَ وَلأُبَيِّنَ لَكَ عَمَّا سَأَلْتَنِي عَنْهُ، أَمَّا فِرَارُهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ فَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَفَا عَنْهُ، وَأَمَّا تَغَيُّبُهُ عَنْ بَدْرٍ فَإِنَّهُ كَانَ تَحْتَهُ بِنْتُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَكَانَتْ مَرِيضَةً، فَقَالَ لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ لَكَ أَجْرَ رَجُلٍ مِمَّنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَسَهْمَهُ. وَأَمَّا تَغَيُّبُهُ عَنْ بَيْعَةِ الرُّضْوَانِ فَإِنَّهُ لَوْ كَانَ أَحَدٌ أَعَزَّ بِبَطْنِ مَكَّةَ مِنْ عُثْمَانَ بْنِ عَفَّانَ لَبَعَثَهُ مَكَانَهُ، فَبَعَثَ عُثْمَانَ، وَكَانَ بَيْعَةُ الرُّضْوَانِ بَعْدَ مَا ذَهَبَ عُثْمَانُ إِلَى مَكَّةَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِيَدِهِ الْيُمْنَى: هَذِهِ يَدُ عُثْمَانَ. فَضَرَبَ بِهَا عَلَى يَدِهِ فَقَالَ: هَذِهِ لِعُثْمَانَ. اذْهَبْ بِهَذَا الْآنَ مَعَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4066) عن عبدان، أخبرنا أبو ضمرة، عن عثمان بن موهب قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عفو الله عز وجل عمّن فرّ من غزوة أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4066).","chapter_en":"Allah Almighty Pardoning Those Who Fled from the Battle of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUthman ibn Mawhab reported: A man who had performed the pilgrimage came and saw a group of people sitting together. He asked, “Who are these people sitting here?” They replied, “They are Quraysh.” He asked, “Who is the elder?” They replied, “Ibn ʿUmar.” He approached him and said, “I am going to ask you about something. Will you answer me? I adjure you by the sanctity of this House: do you know that ʿUthman fled on the day of Uhud?” Ibn ʿUmar replied, “Yes.” He asked, “Do you know that he was absent from Badr and did not attend it?” He replied, “Yes.” He asked, “Do you know that he remained behind from the Pledge of al-Ridwan and did not attend it?” He replied, “Yes.” The man then proclaimed, “Allahu Akbar!” Ibn ʿUmar said: “Come here, so that I may inform you and clarify the matters about which you asked me. As for his flight on the day of Uhud, I testify that Allah pardoned him. As for his absence from Badr, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was his wife, and she was ill. The Prophet ﷺ therefore told him, ‘You will receive the reward and the share of a man who attended Badr.’ “As for his absence from the Pledge of al-Ridwan, had there been anyone in the valley of Makkah possessing greater influence and protection than ʿUthman ibn ʿAffan, the Prophet ﷺ would have sent that person in his place. Instead, he sent ʿUthman. The Pledge of al-Ridwan took place after ʿUthman had gone to Makkah. The Prophet ﷺ indicated his right hand and said, ‘This is the hand of ʿUthman.’ He then struck it against his other hand and said, ‘This pledge is for ʿUthman.’ Now take this explanation with you.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله عز وجل: ﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوْا مِنْكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعَانِ إِنَّمَا اسْتَزَلَّهُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ بِبَعْضِ مَا كَسَبُوا وَلَقَدْ عَفَا اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ﴾ [آل عمران: ١٥٥]."],"en":["Allah Almighty says:","“Indeed, those of you who turned away on the day the two armies met were only caused to slip by Satan because of some of what they had earned. Yet Allah has certainly pardoned them. Indeed, Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Forbearing.” [Ali ʿImran: 155]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",418],"full":1,"rep":[8991,13318],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4066)."},{"num":8827,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن الزبير قال: سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: أوجب طلحة حين صنع ما صنع برسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وقد كان الناس انهزموا عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم حتى انتهى بعضهم إلى المنقا دون الأعوص، وفر عثمان بن عفان وعقبة بن عثمان وسعد بن عثمان رجلان من الأنصار ثم من بني زريق حتى بلغوا الجلعب – جبلا بناحية المدينة، فأقاموا به ثلاثا، ثم رجعوا إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: لقد ذهبتم فيها عريضة."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه محمد بن إسحاق في سيرته (514) قال: حدثني يحيى بن عباد بن عبدالله بن الزبير، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن الزبير فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عفو الله عز وجل عمّن فرّ من غزوة أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Muhammad ibn Ishaq in his Sirah (514).","chapter_en":"Allah Almighty Pardoning Those Who Fled from the Battle of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullah ibn al-Zubayr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Talhah has secured Paradise,” after Talhah had done what he did in defense of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The people had fled from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until some of them reached al-Munaqqa, short of al-Aʿwas. ʿUthman ibn ʿAffan fled, as did ʿUqbah ibn ʿUthman and Saʿd ibn ʿUthman—the latter two being men of the Ansar from Banu Zurayq—until they reached al-Jalʿab, a mountain in the vicinity of Madinah. They remained there for three days and then returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You certainly went very far in your flight.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",419],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9935],"tks":"حسن: رواه محمد بن إسحاق في «سيرته» (514)."},{"num":8828,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ شَقِيقٍ، قَالَ: لَقِيَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ الْوَلِيدَ بْنَ عُقْبَةَ، فَقَالَ لَهُ الْوَلِيدُ: مَا لِي أَرَاكَ قَدْ جَفَوْتَ أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عُثْمَانَ؟ فَقَالَ لَهُ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ: أَبْلِغْهُ أَنِّي لَمْ أَفِرَّ يَوْمَ عَيْنَيْنِ - قَالَ عَاصِمٌ: يَقُولُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، - وَلَمْ أَتَخَلَّفْ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ، وَلَمْ أَتْرُكْ سُنَّةَ عُمَرَ. قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقَ فَخَبَّرَ ذَلِكَ عُثْمَانَ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ: أَمَّا قَوْلُهُ: إِنِّي لَمْ أَفِرَّ يَوْمَ عَيْنَيْنَ، فَكَيْفَ يُعَيِّرُنِي بِذَنْبٍ وَقَدْ عَفَا اللهُ عَنْهُ، فَقَالَ: ﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوْا مِنْكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعَانِ إِنَّمَا اسْتَزَلَّهُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ بِبَعْضِ مَا كَسَبُوا وَلَقَدْ عَفَا اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ﴾ [آل عِمْرَانَ: ١٥٥]، وَأَمَّا قَوْلُهُ: إِنِّي تَخَلَّفْتُ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ، فَإِنِّي كُنْتُ أُمَرِّضُ رُقَيَّةَ بِنْتَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى مَاتَتْ وَقَدْ ضَرَبَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِسَهْمِي، وَمَنْ ضَرَبَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِسَهْمِهِ فَقَدْ شَهِدَ، وَأَمَّا قَوْلُهُ: إِنِّي لَمْ أَتْرُكْ سُنَّةَ عُمَرَ، فَإِنِّي لَا أُطِيقُهَا وَلا هُوَ، فَائْتِهِ فَحَدِّثْهُ بِذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (490) والبزار – كشف الأستار (2512) والطبراني في الكبير (1/45) كلهم من حديث عاصم بن أبي النجود، عن شقيق بن سلمة قال: فذكره. وإسناده حسن من أجل عاصم بن أبي النجود فإنه حسن الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عفو الله عز وجل عمّن فرّ من غزوة أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (490), al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (2512), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabir (1/45).","chapter_en":"Allah Almighty Pardoning Those Who Fled from the Battle of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Shaqiq reported: ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn ʿAwf met al-Walid ibn ʿUqbah. Al-Walid said to him, “Why do I see that you have distanced yourself from the Commander of the Believers, ʿUthman?” ʿAbd al-Rahman replied, “Convey to him that I did not flee on the day of ʿAynayn”—ʿAsim said that he meant the day of Uhud—“I did not remain behind on the day of Badr, and I did not abandon the way of ʿUmar.” Al-Walid went and informed ʿUthman of this. ʿUthman said: “As for his statement, ‘I did not flee on the day of ʿAynayn,’ how can he reproach me for a sin that Allah has already pardoned?” Allah said: “Indeed, those of you who turned away on the day the two armies met were only caused to slip by Satan because of some of what they had earned. Yet Allah has certainly pardoned them.” [Ali ʿImran: 155] “As for his statement that I remained behind on the day of Badr, I was nursing Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, until she died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned me my share, and anyone to whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned a share is counted among those who attended. “As for his statement, ‘I did not abandon the way of ʿUmar,’ neither I nor he is capable of following it fully. Go to him and relate this to him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “the day of ʿAynayn”: ʿAynayn is a hill belonging to Mount Uhud in Madinah. It is also said that the name refers to two hills near Uhud.","His statement, “the way of ʿUmar”: This refers to his asceticism, his fairness toward those who were wronged, and his forceful treatment of oppressive evildoers. Allah Most High had granted him strength and awe. Thus, ʿUthman said: “Neither I nor he is capable of following it fully. Go to him and relate this to him.”","It appears that their excuse for fleeing was the report that had spread that the Prophet ﷺ had been killed—for what reason, then, would they continue fighting? Allah therefore pardoned them and accepted their excuse. The first person to announce the glad tidings that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was alive was Kaʿb ibn Malik, as related in the following hadith:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (490)، والبزار في «كشف الأستار» (2512)، والطبراني في «الكبير» (1/45)."},{"num":8829,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ كَعْبِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: كَانَ كَعْبٌ أَوَّلَ مَنْ عَرَفَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدَ الْهَزِيمَةِ، وَقَوْلِ النَّاسِ: قُتِلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. قَالَ كَعْبٌ: عَرَفْتُ عَيْنَيْهِ تَزْهَرَانِ مِنْ تَحْتِ الْمِغْفَرِ، فَنَادَيْتُ بِأَعْلَى صَوْتِي: يَا مَعْشَرَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ أَبْشِرُوا هَذَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَشَارَ إِلَيَّ أَنْ أَنْصِتْ، فَلَمَّا عَرَفُوا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ نَهَضُوا بِهِ مَعَهُمْ نَحْوَ الشِّعْبِ مَعَهُ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ وَعَلِيٌّ وَطَلْحَةُ وَالزُّبَيْرُ وَالْحَارِثُ بْنُ الصِّمَّةِ فِي رَهْطٍ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ، وَلَمَّا أُسْنِدَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الشِّعْبِ أَدْرَكَهُ أُبَيُّ بْنُ خَلَفٍ وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: يَا مُحَمَّدُ لَا نَجَوْتُ إِنْ نَجَوْتَ. فَقَالَ الْقَوْمُ: أَيَعْطِفُ عَلَيْهِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ رَجُلٌ مِنَّا؟ فَقَالَ: دَعُوهُ. فَلَمَّا دَنَا تَنَاوَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْحَرْبَةَ مِنَ الْحَارِثِ بْنِ الصِّمَّةِ. يَقُولُ بَعْضُ الْقَوْمِ فِيمَا ذُكِرَ لِي: فَلَمَّا أَخَذَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ انْتَفَضَ بِهَا انْتِفَاضَةً تَطَايَرْنَا عَنْهُ تَطَايُرَ الشَّعْرِ عَنْ ظَهْرِ الْبَعِيرِ إِذَا انْتَفَضَ ثُمَّ اسْتَقْبَلَهُ فَطَعَنَهُ بِهَا طَعْنَةً تَدَأْدَأَ مِنْهَا عَنْ ظَهْرِ فَرَسِهِ مِرَارًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو نعيم في الدلائل (415) من طريق محمد بن مسلمة، عن محمد بن إسحاق، قال: حدثني ابن شهاب، عن عبد الله بن كعب بن مالك فذكره. وإسناده حسن من أجل محمد بن إسحاق.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أول من عرف النبي ﷺ بأنه حي هو كعب بن مالك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Nuʿaym in al-Dala’il (2/619–620).","chapter_en":"Kaʿb ibn Malik Was the First to Recognize That the Prophet ﷺ Was Alive","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullah ibn Kaʿb ibn Malik reported that Kaʿb was the first person to recognize the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the defeat, when the people were saying, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been killed.” Kaʿb said: “I recognized his eyes gleaming beneath his helmet, so I called out at the top of my voice, ‘Muslims, rejoice! This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!’ He motioned to me to remain silent. “When the Muslims recognized the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they rose with him and headed toward the mountain pass. Accompanying him were Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, ʿAli, Talhah, al-Zubayr, al-Harith ibn al-Simmah, and a group of Muslims. “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took shelter in the mountain pass, Ubayy ibn Khalaf caught up with him, saying, ‘Muhammad, may I not survive if you survive!’ The men asked, ‘Messenger of Allah, should one of us turn upon him?’ He replied, ‘Leave him.’ “When Ubayy drew near, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the spear from al-Harith ibn al-Simmah. One of the men, according to what was related to me, said: ‘When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it, he shook himself with such force that we scattered away from him like biting flies scattering from the back of a camel when it shakes itself. He then faced Ubayy and struck him with the spear, causing him repeatedly to tumble from the back of his horse.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",421],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو نعيم في «الدلائل» (2/619-620)."},{"num":8830,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: جَعَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الرُّمَاةِ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ جُبَيْرٍ، فَأَصَابُوا مِنَّا سَبْعِينَ، وَكَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابُهُ أَصَابُوا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ أَرْبَعِينَ وَمِائَةً، سَبْعِينَ أَسِيرًا وَسَبْعِينَ قَتِيلاً. قَالَ أَبُو سُفْيَانَ: يَوْمٌ بِيَوْمِ بَدْرٍ، وَالْحَرْبُ سِجَالٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3986) عن عمرو بن خالد، حدثنا زهير، حدثنا أبو إسحاق، قال: سمعت البراء بن عازب يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3986).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Baraʾ ibn ʿAzib reported: “On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ placed ʿAbdullah ibn Jubayr in command of the archers. The polytheists killed seventy of us, whereas the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions had inflicted one hundred and forty casualties upon the polytheists on the day of Badr: seventy captives and seventy killed. Abū Sufyan said, ‘A day in return for the day of Badr; war has its alternating fortunes.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",422],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3986)."},{"num":8831,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ قَتَادَةَ، قَالَ: مَا نَعْلَمُ حَيًّا مِنْ أَحْيَاءِ الْعَرَبِ أَكْثَرَ شَهِيدًا، أَعَزَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ.","قَالَ قَتَادَةُ: وَحَدَّثَنَا أَنَسُ بْنُ مَالِكٍ أَنَّهُ قُتِلَ مِنْهُمْ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ سَبْعُونَ، وَيَوْمَ بِئْرِ مَعُونَةَ سَبْعُونَ، وَيَوْمَ اليَمَامَةِ سَبْعُونَ.","قَالَ: وَكَانَ بِئْرُ مَعُونَةَ عَلَى عَهْدِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَيَوْمُ اليَمَامَةِ عَلَى عَهْدِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ الصديق يَوْمَ مُسَيْلِمَةَ الكَذَّابِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4078) عن عمرو بن علي، حدثنا معاذ بن هشام، قال: حدثني أبي، عن قتادة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4078).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Qatadah said: “We do not know of any clan among the Arab clans having more martyrs, or being more honored on the Day of Resurrection, than the Ansar.” Qatadah said: “Anas ibn Malik related to us that seventy of them were killed on the day of Uhud, seventy on the day of Bi’r Maʿunah, and seventy on the day of al-Yamamah. Bi’r Maʿunah occurred during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while the day of al-Yamamah occurred during the caliphate of Abū Bakr al-Siddiq, on the occasion of Musaylimah the Liar.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",423],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4078)."},{"num":8832,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، قَالَ: صَبَّحَ أُنَاسٌ غَدَاةَ أُحُدٍ الْخَمْرَ، فَقُتِلُوا مِنْ يَوْمِهِمْ جَمِيعًا شُهَدَاءَ، وَذَلِكَ قَبْلَ تَحْرِيمِهَا.","منهم: حمزة بن عبد المطلب، واليمان أبو حذيفة، وأنس بن النضر، ومصعب بن عمير."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4618) عن صدقة بن الفضل، أخبرنا ابن عيينة، عن عمرو (هو ابن دينار) عن جابر قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4618).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir reported: “Some people drank wine on the morning of Uhud and were all killed as martyrs that same day. This occurred before wine was prohibited.” Among them were Hamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muttalib, al-Yaman—the father of Hudhayfah—Anas ibn al-Nadr, and Musʿab ibn ʿUmayr."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",424],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4618)."},{"num":8833,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بن عَوْفٍ أُتِيَ بِطَعَامٍ، وَكَانَ صَائِمًا فَقَالَ: قُتِلَ مُصْعَبُ بْنُ عُمَيْرٍ، وَهْوَ خَيْرٌ مِنِّي، كُفِّنَ فِي بُرْدَةٍ، إِنْ غُطِّيَ رَأْسُهُ بَدَتْ رِجْلاَهُ، وَإِنْ غُطِّيَ رِجْلاَهُ بَدَا رَأْسُهُ ـ وَأُرَاهُ قَالَ: ـ وَقُتِلَ حَمْزَةُ وَهْوَ خَيْرٌ مِنِّي، ثُمَّ بُسِطَ لَنَا مِنَ الدُّنْيَا مَا بُسِطَ، أَوْ قَالَ: أُعْطِينَا مِنَ الدُّنْيَا مَا أُعْطِينَا، وَقَدْ خَشِينَا أَنْ تَكُونَ حَسَنَاتُنَا عُجِّلَتْ لَنَا. ثُمَّ جَعَلَ يَبْكِي حَتَّى تَرَكَ الطَّعَامَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4045) عن عبدان (وهو عبد الله بن عثمان المروزي) حدثنا عبد الله (هو ابن المبارك) عن سعد بن إبراهيم (هو ابن عبد الرحمن بن عوف) عن أبيه إبراهيم أن عبد الرحمن بن عوف أُتي بطعام فذكر الحديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4045). His statement, “He was better than I,” was said out of humility.","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Food was brought to ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn ʿAwf while he was fasting. He said: “Musʿab ibn ʿUmayr was killed, and he was better than I. He was shrouded in a cloak: when his head was covered, his feet became exposed, and when his feet were covered, his head became exposed.” The narrator said: “I think he also said, ‘Hamzah was killed, and he was better than I.’” ʿAbd al-Rahman continued: “Then the worldly provisions that were spread out for us were spread out—or he said: we were given of this world what we were given—and we fear that the rewards for our good deeds may have been hastened for us in this world.” He then began to weep until he left the food untouched."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",425],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4045). قوله: «وهو خير مني» قال ذلك تواضعا."},{"num":8834,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ خَبَّابِ بْنِ الْأَرَتِّ قَالَ:  هَاجَرْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، نَبْتَغِي وَجْهَ اللَّهِ، فَوَجَبَ أَجْرُنَا عَلَى اللَّهِ، فَمِنَّا مَنْ مَضَى لَمْ يَأْكُلْ مِنْ أَجْرِهِ شَيْئًا، مِنْهُمْ مُصْعَبُ بْنُ عُمَيْرٍ، قُتِلَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، فَلَمْ يُوجَدْ لَهُ شَيْءٌ يُكَفَّنُ فِيهِ إِلَّا نَمِرَةٌ، فَكُنَّا إِذَا وَضَعْنَاهَا عَلَى رَأْسِهِ، خَرَجَتْ رِجْلَاهُ، وَإِذَا وَضَعْنَاهَا عَلَى رِجْلَيْهِ خَرَجَ رَأْسُهُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ضَعُوهَا مِمَّا يَلِي رَأْسَهُ، وَاجْعَلُوا عَلَى رِجْلَيْهِ الْإِذْخِرَ، وَمِنَّا مَنْ أَيْنَعَتْ لَهُ ثَمَرَتُهُ فَهُوَ يَهْدِبُهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4047) ومسلم في الجنائز (940: 44) كلاهما من طريق الأعمش، عن شقيق، عن خباب بن الأرت قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4047) and Muslim (44:940).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khabbab ibn al-Aratt reported: “We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the cause of Allah, seeking the countenance of Allah, and our reward became assured with Allah. Some of us passed away without consuming anything of their reward in this world. Among them was Musʿab ibn ʿUmayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud. Nothing could be found in which to shroud him except a short striped cloak. Whenever we placed it over his head, his feet became exposed, and whenever we placed it over his feet, his head became exposed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ therefore said, ‘Place it over the side of his head and cover his feet with idhkhir grass.’ “Others among us lived until their fruits ripened, and they are now gathering them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",426],"full":1,"rep":[3634],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4047)، ومسلم (940: 44)."},{"num":8835,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عبدالله رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: قَالَ رَجُلٌ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ: أَرَأَيْتَ إِنْ قُتِلْتُ فَأَيْنَ أَنَا؟ قَالَ: فِي الْجَنَّةِ فَأَلْقَى تَمَرَاتٍ فِي يَدِهِ، ثُمَّ قَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4046) ومسلم في الإمارة (143:1899) كلاهما من طريق سفيان (هو ابن عيينة) عن عمرو، سمع جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4046) and Muslim (143:1899).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah reported that on the day of Uhud, a man asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Tell me: if I am killed, where will I be?” He replied, “In Paradise.” The man threw away the dates he was holding and fought until he was killed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",427],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8093],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4046)، ومسلم (143: 1899)."},{"num":8836,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: غَابَ عَمِّي أَنَسُ بْنُ النَّضْرِ عَنْ قِتَالِ بَدْرٍ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، غِبْتُ عَنْ أَوَّلِ قِتَالٍ قَاتَلْتَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، لَئِنِ اللَّهُ أَشْهَدَنِي قِتَالَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ لَيَرَيَنَّ اللَّهُ مَا أَصْنَعُ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ وَانْكَشَفَ الْمُسْلِمُونَ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعْتَذِرُ إِلَيْكَ مِمَّا صَنَعَ هَؤُلاَءِ، ـ يَعْنِي أَصْحَابَهُ، ـ وَأَبْرَأُ إِلَيْكَ مِمَّا صَنَعَ هَؤُلاَءِ، ـ يَعْنِي الْمُشْرِكِينَ، ـ ثُمَّ تَقَدَّمَ، فَاسْتَقْبَلَهُ سَعْدُ بْنُ مُعَاذٍ، فَقَالَ: يَا سَعْدُ بْنَ مُعَاذٍ، الْجَنَّةَ، وَرَبِّ النَّضْرِ، إِنِّي أَجِدُ رِيحَهَا مِنْ دُونِ أُحُدٍ. قَالَ سَعْدٌ: فَمَا اسْتَطَعْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مَا صَنَعَ. قَالَ أَنَسٌ: فَوَجَدْنَا بِهِ بِضْعًا وَثَمَانِينَ ضَرْبَةً بِالسَّيْفِ أَوْ طَعْنَةً بِرُمْحٍ أَوْ رَمْيَةً بِسَهْمٍ، وَوَجَدْنَاهُ قَدْ قُتِلَ وَقَدْ مَثَّلَ بِهِ الْمُشْرِكُونَ، فَمَا عَرَفَهُ أَحَدٌ إِلاَّ أُخْتُهُ بِبَنَانِهِ. قَالَ أَنَسٌ: كُنَّا نَرَى أَوْ نَظُنُّ أَنَّ هَذِهِ الآيَةَ نَزَلَتْ فِيهِ وَفِي أَشْبَاهِهِ ﴿مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ رِجَالٌ صَدَقُوا مَا عَاهَدُوا اللَّهَ عَلَيْهِ﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: 23]} إِلَى."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (2805) من طريق حميد، ومسلم في الإمارة (48:1903) من طريق ثابت – كلاهما عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2805) and Muslim (48:1903).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: “My paternal uncle Anas ibn al-Nadr was absent from the fighting at Badr. He said, ‘Messenger of Allah, I was absent from the first battle in which you fought the polytheists. If Allah allows me to witness another battle against the polytheists, Allah will certainly see what I shall do.’ “When the day of Uhud came and the Muslims retreated, he said, ‘O Allah, I apologize to You for what these people have done’—meaning his companions—‘and I disassociate myself before You from what these people have done’—meaning the polytheists. “He then advanced and encountered Saʿd ibn Muʿadh. He said, ‘Saʿd ibn Muʿadh! Paradise, by the Lord of al-Nadr! I can smell its fragrance from this side of Uhud.’ “Saʿd later said, ‘Messenger of Allah, I could not accomplish what he accomplished.’” Anas continued: “We found more than eighty wounds upon him—blows from swords, thrusts from spears, and shots from arrows. We found that he had been killed and that the polytheists had mutilated him. No one could recognize him except his sister, who recognized him by his fingertips. “We used to believe—or suppose—that the following verse was revealed concerning him and others like him: ‘Among the believers are men who have been true to the covenant they made with Allah.’” [Al-Ahzab: 23]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",428],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2805)، ومسلم (48: 1903)."},{"num":8837,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: لَقَدْ وَجَدْنَا بِأَنَسِ بْنِ النَّضْرِ يَوْمَئِذٍ سَبْعِينَ ضَرْبَةً، مَا عَرَفْتُهُ إِلاَّ أُخْتَهُ، عرفته ببنانه."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن إسحاق قال: حدثني حميد الطويل، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره، سيرة ابن إسحاق (510) وإسناده حسن من أجل ابن إسحاق.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Ishaq in his Sirah (510).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik reported: “That day, we found seventy wounds upon Anas ibn al-Nadr. No one recognized him except his sister, who recognized him by his fingertips.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",429],"full":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن إسحاق في «سيرته» (510)."},{"num":8838,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عبدالله رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: جِيءَ بِأَبِي يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، قَدْ مُثِّلَ بِهِ حَتَّى وُضِعَ بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ سُجِّيَ ثَوْبًا، فَذَهَبْتُ أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَكْشِفَ عَنْهُ، فَنَهَانِي قَوْمِي، ثُمَّ ذَهَبْتُ أَكْشِفُ عَنْهُ فَنَهَانِي قَوْمِي، فَأَمَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَرُفِعَ، فَسَمِعَ صَوْتَ صَائِحَةٍ، فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذِهِ. فَقَالُوا: ابْنَةُ عَمْرٍو أَوْ أُخْتُ عَمْرٍو. قَالَ: فَلِمَ تَبْكِي؟ أَوْ لاَ تَبْكِي فَمَا زَالَتِ الْمَلاَئِكَةُ تُظِلُّهُ بِأَجْنِحَتِهَا حَتَّى رُفِعَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجنائز (1293) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (129:2471) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، حدثنا ابن المنكدر، قال: سمعت جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1293) and Muslim (129:2471).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir reported: “My father was brought on the day of Uhud after he had been mutilated. He was placed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and covered with a cloth. I went to uncover him, but my people stopped me. I went again to uncover him, but my people stopped me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then ordered that he be carried away. “He heard the voice of a woman crying and asked, ‘Who is this?’ They replied, ‘The daughter of ʿAmr’—or: ‘the sister of ʿAmr.’ He said, ‘Why is she weeping?’—or: ‘Do not weep. The angels continued shading him with their wings until he was lifted away.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",430],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[597,3579],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1293)، ومسلم (129: 2471)."},{"num":8839,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: لَمَّا حَضَرَ أُحُدٌ دَعَانِي أَبِي مِنَ اللَّيْلِ فَقَالَ: مَا أُرَانِي إِلاَّ مَقْتُولاً فِي أَوَّلِ مَنْ يُقْتَلُ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَإِنِّي لاَ أَتْرُكُ بَعْدِي أَعَزَّ عَلَىَّ مِنْكَ، غَيْرَ نَفْسِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَإِنَّ عَلَىَّ دَيْنًا فَاقْضِ، وَاسْتَوْصِ بِأَخَوَاتِكَ خَيْرًا. فَأَصْبَحْنَا فَكَانَ أَوَّلَ قَتِيلٍ، وَدُفِنَ مَعَهُ آخَرُ فِي قَبْرٍ، ثُمَّ لَمْ تَطِبْ نَفْسِي أَنْ أَتْرُكَهُ مَعَ الآخَرِ، فَاسْتَخْرَجْتُهُ بَعْدَ سِتَّةِ أَشْهُرٍ، فَإِذَا هُوَ كَيَوْمِ وَضَعْتُهُ هُنَيَّةً غَيْرَ أُذُنِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الجنائز (1351) عن مسدد، أخبرنا بشر بن المفضل، حدثنا حسين المعلم، عن عطاء، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1351).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir reported: “When the time of Uhud approached, my father called me during the night and said, ‘I believe that I will be among the first of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ to be killed. Apart from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself, I leave behind no one dearer to me than you. I have a debt, so repay it, and treat your sisters well.’ “When morning came, he was the first person killed. Another man was buried with him in the same grave. My heart was not content to leave him with the other man, so I exhumed him six months later. He was just as he had been on the day I buried him, except for a slight change near his ear.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",431],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[3810],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1351)."},{"num":8840,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي قَتَادَةَ أَنَّهُ حَضَرَ ذَلِكَ قَالَ: أَتَى عَمْرُو بْنُ الْجَمُوحِ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَرَأَيْتَ إِنْ قَاتَلْتُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ حَتَّى أُقْتَلَ أَمْشِي بِرِجْلِي هَذِهِ صَحِيحَةً فِي الْجَنَّةِ؟، وَكَانَتْ رِجْلُهُ عرْجَاءَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نَعَمْ. فَقَتَلُوهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ هُوَ وَابْنُ أَخِيهِ وَمَوْلًى لَهُمْ، فَمَرَّ عَلَيْهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: كَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَيْكَ تَمْشِي بِرِجْلِكَ هَذِهِ صَحِيحَةً فِي الْجَنَّةِ. فَأَمَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِهِمَا وَبِمَوْلَاهُمَا فَجُعِلُوا فِي قَبْرٍ وَاحِدٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (22553) عن أبي عبد الرحمن المقرئ، حدثنا حيوة، حدثنا أبو صخر حميد بن زياد، أن يحيى بن النضر حدثه عن أبي قتادة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (22553).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Qatadah, who was present on that occasion, reported: ʿAmr ibn al-Jamuh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked, “Messenger of Allah, if I fight in the cause of Allah until I am killed, will I walk in Paradise with this leg of mine restored to health?” His leg was lame. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, “Yes.” He, his nephew, and one of their freedmen were killed on the day of Uhud. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him and said, “It is as though I can see you walking in Paradise with this leg of yours restored to health.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he and his freedman be placed together in one grave."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",432],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (22553)."},{"num":8841,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أُفْرِدَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ فِي سَبْعَةٍ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ وَرَجُلَيْنِ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ، فَلَمَّا رَهِقُوهُ قَالَ: مَنْ يَرُدُّهُمْ عَنَّا وَلَهُ الْجَنَّةُ، أَوْ هُوَ رَفِيقِي فِي الْجَنَّةِ. فَتَقَدَّمَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ رَهِقُوهُ أَيْضًا، فَقَالَ: مَنْ يَرُدُّهُمْ عَنَّا وَلَهُ الْجَنَّةُ، أَوْ هُوَ رَفِيقِي فِي الْجَنَّةِ. فَتَقَدَّمَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، فَلَمْ يَزَلْ كَذَلِكَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ السَّبْعَةُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِصَاحِبَيْهِ: مَا أَنْصَفْنَا أَصْحَابَنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد والسير (100:1789) عن هدّاب بن خالد الأزدي، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن علي بن زيد وثابت البناني، عن أنس بن مالك، قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (100:1789).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik reported that on the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was left isolated with seven men from the Ansar and two men from Quraysh. When the enemy closed in upon him, he said, “Who will repel them from us in return for Paradise—or so that he may be my companion in Paradise?” A man from the Ansar advanced and fought until he was killed. The enemy then closed in upon them again, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “Who will repel them from us in return for Paradise—or so that he may be my companion in Paradise?” Another man from the Ansar advanced and fought until he was killed. This continued until all seven were killed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said to his two companions, “We did not deal fairly with our companions.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",433],"full":1,"rep":[8863],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (100: 1789)."},{"num":8842,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُبَيِّ بْنِ كَعْبٍ، قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ قُتِلَ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ أَرْبَعَةٌ وَسِتُّونَ رَجُلًا، وَمِنَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ سِتَّةٌ، فَقَالَ أَصْحَابُ رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : لَئِنْ كَانَ لَنَا يَوْمٌ مِثْلُ هَذَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، لَنُرْبِيَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ الْفَتْحِ قَالَ رَجُلٌ لَا يُعْرَفُ: لَا قُرَيْشَ بَعْدَ الْيَوْمِ، فَنَادَى مُنَادِي رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  أَمِنَ الْأَسْوَدُ وَالْأَبْيَضُ إِلَّا فُلَانًا وَفُلَانًا، نَاسًا سَمَّاهُمْ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللهُ تبارك وتعالى: ﴿وَإِنْ عَاقَبْتُمْ فَعَاقِبُوا بِمِثْلِ مَا عُوقِبْتُمْ بِهِ وَلَئِنْ صَبَرْتُمْ لَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لِلصَّابِرِينَ﴾ [النحل: ١٢٦] فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : نَصْبِرُ وَلَا نُعَاقِبُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3129) وعبد الله بن أحمد في مسند أبيه (21230،21229) واللفظ له، و ابن حبان (487) والحاكم (3368) كلهم من طرق عن الفضل بن موسى، حدثنا عيسى بن عبيد، عن الربيع بن أنس، عن أبي العالية، عن أبي بن كعب فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (3129) and ʿAbdullah ibn Aḥmad in his father’s Musnad (21229, 21230); authenticated by Ibn Hibban (487).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ubayy ibn Kaʿb reported: “On the day of Uhud, sixty-four men from the Ansar and six from the Muhajirun were killed, among them Hamzah. The polytheists mutilated their dead. “The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘If we are ever given a day against the polytheists like this day, we will certainly inflict more upon them.’ “When the day of the Conquest came, an unidentified man said, ‘There will be no Quraysh after today!’ The herald of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ then proclaimed, ‘Everyone, black and white, has been granted safety except for so-and-so and so-and-so,’ naming certain people. “Allah Almighty then revealed: ‘If you retaliate, then retaliate with the equivalent of what you were made to suffer. But if you remain patient, that is certainly better for those who are patient.’ [Al-Nahl: 126] “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘We shall remain patient and shall not retaliate.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12636],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3129)، وعبد الله بن أحمد في «مسند أبيه» (21229، 21230)، وصححه ابن حبان (487)."},{"num":8843,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنَّ عَمْرَو بْنَ أُقَيْشٍ، كَانَ لَهُ رِبًا فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، فَكَرِهَ أَنْ يُسْلِمَ حَتَّى يَأْخُذَهُ، فَجَاءَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ. فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ بَنُو عَمِّي؟ قَالُوا: بِأُحُدٍ. قَالَ: أَيْنَ فُلاَنٌ؟ قَالُوا: بِأُحُدٍ. قَالَ: أَيْنَ فُلاَنٌ؟ قَالُوا: بِأُحُدٍ. فَلَبِسَ لأْمَتَهُ، وَرَكِبَ فَرَسَهُ، ثُمَّ تَوَجَّهَ قِبَلَهُمْ، فَلَمَّا رَآهُ الْمُسْلِمُونَ، قَالُوا: إِلَيْكَ عَنَّا يَا عَمْرُو. قَالَ: إِنِّي قَدْ آمَنْتُ. فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى جُرِحَ، فَحُمِلَ إِلَى أَهْلِهِ جَرِيحًا، فَجَاءَهُ سَعْدُ بْنُ مُعَاذٍ فَقَالَ لأُخْتِهِ: سَلِيهِ: حَمِيَّةً لِقَوْمِكَ أَوْ غَضَبًا لَهُمْ، أَمْ غَضَبًا لِلَّهِ؟ فَقَالَ: بَلْ غَضَبًا لِلَّهِ وَلِرَسُولِهِ! فَمَاتَ. فَدَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَا صَلَّى لِلَّهِ صَلاَةً."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2537) والحاكم (2533) وعنه البيهقي (18543) من طريق موسى بن إسماعيل، حدثنا حماد، أخبرنا محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dawud (2537) and al-Ḥākim (2533).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that ʿAmr ibn Uqaysh had money owed to him through usury during the Age of Ignorance, and he was unwilling to embrace Islam until he had collected it. On the day of Uhud, he came and asked, “Where are my cousins?” They replied, “At Uhud.” He asked, “Where is so-and-so?” They replied, “At Uhud.” He asked, “Where is so-and-so?” They replied, “At Uhud.” He put on his armor, mounted his horse, and headed toward them. When the Muslims saw him, they said, “Keep away from us, ʿAmr!” He replied, “I have believed.” He fought until he was wounded and was carried back to his family. Saʿd ibn Muʿadh came and told his sister, “Ask him whether he fought out of tribal zeal for his people, out of anger on their behalf, or out of anger for Allah.” He replied, “Rather, it was out of anger for Allah and His Messenger!” He died, entered Paradise, and had never performed a single prayer for Allah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",435],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2537)، والحاكم (2533)."},{"num":8844,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: كَانَ يَقُولُ: حَدِّثُونِي عَنْ رَجُلٍ دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ لَمْ يُصَلِّ قَطُّ، فَإِذَا لَمْ يَعْرِفْهُ النَّاسُ سَأَلُوهُ: مَنْ هُوَ؟ فَيَقُولُ: أُصَيْرِمُ بَنِي عَبْدِ الْأَشْهَلِ عَمْرُو بْنُ ثَابِتِ بْنِ وَقْشٍ.","قَالَ الْحُصَيْنُ: فَقُلْتُ لِمَحْمُودِ بْنِ لَبِيدٍ: كَيْفَ كَانَ شَأْنُ الأُصَيْرِمِ؟ قَالَ: كَانَ يَأْبَى الإِسْلَامَ عَلَى قَوْمِهِ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ وَخَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلَى أُحُدٍ، بَدَا لَهُ الإِسْلَامُ فَأَسْلَمَ، فَأَخَذَ سَيْفَهُ فَغَدَا حَتَّى أَتَى الْقَوْمَ فَدَخَلَ فِي عُرْضِ النَّاسِ، فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى أَثْبَتَتْهُ الْجِرَاحَةُ، قَالَ: فَبَيْنَمَا رِجَالُ بَنِي عَبْدِ الأَشْهَلِ يَلْتَمِسُونَ قَتْلَاهُمْ فِي الْمَعْرَكَةِ إِذَا هُمْ بِهِ، فَقَالُوا: إنه لَلأُصَيْرِمُ، وَمَا جَاءَ؟ لَقَدْ تَرَكْنَاهُ وَإِنَّهُ لَمُنْكِرٌ لِهَذَا الْحَدِيثِ، فاسألوه مَا جَاءَ بِهِ؟ قَالُوا: مَا جَاءَ بِكِ ياعمرو، أحدبا عَلَى قَوْمِكَ أَوْ رَغْبَةً فِي الإِسْلَامِ؟ قَالَ: بَلْ رَغْبَةً فِي الإِسْلَامِ، آمَنْتُ بِالله وَرَسُولِهِ وَأَسْلَمْتُ، ثُمَّ أَخَذْتُ سَيْفِي فَغَدَوْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَقَاتَلْتُ حَتَّى أَصَابَنِي مَا أَصَابَنِي، قَالَ: ثُمَّ لَمْ يَلْبَثْ أَنْ مَاتَ فِي أَيْدِيهِمْ، فَذَكَرُوهُ لِرَسُولِ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ لَمِنْ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23634) عن يعقوب بن إبراهيم، حدثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، حدثني الحصين بن عبد الرحمن بن عمرو بن سعد بن معاذ، عن أبي سفيان مولى ابن أبي أحمد، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (23634).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah would say: “Tell me about a man who entered Paradise without ever having performed a prayer.” When the people did not know the answer, they would ask, “Who was he?” He would reply, “The Usayrim of Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal: ʿAmr ibn Thabit ibn Waqsh.” Al-Husayn said: “I asked Mahmud ibn Labid, ‘What was the story of al-Usayrim?’ He replied: “ʿHe had refused to accept Islam despite his people having done so. When the day of Uhud came and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed for Uhud, Islam became appealing to him and he embraced it. He took his sword, went out in the morning until he reached the people, entered the midst of the fighting, and fought until his wounds incapacitated him. “ʿWhile the men of Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal were searching for their dead on the battlefield, they suddenly found him. They said, “By Allah, this is al-Usayrim! What brought him here? We left him behind while he was still opposed to this matter.”","“ʿThey asked him what had brought him. They said, “What brought you here, ʿAmr? Was it concern for your people, or a desire for Islam?” “ʿHe replied, “Rather, it was a desire for Islam. I believed in Allah and His Messenger and embraced Islam. I then took my sword, went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and fought until what has befallen me befell me.” “ʿHe died in their arms shortly afterward. They mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, “He is indeed among the people of Paradise.”’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",436],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10292],"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23634)."},{"num":8845,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ هُزِمَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ، فَصَرَخَ إِبْلِيسُ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ: أَىْ عِبَادَ اللَّهِ، أُخْرَاكُمْ. فَرَجَعَتْ أُولاَهُمْ، فَاجْتَلَدَتْ هِيَ وَأُخْرَاهُمْ فَبَصُرَ حُذَيْفَةُ فَإِذَا هُوَ بِأَبِيهِ الْيَمَانِ، فَقَالَ: أَىْ عِبَادَ اللَّهِ، أَبِي أَبِي. قَالَ قَالَتْ: فَوَاللَّهِ مَا احْتَجَزُوا حَتَّى قَتَلُوهُ، فَقَالَ حُذَيْفَةُ: يَغْفِرُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ. قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: فَوَاللَّهِ مَا زَالَتْ فِي حُذَيْفَةَ بَقِيَّةُ خَيْرٍ حَتَّى لَحِقَ بِاللَّهِ. بَصُرْتُ عَلِمْتُ، مِنَ الْبَصِيرَةِ فِي الأَمْرِ، وَأَبْصَرْتُ مِنْ بَصَرِ الْعَيْنِ وَيُقَالُ بَصُرْتُ وَأَبْصَرْتُ وَاحِدٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4065) عن عبيد الله بن سعيد، حدثنا أبو أسامة، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4065).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah reported: “On the day of Uhud, the polytheists were defeated. Iblis—may Allah’s curse be upon him—then cried out, ‘Servants of Allah, beware of those behind you!’ The foremost ranks turned back, and they began fighting with those behind them. “Hudhayfah looked and saw that the man was his father, al-Yaman. He cried out, ‘Servants of Allah, my father! My father!’ But by Allah, they did not stop until they had killed him. Hudhayfah said, ‘May Allah forgive you.’” ʿUrwah said: “By Allah, a lasting remnant of goodness continued to remain in Hudhayfah until he returned to Allah.” “Basurtu” means “I knew or recognized,” deriving from insight into a matter. “Absartu” refers to seeing with the eye. It is also said that basurtu and absartu have the same meaning."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",437],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4065)."},{"num":8846,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ، قَالَ: مَرَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِامْرَأَةِ مِنْ بَنِي دِينَارٍ، وَقَدْ أُصِيبَ زَوْجُهَا وَأَخُوهَا وَأَبُوهَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِأُحُدٍ، فَلَمَّا نُعُوا لَهَا، قَالَتْ: فَمَا فَعَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالُوا:خَيْرًا يَا أُمَّ فُلَانٍ، هُوَ بِحَمْدِ اللَّهِ كَمَا تُحِبِّينَ، قَالَتْ: أَرُونِيهِ حَتَّى أَنْظُرَ إلَيْهِ؟ قَالَ:فَأُشِيرَ لَهَا إلَيْهِ، حَتَّى إذَا رَأَتْهُ قَالَتْ: كُلُّ مُصِيبَةٍ بَعْدَكَ جَلَلٌ! تُرِيدُ صَغِيرَةً."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه محمد بن إسحاق، قال: حدثني عبد الواحد بن أبي عون، عن إسماعيل، عن محمد، عن سعد بن أبي وقاص فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب عدد مَنْ قُتِلَ من المسلمين يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Muhammad ibn Ishaq, as mentioned by al-Hafiz Ibn Kathir in al-Bidayah wa-al-Nihayah (3/47).","chapter_en":"The Number of Muslims Killed on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a woman from Banu Dinar whose husband, brother, and father had been killed while fighting alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Uhud. When she was informed of their deaths, she asked, “What happened to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” They replied, “He is well, mother of so-and-so. Praise be to Allah, he is as you would wish him to be.” She said, “Show him to me so that I may look at him.” They pointed him out to her, and when she saw him, she said, “Every calamity after seeing you safe is insignificant!” By jalal, she meant something small and insignificant."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",438],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه محمد بن إسحاق، كما ذكره الحافظ ابن كثير في «البداية والنهاية» (3/47)."},{"num":8847,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَعْفَرِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ الضَّمْرِيِّ، قَالَ: خَرَجْتُ مَعَ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَدِيِّ بْنِ الْخِيَارِ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا حِمْصَ قَالَ لِي عُبَيْدُ اللَّهِ هَلْ لَكَ فِي وَحْشِيٍّ نَسْأَلُهُ عَنْ قَتْلِ حَمْزَةَ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. وَكَانَ وَحْشِيٌّ يَسْكُنُ حِمْصَ، فَسَأَلْنَا عَنْهُ، فَقِيلَ لَنَا: هُوَ ذَاكَ فِي ظِلِّ قَصْرِهِ، كَأَنَّهُ حَمِيتٌ. قَالَ: فَجِئْنَا حَتَّى وَقَفْنَا عَلَيْهِ بِيَسِيرٍ، فَسَلَّمْنَا، فَرَدَّ السَّلاَمَ، قَالَ وَعُبَيْدُ اللَّهِ مُعْتَجِرٌ بِعِمَامَتِهِ، مَا يَرَى وَحْشِيٌّ إِلاَّ عَيْنَيْهِ وَرِجْلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ عُبَيْدُ اللَّهِ: يَا وَحْشِيُّ أَتَعْرِفُنِي؟ قَالَ: فَنَظَرَ إِلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: لاَ وَاللَّهِ، إِلاَّ أَنِّي أَعْلَمُ أَنَّ عَدِيَّ بْنَ الْخِيَارِ تَزَوَّجَ امْرَأَةً يُقَالُ لَهَا أُمُّ قِتَالٍ بِنْتُ أَبِي الْعِيصِ، فَوَلَدَتْ لَهُ غُلاَمًا بِمَكَّةَ، فَكُنْتُ أَسْتَرْضِعُ لَهُ، فَحَمَلْتُ ذَلِكَ الْغُلاَمَ مَعَ أُمِّهِ، فَنَاوَلْتُهَا إِيَّاهُ، فَلَكَأَنِّي نَظَرْتُ إِلَى قَدَمَيْكَ. قَالَ فَكَشَفَ عُبَيْدُ اللَّهِ عَنْ وَجْهِهِ ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلاَ تُخْبِرُنَا بِقَتْلِ حَمْزَةَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، إِنَّ حَمْزَةَ قَتَلَ طُعَيْمَةَ بْنَ عَدِيِّ بْنِ الْخِيَارِ بِبَدْرٍ، فَقَالَ لِي مَوْلاَىَ جُبَيْرُ بْنُ مُطْعِمٍ: إِنْ قَتَلْتَ حَمْزَةَ بِعَمِّي فَأَنْتَ حُرٌّ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا أَنْ خَرَجَ النَّاسُ عَامَ عَيْنَيْنِ ـ وَعَيْنَيْنِ جَبَلٌ بِحِيَالِ أُحُدٍ، بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهُ وَادٍ ـ خَرَجْتُ مَعَ النَّاسِ إِلَى الْقِتَالِ، فَلَمَّا اصْطَفُّوا لِلْقِتَالِ خَرَجَ سِبَاعٌ فَقَالَ: هَلْ مِنْ مُبَارِزٍ؟ قَالَ: فَخَرَجَ إِلَيْهِ حَمْزَةُ بْنُ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ، فَقَالَ: يَا سِبَاعُ، يَا ابْنَ أُمِّ أَنْمَارٍ مُقَطِّعَةِ الْبُظُورِ، أَتُحَادُّ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَ: ثُمَّ شَدَّ عَلَيْهِ، فَكَانَ كَأَمْسِ الذَّاهِبِ. ـ قَالَ: ـ وَكَمَنْتُ لِحَمْزَةَ تَحْتَ صَخْرَةٍ، فَلَمَّا دَنَا مِنِّي رَمَيْتُهُ بِحَرْبَتِي، فَأَضَعُهَا فِي ثُنَّتِهِ حَتَّى خَرَجَتْ مِنْ بَيْنِ وَرِكَيْهِ، ـ قَالَ: ـ فَكَانَ ذَاكَ الْعَهْدَ بِهِ، فَلَمَّا رَجَعَ النَّاسُ رَجَعْتُ مَعَهُمْ، فَأَقَمْتُ بِمَكَّةَ، حَتَّى فَشَا فِيهَا الإِسْلاَمُ، ثُمَّ خَرَجْتُ إِلَى الطَّائِفِ، فَأَرْسَلُوا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَسُولاً، فَقِيلَ لِي: إِنَّهُ لاَ يَهِيجُ الرُّسُلَ، ـ قَالَ: ـ فَخَرَجْتُ مَعَهُمْ حَتَّى قَدِمْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمَّا رَآنِي قَالَ: آنْتَ وَحْشِيٌّ. قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: أَنْتَ قَتَلْتَ حَمْزَةَ. قُلْتُ: قَدْ كَانَ مِنَ الأَمْرِ مَا بَلَغَكَ. قَالَ: فَهَلْ تَسْتَطِيعُ أَنْ تُغَيِّبَ وَجْهَكَ عَنِّي. قَالَ: فَخَرَجْتُ، فَلَمَّا قُبِضَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَخَرَجَ مُسَيْلِمَةُ الْكَذَّابُ، قُلْتُ: لأَخْرُجَنَّ إِلَى مُسَيْلِمَةَ لَعَلِّي أَقْتُلُهُ فَأُكَافِئَ بِهِ حَمْزَةَ، ـ قَالَ: ـ فَخَرَجْتُ مَعَ النَّاسِ، فَكَانَ مِنْ أَمْرِهِ مَا كَانَ، ـ قَالَ: ـ فَإِذَا رَجُلٌ قَائِمٌ فِي ثَلْمَةِ جِدَارٍ، كَأَنَّهُ جَمَلٌ أَوْرَقُ ثَائِرُ الرَّأْسِ، ـ قَالَ: ـ فَرَمَيْتُهُ بِحَرْبَتِي، فَأَضَعُهَا بَيْنَ ثَدْيَيْهِ حَتَّى خَرَجَتْ مِنْ بَيْنِ كَتِفَيْهِ، ـ قَالَ ـ وَوَثَبَ إِلَيْهِ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، فَضَرَبَهُ بِالسَّيْفِ عَلَى هَامَتِهِ.","قَالَ: قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ الفَضْلِ: فَأَخْبَرَنِي سُلَيْمَانُ بْنُ يَسَارٍ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ يَقُولُ: فَقَالَتْ جَارِيَةٌ عَلَى ظَهْرِ بَيْتٍ: وَا أَمِيرَ المُؤْمِنِينَ قَتَلَهُ العَبْدُ الأَسْوَدُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4072) عن أبي جعفر محمد بن عبدالله، حدثنا حجين بن المثنى، حدثنا عبد العزيز بن عبد الله بن أبي سلمة، عن عبدالله بن الفضل، عن سليمان بن يسار، عن جعفر بن عمرو بن أمية الضمري فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في استشهاد حمزة بن عبد المطلب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4072).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of Hamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muttalib","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jaʿfar ibn ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Damri reported: “I travelled with ʿUbaydullah ibn ʿAdi ibn al-Khiyar. When we reached Hims, ʿUbaydullah ibn ʿAdi said to me, ‘Would you like to visit Wahshi and ask him about the killing of Hamzah?’ I replied, ‘Yes.’ “Wahshi was living in Hims, so we asked about him. We were told, ‘There he is, sitting in the shade of his palace, looking like a full waterskin.’ “We approached until we stood a short distance from him. We greeted him, and he returned the greeting. ʿUbaydullah had wrapped his turban around his head and face, so Wahshi could see nothing of him except his eyes and feet. “ʿUbaydullah asked, ‘Wahshi, do you recognize me?’ “Wahshi looked at him and said, ‘No, by Allah. However, I know that ʿAdi ibn al-Khiyar married a woman named Umm Qital bint Abi al-ʿIs. She bore him a boy in Makkah, and I used to seek a wet nurse for him. I carried that boy with his mother and handed him to her. It is as though I can still see your feet.’ “ʿUbaydullah uncovered his face and said, ‘Will you not tell us about the killing of Hamzah?’ “He replied, ʿYes. Hamzah had killed Tuʿaymah ibn ʿAdi ibn al-Khiyar at Badr. My master, Jubayr ibn Mutʿim, said to me, “If you kill Hamzah in retaliation for my uncle, you will be free.” “ʿWhen the people set out in the year of ʿAynayn—ʿAynayn being a mountain opposite Uhud, with a valley between them—I went out with the people to fight. When they formed their battle lines, Sibaʿ came forward and called, “Is there anyone who will duel me?” “ʿHamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muttalib came out against him and said, “Sibaʿ, son of Umm Anmar, the circumciser of women! Do you oppose Allah and His Messenger ﷺ?” He then charged him, and Sibaʿ became like yesterday that had passed away. “ʿI concealed myself from Hamzah beneath a rock. When he came near me, I threw my spear at him and lodged it in his lower abdomen until it emerged from between his hips. That was the end of him. “ʿWhen the people returned, I returned with them. I remained in Makkah until Islam became widespread there, after which I departed for al-Ta’if. Its people sent an envoy to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was told that he did not harm envoys. I therefore went with them until I arrived before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. “ʿWhen he saw me, he asked, “Are you Wahshi?” “ʿI replied, “Yes.” “ʿHe asked, “Did you kill Hamzah?” “ʿI replied, “What occurred is as you have been informed.” “ʿHe said, “Can you keep your face out of my sight?” “ʿI then left. After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away and Musaylimah the Liar emerged, I said, “I will certainly go out against Musaylimah. Perhaps I will kill him and thereby compensate for Hamzah.” “‘I went out with the people, and what happened took place. I suddenly saw a man standing in a breach in a wall, looking like an ash-colored camel, with dishevelled hair. I threw my spear at him and lodged it between his breasts until it emerged from between his shoulder blades. A man from the Ansar then sprang upon him and struck him on the crown of his head with his sword.’”","ʿAbdullah ibn al-Fadl said: Sulayman ibn Yasar informed me that he heard ʿAbdullah ibn ʿUmar say: “A slave girl standing upon the roof of a house cried out, ‘Alas, Commander of the Believers! The black slave has killed him!’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Regarding the statement that a slave girl standing upon a roof cried out, “Alas, Commander of the Believers! The black slave has killed him”: There is reason to question the application of the title “Commander of the Believers” to Musaylimah the Liar. Musaylimah claimed to be a commissioned prophet, and his followers used to address him as “Messenger of Allah” and “Prophet of Allah.” The title “Commander of the Believers” arose afterward. The first person to be given that title was ʿUmar, some time after Musaylimah had been killed. This is stated in Fath al-Bari (7/371)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",439],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4072)."},{"num":8848,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، - الْمَعْنَى - أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَرَّ عَلَى حَمْزَةَ، وَقَدْ مُثِّلَ بِهِ، فَقَالَ: لَوْلاَ أَنْ تَجِدَ صَفِيَّةُ فِي نَفْسِهَا لَتَرَكْتُهُ حَتَّى تَأْكُلَهُ الْعَافِيَةُ حَتَّى يُحْشَرَ مِنْ بُطُونِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3136) والترمذي (1016) وأحمد (12300) والحاكم (1/365) كلهم من طرق عن أسامة بن زيد، عن الزهري، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في استشهاد حمزة بن عبد المطلب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dawud (3136), al-Tirmidhi (1016), Aḥmad (12300), and al-Ḥākim (1/365).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of Hamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muttalib","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Hamzah after his body had been mutilated. He said, “Were it not that Safiyyah would be deeply grieved, I would have left him until the beasts and birds of prey consumed him, so that he would be resurrected from their bellies.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",440],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3136)، والترمذي (1016)، وأحمد (12300)، والحاكم (1/365)."},{"num":8849,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُقْبَةَ بْنِ عَامِرٍ، قَالَ: صَلَّى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى قَتْلَى أُحُدٍ بَعْدَ ثَمَانِي سِنِينَ، كَالْمُوَدِّعِ لِلأَحْيَاءِ وَالأَمْوَاتِ، ثُمَّ طَلَعَ الْمِنْبَرَ فَقَالَ: إِنِّي بَيْنَ أَيْدِيكُمْ فَرَطٌ، وَأَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدٌ، وَإِنَّ مَوْعِدَكُمُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4042) ومسلم في الفضائل (30:2296) كلاهما من طريق يزيد بن أبي حبيب، عن أبي الخير، عن عقبة بن عامر قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ لمن استشهد في غزوة أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4042) and Muslim (30:2296).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication for Those Martyred in the Battle of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir reported: “Eight years after the battle, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for those killed at Uhud, like one bidding farewell to both the living and the dead. He then ascended the pulpit and said, ‘I will precede you, and I shall be a witness over you…’” The remainder of the lengthy hadith follows."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى: ﴿وَلَا تَهِنُوا وَلَا تَحْزَنُوا وَأَنْتُمُ الْأَعْلَوْنَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ ۝ إِنْ يَمْسَسْكُمْ قَرْحٌ فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ قَرْحٌ مِثْلُهُ وَتِلْكَ الْأَيَّامُ نُدَاوِلُهَا بَيْنَ النَّاسِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنْكُمْ شُهَدَاءَ وَاللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ ۝ وَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَمْحَقَ الْكَافِرِينَ ۝ أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا مِنْكُمْ وَيَعْلَمَ الصَّابِرِينَ ۝ وَلَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تَمَنَّوْنَ الْمَوْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ تَلْقَوْهُ فَقَدْ رَأَيْتُمُوهُ وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ﴾ [آل عمران: ١٣٩-١٤٣]."],"en":["Allah Most High says:","“Do not lose heart and do not grieve, for you will have the upper hand if you are believers. If a wound has touched you, an equivalent wound has already touched the other people. These are the days that We alternate among the people, so that Allah may make evident those who believe and take martyrs from among you. Allah does not love the wrongdoers; and so that Allah may purify those who believe and destroy the disbelievers.","“Or did you suppose that you would enter Paradise before Allah made evident those among you who struggled and made evident those who remained patient? You had certainly been wishing for death before encountering it. Now you have seen it with your own eyes.” [Ali ʿImran: 139–143]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",443],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4042)، ومسلم (30: 2296)."},{"num":8850,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: لَمَّا بَلَغَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَتْلُ حَمْزَةَ بَكَى، فَلَمَّا نَظَرَ إِلَيْهِ شَهِقَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1794) عن مسلم بن جنادة أبي السائب، ثنا عبدالله بن نمير، ثنا محمد بن علي السلمي، عن عبد الله بن محمد بن عقيل، عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بكاء النبي ﷺ ونساء الأنصار على حمزة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1794).","chapter_en":"The Weeping of the Prophet ﷺ and the Women of the Ansar for Hamzah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah reported: “When news of Hamzah’s death reached the Prophet ﷺ, he wept. When he saw him, he sobbed.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",444],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في «كشف الأستار» (1794)."},{"num":8851,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَرَّ بِنِسَاءِ عَبْدِ الأَشْهَلِ يَبْكِينَ هَلْكَاهُنَّ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَكِنَّ حَمْزَةَ لاَ بَوَاكِيَ لَهُ. فَجَاءَ نِسَاءُ الأَنْصَارِ يَبْكِينَ حَمْزَةَ، فَاسْتَيْقَظَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: وَيْحَهُنَّ مَا انْقَلَبْنَ بَعْدُ؟ مُرُوهُنَّ فَلْيَنْقَلِبْنَ، وَلاَ يَبْكِينَ عَلَى هَالِكٍ بَعْدَ الْيَوْمِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجة (1591) وأحمد (4984) والحاكم (3/195) كلهم من حديث أسامة بن زيد، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره. واللفظ لابن ماجه.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بكاء النبي ﷺ ونساء الأنصار على حمزة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Majah (1591), Aḥmad (4984), and al-Ḥākim (3/195).","chapter_en":"The Weeping of the Prophet ﷺ and the Women of the Ansar for Hamzah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the women of ʿAbd al-Ashhal as they wept for those of their families who had died on the day of Uhud. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “But Hamzah has no women to weep for him.” The women of the Ansar then came and wept for Hamzah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke and said, “Woe to them! Have they still not returned home? Tell them to return, and they must not wail over anyone who dies after today.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",445],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[3589],"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (1591)، وأحمد (4984)، والحاكم (3/195)."},{"num":8852,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن يَحْيَى بن عباد بن الزُّبَيْرِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، عَنْ جَدِّهِ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، يَقُولُ: وَقَدْ كَانَ النَّاسُ انْهَزَمُوا عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى انْتَهَى بَعْضُهُمْ إِلَى دُونِ الأَعْرَاضِ إِلَى جَبَلٍ بِنَاحِيَةِ الْمَدِينَةِ، ثُمَّ رَجَعُوا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ كَانَ حَنْظَلَةُ بْنُ أَبِي عَامِرٍ الْتَقَى هُوَ وَأَبُو سُفْيَانَ بْنُ حَرْبٍ، فَلَمَّا اسْتَعْلَاهُ حَنْظَلَةُ رَآهُ شَدَّادُ بْنُ الأَسْوَدِ، فَعَلَاهُ شَدَّادٌ بِالسَّيْفِ حَتَّى قَتَلَهُ، وَقَدْ كَادَ يَقْتُلُ أَبَا سُفْيَانَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ صَاحِبَكُمْ حَنْظَلَةَ تُغَسِّلُهُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ، فَسَلُوا صَاحِبَتَهُ، فَقَالَتْ: خَرَجَ وَهُوَ جُنُبٌ لَمَّا سَمِعَ الْهَائِعَةَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَذَاكَ قَدْ غَسَّلَتْهُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (7025) والحاكم (3/204-205) كلاهما من حديث ابن إسحاق، قال: حدثني يحيى بن عباد فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب غسل الملائكة حنظلة الراهب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Hibban (7025) and al-Ḥākim (3/204–205).","chapter_en":"The Angels Washing Hanzalah, the Son of the Monk","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yahya ibn ʿAbbad ibn al-Zubayr reported from his father, from his grandfather, who said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say—after the people had fled from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until some of them reached a mountain near Madinah, short of al-Aʿrad, and then returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “ʿHanzalah ibn Abi ʿAmir encountered Abū Sufyan ibn Harb. When Hanzalah overpowered him, Shaddad ibn al-Aswad saw him and struck Hanzalah from above with his sword until he killed him. Hanzalah had nearly killed Abū Sufyan. “ʿThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The angels are washing your companion Hanzalah. Ask his wife about him.” “ʿShe said, “He went out while in a state of major ritual impurity when he heard the alarm calling the people to battle.” “ʿThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “That is why the angels washed him.”’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",446],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (7025)، والحاكم (3/204-205)."},{"num":8853,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن زَيْدِ بن ثَابِتٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ يَقُولُ لَمَّا خَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى أُحُدٍ رَجَعَ نَاسٌ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ فَقَالَتْ فِرْقَةٌ: نَقْتُلُهُمْ. وَقَالَتْ فِرْقَةٌ: لاَ نَقْتُلُهُمْ. فَنَزَلَتْ: ﴿فَمَا لَكُمْ فِي الْمُنَافِقِينِ فِئَتَيْنِ﴾ [سورة النساء: 88]} وَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّهَا تَنْفِي الرِّجَالَ كَمَا تَنْفِي النَّارُ خَبَثَ الْحَدِيدِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل المدينة (1884) ومسلم في صفات المنافقين وأحكامهم (6:2776) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن عدي بن ثابت، عن عبد الله بن يزيد سمعت زيد بن ثابت يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب صفة المنافقين واليهود في غزوة أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1884) and Muslim (6:2776).","chapter_en":"The Conduct of the Hypocrites and the Jews During the Battle of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Thabit reported: “When the Prophet ﷺ set out for Uhud, some of those accompanying him turned back. One group said, ‘We should kill them,’ while another group said, ‘We should not kill them.’ Allah then revealed: ‘Why are you divided into two groups concerning the hypocrites?’ [Al-Nisaʾ: 88] “The Prophet ﷺ said, ‘It expels men just as fire removes impurities from iron.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn Hisham said: “The Prophet ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum to lead the people in prayer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12191],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1884)، ومسلم (6: 2776)."},{"num":8854,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ:  لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ عَنْ يَمِينِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعَنْ يَسَارِهِ، رَجُلَيْنِ عَلَيْهِمَا ثِيَابٌ بِيضٌ، يُقَاتِلَانِ عَنْهُ كَأَشَدِّ الْقِتَالِ، مَا رَأَيْتُهُمَا قَبْلُ وَلَا بَعْدُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4045) ومسلم في الفضائل (47:2306) كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم بن سعد (هو: ابن إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن عوف) عن أبيه سعد، عن جدّه (إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن)، عن سعد بن وقاص قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب شهود الملائكة غزوة أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4045) and Muslim (47:2306).","chapter_en":"The Angels’ Presence at the Battle of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas reported: “On the day of Uhud, I saw two men dressed in white on the right and left of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, fighting in his defense with the fiercest fighting. I never saw them before that day or afterward.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “two men dressed in white,” refers to Jibril and Mika’il, peace be upon them, as explicitly stated in Sahih Muslim (2306)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",448],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4045)، ومسلم (47: 2306)."},{"num":8855,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ انْهَزَمَ النَّاسُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَبُو طَلْحَةَ بَيْنَ يَدَىِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُجَوِّبٌ عَلَيْهِ بِحَجَفَةٍ لَهُ، وَكَانَ أَبُو طَلْحَةَ رَجُلاً رَامِيًا شَدِيدَ النَّزْعِ، كَسَرَ يَوْمَئِذٍ قَوْسَيْنِ أَوْ ثَلاَثًا، وَكَانَ الرَّجُلُ يَمُرُّ مَعَهُ بِجَعْبَةٍ مِنَ النَّبْلِ فَيَقُولُ: انْثُرْهَا لأَبِي طَلْحَةَ. قَالَ وَيُشْرِفُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَنْظُرُ إِلَى الْقَوْمِ، فَيَقُولُ أَبُو طَلْحَةَ: بِأَبِي أَنْتَ وَأُمِّي، لاَ تُشْرِفْ يُصِيبُكَ سَهْمٌ مِنْ سِهَامِ الْقَوْمِ، نَحْرِي دُونَ نَحْرِكَ. وَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ عَائِشَةَ بِنْتَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ وَأُمَّ سُلَيْمٍ، وَإِنَّهُمَا لَمُشَمِّرَتَانِ أَرَى خَدَمَ سُوقِهِمَا تَنْقُزَانِ الْقِرَبَ عَلَى مُتُونِهِمَا، تُفْرِغَانِهِ فِي أَفْوَاهِ الْقَوْمِ، ثُمَّ تَرْجِعَانِ فَتَمْلآنِهَا، ثُمَّ تَجِيئَانِ فَتُفْرِغَانِهِ فِي أَفْوَاهِ الْقَوْمِ، وَلَقَدْ وَقَعَ السَّيْفُ مِنْ يَدَىْ أَبِي طَلْحَةَ إِمَّا مَرَّتَيْنِ وَإِمَّا ثَلاَثًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4064) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (136:1811) كلاهما من طريق عبد الوارث، حدثنا عبد العزيز (هو ابن صهيب) عن أنس بن مالك قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4064) and Muslim (136:1811).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: “On the day of Uhud, the people fled from the Prophet ﷺ, while Abū Talhah stood before him, shielding him with a leather shield. “Abū Talhah was a powerful archer with a strong draw. He broke two or three bows that day. Whenever a man passed carrying a quiver of arrows, the Prophet ﷺ would say, ‘Empty them out for Abū Talhah.’ “The Prophet ﷺ would raise himself to look toward the enemy, and Abū Talhah would say, ‘May my father and mother be sacrificed for you! Do not raise yourself, lest an arrow from the enemy strike you. Let my neck be struck instead of yours.’ “I saw ʿA’ishah bint Abi Bakr and Umm Sulaym with their garments raised. I could see the anklets upon their lower legs as they carried waterskins upon their backs and poured water into the mouths of the men. They would then return, refill the waterskins, come back, and pour the water into the mouths of the men. “The sword fell from Abū Talhah’s hands twice or three times.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",449],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4064)، ومسلم (136: 1811)."},{"num":8856,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: مَا سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَمَعَ أَبَوَيْهِ لأَحَدٍ إِلاَّ لِسَعْدِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، فَإِنِّي سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ: يَا سَعْدُ ارْمِ، فِدَاكَ أَبِي وَأُمِّي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4059) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (41:2411) كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم بن سعد، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن شدّاد، عن علي قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4059) and Muslim (41:2411).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAli ibn Abi Talib reported: “I never heard the Prophet ﷺ offer both his parents as a ransom for anyone except Saʿd ibn Malik. I heard him say on the day of Uhud, ‘Saʿd, shoot! May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“Saʿd ibn Malik” is Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",450],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14630],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4059)، ومسلم (41: 2411)."},{"num":8857,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ لَقَدْ جَمَعَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ أَبَوَيْهِ كِلَيْهِمَا. يُرِيدُ حِينَ قَالَ: فِدَاكَ أَبِي وَأُمِّي. وَهُوَ يُقَاتِلُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4057) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (42:2412) كلاهما من طريق يحيى (هو ابن سعيد الأنصاري) عن سعيد بن المسيب، عن سعد بن وقاص قال: فذكره. والسياق للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4057) and Muslim (42:2412). This wording is al-Bukhārī’s.","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas reported: “On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered both of his parents as a ransom for me.” He meant the occasion when the Prophet ﷺ said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you,” while Saʿd was fighting."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",451],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4057)، ومسلم (42: 2412). والسياق للبخاري."},{"num":8858,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَمَعَ لَهُ أَبَوَيْهِ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، قَالَ: كَانَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ قَدْ أَحْرَقَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ فَقَالَ لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : ارْمِ فِدَاكَ أَبِي وَأُمِّي قَالَ: فَنَزَعْتُ لَهُ بِسَهْمٍ لَيْسَ فِيهِ نصْل، فَأَصَبْتُ جَنْبَهُ فَسَقَطَ، فَانْكَشَفَتْ عَوْرَتُهُ، فَضَحِكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى نَظَرْتُ إِلَى نَوَاجِذِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (42:2412) عن محمد بن عباد، حدثنا حاتم (هو ابن إسماعيل) عن بكير بن مسمار، عن عامر بني سعد، عن أبيه سعد بن أبي وقاص فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (42:2412).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas reported that on the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ offered both of his parents as a ransom for him. Saʿd said: “A man from among the polytheists had inflicted severe harm upon the Muslims. The Prophet ﷺ said to me, ‘Shoot! May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.’ “I drew an arrow that had no arrowhead and struck the man in his side. He fell, and his private parts became exposed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until I could see his molar teeth.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “He had burned the Muslims,” means that the man had inflicted many casualties upon them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",452],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9525],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (42: 2412)."},{"num":8859,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ يَقُولُ نَثَلَ لِي النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كِنَانَتَهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ فَقَالَ: ارْمِ فِدَاكَ أَبِي وَأُمِّي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4055) عن عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا مروان بن معاوية، حدثنا هاشم بن هاشم السعدي قال: سمعت سعيد بن المسيب يقول: سمعت سعد بن أبي وقاص يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4055).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas reported: “On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ emptied his quiver out for me and said, ‘Shoot! May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“Nathala” means that he took out and emptied its contents. A kinanah is a container for arrows."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",453],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4055)."},{"num":8860,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي عُثْمَانَ (هُوَ النهدي عبد الرَّحْمَنِ بن ملّ) قَالَ: لَمْ يَبْقَ مَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَعْضِ تِلْكَ الأَيَّامِ الَّتِي قَاتَلَ فِيهِنَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ غَيْرُ طَلْحَةَ وَسَعْدٍ عَنْ حَدِيثِهِمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3723،3722) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (47:2414) كلاهما عن محمد بن أبي بكر القدمي، حدثنا معتمر، عن أبيه، عن أبي عثمان فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3722, 3723) and Muslim (47:2414).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū ʿUthman—Abū ʿUthman al-Nahdi, ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn Mull—reported: “During one of those days on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought, no one remained with him except Talhah and Saʿd.” This was reported on their own authority."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",454],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3722، 3723)، ومسلم (47: 2414)."},{"num":8861,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن السَّائِبِ بن يَزِيدَ قَالَ: صَحِبْتُ عَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنَ عَوْفٍ، وَطَلْحَةَ بْنَ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ، وَالْمِقْدَادَ وَسَعْدًا رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ. فَمَا سَمِعْتُ أَحَدًا مِنْهُمْ يُحَدِّثُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، إِلاَّ أَنِّي سَمِعْتُ طَلْحَةَ يُحَدِّثُ عَنْ يَوْمِ أُحُدٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4062) عن عبد الله بن أبي الأسود، حدثنا حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن محمد بن يوسف قال: سمعت السائب بن يزيد فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4062).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid reported: “I accompanied ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn ʿAwf, Talhah ibn ʿUbaydillah, al-Miqdad, and Saʿd—may Allah be pleased with them. I did not hear any of them narrate from the Prophet ﷺ, except that I heard Talhah narrating concerning the day of Uhud.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",455],"full":1,"rep":[9938],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4062)."},{"num":8862,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ قَيْسٍ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ يَدَ طَلْحَةَ شَلاَّءَ، وَقَى بِهَا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4063) عن عبد الله بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا وكيع، عن إسماعيل، عن قيس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4063).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Qays ibn Abi Hazim reported: “I saw that Talhah’s hand was paralyzed. He had used it to shield the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",456],"full":1,"rep":[9939],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4063)."},{"num":8863,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أُفْرِدَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ فِي سَبْعَةٍ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ، وَرَجُلَيْنِ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ، فَلَمَّا رَهِقُوهُ قَالَ: مَنْ يَرُدُّهُمْ عَنَّا وَلَهُ الْجَنَّةُ، أَوْ هُوَ رَفِيقِي فِي الْجَنَّةِ. فَتَقَدَّمَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ رَهِقُوهُ أَيْضًا، فَقَالَ: مَنْ يَرُدُّهُمْ عَنَّا وَلَهُ الْجَنَّةُ، أَوْ هُوَ رَفِيقِي فِي الْجَنَّةِ. فَتَقَدَّمَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ، فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، فَلَمْ يَزَلْ كَذَلِكَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ السَّبْعَةُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِصَاحِبَيْهِ: مَا أَنْصَفْنَا أَصْحَابَنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد (1789) عن هداب بن خالد الأزدي، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن علي بن زيد وثابت البناني، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1789).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik reported that on the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was left isolated with seven men from the Ansar and two men from Quraysh. When the enemy closed in upon him, he said, “Who will repel them from us in return for Paradise—or so that he may be my companion in Paradise?” A man from the Ansar advanced and fought until he was killed. The enemy then closed in upon them again, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “Who will repel them from us in return for Paradise—or so that he may be my companion in Paradise?” Another man from the Ansar advanced and fought until he was killed. This continued until all seven were killed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said to his two companions, “We have not dealt fairly with our companions.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Regarding his statement, “We have not dealt fairly with our companions”: This means that the two men of Quraysh had not dealt fairly with the Ansar, because the two Qurashis did not go out to fight, while the men of the Ansar went out one after another. Al-Nawawi mentioned this explanation."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",457],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8841],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1789)."},{"num":8864,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ وَوَلَّى النَّاسُ، كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي نَاحِيَةٍ فِي اثْنَىْ عَشَرَ رَجُلاً مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، وَفِيهِمْ طَلْحَةُ بْنُ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ، فَأَدْرَكَهُمُ الْمُشْرِكُونَ، فَالْتَفَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَالَ مَنْ لِلْقَوْمِ. فَقَالَ طَلْحَةُ: أَنَا. قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَمَا أَنْتَ. فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ: أَنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. فَقَالَ: أَنْتَ. فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ الْتَفَتَ فَإِذَا الْمُشْرِكُونَ، فَقَالَ: مَنْ لِلْقَوْمِ. فَقَالَ طَلْحَةُ: أَنَا. قَالَ: كَمَا أَنْتَ. فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ: أَنَا. فَقَالَ: أَنْتَ. فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ لَمْ يَزَلْ يَقُولُ ذَلِكَ، وَيَخْرُجُ إِلَيْهِمْ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ فَيُقَاتِلُ قِتَالَ مَنْ قَبْلَهُ حَتَّى يُقْتَلَ، حَتَّى بَقِيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَطَلْحَةُ بْنُ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ لِلْقَوْمِ. فَقَالَ طَلْحَةُ: أَنَا. فَقَاتَلَ طَلْحَةُ قِتَالَ الأَحَدَ عَشَرَ، حَتَّى ضُرِبَتْ يَدُهُ، فَقُطِعَتْ أَصَابِعُهُ، فَقَالَ: حَسِّ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَوْ قُلْتَ: بِسْمِ اللَّهِ لَرَفَعَتْكَ الْمَلاَئِكَةُ وَالنَّاسُ يَنْظُرُونَ. ثُمَّ رَدَّ اللَّهُ الْمُشْرِكِينَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3149) وعنه ابن السني في عمل اليوم والليلة (670) – عن عمرو بن سوّاد قال: أنبأنا ابن وهب، أخبرني يحيى بن أيوب وذكر آخر قبله، عن عمارة بن غزية، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من ثبت مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3149), and through him by Ibn al-Sunni in ʿAmal al-Yawm wa-al-Laylah (670).","chapter_en":"Those Who Remained Steadfast with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah reported: “When the people turned away on the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing to one side with twelve men from the Ansar, among whom was Talhah ibn ʿUbaydillah. The polytheists caught up with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned and asked, ‘Who will confront these people?’ “Talhah said, ‘I will.’ “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Remain where you are.’ “A man from the Ansar said, ‘I will, Messenger of Allah.’ “He said, ‘Then you go.’ The man fought until he was killed. “The Prophet ﷺ turned again and saw the polytheists. He asked, ‘Who will confront these people?’ “Talhah said, ‘I will.’ “He said, ‘Remain where you are.’ “Another man from the Ansar said, ‘I will.’ “He said, ‘Then you go.’ The man fought until he was killed. “The Prophet ﷺ continued asking the same question, and each time a man from the Ansar went out and fought as the man before him had fought until he was killed. Eventually, only the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Talhah ibn ʿUbaydillah remained. “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, ‘Who will confront these people?’ “Talhah replied, ‘I will.’ “Talhah then fought with the strength of all eleven men. His hand was struck and his fingers were severed, causing him to exclaim, ‘Hass!’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Had you said, “In the name of Allah,” the angels would have lifted you while the people watched.’ “Allah then repelled the polytheists.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",458],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9940],"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3149)، وعنه ابن السني في «عمل اليوم والليلة» (670)."},{"num":8865,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عُمَرَ بن الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَسَمَ مُرُوطًا بَيْنَ نِسَاءٍ مِنْ نِسَاءِ أَهْلِ الْمَدِينَةِ، فَبَقِيَ مِنْهَا مِرْطٌ جَيِّدٌ، فَقَالَ لَهُ بَعْضُ مَنْ عِنْدَهُ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، أَعْطِ هَذَا بِنْتَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الَّتِي عِنْدَكَ. يُرِيدُونَ أُمَّ كُلْثُومٍ بِنْتَ عَلِيٍّ. فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: أُمُّ سَلِيطٍ أَحَقُّ بِهِ. وَأُمُّ سَلِيطٍ مِنْ نِسَاءِ الأَنْصَارِ مِمَّنْ بَايَعَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ عُمَرُ: فَإِنَّهَا كَانَتْ تُزْفِرُ لَنَا الْقِرَبَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4071) عن يحيى بن بكير، حدثنا الليث (هو ابن سعد) عن يونس، عن ابن شهاب، قال ثعلبة بن أبي مالك إن عمر بن الخطاب قسم مروطا...فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب خدمة النساء يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4071).","chapter_en":"The Women’s Service on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab distributed woolen garments among some of the women of Madinah. One fine garment remained, so some of those with him said, “Commander of the Believers, give this to the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who is married to you.” They meant Umm Kulthum bint ʿAli. ʿUmar replied, “Umm Sulayt has a greater right to it.” Umm Sulayt was one of the women of the Ansar who had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar said, “She used to carry the waterskins for us on the day of Uhud.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Umm Sulayt was the mother of Abū Saʿid al-Khudri. She had been married to Abū Sulayt, who died before the Hijrah. Malik ibn Sinan al-Khudri then married her, and she bore him Abū Saʿid. Al-Hafiz Ibn Hajar stated this in Fath al-Bari."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",459],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4071)."},{"num":8866,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ انْهَزَمَ النَّاسُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَأَبُو طَلْحَةَ بَيْنَ يدي النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فجوّب عَلَيْهِ بجحفة لَهُ. فَذَكَرَ الْحَدِيثَ. وَجَاءَ فِيهِ: وَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ عَائِشَةَ بِنْتَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ وَأُمَّ سُلَيْمٍ وَإِنَّهُمَا لَمُشَمِّرَتَانِ، أَرَى خَدَمَ سُوقِهِمَا تَنْقُزَانِ الْقِرَبَ عَلَى مُتُونِهِمَا، تُفْرِغَانِهِ فِي أَفْوَاهِ الْقَوْمِ، ثُمَّ تَرْجِعَانِ فتملآنهما، ثُمَّ تَجِيئَانِ فتفرغانه فِي أَفْوَاهِ الْقَوْمِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4064) ومسلم في الجهاد (136:1811) كلاهما من طريق عبدالوارث، حدثنا عبدالعزيز، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب خدمة النساء يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4064) and Muslim (136:1811).","chapter_en":"The Women’s Service on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: “On the day of Uhud, the people fled from the Prophet ﷺ, while Abū Talhah stood before him, shielding him with a leather shield.” He then related the hadith. It contains the following: “I saw ʿA’ishah bint Abi Bakr and Umm Sulaym with their garments raised. I could see the anklets upon their lower legs as they carried waterskins upon their backs and poured water into the mouths of the men. They would then return, refill the waterskins, and come back to pour the water into the mouths of the men.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",460],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4064)، ومسلم (136: 1811)."},{"num":8867,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : اشْتَدَّ غَضَبُ اللَّهِ عَلَى قَوْمٍ فَعَلُوا بِنَبِيِّهِ – يُشِيرُ إِلَى رَبَاعِيَتِهِ – اشْتَدَّ غَضَبُ اللَّهِ عَلَى رَجُلٍ يَقْتُلُهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4073) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (106:1793) كلاهما من طريق عبد الرزاق، حدثنا معمر، عن همّام بن منبّه، سمع أبا هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4073) and Muslim (106:1793).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The wrath of Allah became severe against a people who did this to His Prophet”—and he pointed to his incisor tooth—“and the wrath of Allah became severe against a man whom the Messenger of Allah kills in the cause of Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",461],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4073)، ومسلم (106: 1793)."},{"num":8868,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: اشْتَدَّ غَضَبُ اللَّهِ عَلَى قَوْمٍ هَشَّمُوا الْبَيْضَةَ عَلَى رَأْسِ نَبِيِّهِمْ، وَهُوَ يَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَى اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1793) عن محمد بن معمر، ثنا سهل بن بكار، ثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره. وإسناده حسن من أجل محمد بن عمرو فإنه حسن الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1793).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said, “The wrath of Allah became severe against a people who shattered the helmet upon the head of their Prophet while he was calling them to Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",462],"full":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في «كشف الأستار» (1793)."},{"num":8869,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن مَسْعُودٍ كَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَحْكِي نَبِيًّا مِنَ الأَنْبِيَاءِ ضَرَبَهُ قَوْمُهُ فَأَدْمَوْهُ، وَهْوَ يَمْسَحُ الدَّمَ عَنْ وَجْهِهِ، وَيَقُولُ: اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِقَوْمِي فَإِنَّهُمْ لاَ يَعْلَمُونَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في أحاديث الأنبياء (3477) ومسلم في الجهاد (1792) كلاهما من حديث الأعمش، قال: حدثني شقيق، عن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3477) and Muslim (1792).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud reported: “It is as though I can see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relating the story of a prophet whose people struck him and made him bleed. As he wiped the blood from his face, he said, ‘O Allah, forgive my people, for they do not know.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration of Muslim: “While he was wiping the blood from his forehead.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",463],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8492,10959],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3477)، ومسلم (1792)."},{"num":8870,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: اشْتَدَّ غَضَبُ اللَّهِ عَلَى مَنْ قَتَلَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، اشْتَدَّ غَضَبُ اللَّهِ عَلَى قَوْمٍ دَمَّوْا وَجْهَ نَبِيِّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4074) عن مخلد بن مالك، حدثنا يحيى بن سعيد الأموي، حدثنا ابن جريج، عمرو بن دينار، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4074).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbas reported: “The wrath of Allah became severe against the person whom the Prophet ﷺ killed in the cause of Allah, and the wrath of Allah became severe against the people who bloodied the face of Allah’s Prophet ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",464],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4074)."},{"num":8871,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الزُّبَيْرِ قَالَ: أَمَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلِيَّ بْنَ أَبِي طَالِبٍ يَأْتِي الْمِهْرَاسَ، فَأَتَاهُ بِمَاءٍ فِي دَرَقَتِهِ، فَأَتَى بِهِ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَرَادَ أَنْ يَشْرَبَ مِنْهُ، فَوَجَدَ لَهُ رِيحًا فَعَافَهُ، فَغَسَلَ بِهِ وَجْهَهُ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الدِّمَاءِ الَّتِي أَصَابَتْهُ وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: اشْتَدَّ غَضَبُ اللَّهِ على من أدمى وَجْهَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ.","وكان الذي أدماه يَوْمَئِذٍ عُتْبَةُ بْنُ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه في مسنده كما في المطالب (4260)، عن وهب، حدثنا أبي، قال: سمعت محمد بن إسحاق يقول: حدثني يحيى بن عباد، عن أبيه، عن عبدالله بن الزبير، عن الزبير فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, as cited in al-Matalib al-ʿAliyah (4260).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Zubayr reported: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed ʿAli ibn Abi Talib to go to al-Mihras. ʿAli brought him water in his shield. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to drink from it, but he detected an odor in it and found it distasteful. He therefore used it to wash from his face the blood that had struck him, while saying, ‘The wrath of Allah became severe against the one who bloodied the face of the Messenger of Allah.’ “The person who bloodied him that day was ʿUtbah ibn Abi Waqqas.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",465],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه كما في «المطالب العالية» (4260)."},{"num":8872,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سهل بْنِ سَعْدٍ – وهو يسأل عَنْ جُرْحِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: أَمَا وَاللَّهِ إِنِّي لأَعْرِفُ مَنْ كَانَ يَغْسِلُ جُرْحَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ وَكَانَ يَسْكُبُ الْمَاءَ، وَبِمَا دُووِيَ، قَالَ: كَانَتْ فَاطِمَةُ عَلَيْهَا السَّلاَمُ بِنْتُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَغْسِلُهُ، وَعَلِيٌّ يَسْكُبُ الْمَاءَ بِالْمِجَنِّ، فَلَمَّا رَأَتْ فَاطِمَةُ أَنَّ الْمَاءَ لاَ يَزِيدُ الدَّمَ إِلاَّ كَثْرَةً، أَخَذَتْ قِطْعَةً مِنْ حَصِيرٍ فَأَحْرَقَتْهَا وَأَلْصَقَتْهَا، فَاسْتَمْسَكَ الدَّمُ، وَكُسِرَتْ رَبَاعِيَتُهُ يَوْمَئِذٍ، وَجُرِحَ وَجْهُهُ، وَكُسِرَتِ الْبَيْضَةُ عَلَى رَأْسِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4075) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (102:1790) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا يعقوب (هو ابن عبد الرحمن القاري) عن أبي حازم أنه سمع سهل بن سعد قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4075) and Muslim (102:1790).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd was asked about the wound of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He replied: “By Allah, I know who washed the wound of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who poured the water, and what was used to treat him. “Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, washed the wound, while ʿAli poured water from a shield. When Fatimah saw that the water only caused the bleeding to increase, she took a piece of matting, burned it, and pressed it against the wound, and the bleeding stopped. His incisor tooth was broken that day, his face was wounded, and the helmet upon his head was shattered.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",466],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4075)، ومسلم (102: 1790)."},{"num":8873,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ: ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا ﴿الَّذِينَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَصَابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا مِنْهُمْ وَاتَّقَوْا أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ﴾ [سورة آل عمران: 172]} قَالَتْ لِعُرْوَةَ: يَا ابْنَ أُخْتِي، كَانَ أَبُوكَ مِنْهُمُ: الزُّبَيْرُ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ، لَمَّا أَصَابَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَا أَصَابَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، وَانْصَرَفَ عَنْهُ الْمُشْرِكُونَ، خَافَ أَنْ يَرْجِعُوا قَالَ: مَنْ يَذْهَبُ فِي إِثْرِهِمْ. فَانْتَدَبَ مِنْهُمْ سَبْعُونَ رَجُلاً، قَالَ: كَانَ فِيهِمْ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَالزُّبَيْرُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4077) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (51:2418) كلاهما من طريق هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4077) and Muslim (51:2418).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Regarding the verse: “Those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after suffering injury—for those among them who did good and remained mindful of Allah there is a magnificent reward.” [Ali ʿImran: 172] ʿA’ishah said to ʿUrwah: “Son of my sister, both of your fathers were among them: al-Zubayr and Abū Bakr. After what befell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud and the polytheists withdrew from him, he feared that they might return. He therefore asked, ‘Who will pursue them?’ Seventy men volunteered, among whom were Abū Bakr and al-Zubayr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[8877],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4077)، ومسلم (51: 2418)."},{"num":8874,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كُسِرَتْ رَبَاعِيَتُهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، وَشُجَّ فِي رَأْسِهِ، فَجَعَلَ يَسْلُتُ الدَّمَ عَنْهُ وَيَقُولُ: كَيْفَ يُفْلِحُ قَوْمٌ شَجُّوا نَبِيَّهُمْ وَكَسَرُوا رَبَاعِيَتَهُ، وَهُوَ يَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَى اللَّهِ؟! فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد والسير (104:1791) عن عبد الله بن مسلمة بن قعنب، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن ثابت، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما أصاب النبي ﷺ من الجروح يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (104:1791).","chapter_en":"The Wounds Suffered by the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uhud","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that the incisor tooth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was broken on the day of Uhud and his head was wounded. As he wiped the blood from himself, he said, “How can a people succeed when they have wounded the head of their Prophet and broken his incisor tooth while he is calling them to Allah?” Allah Almighty then revealed: “You have no authority whatsoever in this matter.” [Ali ʿImran: 128]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",468],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12096],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (104: 1791)."},{"num":8875,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: كَانَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَ الرَّجُلَيْنِ مِنْ قَتْلَى أُحُدٍ فِي ثَوْبٍ وَاحِدٍ ثُمَّ يَقُولُ: أَيُّهُمْ أَكْثَرُ أَخْذًا لِلْقُرْآنِ؟ فَإِذَا أُشِيرَ لَهُ إِلَى أَحَدٍ قَدَّمَهُ فِي اللَّحْدِ وَقَالَ: أَنَا شَهِيدٌ عَلَى هَؤُلاَءِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، وَأَمَرَ بِدَفْنِهِمْ بِدِمَائِهِمْ، وَلَمْ يصلّ عَلَيْهِمْ، وَلَمْ يُغَسَّلُوا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4079) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا الليث، عن ابن شهاب، عن عبد الرحمن بن كعب بن مالك، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب كيف دفن من قتل في غزوة أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4079).","chapter_en":"How Those Killed in the Battle of Uhud Were Buried","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah reported: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place two of those killed at Uhud together in a single cloth. He would then ask, ‘Which of them had learned more of the Qur’an?’ When one of them was pointed out, he would place him first in the grave. “He said, ‘I shall be a witness over these people on the Day of Resurrection.’ He ordered that they be buried with their blood upon them. They were neither washed nor was the funeral prayer performed over them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",469],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4079)."},{"num":8876,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُبَيْدِ بْنِ رِفَاعَةَ الزرفي، عن أَبِيهِ قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ، وَانْكَفَأَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : اسْتَوُوا حَتَّى أُثْنِيَ عَلَى رَبِّي عَزَّ وَجَلَّ فَصَارُوا خَلْفَهُ صُفُوفًا فَقَالَ: اللهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ كُلُّهُ، اللهُمَّ لَا قَابِضَ لِمَا بَسَطْتَ، وَلَا مُقَرِّبَ لِمَا بَاعَدْتَ، وَلَا مُبَاعِدَ لِمَا قَرَّبْتَ، وَلَا مُعْطِيَ لِمَا مَنَعْتَ، وَلَا مَانِعَ لِمَا أَعْطَيْتَ. اللهُمَّ ابْسُطْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ بَرَكَاتِكَ وَرَحْمَتِكَ وَفَضْلِكَ وَرِزْقِكَ، اللهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ النَّعِيمَ الْمُقِيمَ الَّذِي لَا يَحُولُ وَلَا يَزُولُ، اللهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ النَّعِيمَ يَوْمَ الْعَيْلَةِ، وَالْأَمْنَ يَوْمَ الحرب، اللهُمَّ عائذا بِكَ مِنْ سُوءِ مَا أَعْطَيْتَنَا، وَشَرِّ مَا مَنَعْتَ مِنَّا. اللهُمَّ حَبِّبْ إِلَيْنَا الْإِيمَانَ وَزَيِّنْهُ فِي قُلُوبِنَا، وَكَرِّهْ إِلَيْنَا الْكُفْرَ وَالْفُسُوقَ وَالْعِصْيَانَ، وَاجْعَلْنَا مِنَ الرَّاشِدِينَ، اللهُمَّ تَوَفَّنَا مُسْلِمِينَ، وَأَحْيِنَا مُسْلِمِينَ، وَأَلْحِقْنَا بِالصَّالِحِينَ، غَيْرَ خَزَايَا وَلَا مَفْتُونِينَ، اللهُمَّ قَاتِلِ الْكَفَرَةَ الَّذِينَ يصدون عَنْ سَبِيلِكَ ويكذبون رُسُلَكَ، وَاجْعَلْ عَلَيْهِمْ رِجْزَكَ وَعَذَابَكَ، اللهُمَّ قَاتِلِ الْكَفَرَةَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ، إِلَهَ الْحَقِّ قَالَ علي: وسمعته من مُحَمَّدٍ بن بِشْرٍ، وأسنده، وَلَا أجيء بِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (15492) والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (699) والبزار – كشف الأستار (1800) والحاكم (4308) والطبراني في الدعاء (1075) كلهم من طرق عن عبد الواحد بن أيمن، عن عبيد بن رفاعة الزرفي، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ بعد دفن الشهداء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (15492), al-Bukhārī in al-Adab al-Mufrad (699), and al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1800).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication After the Burial of the Martyrs","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbayd ibn Rifaʿah al-Zuraqi reported from his father: “When the day of Uhud came and the polytheists withdrew, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Stand in orderly rows so that I may praise my Lord Almighty.’ “They formed rows behind him, and he said: “ʿO Allah, all praise belongs entirely to You. O Allah, none can withhold what You have expanded, none can bring near what You have placed far away, none can distance what You have brought near, none can give what You have withheld, and none can withhold what You have given. “ʿO Allah, spread over us Your blessings, mercy, bounty, and provision. O Allah, I ask You for lasting bliss that neither changes nor disappears. O Allah, I ask You for bliss on the day of destitution and security on the day of war. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have given us and the evil of what You have withheld from us. “ʿO Allah, make faith beloved to us and beautify it within our hearts. Make disbelief, wickedness, and disobedience hateful to us, and make us among those who are rightly guided. “ʿO Allah, cause us to die as Muslims, keep us alive as Muslims, and join us with the righteous, neither disgraced nor subjected to trials. “‘O Allah, fight the disbelievers who turn others away from Your path and deny Your messengers, and place upon them Your punishment and torment. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who were given the Scripture, O Allah of truth.’” ʿAli said: “I also heard it from Muhammad ibn Bishr, who narrated it with a connected chain, but I will not relate it here.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",470],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (15492)، والبخاري في «الأدب المفرد» (699)، والبزار في «كشف الأستار» (1800)."},{"num":8877,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا ﴿الَّذِينَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَصَابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا مِنْهُمْ وَاتَّقَوْا أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ﴾ [سورة آل عمران: 172]} قَالَتْ لِعُرْوَةَ يَا ابْنَ أُخْتِي كَانَ أَبُوكَ مِنْهُمُ: الزُّبَيْرُ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ، لَمَّا أَصَابَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَا أَصَابَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، وَانْصَرَفَ عَنْهُ الْمُشْرِكُونَ خَافَ أَنْ يَرْجِعُوا قَالَ: مَنْ يَذْهَبُ فِي إِثْرِهِمْ. فَانْتَدَبَ مِنْهُمْ سَبْعُونَ رَجُلاً، قَالَ: كَانَ فِيهِمْ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَالزُّبَيْرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4077) عن محمد (وهو ابن سلام) ثنا أبو معاوية، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب خروج النبي ﷺ لمتابعة العدو حتى لا يقصدوا المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4077).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Setting Out in Pursuit of the Enemy to Prevent Them from Attacking Madinah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جُموع ما جاء في غزوة أحد","group_en":"Collection of What Came Concerning the Battle of Uḥud","part_no":48,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Regarding the verse: “Those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after suffering injury—for those among them who did good and remained mindful of Allah there is a magnificent reward.” [Ali ʿImran: 172] ʿA’ishah said to ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr: “Son of my sister, both of your fathers were among them: al-Zubayr and Abū Bakr. After what befell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud and the polytheists withdrew from him, he feared that they might return. He therefore asked, ‘Who will pursue them?’ Seventy men volunteered, among whom were Abū Bakr and al-Zubayr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8873],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4077)."},{"num":8878,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: بَعَثَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَرِيَّةً عَيْنًا، وَأَمَّرَ عَلَيْهِمْ عَاصِمَ بْنَ ثَابِتٍ، ـ وَهْوَ جَدُّ عَاصِمِ بْنِ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ، ـ فَانْطَلَقُوا حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ بَيْنَ عُسْفَانَ وَمَكَّةَ، ذُكِرُوا لَحِيٍّ مِنْ هُذَيْلٍ، يُقَالُ لَهُمْ: بَنُو لَحْيَانَ، فَتَبِعُوهُمْ بِقَرِيبٍ مِنْ مِائَةِ رَامٍ، فَاقْتَصُّوا آثَارَهُمْ حَتَّى أَتَوْا مَنْزِلاً نَزَلُوهُ، فَوَجَدُوا فِيهِ نَوَى تَمْرٍ تَزَوَّدُوهُ مِنَ الْمَدِينَةِ، فَقَالُوا: هَذَا تَمْرُ يَثْرِبَ. فَتَبِعُوا آثَارَهُمْ حَتَّى لَحِقُوهُمْ، فَلَمَّا انْتَهَى عَاصِمٌ وَأَصْحَابُهُ لَجَئُوا إِلَى فَدْفَدٍ، وَجَاءَ الْقَوْمُ فَأَحَاطُوا بِهِمْ، فَقَالُوا: لَكُمُ الْعَهْدُ وَالْمِيثَاقُ إِنْ نَزَلْتُمْ إِلَيْنَا أَنْ لاَ نَقْتُلَ مِنْكُمْ رَجُلاً. فَقَالَ عَاصِمٌ: أَمَّا أَنَا فَلاَ أَنْزِلُ فِي ذِمَّةِ كَافِرٍ، اللَّهُمَّ أَخْبِرْ عَنَّا نَبِيَّكَ. فَقَاتَلُوهُمْ حَتَّى قَتَلُوا عَاصِمًا فِي سَبْعَةِ نَفَرٍ بِالنَّبْلِ، وَبَقِيَ خُبَيْبٌ، وَزَيْدٌ وَرَجُلٌ آخَرُ، فَأَعْطَوْهُمُ الْعَهْدَ وَالْمِيثَاقَ، فَلَمَّا أَعْطَوْهُمُ الْعَهْدَ وَالْمِيثَاقَ نَزَلُوا إِلَيْهِمْ، فَلَمَّا اسْتَمْكَنُوا مِنْهُمْ حَلُّوا أَوْتَارَ قِسِيِّهِمْ فَرَبَطُوهُمْ بِهَا. فَقَالَ الرَّجُلُ الثَّالِثُ الَّذِي مَعَهُمَا: هَذَا أَوَّلُ الْغَدْرِ. فَأَبَى أَنْ يَصْحَبَهُمْ فَجَرَّرُوهُ وَعَالَجُوهُ عَلَى أَنْ يَصْحَبَهُمْ، فَلَمْ يَفْعَلْ، فَقَتَلُوهُ، وَانْطَلَقُوا بِخُبَيْبٍ وَزَيْدٍ حَتَّى بَاعُوهُمَا بِمَكَّةَ، فَاشْتَرَى خُبَيْبًا بَنُو الْحَارِثِ بْنِ عَامِرِ بْنِ نَوْفَلٍ، وَكَانَ خُبَيْبٌ هُوَ قَتَلَ الْحَارِثَ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ، فَمَكَثَ عِنْدَهُمْ أَسِيرًا، حَتَّى إِذَا أَجْمَعُوا قَتْلَهُ اسْتَعَارَ مُوسَى مِنْ بَعْضِ بَنَاتِ الْحَارِثِ أَسْتَحِدَّ بِهَا فَأَعَارَتْهُ، قَالَتْ: فَغَفَلْتُ عَنْ صَبِيٍّ لِي، فَدَرَجَ إِلَيْهِ حَتَّى أَتَاهُ، فَوَضَعَهُ عَلَى فَخِذِهِ، فَلَمَّا رَأَيْتُهُ فَزِعْتُ فَزْعَةً عَرَفَ ذَاكَ مِنِّي، وَفِي يَدِهِ الْمُوسَى، فَقَالَ: أَتَخْشَيْنَ أَنْ أَقْتُلَهُ؟ مَا كُنْتُ لأَفْعَلَ ذَاكِ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ. وَكَانَتْ تَقُولُ: مَا رَأَيْتُ أَسِيرًا قَطُّ خَيْرًا مِنْ خُبَيْبٍ، لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُهُ يَأْكُلُ مِنْ قِطْفِ عِنَبٍ، وَمَا بِمَكَّةَ يَوْمَئِذٍ ثَمَرَةٌ، وَإِنَّهُ لَمُوثَقٌ فِي الْحَدِيدِ، وَمَا كَانَ إِلاَّ رِزْقٌ رَزَقَهُ اللَّهُ، فَخَرَجُوا بِهِ مِنَ الْحَرَمِ، لِيَقْتُلُوهُ، فَقَالَ: دَعُونِي أُصَلِّي رَكْعَتَيْنِ. ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ إِلَيْهِمْ فَقَالَ: لَوْلاَ أَنْ تَرَوْا أَنَّ مَا بِي جَزَعٌ مِنَ الْمَوْتِ، لَزِدْتُ. فَكَانَ أَوَّلَ مَنْ سَنَّ الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ عِنْدَ الْقَتْلِ هُوَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ أَحْصِهِمْ عَدَدًا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: مَا أُبَالِي حِينَ أُقْتَلُ مُسْلِمًا عَلَى أَىِّ شِقٍّ كَانَ لِلَّهِ مَصْرَعِي وَذَلِكَ فِي ذَاتِ الإِلَهِ وَإِنْ يَشَأْ يُبَارِكْ عَلَى أَوْصَالِ شِلْوٍ مُمَزَّعِ ثُمَّ قَامَ إِلَيْهِ عُقْبَةُ بْنُ الْحَارِثِ فَقَتَلَهُ، وَبَعَثَ قُرَيْشٌ إِلَى عَاصِمٍ لِيُؤْتَوْا بِشَىْءٍ مِنْ جَسَدِهِ يَعْرِفُونَهُ، وَكَانَ عَاصِمٌ قَتَلَ عَظِيمًا مِنْ عُظَمَائِهِمْ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ، فَبَعَثَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ مِثْلَ الظُّلَّةِ مِنَ الدَّبْرِ، فَحَمَتْهُ مِنْ رُسُلِهِمْ، فَلَمْ يَقْدِرُوا مِنْهُ عَلَى شَىْءٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4086) عن إبراهيم بن موسى، أخبرنا هشام بن يوسف، عن معمر، عن الزهري، عن عمرو بن أبي سفيان الثقفي، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"غزوة الرجيع في سنة ثلاث","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghazi (4086), from Ibrahim ibn Musa: Hisham ibn Yusuf informed us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhri, from ʿAmr ibn Abi Sufyan al-Thaqafi, from Abū Hurayrah, who narrated it.","chapter_en":"The Expedition of al-Rajiʿ in the Third Year","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: “The Prophet ﷺ sent a reconnaissance detachment and appointed ʿAsim ibn Thabit as its commander. He was the maternal grandfather of ʿAsim ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab. “They travelled until they reached a place between ʿUsfan and Makkah. News of them reached a clan of Hudhayl known as Banu Lihyan, who pursued them with nearly one hundred archers. They followed their tracks until they reached a campsite at which the Muslims had stopped. There they found date stones from provisions the Muslims had brought from Madinah. They said, ‘These are dates from Yathrib,’ and continued following their tracks until they caught up with them. “When ʿAsim and his companions realized that they had been overtaken, they sought refuge upon a raised piece of ground. The enemy surrounded them and said, ‘You have our solemn covenant and pledge that if you come down to us, we will not kill any one of you.’ “ʿAsim replied, ʿAs for me, I will not descend under the protection of a disbeliever. O Allah, inform Your Prophet about us.’ “They shot arrows at them until they killed ʿAsim and seven other men. Khubayb, Zayd, and one other man remained. The enemy gave them their solemn covenant and pledge, so they descended to them. Once they had gained control of them, they unstrung their bows and tied the three men with the bowstrings. “The third man said, ‘This is the first act of treachery.’ He refused to accompany them. They dragged him and tried to force him to go with them, but when he continued to refuse, they killed him. “They took Khubayb and Zayd away and sold them in Makkah. Banu al-Harith ibn ʿAmir ibn Nawfal purchased Khubayb, because Khubayb had killed al-Harith on the day of Badr. “Khubayb remained their prisoner until they unanimously decided to kill him. He borrowed a razor from one of the daughters of al-Harith so that he could remove his pubic hair, and she lent it to him. “She later said: ʿI became distracted from one of my young children, who crawled over to Khubayb. Khubayb placed him upon his thigh. When I saw him there, I became so terrified that Khubayb recognized my fear, for the razor was still in his hand. “ʿHe said, “Do you fear that I will kill him? I would never do that, Allah willing.” “‘I never saw a prisoner better than Khubayb. I once saw him eating from a bunch of grapes when there was no fruit in Makkah at that time, while he was bound in iron chains. It could only have been provision that Allah had granted him.’ “They took him outside the Sacred Precinct to kill him. He said, ‘Allow me to pray two units of prayer.’ When he finished, he returned to them and said, ‘Were it not that you might think I was prolonging the prayer out of fear of death, I would have prayed more.’ He was the first person to establish the practice of praying two units before being killed. “He then said, ‘O Allah, count them one by one.’ He recited: “I do not care, when I am killed as a Muslim, On which side, for Allah, my death may fall. “That is entirely for the sake of Allah; and if He wills, He will bless the severed limbs of a body torn apart.” “ʿUqbah ibn al-Harith then approached and killed him. “Quraysh sent men to retrieve a recognizable part of ʿAsim’s body, because ʿAsim had killed one of their great leaders on the day of Badr. Allah sent over his body a swarm of hornets resembling a protective canopy. They protected him from the men Quraysh had sent, and they were unable to take anything from his body.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال محمد بن إسحاق: حدثنا عاصم بن عمر بن قتادة قال: قدم على رسول الله ﷺ بعد أحد رهط من عضل والقارة فقالوا: يا رسول الله! إن فينا إسلامًا، فابعث معنا نفرًا من أصحابك يفقهوننا في الدين، ويقرئوننا القرآن، ويعلموننا شرائع الإسلام. فبعث رسول الله ﷺ معهم نفرًا ستة من أصحابه، وهم: مرثد بن أبي مرثد الغنوي، حليف حمزة بن عبد المطلب - قال ابن إسحاق: وهو أمير القوم - وخالد بن البكير الليثي، حليف بني عدي، وعاصم بن ثابت بن أبي الأقلح، أخو بني عمرو بن عوف، وخبيب بن عدي أخو بني جحجبى بن كلفة بن عمرو بن عوف، وزيد بن الدثنة، أخو بني بياضة بن عامر، وعبد الله بن طارق، حليف بني ظفر، رضي الله عنهم.","هكذا قال ابن إسحاق: إنهم كانوا ستة، وكذا ذكر موسى بن عقبة، وسماهم كما قال ابن إسحاق. وعند البخاري أنهم كانوا عشرة، وعنده أن أميرهم عاصم بن ثابت بن أبي الأقلح، فالله أعلم.","قال ابن إسحاق: فخرجوا مع القوم حتى إذا كانوا على الرجيع - ماء لهذيل بناحية الحجاز، من صدور الهدأة - غدروا بهم، فاستصرخوا عليهم هذيلًا، فلم يرع القوم - وهم في رحالهم - إلا الرجال بأيديهم السيوف قد غشوهم. فأخذوا أسيافهم ليقاتلوا القوم، فقالوا لهم: إنا والله ما نريد قتلكم، ولكنا نريد أن نصيب بكم شيئًا من أهل مكة، ولكن عهد الله وميثاقه أن لا نقتلكم. فأما مرثد وخالد بن البكير وعاصم بن ثابت فقالوا: والله لا نقبل من مشرك عهدًا ولا عقدًا أبدًا.","وقال عاصم بن ثابت:","ما علتي وأنا جلد نابل   والقوس فيها وتر عنابل","تزل عن صفحتها المعابل   الموت حق والحياة باطل","وكل ما حم الإله نازل   بالمرء والمرء إليه آيل","إن لم أقاتلكم فأمي هابل","وقال عاصم أيضًا:","أبو سليمان وريش المقعد   وضالة مثل الجحيم الموقد","إذا النواحي افترشت لم أرعد   ومجنأ من جلد ثور أجرد","ومؤمن بما على محمد","وقال أيضًا:","أبو سليمان ومثلي رامى   وكان قومي معشرًا كرامًا","قال: ثم قاتل حتى قتل، وقتل صاحباه. فلما قتل عاصم، أرادت هذيل أخذ رأسه ليبيعوه من سلافة بنت سعد بن شهيد، وكانت قد نذرت حين أصاب ابنيها يوم أحد: لئن قدرت على رأس عاصم لتشربن في قحفه الخمر. فمنعته الدبر. فلما حالت بينهم وبينه قالوا: دعوه حتى يمسي فتذهب عنه فنأخذه. فبعث الله الوادي، فاحتمل عاصمًا فذهب به. وقد كان عاصم قد أعطى الله عهدًا أن لا يمسه مشرك، ولا يمس مشركًا أبدًا تنجسًا. فكان عمر بن الخطاب يقول حين بلغه أن الدبر منعته: يحفظ الله العبد المؤمن؛ كان عاصم نذر أن لا يمسه مشرك ولا يمس مشركًا أبدًا في حياته، فمنعه الله بعد وفاته كما امتنع منه في حياته.","قال ابن إسحاق: وأما خبيب وزيد بن الدثنة وعبد الله بن طارق فلانوا ورقوا ورغبوا في الحياة، وأعطوا بأيديهم فأسروهم، ثم خرجوا بهم إلى مكة ليبيعوهم بها. حتى إذا كانوا بالظهران، انتزع عبد الله بن طارق يده من القران، ثم أخذ سيفه، واستأخر عنه القوم، فرموه بالحجارة حتى قتلوه، فقبره بالظهران. وأما خبيب بن عدي وزيد بن الدثنة فقدموا بهما مكة. قال ابن هشام: فباعوهما من قريش بأسيرين من هذيل كانا بمكة.","قلت: الدبر هو ذكور النحل، وقيل: الزنابير. والقحف، بكسر القاف: أعلى الدماغ.","قال ابن إسحاق: فابتاع خبيبًا حجير بن أبي إهاب التميمي، حليف بني نوفل، لعقبة بن الحارث بن عامر بن نوفل، وكان أبو إهاب أخا الحارث بن عامر لأمه، ليقتله بأبيه. قال: وأما زيد بن الدثنة فابتاعه صفوان بن أمية ليقتله بأبيه، فبعثه مع مولى له يقال له نسطاس إلى التنعيم، وأخرجه من الحرم ليقتله. واجتمع رهط قريش، فيهم أبو سفيان بن حرب، فقال له أبو سفيان حين قدم ليقتل: أنشدك الله يا زيد، أتحب أن محمدًا عندنا الآن مكانك نضرب عنقه وأنك في أهلك؟ قال: والله ما أحب أن محمدًا الآن في مكانه الذي هو فيه تصيبه شوكة تؤذيه وأنا جالس في أهلي.","قال: يقول أبو سفيان: ما رأيت من الناس أحدًا يحب أحدًا كحب أصحاب محمد محمدًا. قال: ثم قتله نسطاس.","قال: وأما خبيب بن عدي فحدثني عبد الله بن أبي نجيح أنه حدث عن ماوية مولاة حجير بن أبي إهاب، وكانت قد أسلمت، قالت: كان خبيب عندي، حبس في بيتي، فلقد اطلعت عليه يومًا وإن في يده لقطفًا من عنب مثل رأس الرجل يأكل منه، وما أعلم في أرض الله عنبًا يؤكل.","قال ابن إسحاق: وحدثني عاصم بن عمر بن قتادة وعبد الله بن أبي نجيح أنهما قالا: قالت: قال لي حين حضره القتل: ابعثي إلي بحديدة أتطهر بها للقتل. قالت: فأعطيت غلامًا من الحي الموسى، فقلت له: ادخل بها على هذا الرجل البيت. قالت: فوالله إن هو إلا أن ولى الغلام بها إليه، فقلت: ماذا صنعت؟ أصاب والله الرجل ثأره بقتل هذا الغلام، فيكون رجلًا برجل. فلما ناوله الحديدة أخذها من يده، ثم قال: لعمرك ما خافت أمك غدري حين بعثتك بهذه الحديدة إلي. ثم خلى سبيله.","قال ابن إسحاق: قال عاصم: ثم خرجوا بخبيب حتى جاؤوا به إلى التنعيم ليصلبوه. قال لهم: إن رأيتم أن تدعوني حتى أركع ركعتين فافعلوا. قالوا: دونك فاركع. فركع ركعتين أتمهما وأحسنهما، ثم أقبل على القوم فقال: أما والله لولا أن تظنوا أني إنما طولت جزعًا من القتل، لاستكثرت من الصلاة. قال: فكان خبيب أول من سن هاتين الركعتين عند القتل للمسلمين.","قال: ثم رفعوه على خشبة، فلما أوثقوه قال: اللهم إنا قد بلغنا رسالة رسولك، فبلغه الغداة ما يصنع بنا. ثم قال: اللهم أحصهم عددًا، واقتلهم بددًا، ولا تغادر منهم أحدًا. ثم قتلوه. وكان معاوية بن أبي سفيان يقول: حضرته يومئذ فيمن حضره مع أبي سفيان، فلقد رأيته يلقيني إلى الأرض فرقًا من دعوة خبيب، وكانوا يقولون: إن الرجل إذا دعي عليه فاضطجع لجنبه زلت عنه.","سيرة ابن هشام (٢/١٦٩-١٧٣)، ونقل عنه الحافظ ابن كثير في البداية والنهاية (٥/٤٩٨-٥٠٧) وأطال في ذكره. إلا أن محمد بن إسحاق - وإن كان إمامًا في المغازي، كما قال الشافعي: «من أراد المغازي فهو عيال على محمد بن إسحاق» - لم يسند جميع ما ذكره، كعادته في كتابه المغازي عمومًا؛ ولذا قد يقع خلاف بينه وبين من أسنده. وإليكم ما أسنده الإمام البخاري ومسلم في صحيحيهما من أخبار غزوة الرجيع."],"en":["Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to us that, after Uhud, a group from Adal and al-Qarah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, there are people among us who have accepted Islam. Send with us some of your Companions to instruct us in the religion, recite the Qur’an to us, and teach us the laws of Islam.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ therefore sent six of his Companions with them: Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, an ally of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib — Ibn Ishaq said that he was the commander of the group — Khalid ibn al-Bukayr al-Laythi, an ally of Banu Adi; Asim ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Aqlah, of Banu Amr ibn Awf; Khubayb ibn Adi, of Banu Jahjaba ibn Kulfa ibn Amr ibn Awf; Zayd ibn al-Dathinnah, of Banu Bayadah ibn Amir; and Abdullah ibn Tariq, an ally of Banu Zafar, may Allah be pleased with them.","Ibn Ishaq stated that they were six, and Musa ibn Uqbah likewise mentioned six and named them as Ibn Ishaq did. In al-Bukhārī, however, they were ten, and there Asim ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Aqlah was their commander. Allah knows best.","Ibn Ishaq said: They went out with the people until they reached al-Raji, a watering place belonging to Hudhayl in the Hijaz, near the upper reaches of al-Hadah. There the people betrayed them and called Hudhayl against them. While the Companions were still with their baggage, they suddenly found armed men surrounding them with swords in hand. They drew their swords to fight. The others said: “By Allah, we do not intend to kill you. We only want to obtain something for you from the people of Makkah. You have Allah’s covenant and pledge that we will not kill you.” Marthad, Khalid ibn al-Bukayr, and Asim ibn Thabit said: “By Allah, we will never accept any covenant or pact from a polytheist.”","Asim ibn Thabit then recited:","“What ailment have I, when I am a strong archer,","And the bow carries a taut, resonant string?","The broad-headed arrows glide from its face;","Death is true, while worldly life is fleeting.","Whatever Allah has decreed must descend upon a man,","And every man is returning to Him.","If I do not fight you, may my mother be bereaved of me.”","Asim also recited verses describing himself as Abū Sulayman, an archer equipped with feathered arrows, a blazing bow, and a shield of bull-hide, declaring that when battle spread on every side he did not tremble and that he believed in what had been revealed to Muhammad ﷺ.","He also said:","“I am Abū Sulayman, and one such as I is an archer;","My people have always been a noble people.”","He fought until he was killed, and his two companions were also killed. After Asim was killed, Hudhayl wanted to take his head and sell it to Sulafah bint Sad ibn Shahid. When Asim had killed her two sons at Uhud, she had vowed that if she ever obtained his head she would drink wine from his skull. A swarm of hornets prevented them from reaching his body. They said: “Leave him until evening, when the swarm departs, then we will take him.” Allah then sent a flood through the valley which carried Asim away. During his lifetime Asim had pledged to Allah that no polytheist would ever touch him and that he would never touch a polytheist out of ritual aversion. When Umar ibn al-Khattab heard that the hornets had protected him, he said: “Allah protects the believing servant. Asim had vowed that no polytheist would touch him and that he would never touch a polytheist during his life, so Allah protected him after his death just as he had protected himself during his life.”","Ibn Ishaq said: As for Khubayb, Zayd ibn al-Dathinnah, and Abdullah ibn Tariq, they yielded, softened, and desired to live, so they surrendered and were taken prisoner. Their captors set out with them toward Makkah to sell them there. When they reached al-Zahran, Abdullah ibn Tariq pulled his hand free from the binding, seized his sword, and held the men off. They stoned him until they killed him, and his grave is at al-Zahran. Khubayb ibn Adi and Zayd ibn al-Dathinnah were taken on to Makkah. Ibn Hisham said that they were sold to Quraysh in exchange for two prisoners from Hudhayl who were then in Makkah.","I say: al-dabr refers to male bees, and it is also said to mean hornets. Al-qihf, with a kasrah on the qaf, means the upper part of the skull.","Ibn Ishaq said: Hujayr ibn Abi Ihab al-Tamimi, an ally of Banu Nawfal, bought Khubayb for Uqbah ibn al-Harith ibn Amir ibn Nawfal so that he could kill him in retaliation for his father. As for Zayd ibn al-Dathinnah, Safwan ibn Umayyah bought him in order to kill him in retaliation for his father. He sent him with a freedman named Nistas to al-Tanim, taking him outside the Sacred Precinct to be killed. A group of Quraysh gathered there, including Abū Sufyan ibn Harb. When Zayd was brought forward to be killed, Abū Sufyan said: “I ask you by Allah, O Zayd: would you like Muhammad to be here in your place now so that we could strike off his neck while you were sitting safely with your family?” Zayd replied: “By Allah, I would not even like Muhammad ﷺ, where he is now, to be pricked by a thorn that harms him while I sit with my family.”","Abū Sufyan said: “I have never seen any people love another person as the Companions of Muhammad love Muhammad ﷺ.” Then Nistas killed Zayd.","As for Khubayb ibn Adi, Ibn Ishaq said that Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated from Mawiyyah, the freedwoman of Hujayr ibn Abi Ihab, who had embraced Islam. She said: “Khubayb was held in my house. One day I looked in and saw in his hand a bunch of grapes as large as a man’s head, from which he was eating, though I knew of no grapes anywhere in the land at that time.”","Ibn Ishaq said: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah and Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated that she said: “When the time for his execution approached, Khubayb said to me: ‘Send me a blade with which I may prepare myself for death.’ I gave a boy from the household a razor and told him to take it into the house to Khubayb. By Allah, as soon as the boy went toward him with it, I said to myself: ‘What have I done? By Allah, this man can now take his revenge by killing this boy — one man for one man.’ When the boy handed him the blade, Khubayb took it and said: ‘By your life, your mother did not fear treachery from me when she sent you to me with this blade.’ Then he let the boy go.”","Ibn Ishaq said: Asim related that they took Khubayb out to al-Tanim to crucify him. He said to them: “If you will allow me to pray two units first, do so.” They said: “Go ahead and pray.” He prayed two complete and beautiful units, then turned to the people and said: “By Allah, were it not that you would think I prolonged them out of fear of death, I would have prayed more.” Khubayb was therefore the first to establish for Muslims the practice of praying two units before execution.","They then raised him upon a wooden structure. When they had secured him, he said: “O Allah, we have conveyed the message of Your Messenger, so inform him tomorrow morning of what is being done to us.” Then he said: “O Allah, count them one by one, kill them scattered, and leave none of them.” Then they killed him. Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan later said that he had been present that day with Abū Sufyan, and that his father threw him to the ground out of fear of Khubayb’s supplication, because they used to say that if a person against whom a supplication had been made lay down on his side, the supplication would pass him by.","See Sirat Ibn Hisham (2/169–173). Al-Hafiz Ibn Kathir transmitted this account in al-Bidayah wa al-Nihayah (5/498–507) and discussed it at length. Muhammad ibn Ishaq, although an imam in the maghazi — as al-Shafii said, “Whoever wants the maghazi is dependent upon Muhammad ibn Ishaq” — did not provide connected chains for everything he mentioned, as was generally his practice in his Maghazi. Consequently, his account may differ from reports that are transmitted with connected chains. What follows is what Imams al-Bukhārī and Muslim transmitted with chains in their two Sahih collections concerning the expedition of al-Raji."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",473],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4086)."},{"num":8879,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن أُنَيْسٍ عَنِ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: دَعَانِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ قَدْ بَلَغَنِي أَنَّ خَالِدَ بْنَ سُفْيَانَ بْنِ نُبَيْحٍ الْهُذَلِيَّ، يَجْمَعُ لِي النَّاسَ لِيَغْزُوَنِي، وَهُوَ بِعُرَنَةَ، فَأْتِهِ فَاقْتُلْهُ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، انْعَتْهُ لِي حَتَّى أَعْرِفَهُ، قَالَ: إِذَا رَأَيْتَهُ وَجَدْتَ لَهُ إِقْشَعْرِيَرَةً قَالَ: فَخَرَجْتُ مُتَوَشِّحًا بِسَيْفِي حَتَّى وَقَعْتُ عَلَيْهِ، وَهُوَ بِعُرَنَةَ مَعَ ظُعُنٍ يَرْتَادُ لَهُنَّ مَنْزِلًا، وَحِينَ كَانَ وَقْتُ الْعَصْرِ، فَلَمَّا رَأَيْتُهُ وَجَدْتُ مَا وَصَفَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الْإِقْشَعْرِيرَةِ، فَأَقْبَلْتُ نَحْوَهُ، وَخَشِيتُ أَنْ يَكُونَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَهُ مُحَاوَلَةٌ تَشْغَلُنِي عَنِ الصَّلَاةِ، فَصَلَّيْتُ وَأَنَا أَمْشِي نَحْوَهُ أُومِئُ بِرَأْسِي الرُّكُوعَ، وَالسُّجُودَ، فَلَمَّا انْتَهَيْتُ إِلَيْهِ، قَالَ: مَنِ الرَّجُلُ؟ قُلْتُ: رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْعَرَبِ سَمِعَ بِكَ، وَبِجَمْعِكَ لِهَذَا الرَّجُلِ، فَجَاءَكَ لِهَذَا، قَالَ: أَجَلْ أَنَا فِي ذَلِكَ، قَالَ: فَمَشَيْتُ مَعَهُ شَيْئًا، حَتَّى إِذَا أَمْكَنَنِي حَمَلْتُ عَلَيْهِ السَّيْفَ حَتَّى قَتَلْتُهُ، ثُمَّ خَرَجْتُ، وَتَرَكْتُ ظَعَائِنَهُ مُكِبَّاتٍ عَلَيْهِ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَرَآنِي، فَقَالَ: أَفْلَحَ الْوَجْهُ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: قَتَلْتُهُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ قَالَ: ثُمَّ قَامَ مَعِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَدَخَلَ بِي بَيْتَهُ، فَأَعْطَانِي عَصًا، فَقَالَ: أَمْسِكْ هَذِهِ عِنْدَكَ، يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ أُنَيْسٍ قَالَ: فَخَرَجْتُ بِهَا عَلَى النَّاسِ، فَقَالُوا: مَا هَذِهِ الْعَصَا؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: أَعْطَانِيهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَمَرَنِي أَنْ أَمْسِكَهَا، قَالُوا: أَوَلَا تَرْجِعُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَتَسْأَلَهُ عَنْ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالَ: فَرَجَعْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لِمَ أَعْطَيْتَنِي هَذِهِ الْعَصَا؟ قَالَ: آيَةٌ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَكَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، إِنَّ أَقَلَّ النَّاسِ الْمُتَخَصِّرُونَ يَوْمَئِذٍ قَالَ:، فَقَرَنَهَا عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بِسَيْفِهِ، فَلَمْ تَزَلْ مَعَهُ حَتَّى إِذَا مَاتَ أَمَرَ بِهَا فَصُبَّتْ مَعَهُ فِي كَفَنِهِ، ثُمَّ دُفِنَا جَمِيعًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (16047)، وأبو يعلى (905)، وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (983)، وابن حبان (7160) كلهم من طريق يعقوب بن إبراهيم بن سعد، عن أبيه، عن ابن إسحاق قال: حدثني محمد بن جعفر بن الزبير، عن ابن عبد الله بن أنيس، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"سرية عبد الله بن أنيس إلى خالد بن سفيان بعُرَنَة في المحرم سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (16047) and Abū Yaʿlā (905); authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (983) and Ibn Ḥibbān (7160).","chapter_en":"The Expedition of ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays Against Khālid ibn Sufyān at ʿUranah in Muḥarram, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned me and said: “I have been informed that Khālid ibn Sufyān ibn Nubayḥ al-Hudhalī is gathering people to attack me. He is at ʿUranah, so go to him and kill him.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me so that I may recognize him.” He said: “When you see him, you will experience a shudder.” He said: I set out with my sword strapped across me until I came upon him at ʿUranah, accompanied by women traveling in litters, while he was searching for a place for them to camp. It was then the time of the afternoon prayer. When I saw him, I experienced the shudder that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had described. I advanced toward him, fearing that an encounter between us might distract me from the prayer, so I prayed while walking toward him, indicating the bowing and prostration by motions of my head. When I reached him, he asked, “Who are you?” I replied, “A man of the Arabs who heard about you and the forces you are gathering against this man, and so has come to you for that purpose.” He said, “Yes, I am engaged in that.” I walked with him for a while. When I gained the opportunity, I attacked him with my sword until I killed him. I then departed, leaving his women bent over him. When I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he saw me, he said: “The face has prospered.” I said, “I killed him, O Messenger of Allah.” He replied: “You have spoken the truth.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then rose with me, took me into his house, and gave me a staff, saying: “Keep this with you, O ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays.” I went out among the people carrying it, and they asked, “What is this staff?” I replied, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave it to me and instructed me to keep it.” They said, “Why do you not return to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him about it?” I returned and said, “O Messenger of Allah, why did you give me this staff?” He replied: “It will be a sign between you and me on the Day of Resurrection, for few people on that day will be carrying staffs.” ʿAbdullāh therefore fastened it alongside his sword, and it remained with him. When he died, he instructed that it be placed with him inside his shroud, and the two were buried together."]},"intro":{"ar":["ثم سرية عبد الله بن أنيس إلى سفيان بن خالد بن نبيح الهذلي بعُرَنَة. خرج من المدينة يوم الاثنين لخمس خلون من المحرم، على رأس خمسة وثلاثين شهرًا من مهاجر رسول الله ﷺ. وذلك أنه بلغ رسول الله ﷺ أن سفيان بن خالد الهذلي، ثم اللحياني، وكان ينزل عُرَنَة وما والاها في ناس من قومه وغيرهم، قد جمع الجموع لرسول الله ﷺ. فبعث رسول الله ﷺ عبد الله بن أنيس ليقتله.","فقال: صفه لي يا رسول الله. قال: «إذا رأيته هبته، وفرقت منه، وذكرت الشيطان». قال: وكنت لا أهاب الرجال، واستأذنت رسول الله ﷺ أن أقول، فأذن لي. فأخذت سيفي، وخرجت أعتزي إلى خزاعة، حتى إذا كنت ببطن عُرَنَة لقيته يمشي ووراءه الأحابيش ومن ضوى إليه، فعرفته بنعت رسول الله ﷺ وهبته، فرأيتني أقطر، فقلت: صدق الله ورسوله.","فقال: من الرجل؟ فقلت: رجل من خزاعة، سمعت بجمعك لمحمد، فجئتك لأكون معك. قال: أجل، إني لأجمع له. فمشيت معه وحدثته، واستحلى حديثي، حتى انتهى إلى خبائه، وتفرق عنه أصحابه. حتى إذا هدأ الناس وناموا اغتررته فقتلته، وأخذت رأسه، ثم دخلت غارًا في الجبل، وضربت العنكبوت عليَّ، وجاء الطلب فلم يجدوا شيئًا، فانصرفوا راجعين.","ثم خرجت، فكنت أسير الليل وأتوارى بالنهار، حتى قدمت المدينة، فوجدت رسول الله ﷺ في المسجد. فلما رآني قال: «أفلح الوجه». قلت: أفلح وجهك يا رسول الله. فوضعت رأسه بين يديه، وأخبرته خبري، فدفع إليَّ عصًا وقال: «تخصَّر بهذه في الجنة». فكانت عنده، فلما حضرته الوفاة أوصى أهله أن يدرجوها في كفنه، ففعلوا. وكانت غيبته ثماني عشرة ليلة، وقدم السبت لسبع بقين من المحرم.","ذكره ابن سعد في الطبقات (٢/٥٠–٥٢). واختلف في اسم هذا الرجل، فقيل: خالد بن سفيان، وقيل: سفيان بن خالد، وقيل غير ذلك.","وقوله: «عُرَنَة»: اسم لوادٍ يمر بطرف عرفة."],"en":["Then came the expedition of ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays against Sufyān ibn Khālid ibn Nubayḥ al-Hudhalī, of Banū Liḥyān, at ʿUranah. He left Madinah on Monday, when five nights of Muḥarram had passed, thirty-five months after the emigration of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had learned that Sufyān ibn Khālid al-Hudhalī al-Liḥyānī, who was staying at ʿUranah and its surrounding area with some of his people and others, was gathering forces against him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ therefore sent ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays to kill him.","He said, “Describe him to me, O Messenger of Allah.” He replied: “When you see him, you will be struck with awe and fear of him, and you will be reminded of Satan.” ʿAbdullāh said: “I was not a man who feared other men. I sought the Messenger of Allah’s permission to say whatever circumstances required, and he permitted me. I took my sword and set out, presenting myself as a member of Khuzāʿah. When I reached the valley of ʿUranah, I met him walking with the Aḥābīsh and those who had joined him behind him. I recognized him from the Messenger of Allah’s description and was struck with awe. I found myself trembling, so I said, ‘Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.’”","He asked, “Who are you?” I replied, “A man of Khuzāʿah. I heard that you were assembling forces against Muhammad, so I have come to join you.” He said, “Yes, I am indeed gathering forces against him.” I walked with him and spoke to him, and he found my conversation agreeable. When he reached his tent, his companions dispersed. After the people had settled down and fallen asleep, I caught him unawares and killed him. I took his head and entered a cave in the mountain. A spider spun its web over me. The search party came but found nothing, so they turned back.","I then came out and traveled by night while concealing myself by day, until I reached Madinah and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque. When he saw me, he said: “The face has prospered.” I replied, “May your face prosper, O Messenger of Allah.” I placed the man’s head before him and told him what had happened. He handed me a staff and said: “Use this as a staff in Paradise.” It remained with him, and when death approached him, he instructed his family to place it inside his shroud, which they did. He had been absent for eighteen nights and returned on Saturday, with seven nights remaining in Muḥarram.","Ibn Saʿd mentioned it in Al-Ṭabaqāt (2/50–52). The scholars differed concerning this man’s name: he was called Khālid ibn Sufyān, Sufyān ibn Khālid, and other names.","“ʿUranah” is the name of a valley that passes along the edge of ʿArafah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",476],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (16047)، وأبو يعلى (905)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (983)، وابن حبان (7160)."},{"num":8880,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: بَعَثَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَبْعِينَ رَجُلاً لِحَاجَةٍ يُقَالُ لَهُمُ: الْقُرَّاءُ، فَعَرَضَ لَهُمْ حَيَّانِ مِنْ بَنِي سُلَيْمٍ رِعْلٌ وَذَكْوَانُ، عِنْدَ بِئْرٍ يُقَالُ لَهَا بِئْرُ مَعُونَةَ، فَقَالَ الْقَوْمُ: وَاللَّهِ مَا إِيَّاكُمْ أَرَدْنَا، إِنَّمَا نَحْنُ مُجْتَازُونَ فِي حَاجَةٍ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَتَلُوهُمْ. فَدَعَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهْرًا فِي صَلاَةِ الْغَدَاةِ، وَذَلِكَ بَدْءُ الْقُنُوتِ، وَمَا كُنَّا نَقْنُتُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4088) عن أبي معمر، حدثنا عبد الوارث، حدثنا عبد العزيز، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4088), from Abū Maʿmar, from ʿAbd al-Wārith, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from Anas.","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent seventy men on a mission. They were known as “the Reciters.” Two clans of Banū Sulaym—Riʿl and Dhakwān—intercepted them at a well known as Bi’r Maʿūnah. The men said, “By Allah, we did not come for you; we are merely passing through on a mission for the Prophet ﷺ.” Nevertheless, they killed them. The Prophet ﷺ supplicated against them for a month during the dawn prayer. That was the beginning of the qunūt supplication, as we had not previously performed it."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words “on a mission” refer to teaching, as expressly stated in the narration of Muslim (677/147). Anas ibn Mālik reported: Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Send men with us to teach us the Qur’an and the Sunnah.” He sent seventy men of the Anṣār with them who were known as “the Reciters.” Among them was my maternal uncle Ḥarām. They recited and studied the Qur’an together at night in order to learn it. During the day, they would bring water and place it in the mosque. They would also gather firewood and sell it, using the proceeds to purchase food for the people of al-Ṣuffah and the poor.","The Prophet ﷺ sent them to those people, but they intercepted and killed them before they reached their destination. The martyrs said: “O Allah, convey to our Prophet on our behalf that we have met You, that we are pleased with You and You are pleased with us.”","Anas said: A man approached Ḥarām, the maternal uncle of Anas, from behind and thrust a spear through him. Ḥarām exclaimed: “I have triumphed, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his Companions: “Your brothers have been killed. They said: ‘O Allah, convey to our Prophet on our behalf that we have met You, that we are pleased with You and You are pleased with us.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",477],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4088)."},{"num":8881,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رِعْلاً، وَذَكْوَانَ وَعُصَيَّةَ وَبَنِي لَحْيَانَ اسْتَمَدُّوا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى عَدُوٍّ، فَأَمَدَّهُمْ بِسَبْعِينَ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، كُنَّا نُسَمِّيهِمُ الْقُرَّاءَ فِي زَمَانِهِمْ، كَانُوا يَحْتَطِبُونَ بِالنَّهَارِ، وَيُصَلُّونَ بِاللَّيْلِ، حَتَّى كَانُوا بِبِئْرِ مَعُونَةَ قَتَلُوهُمْ، وَغَدَرُوا بِهِمْ، فَبَلَغَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَنَتَ شَهْرًا يَدْعُو فِي الصُّبْحِ عَلَى أَحْيَاءٍ مِنْ أَحْيَاءِ الْعَرَبِ، عَلَى رِعْلٍ وَذَكْوَانَ وَعُصَيَّةَ وَبَنِي لَحْيَانَ. قَالَ أَنَسٌ: فَقَرَأْنَا فِيهِمْ قُرْآنًا، ثُمِّ إِنَّ ذَلِكَ رُفِعَ: بَلِّغُوا عَنَّا قَوْمَنَا، أَنَّا لَقِينَا رَبَّنَا، فَرَضِيَ عَنَّا وَأَرْضَانَا. وَعَنْ قَتَادَةَ عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ حَدَّثَهُ أَنَّ نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَنَتَ شَهْرًا فِي صَلاَةِ الصُّبْحِ يَدْعُو عَلَى أَحْيَاءٍ مِنْ أَحْيَاءِ الْعَرَبِ، عَلَى رِعْلٍ وَذَكْوَانَ وَعُصَيَّةَ وَبَنِي لَحْيَانَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4090) عن عبد الأعلى بن حماد، حدثنا يزيد بن زريع، حدثنا سعيد، عن قتادة، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4090), from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād, from Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik.","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported that Riʿl, Dhakwān, ʿUṣayyah, and Banū Liḥyān asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for reinforcements against an enemy. He supported them with seventy men of the Anṣār whom we called “the Reciters” in their time. They would gather firewood by day and pray by night. When they reached Bi’r Maʿūnah, those people treacherously attacked and killed them. When the news reached the Prophet ﷺ, he performed qunūt for a month, supplicating during the dawn prayer against several Arab clans: Riʿl, Dhakwān, ʿUṣayyah, and Banū Liḥyān. Anas said: We used to recite concerning them a passage of the Qur’an that was subsequently withdrawn: “Convey to our people on our behalf that we have met our Lord; He is pleased with us and has made us pleased.” Qatādah also related from Anas ibn Mālik that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt for a month during the dawn prayer, supplicating against several Arab clans: Riʿl, Dhakwān, ʿUṣayyah, and Banū Liḥyān."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words “they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for reinforcements against an enemy” apparently indicate that they came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking military assistance against their enemy, which differs from the preceding account. The two reports may be reconciled by understanding that they asked the Prophet ﷺ for both things: instruction and then assistance. The Prophet ﷺ therefore sent the seventy Reciters for both teaching and support."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",478],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4090)."},{"num":8882,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس: أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعَثَ خَالَهُ، أَخٌ لأُمِّ سُلَيْمٍ، فِي سَبْعِينَ رَاكِبًا، وَكَانَ رَئِيسَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ عَامِرُ بْنُ الطُّفَيْلِ، خَيَّرَ بَيْنَ ثَلاَثِ خِصَالٍ: فَقَالَ: يَكُونُ لَكَ أَهْلُ السَّهْلِ، وَلِي أَهْلُ الْمَدَرِ، أَوْ أَكُونُ خَلِيفَتَكَ، أَوْ أَغْزُوكَ بِأَهْلِ غَطَفَانَ بِأَلْفٍ وَأَلْفٍ، فَطُعِنَ عَامِرٌ فِي بَيْتِ أُمِّ فُلاَنٍ، فَقَالَ: غُدَّةٌ كَغُدَّةِ الْبَكْرِ، فِي بَيْتِ امْرَأَةٍ مِنْ آلِ فُلاَنٍ، ائْتُونِي بِفَرَسِي. فَمَاتَ عَلَى ظَهْرِ فَرَسِهِ، فَانْطَلَقَ حَرَامٌ أَخُو أُمِّ سُلَيْمٍ، هُوَ {وَ} رَجُلٌ أَعْرَجُ، وَرَجُلٌ مِنْ بَنِي فُلاَنٍ، قَالَ: كُونَا قَرِيبًا حَتَّى آتِيَهُمْ، فَإِنْ آمَنُونِي كُنْتُمْ، وَإِنْ قَتَلُونِي أَتَيْتُمْ أَصْحَابَكُمْ. فَقَالَ: أَتُؤْمِنُونِي أُبَلِّغْ رِسَالَةَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. فَجَعَلَ يُحَدِّثُهُمْ، وَأَوْمَئُوا إِلَى رَجُلٍ، فَأَتَاهُ مِنْ خَلْفِهِ فَطَعَنَهُ، ـ قَالَ هَمَّامٌ أَحْسِبُهُ حَتَّى أَنْفَذَهُ ـ بِالرُّمْحِ، قَالَ: اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ، فُزْتُ وَرَبِّ الْكَعْبَةِ. فَلُحِقَ الرَّجُلُ، فَقُتِلُوا كُلُّهُمْ غَيْرَ الأَعْرَجِ، كَانَ فِي رَأْسِ جَبَلٍ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْنَا، ثُمَّ كَانَ مِنَ الْمَنْسُوخِ: إِنَّا قَدْ لَقِينَا رَبَّنَا فَرَضِيَ عَنَّا وَأَرْضَانَا. فَدَعَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْهِمْ ثَلاَثِينَ صَبَاحًا، عَلَى رِعْلٍ وَذَكْوَانَ وَبَنِي لَحْيَانَ وَعُصَيَّةَ، الَّذِينَ عَصَوُا اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4091) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، حدثنا همام، عن إسحاق بن عبد الله بن أبي طلحة قال: حدثني أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4091).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ sent his maternal uncle—the brother of Umm Sulaym—among seventy mounted men. The leader of the polytheists was ʿĀmir ibn al-Ṭufayl. He was given a choice of three options, and said: “The people of the plains will be yours and the people of the settled highlands will be mine; or I will be your successor; or I will attack you with one thousand and another thousand men of Ghaṭafān.” ʿĀmir was then afflicted by a plague-swelling in the house of a certain woman. He exclaimed: “A swelling like that of a young camel, and in the house of a woman from such-and-such a family! Bring me my horse.” He died upon the back of his horse. Ḥarām, the brother of Umm Sulaym, then went forward, together with a lame man and another man from a certain clan. He said to them, “Remain nearby while I approach them. If they grant me safety, remain where you are; but if they kill me, return to your companions.” He asked the enemy, “Will you grant me safety so that I may convey the message of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He began speaking to them, but they signaled to a man who approached him from behind and stabbed him—Hammām said, “I think”—until the spear passed through him. Ḥarām exclaimed: “Allah is the Greatest! I have triumphed, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!” The enemy then caught up with the men and killed all of them except the lame man, who was on the top of a mountain. Allah revealed concerning them a passage that was later withdrawn: “We have met our Lord; He is pleased with us and has made us pleased.” The Prophet ﷺ supplicated against them for thirty mornings—against Riʿl, Dhakwān, Banū Liḥyān, and ʿUṣayyah, who had disobeyed Allah and His Messenger ﷺ."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In the wording, “Ḥarām, the brother of Umm Sulaym—who was a lame man—and a man from such-and-such a clan went forward,” the description “lame” appears to refer to Ḥarām. This is incorrect, for the lame man was someone else. As Ibn Ḥajar states, it appears that the conjunction “and” was inadvertently omitted by the copyist and should be moved, so that the correct wording becomes: “He went forward, together with a lame man.” The lame man was Kaʿb ibn Zayd of Banū Dīnār ibn al-Najjār, while Ḥarām was Ibn Milḥān."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",479],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4091)."},{"num":8883,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ يَقُولُ: لَمَّا طُعِنَ حَرَامُ بْنُ مِلْحَانَ ـ وَكَانَ خَالَهُ ـ يَوْمَ بِئْرِ مَعُونَةَ قَالَ بِالدَّمِ هَكَذَا، فَنَضَحَهُ عَلَى وَجْهِهِ وَرَأْسِهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: فُزْتُ وَرَبِّ الْكَعْبَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4092) عن حبان، حدثنا عبد الله، أخبرني معمر، حدثني ثمامة بن عبد الله بن أنس، أنه سمع أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4092).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: When Ḥarām ibn Milḥān—who was his maternal uncle—was stabbed on the day of Bi’r Maʿūnah, he took some of his blood like this and splashed it over his face and head. He then exclaimed: “I have triumphed, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",480],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4092)."},{"num":8884,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتِ: اسْتَأْذَنَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فِي الْخُرُوجِ حِينَ اشْتَدَّ عَلَيْهِ الأَذَى، فَقَالَ لَهُ: أَقِمْ. فَقَالَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَتَطْمَعُ أَنْ يُؤْذَنَ لَكَ، فَكَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِنِّي لأَرْجُو ذَلِكَ قَالَتْ: فَانْتَظَرَهُ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَأَتَاهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ يَوْمٍ ظُهْرًا، فَنَادَاهُ فَقَالَ: أَخْرِجْ مَنْ عِنْدَكَ. فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: إِنَّمَا هُمَا ابْنَتَاىَ. فَقَالَ: أَشَعَرْتَ أَنَّهُ قَدْ أُذِنَ لِي فِي الْخُرُوجِ. فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ الصُّحْبَةُ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الصُّحْبَةُ. قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، عِنْدِي نَاقَتَانِ، قَدْ كُنْتُ أَعْدَدْتُهُمَا لِلْخُرُوجِ. فَأَعْطَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِحْدَاهُمَا وَهْىَ الْجَدْعَاءُ، فَرَكِبَا، فَانْطَلَقَا حَتَّى أَتَيَا الْغَارَ، وَهْوَ بِثَوْرٍ، فَتَوَارَيَا فِيهِ، فَكَانَ عَامِرُ بْنُ فُهَيْرَةَ غُلاَمًا لِعَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ الطُّفَيْلِ بْنِ سَخْبَرَةَ أَخُو عَائِشَةَ لأُمِّهَا، وَكَانَتْ لأَبِي بَكْرٍ مِنْحَةٌ، فَكَانَ يَرُوحُ بِهَا وَيَغْدُو عَلَيْهِمْ، وَيُصْبِحُ، فَيَدَّلِجُ إِلَيْهِمَا ثُمَّ يَسْرَحُ، فَلاَ يَفْطُنُ بِهِ أَحَدٌ مِنَ الرِّعَاءِ، فَلَمَّا خَرَجَ خَرَجَ مَعَهُمَا يُعْقِبَانِهِ حَتَّى قَدِمَا الْمَدِينَةَ، فَقُتِلَ عَامِرُ بْنُ فُهَيْرَةَ يَوْمَ بِئْرِ مَعُونَةَ. وَعَنْ أَبِي أُسَامَةَ قَالَ قَالَ هِشَامُ بْنُ عُرْوَةَ فَأَخْبَرَنِي أَبِي قَالَ لَمَّا قُتِلَ الَّذِينَ بِبِئْرِ مَعُونَةَ وَأُسِرَ عَمْرُو بْنُ أُمَيَّةَ الضَّمْرِيُّ قَالَ لَهُ عَامِرُ بْنُ الطُّفَيْلِ مَنْ هَذَا فَأَشَارَ إِلَى قَتِيلٍ، فَقَالَ لَهُ عَمْرُو بْنُ أُمَيَّةَ هَذَا عَامِرُ بْنُ فُهَيْرَةَ. فَقَالَ لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُهُ بَعْدَ مَا قُتِلَ رُفِعَ إِلَى السَّمَاءِ حَتَّى إِنِّي لأَنْظُرُ إِلَى السَّمَاءِ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَ الأَرْضِ، ثُمَّ وُضِعَ. فَأَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَبَرُهُمْ فَنَعَاهُمْ فَقَالَ إِنَّ أَصْحَابَكُمْ قَدْ أُصِيبُوا، وَإِنَّهُمْ قَدْ سَأَلُوا رَبَّهُمْ، فَقَالُوا رَبَّنَا أَخْبِرْ عَنَّا إِخْوَانَنَا بِمَا رَضِينَا عَنْكَ وَرَضِيتَ عَنَّا. فَأَخْبَرَهُمْ عَنْهُمْ. وَأُصِيبَ يَوْمَئِذٍ فِيهِمْ عُرْوَةُ بْنُ أَسْمَاءَ بْنِ الصَّلْتِ، فَسُمِّيَ عُرْوَةُ بِهِ، وَمُنْذِرُ بْنُ عَمْرٍو سُمِّيَ بِهِ مُنْذِرًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4093) عن عبيد بن إسماعيل حدثنا أبو أسامة، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4093).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: When the persecution of Abū Bakr became severe, he sought the Prophet’s ﷺ permission to depart. The Prophet ﷺ told him: “Remain.” Abū Bakr asked, “O Messenger of Allah, do you hope that permission will be granted to you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: “I do indeed hope for that.” She said: Abū Bakr therefore waited for him. One day at noon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and called out to him, saying: “Have everyone with you leave.” Abū Bakr replied, “They are only my two daughters.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you realize that I have been granted permission to depart?” Abū Bakr asked, “O Messenger of Allah, may I accompany you?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “You may accompany me.” Abū Bakr said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have two she-camels that I prepared for the journey.” He gave one of them—the she-camel called al-Jadʿāʾ—to the Prophet ﷺ. They mounted and departed until they reached the cave at Mount Thawr, where they concealed themselves. ʿĀmir ibn Fuhayrah had been an enslaved servant of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ṭufayl ibn Sakhbarah, ʿĀ’ishah’s maternal half-brother. Abū Bakr had a milch animal, which ʿĀmir would take out in the evening and bring to them in the morning. He would travel to them during the latter part of the night, then take the animal out to pasture, so that none of the shepherds noticed him. When the Prophet ﷺ and Abū Bakr departed, ʿĀmir went with them, riding behind them in turns, until they reached Madinah. ʿĀmir ibn Fuhayrah was later killed on the day of Bi’r Maʿūnah. Abū Usāmah also reported that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah said: My father informed me that when the men at Bi’r Maʿūnah were killed and ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī was taken captive, ʿĀmir ibn al-Ṭufayl pointed to one of the slain men and asked him, “Who is this?” ʿAmr ibn Umayyah replied, “This is ʿĀmir ibn Fuhayrah.” He said, “After he was killed, I saw him raised toward the sky, until I could see the sky between him and the earth; then he was set down.” The news reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he announced their deaths, saying: “Your companions have been slain. They asked their Lord, saying: ‘Our Lord, inform our brothers on our behalf that we are pleased with You and You are pleased with us.’ So He informed them concerning their brothers.” Among those killed that day was ʿUrwah ibn Asmāʾ ibn al-Ṣalt, after whom ʿUrwah was named; and also Mundhir ibn ʿAmr, after whom al-Mundhir was named."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",481],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4093)."},{"num":8885,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، قَالَ: دَعَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ قَتَلُوا ـ يَعْنِي ـ أَصْحَابَهُ بِبِئْرِ مَعُونَةَ ثَلاَثِينَ صَبَاحًا، حِينَ يَدْعُو عَلَى رِعْلٍ وَلِحْيَانَ: وَعُصَيَّةَ عَصَتِ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. قَالَ أَنَسٌ: فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى لِنَبِيِّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا أَصْحَابِ بِئْرِ مَعُونَةَ قُرْآنًا قَرَأْنَاهُ حَتَّى نُسِخَ بَعْدُ: بَلِّغُوا قَوْمَنَا فَقَدْ لَقِينَا رَبَّنَا فَرَضِيَ عَنَّا وَرَضِينَا عَنْهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4095) عن يحيى بن بكير، حدثنا مالك، عن إسحاق بن عبدالله بن أبي طلحة، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4095).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: The Prophet ﷺ supplicated for thirty mornings against those who had killed his Companions at Bi’r Maʿūnah. He would supplicate against Riʿl and Liḥyān, saying: “And ʿUṣayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.” Anas said: Allah Most High revealed to His Prophet ﷺ concerning those who were killed—the Companions of Bi’r Maʿūnah—a passage of the Qur’an that we recited until it was later abrogated: “Convey to our people that we have met our Lord; He is pleased with us and we are pleased with Him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",482],"full":1,"rep":[2841,11074],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4095)."},{"num":8886,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عاصم الأحول قَالَ: سَأَلْتُ أَنَسَ بْنَ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ الْقُنُوتِ، فِي الصَّلاَةِ؟ فَقَالَ: نَعَمْ. فَقُلْتُ: كَانَ قَبْلَ الرُّكُوعِ أَوْ بَعْدَهُ؟ قَالَ: قَبْلَهُ. قُلْتُ: فَإِنَّ فُلاَنًا أَخْبَرَنِي عَنْكَ أَنَّكَ قُلْتَ بَعْدَهُ، قَالَ: كَذَبَ، إِنَّمَا قَنَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدَ الرُّكُوعِ شَهْرًا، أَنَّهُ كَانَ بَعَثَ نَاسًا يُقَالُ لَهُمُ الْقُرَّاءُ، وَهُمْ سَبْعُونَ رَجُلاً، إِلَى نَاسٍ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، وَبَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَهْدٌ قِبَلَهُمْ، فَظَهَرَ هَؤُلاَءِ الَّذِينَ كَانَ بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَهْدٌ، فَقَنَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدَ الرُّكُوعِ شَهْرًا يَدْعُو عَلَيْهِمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4096) عن موسى بن إسماعيل حدثنا عبد الواحد، حدثنا عاصم الأحول قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4096).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal reported: I asked Anas ibn Mālik about qunūt in prayer, and he said, “Yes.” I asked, “Was it before bowing or after it?” He replied, “Before it.” I said, “But a certain person informed me that you said it was after it.” He replied, “He has lied. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt after bowing only for one month. He had sent some men known as the Reciters, numbering seventy, to a group of polytheists. Some people who had a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ betrayed them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ therefore performed qunūt after bowing for one month, supplicating against them.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-ʿAynī said: “The implied meaning is that he sent them to some polytheists who were not party to a treaty, while another group among them—the counterparts of those to whom the Reciters had been sent—had a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Those treaty-bound people gained the upper hand, betrayed the agreement, and killed the Reciters who had been sent to assist them against their enemy.” ʿUmdat al-Qārī (17/176)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",483],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4096)."},{"num":8887,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَنَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ شَهْرًا مُتَتَابِعًا فِي الظُّهْرِ، وَالْعَصْرِ، وَالْمَغْرِبِ، وَالْعِشَاءِ، وَالصُّبْحِ، فِي دُبُرِ كُلِّ صَلاةٍ، إِذَا قَالَ: سَمِعَ اللَّهُ لِمَنْ حَمِدَهُ، مِنَ الرَّكْعَةِ الْأَخِيرَةِ، يَدْعُو عَلَيْهِمْ، عَلَى حَيٍّ مِنْ بَنِي سُلَيْمٍ، عَلَى رِعْلٍ وَذَكْوَانَ وَعُصَيَّةَ، وَيُؤَمِّنُ مَنْ خَلْفَهُ، أَرْسَلَ إِلَيْهِمْ يَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَى الْإِسْلامِ، فَقَتَلُوهُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1443) وأحمد (2746) وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (618) والحاكم (820) كلهم من طريق ثابت بن يزيد الأحول، حدثنا هلال، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره. قال الحاكم: على شرط البخاري.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب استشهاد القراء في بئر معونة في صفر سنة أربع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1443) and Aḥmad (2746); authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (618) and al-Ḥākim (820).","chapter_en":"The Martyrdom of the Qur’an Reciters at Bi’r Maʿūnah in Ṣafar, Year Four","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt for one continuous month during the noon, afternoon, sunset, night, and dawn prayers. He did so at the end of each prayer, after saying, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” in the final unit. He supplicated against a clan of Banū Sulaym—Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayyah—while those behind him said, “Āmīn.” He had sent people to them to invite them to Islam, but they killed them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",484],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1443)، وأحمد (2746)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (618)، والحاكم (820)."},{"num":8888,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: إن الرَّجُلَ كَانَ يَجْعَلُ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ النَّخَلَاتِ مِنْ أَرْضِهِ، حَتَّى فُتِحَتْ عَلَيْهِ قُرَيْظَةُ وَالنَّضِيرُ، فَجَعَلَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ يردّ عَلَيْهِ مَا كَانَ أَعْطَاهُ.","قَالَ أَنَسٌ: إن أَهْلِي أَمَرُونِي أَنْ آتِيَ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَأَسْأَلَهُ مَا كَانَ أَهْلُهُ أَعْطَوْهُ أَوْ بَعْضَهُ، وَكَانَ نَبِيُّ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَدْ أَعْطَاهُ أُمَّ أَيْمَنَ، فَأَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَأَعْطَانِيهِنَّ، فَجَاءَتْ أُمُّ أَيْمَنَ فَجَعَلَتِ الثَّوْبَ فِي عُنُقِي، وَقَالَتْ: وَاللهِ لَا نُعْطِيكَهُنَّ وَقَدْ أَعْطَانِيهِنَّ، فَقَالَ نَبِيُّ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم: يَا أُمَّ أَيْمَنَ اتْرُكِيهِ، وَلَكِ كَذَا وَكَذَا وَتَقُولُ: كَلَّا، وَالَّذِي لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا هُوَ! فَجَعَلَ يَقُولُ: كَذَا حَتَّى أَعْطَاهَا عَشَرَةَ أَمْثَالِهِ، أَوْ قَرِيبًا مِنْ عَشَرَةِ أَمْثَالِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4120)، ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (71:1771) كلاهما من طريق معتمر بن سليمان، عن أبيه، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4120) and Muslim (1771/71).","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: A man would assign some palm trees from his land to the Prophet ﷺ. When the lands of Qurayẓah and al-Naḍīr were conquered for him, the Prophet ﷺ began returning to each man what he had given him. Anas said: My family instructed me to go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him to return what they had given him, or part of it. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ had given it to Umm Ayman, but when I went to him, he gave the palm trees back to me. Umm Ayman came, placed a cloth around my neck, and said, “By Allah, we shall not give them to you after he has given them to me!” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Umm Ayman, let him go, and you shall have such-and-such.” She replied, “No, by Him besides whom there is no deity!” He continued increasing his offer until he gave her ten times their value, or nearly ten times their value."]},"intro":{"ar":["ذكر ابن إسحاق أنه كان بعد بئر معونة وأحد، ورجوع عمرو بن أمية، وقتله ذينك الرجلين من بني عامر، ولم يشعر بعهدهما الذي معهما من رسول الله ﷺ. ولهذا قال له رسول الله ﷺ: «لقد قتلت الرجلين لأدينهما».","قال ابن إسحاق: ثم خرج رسول الله ﷺ إلى بني النضير يستعينهم في دية ذينك القتيلين من بني عامر، اللذين قتلهما عمرو بن أمية، للعهد الذي كان رسول الله ﷺ أعطاهما. وكان بين بني النضير وبين بني عامر عقد وحلف.","فلما أتاهم رسول الله ﷺ قالوا: نعم يا أبا القاسم، نعينك على ما أحببت. ثم خلا بعضهم ببعض، فقالوا: إنكم لن تجدوا الرجل على مثل حاله هذه – ورسول الله ﷺ إلى جنب جدار من بيوتهم قاعد – فمن رجل يعلو على هذا البيت، فيلقي عليه صخرة ويريحنا منه؟ فانتدب لذلك عمرو بن جحاش بن كعب، فقال: أنا لذلك. فصعد ليلقي عليه صخرة كما قال.","ورسول الله ﷺ في نفر من أصحابه، فيهم أبو بكر وعمر وعلي، فأتى رسول الله ﷺ الخبر من السماء بما أراد القوم، فقام وخرج راجعًا إلى المدينة. فلما استلبث أصحاب النبي ﷺ النبيَّ قاموا في طلبه، فلقوا رجلًا مقبلًا من المدينة فسألوه عنه، فقال: رأيته داخلًا المدينة. فأقبل أصحابه حتى انتهوا إليه، فأخبرهم الخبر بما كانت يهود أرادت من الغدر به.","وأمر رسول الله ﷺ بالتهيؤ لحربهم والسير إليهم. قال ابن هشام: فحاصرهم ست ليال، ونزل تحريم الخمر.","قال ابن إسحاق: فتحصنوا منه في الحصون، فأمر رسول الله ﷺ بقطع النخيل والتحريق فيها. فنادوه: يا محمد، قد كنت تنهى عن الفساد وتعيبه على من صنعه، فما بال قطع النخل وتحريقها؟","وكان رهط من بني عوف بن الخزرج، منهم عبد الله بن أبي بن سلول، ووديعة، ومالك بن أبي قوقل، وسويد، وداعس، قد بعثوا إلى بني النضير: أن اثبتوا وتمنعوا، فإنا لن نسلمكم؛ إن قوتلتم قاتلنا معكم، وإن أُخرجتم خرجنا معكم. فتربصوا ذلك من نصرهم فلم يفعلوا، وقذف الله في قلوبهم الرعب.","وسألوا رسول الله ﷺ أن يجليهم ويكف عن دمائهم، على أن لهم ما حملت الإبل من أموالهم إلا الحلقة – السلاح – ففعل. فاحتملوا من أموالهم ما استقلت به الإبل. فكان الرجل منهم يهدم بيته عن نجاف بابه، فيضعه على ظهر بعيره وينطلق به. فخرجوا إلى خيبر، ومنهم من سار إلى الشام.","قال ابن إسحاق: وخلوا الأموال لرسول الله ﷺ، فكانت لرسول الله ﷺ خاصة، يضعها حيث يشاء. قسمها رسول الله ﷺ على المهاجرين الأولين دون الأنصار، إلا سهل بن حنيف وأبا دجانة سماك بن خرشة؛ ذكرا فقرًا، فأعطاهما رسول الله ﷺ. وقال ابن إسحاق: ونزل في بني النضير سورة الحشر بأسرها.","سيرة ابن هشام (٢/١٩٠–١٩٢)."],"en":["Ibn Isḥāq stated that this occurred after Bi’r Maʿūnah and Uḥud, and after ʿAmr ibn Umayyah returned and killed the two men of Banū ʿĀmir, unaware that they possessed a covenant from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. For this reason, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told him: “You have killed two men whose blood money I must certainly pay.”","Ibn Isḥāq said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then went to Banū al-Naḍīr to seek their assistance in paying the blood money for the two slain men of Banū ʿĀmir whom ʿAmr ibn Umayyah had killed, because of the covenant granted to them by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Banū al-Naḍīr and Banū ʿĀmir also had a pact and alliance with one another.","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them, they said, “Yes, Abū al-Qāsim, we shall assist you with what you seek.” They then withdrew to confer privately and said, “You will never find this man in a more vulnerable position than he is now”—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting beside the wall of one of their houses—“so who will climb onto this house, cast a rock down upon him, and rid us of him?” ʿAmr ibn Jiḥāsh ibn Kaʿb volunteered, saying, “I will do it.” He climbed up to throw a rock down upon him as they had proposed.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was accompanied by several of his Companions, including Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿAlī. News came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from heaven concerning what the people intended, so he rose and returned to Madinah. When his Companions felt that he had been away for too long, they set out to look for him. They met a man coming from Madinah and asked him about the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “I saw him entering Madinah.” His Companions proceeded until they reached him, and he informed them of the treachery the Jews had intended against him.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the Muslims to prepare for war and march against them. Ibn Hishām said: He besieged them for six nights, and the prohibition of wine was revealed.","Ibn Isḥāq said: They fortified themselves against him inside their strongholds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that some of their palm trees be cut down and burned. They called out to him, “Muhammad, you used to forbid corruption and condemn those who committed it, so why are the palm trees being cut down and burned?”","A group from Banū ʿAwf ibn al-Khazraj—including ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl, Wadīʿah, Mālik ibn Abī Qawqal, Suwayd, and Dāʿis—had sent word to Banū al-Naḍīr: “Remain steadfast and defend yourselves, for we will never surrender you. If you are fought, we shall fight alongside you, and if you are expelled, we shall leave with you.” Banū al-Naḍīr waited for their promised support, but they did nothing, and Allah cast terror into their hearts.","They asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to permit them to depart and spare their lives, on condition that they could take whatever possessions their camels could carry, except weapons. He agreed. They loaded onto their camels whatever property the animals could bear. A man among them would demolish his house to remove the lintel of its door, place it upon his camel, and depart with it. They left for Khaybar, while some traveled to Syria.","Ibn Isḥāq said: They left the property to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It belonged exclusively to him, and he could dispose of it as he wished. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed it among the earliest Emigrants rather than the Anṣār, except for Sahl ibn Ḥunayf and Abū Dujānah Simāk ibn Kharashah, who mentioned their poverty, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them a share. Ibn Isḥāq also said: The whole of Sūrat al-Ḥashr was revealed concerning Banū al-Naḍīr.","The Sīrah of Ibn Hishām (2/190–192)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",486],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4120)، ومسلم (71:1771)."},{"num":8889,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ:  لَمَّا قَدِمَ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ مِنْ مَكَّةَ الْمَدِينَةَ قَدِمُوا وَلَيْسَ بِأَيْدِيهِمْ شَيْءٌ، وَكَانَ الْأَنْصَارُ أَهْلَ الْأَرْضِ وَالْعَقَارِ، فَقَاسَمَهُمُ الْأَنْصَارُ عَلَى أَنْ أَعْطَوْهُمْ أَنْصَافَ ثِمَارِ أَمْوَالِهِمْ، كُلَّ عَامٍ، وَيَكْفُونَهُمُ الْعَمَلَ وَالْمَؤُونَةَ، وَكَانَتْ أُمُّ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، وَهِْيَ تُدْعَى: أُمَّ سُلَيْمٍ، وَكَانَتْ أُمَّ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ أَبِي طَلْحَةَ، كَانَ أَخًا لِأَنَسٍ لِأُمِّهِ، وَكَانَتْ أَعْطَتْ أُمُّ أَنَسٍ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عِذَاقًا لَهَا، فَأَعْطَاهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أُمَّ أَيْمَنَ، مَوْلَاتَهُ، أُمَّ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ.","قَالَ ابْنُ شِهَابٍ: فَأَخْبَرَنِي أَنَسُ بْنُ مَالِكٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا فَرَغَ مِنْ قِتَالِ أَهْلِ خَيْبَرَ، وَانْصَرَفَ إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ، رَدَّ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ إِلَى الْأَنْصَارِ مَنَائِحَهُمُ الَّتِي كَانُوا مَنَحُوهُمْ مِنْ ثِمَارِهِمْ، قَالَ: فَرَدَّ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى أُمِّي عِذَاقَهَا، وَأَعْطَى رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أُمَّ أَيْمَنَ مَكَانَهُنَّ مِنْ حَائِطِهِ.","قَالَ ابْنُ شِهَابٍ: وَكَانَ مِنْ شَأْنِ أُمِّ أَيْمَنَ، أُمِّ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ، أَنَّهَا كَانَتْ وَصِيفَةً لِعَبْدِ اللهِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ، وَكَانَتْ مِنَ الْحَبَشَةِ، فَلَمَّا وَلَدَتْ آمِنَةُ رَسُولَ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم بَعْدَمَا تُوُفِّيَ أَبُوهُ، فَكَانَتْ أُمُّ أَيْمَنَ تَحْضُنُهُ، حَتَّى كَبِرَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَأَعْتَقَهَا، ثُمَّ أَنْكَحَهَا زَيْدَ بْنَ حَارِثَةَ، ثُمَّ تُوُفِّيَتْ بَعْدَمَا تُوُفِّيَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم بِخَمْسَةِ أَشْهُرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الهبة (2630) ومسلم في الجهاد (1771) كلاهما من طريق ابن وهب، أخبرني يونس، عن ابن شهاب، عن أنس فذكره. واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2630) and Muslim (1771). This wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: When the Emigrants arrived in Madinah from Makkah, they came possessing nothing, whereas the Anṣār owned land and palm groves. The Anṣār entered into an arrangement with them whereby they would give them half the annual produce of their properties and spare them the labor and expenses. The mother of Anas ibn Mālik, known as Umm Sulaym, was also the mother of ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, Anas’s maternal brother. She had given the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some of her palm trees, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them to his freedwoman Umm Ayman, the mother of Usāmah ibn Zayd. Ibn Shihāb said: Anas ibn Mālik informed me that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished fighting the people of Khaybar and returned to Madinah, the Emigrants returned to the Anṣār the grants of fruit that the Anṣār had provided them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ therefore returned my mother’s palm trees to her and gave Umm Ayman others in their place from his own orchard. Ibn Shihāb said: Umm Ayman, the mother of Usāmah ibn Zayd, had been an enslaved servant of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib and was originally from Abyssinia. When Āminah gave birth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after his father had died, Umm Ayman cared for him until he grew up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then emancipated her and married her to Zayd ibn Ḥārithah. She died five months after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word al-ʿaqār here means palm trees. Al-Zajjāj said: “ʿAqār is anything having firmly rooted foundations.” It has also been said that the term refers specifically to palm trees.","The word ʿidhāq is the plural of ʿadhq, meaning a palm tree.","The words “when he had finished fighting the people of Khaybar” refer generally to the Emigrants returning the grants to the Anṣār. The particular incident involving Umm Ayman, however, occurred when Banū al-Naḍīr were expelled, as previously related.","The words “the Emigrants returned to the Anṣār the grants of fruit that they had provided them” demonstrate that these were grants of produce, not transfers of ownership of the palm trees themselves. Had ownership of the trees been given as a gift, they would not have taken them back, since a gift may not be reclaimed after the recipient has taken possession of it. Permission to benefit from something, however, may be withdrawn whenever the owner wishes."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",487],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2630)، ومسلم (1771)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":8890,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: كَانَتْ أَمْوَالُ بَنِي النَّضِيرِ مِمَّا أَفَاءَ اللَّهُ عَلَى رَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِمَّا لَمْ يُوجِفِ الْمُسْلِمُونَ عَلَيْهِ بِخَيْلٍ وَلاَ رِكَابٍ، فَكَانَتْ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَاصَّةً، يُنْفِقُ عَلَى أَهْلِهِ مِنْهَا نَفَقَةَ سَنَتِهِ، ثُمَّ يَجْعَلُ مَا بَقِيَ فِي السِّلاَحِ وَالْكُرَاعِ، عُدَّةً فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4885) ومسلم في الجهاد (1757) كلاهما من حديث سفيان، عن عمرو، عن الزهري، عن مالك بن أوس بن الحدثان، عن عمر بن الخطاب قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4885) and Muslim (1757).","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb reported: The property of Banū al-Naḍīr was among what Allah bestowed upon His Messenger ﷺ as spoils for which the Muslims had spurred neither horses nor riding camels. It therefore belonged exclusively to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. From it, he would provide his family with their maintenance for a year, then place what remained into weapons and riding animals as equipment in the cause of Allah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",488],"full":1,"rep":[13516],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4885)، ومسلم (1757)."},{"num":8891,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: حَارَبَتِ النَّضِيرُ وَقُرَيْظَةُ، فَأَجْلَى بَنِي النَّضِيرِ، وَأَقَرَّ قُرَيْظَةَ وَمَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ، حَتَّى حَارَبَتْ قُرَيْظَةُ، فَقَتَلَ رِجَالَهُمْ، وَقَسَمَ نِسَاءَهُمْ، وَأَوْلاَدَهُمْ، وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ بَيْنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ إِلاَّ بَعْضَهُمْ لَحِقُوا بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَآمَنَهُمْ وَأَسْلَمُوا، وَأَجْلَى يَهُودَ الْمَدِينَةِ كُلَّهُمْ، بَنِي قَيْنُقَاعَ وَهُمْ رَهْطُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ سَلاَمٍ وَيَهُودَ بَنِي حَارِثَةَ، وَكُلَّ يَهُودِ الْمَدِينَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4028) ومسلم في الجهاد (1766) كلاهما من طريق عبد الرزاق، أخبرنا ابن جريج، عن موسى بن عقبة، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر قال:فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4028) and Muslim (1766).","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: The Prophet ﷺ fought Banū al-Naḍīr and Qurayẓah. He expelled Banū al-Naḍīr but allowed Qurayẓah to remain and showed them favor. Later, when Qurayẓah fought, he had their fighting men killed and divided their women, children, and property among the Muslims. Some of them, however, joined the Prophet ﷺ, who granted them safety, and they embraced Islam. He expelled all the Jews of Madinah: Banū Qaynuqāʿ—the clan of ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām—the Jews of Banū Ḥārithah, and all the other Jews of Madinah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",489],"full":1,"rep":[8544,8948,13056],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4028)، ومسلم (1766)."},{"num":8892,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن عمر قال: حرق النبي صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نخل بني النضير – وقطع وهي البويرة – فنزلت: ﴿مَا قَطَعْتُمْ مِنْ لِينَةٍ أَوْ تَرَكْتُمُوهَا قَائِمَةً عَلَى أُصُولِهَا فَبِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ﴾ [الحشر: ٥]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4031) ومسلم في الجهاد (1746) كلاهما من حديث الليث، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4031) and Muslim (1746).","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported: The Prophet ﷺ burned and cut down the palm trees of Banū al-Naḍīr at al-Buwayrah. Then the following was revealed: “Whatever palm trees you cut down or left standing upon their trunks was by Allah’s permission.” [Al-Ḥashr 59:5]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4031)، ومسلم (1746)."},{"num":8893,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَرَّقَ نَخْلَ بَنِي النَّضِيرِ قَالَ: وَلَهَا يَقُولُ حَسَّانُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ: وَهَانَ عَلَى سَرَاةِ بَنِي لُؤَىٍّ حَرِيقٌ بِالْبُوَيْرَةِ مُسْتَطِيرُ.","قَالَ: فَأَجَابَهُ أَبُو سُفْيَانَ بْنُ الحَارِثِ:","أَدَامَ اللَّهُ ذَلِكَ مِنْ صَنِيعٍ وَحَرَّقَ فِي نَوَاحِيهَا السَّعِيرُ.","سَتَعْلَمُ أَيُّنَا مِنْهَا بِنُزْهٍ وَتَعْلَمُ أَىَّ أَرْضَيْنَا تَضِيرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4032) عن إسحاق، أخبرنا حبّان، أخبرنا جويرية بن أسماء، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4032) and Muslim (1746/30).","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Prophet ﷺ burned the palm trees of Banū al-Naḍīr. He said: Concerning this, Ḥassān ibn Thābit composed: How lightly the chiefs of Banū Lu’ayy took the sweeping blaze at al-Buwayrah! Abū Sufyān ibn al-Ḥārith replied: May Allah perpetuate that deed of yours, and may flames consume its surrounding lands. You will come to know which of us remains far from its harm, and which of our two lands is truly injured."]},"buhuth":{"en":["He also said: Concerning this, the following was revealed:","“Whatever palm trees you cut down or left standing upon their trunks was by Allah’s permission.”","[Al-Ḥashr 59:5]","“Which of our two lands” refers to the land of Banū al-Naḍīr and the land of the Anṣār. Nuzh means distance or remoteness, while taḍīr means to harm."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4032)، ومسلم (1746/30)."},{"num":8894,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَالِكِ بن أَوْسٍ بْنِ الْحَدَثَانِ، قَالَ: بَيْنَا أَنَا جَالِسٌ فِي أَهْلِي حِينَ مَتَعَ النَّهَارُ، إِذَا رَسُولُ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ يَأْتِينِي، فَقَالَ: أَجِبْ أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، فَانْطَلَقْتُ مَعَهُ حَتَّى أَدْخُلَ عَلَى عُمَرَ، فَإِذَا هُوَ جَالِسٌ عَلَى رِمَالِ سَرِيرٍ، لَيْسَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهُ فِرَاشٌ، مُتَّكِئٌ عَلَى وِسَادَةٍ مِنْ أَدَمٍ، فَسَلَّمْتُ عَلَيْهِ ثُمَّ جَلَسْتُ، فَقَالَ: يَا مَالِ، إِنَّهُ قَدِمَ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ قَوْمِكَ أَهْلُ أَبْيَاتٍ، وَقَدْ أَمَرْتُ فِيهِمْ بِرَضْخٍ، فَاقْبِضْهُ فَاقْسِمْهُ بَيْنَهُمْ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ لَوْ أَمَرْتَ بِهِ غَيْرِي، قَالَ: اقْبِضْهُ أَيُّهَا الْمَرْءُ، فَبَيْنَا أَنَا جَالِسٌ عِنْدَهُ أَتَاهُ حَاجِبُهُ يرفأ، فَقَالَ: هَلْ لَكَ فِي عُثْمَانَ وَعَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ وَالزُّبَيْرِ وَسَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ يَسْتَأْذِنُونَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، فَأَذِنَ لَهُمْ فَدَخَلُوا فَسَلَّمُوا وَجَلَسُوا، ثُمَّ جَلَسَ يرفأ يَسِيرًا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: هَلْ لَكَ فِي عَلِيٍّ وَعَبَّاسٍ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، فَأَذِنَ لَهُمَا فَدَخَلاَ فَسَلَّمَا فَجَلَسَا، فَقَالَ عَبَّاسٌ: يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ اقْضِ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ هَذَا، وَهُمَا يَخْتَصِمَانِ فِيمَا أَفَاءَ اللَّهُ عَلَى رَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ مَالِ بَنِي النَّضِيرِ، فَقَالَ الرَّهْطُ، عُثْمَانُ وَأَصْحَابُهُ: يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ اقْضِ بَيْنَهُمَا، وَأَرِحْ أَحَدَهُمَا مِنَ الآخَرِ، قَالَ عُمَرُ: تَيْدَكُمْ، أَنْشُدُكُمْ بِاللَّهِ الَّذِي بِإِذْنِهِ تَقُومُ السَّمَاءُ وَالأَرْضُ، هَلْ تَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لاَ نُورَثُ، مَا تَرَكْنَا صَدَقَةٌ. يُرِيدُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَفْسَهُ؟ قَالَ الرَّهْطُ: قَدْ قَالَ ذَلِكَ، فَأَقْبَلَ عُمَرُ عَلَى عَلِيٍّ وَعَبَّاسٍ، فَقَالَ: أَنْشُدُكُمَا اللَّهَ، أَتَعْلَمَانِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدْ قَالَ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالاَ: قَدْ قَالَ ذَلِكَ، قَالَ عُمَرُ: فَإِنِّي أُحَدِّثُكُمْ عَنْ هَذَا الأَمْرِ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ خَصَّ رَسُولَهُ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي هَذَا الفيء بشيء لَمْ يُعْطِهِ أَحَدًا غَيْرَهُ، ثُمَّ قَرَأَ: ﴿وَمَا أَفَاءَ اللَّهُ عَلَى رَسُولِهِ مِنْهُمْ فَمَا أَوْجَفْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ خَيْلٍ وَلَا رِكَابٍ وَلَكِنَّ اللَّهَ يُسَلِّطُ رُسُلَهُ عَلَى مَنْ يَشَاءُ وَاللَّهُ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ﴾ [الحشر: ٦] فَكَانَتْ هَذِهِ خَالِصَةً لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَاللَّهِ مَا احْتَازَهَا دُونَكُمْ، وَلاَ اسْتَأْثَرَ بِهَا عَلَيْكُمْ، قَدْ أعطاكموها وَبَثَّهَا فِيكُمْ، حَتَّى بَقِيَ مِنْهَا هَذَا الْمَالُ، فَكَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُنْفِقُ عَلَى أَهْلِهِ نَفَقَةَ سَنَتِهِمْ مِنْ هَذَا الْمَالِ، ثُمَّ يَأْخُذُ مَا بَقِيَ فَيَجْعَلُهُ مَجْعَلَ مَالِ اللَّهِ، فَعَمِلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِذَلِكَ حَيَاتَهُ، أَنْشُدُكُمْ بِاللَّهِ هَلْ تَعْلَمُونَ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالُوا: نَعَمْ، ثُمَّ قَالَ لِعَلِيٍّ وَعَبَّاسٍ: أَنْشُدُكُمْ بِاللَّهِ هَلْ تَعْلَمَانِ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالَ عُمَرُ: ثُمَّ تَوَفَّى اللَّهُ نَبِيَّهُ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: أَنَا وَلِيُّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَقَبَضَهَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَعَمِلَ فِيهَا بِمَا عَمِلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ: إِنَّهُ فِيهَا لَصَادِقٌ بَارٌّ رَاشِدٌ تَابِعٌ لِلْحَقِّ، ثُمَّ تَوَفَّى اللَّهُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ، فَكُنْتُ أَنَا وَلِيَّ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَقَبَضْتُهَا سَنَتَيْنِ مِنْ إِمَارَتِي، أَعْمَلُ فِيهَا بِمَا عَمِلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَا عَمِلَ فِيهَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ: إِنِّي فِيهَا لَصَادِقٌ بَارٌّ رَاشِدٌ تَابِعٌ لِلْحَقِّ، ثُمَّ جِئْتُمَانِي تُكَلِّمَانِي، وَكَلِمَتُكُمَا وَاحِدَةٌ وَأَمْرُكُمَا وَاحِدٌ، جِئْتَنِي يَا عَبَّاسُ تَسْأَلُنِي نَصِيبَكَ مِنِ ابْنِ أَخِيكَ، وَجَاءَنِي هَذَا - يُرِيدُ عَلِيًّا - يُرِيدُ نَصِيبَ امْرَأَتِهِ مِنْ أَبِيهَا، فَقُلْتُ لَكُمَا: إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لاَ نُورَثُ، مَا تَرَكْنَا صَدَقَةٌ. فَلَمَّا بَدَا لِي أَنْ أَدْفَعَهُ إِلَيْكُمَا، قُلْتُ: إِنْ شِئْتُمَا دفعتهما إِلَيْكُمَا، عَلَى أَنَّ عَلَيْكُمَا عَهْدَ اللَّهِ وَمِيثَاقَهُ: لَتَعْمَلاَنِ فِيهَا بِمَا عَمِلَ فِيهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَبِمَا عَمِلَ فِيهَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَبِمَا عَمِلْتُ فِيهَا مُنْذُ وَلِيتُهَا، فَقُلْتُمَا: ادْفَعْهَا إِلَيْنَا، فَبِذَلِكَ دَفَعْتُهَا إِلَيْكُمَا، فَأَنْشُدُكُمْ بِاللَّهِ هَلْ دَفَعْتُهَا إِلَيْهِمَا بِذَلِكَ؟ قَالَ الرَّهْطُ: نَعَمْ، ثُمَّ أَقْبَلَ عَلَى عَلِيٍّ وَعَبَّاسٍ، فَقَالَ: أَنْشُدُكُمَا بِاللَّهِ، هَلْ دَفَعْتُهَا إِلَيْكُمَا بِذَلِكَ؟ قَالاَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَتَلْتَمِسَانِ مِنِّي قَضَاءً غَيْرَ ذَلِكَ، فَوَاللَّهِ الَّذِي بِإِذْنِهِ تَقُومُ السَّمَاءُ وَالأَرْضُ لاَ أَقْضِي فِيهَا قَضَاءً غَيْرَ ذَلِكَ، فَإِنْ عَجَزْتُمَا عَنْهَا فَادْفَعَاهَا إِلَى، فَإِنِّي أَكْفِيكُمَاهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فرض الخمس ( 3094) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (49:1756) من طريق مالك بن أنس، عن ابن شهاب الزهري، أن مالك بن أوس حدثه قال (فذكره)","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3094) and Muslim (1756/49).","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Mālik ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān reported: While I was sitting with my family after the day had advanced, a messenger from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came to me and said, “Answer the summons of the Commander of the Faithful.” I went with him and entered upon ʿUmar. He was sitting upon the woven cords of a bed with no mattress between him and it, leaning against a leather cushion. I greeted him and sat down. He said, “Mālik, some needy households from your people have come to us, and I have ordered that they be given a small allotment. Take it and distribute it among them.” I said, “Commander of the Faithful, if only you would assign that to someone else.” He replied, “Take it, man.” While I was sitting with him, his chamberlain Yarfāʾ came and asked, “Will you receive ʿUthmān, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, al-Zubayr, and Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, who are seeking permission to enter?” He replied, “Yes.” Permission was given, and they entered, greeted him, and sat down. After a short while, Yarfāʾ asked, “Will you receive ʿAlī and al-ʿAbbās?” He replied, “Yes.” He permitted them to enter, and they greeted him and sat down. Al-ʿAbbās said, “Commander of the Faithful, judge between me and this man.” They were disputing over the property of Banū al-Naḍīr that Allah had bestowed upon His Messenger ﷺ. The group—ʿUthmān and his companions—said, “Commander of the Faithful, judge between them and relieve each of the other.” ʿUmar said, “Wait! I adjure you by Allah, by whose permission heaven and earth remain standing: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘We prophets are not inherited from; whatever we leave behind is charity,’ referring to himself?” They replied, “He did say that.” ʿUmar turned to ʿAlī and al-ʿAbbās and said, “I adjure you both by Allah: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that?” They replied, “He did say that.” ʿUmar said: “I shall inform you concerning this matter. Allah granted His Messenger ﷺ an exclusive right regarding this fayʾ that He granted to no one else.” He then recited: “Whatever Allah bestowed upon His Messenger from them—you spurred neither horses nor riding camels for it. But Allah gives His messengers authority over whomever He wills, and Allah has power over all things.” [Al-Ḥashr 59:6] “This property belonged exclusively to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, he neither seized it for himself to your exclusion nor kept it from you. He gave it to you and distributed it among you until only this property remained. From it, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would provide his family with their maintenance for the year, then take what remained and place it where the wealth of Allah was to be placed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ followed this practice throughout his life. I adjure you by Allah: Do you know this?” They replied, “Yes.” He then said to ʿAlī and al-ʿAbbās, “I adjure you both by Allah: Do you know this?” They replied, “Yes.” ʿUmar continued: “Allah then took His Prophet ﷺ in death, and Abū Bakr said, ‘I am the successor entrusted with the affairs of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ Abū Bakr took possession of it and administered it as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had done. Allah knows that in doing so he was truthful, righteous, rightly guided, and a follower of the truth. “Allah then took Abū Bakr in death, and I became Abū Bakr’s successor. I administered it during the first two years of my rule according to the practice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abū Bakr. Allah knows that in doing so I was truthful, righteous, rightly guided, and a follower of the truth. “Then you both came to speak to me. Your claim was one and your matter was the same. You, al-ʿAbbās, came asking me for your share from your nephew, while this man”—meaning ʿAlī—“came seeking his wife’s share from her father. I told you both that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘We prophets are not inherited from; whatever we leave behind is charity.’ “When I decided to entrust it to you, I said, ‘If you wish, I shall entrust it to you on the condition that you accept Allah’s covenant and pledge to administer it as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ administered it, as Abū Bakr administered it, and as I have administered it since assuming responsibility for it.’ You said, ‘Entrust it to us.’ It was upon that condition that I delivered it to you.” He then said, “I adjure you by Allah: Did I entrust it to them on that condition?” The group replied, “Yes.” He turned to ʿAlī and al-ʿAbbās and said, “I adjure you both by Allah: Did I entrust it to you on that condition?” They replied, “Yes.” He said: “Do you now seek from me a judgment other than that? By Allah, by whose permission heaven and earth remain standing, I shall give no judgment concerning it other than this. If you are unable to administer it, return it to me and I shall relieve you of its responsibility.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",492],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3094)، ومسلم (49:1756)."},{"num":8895,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ رَجُلٍ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّ كُفَّارَ قُرَيْشٍ كَتَبُوا إِلَى عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ أُبَيٍّ بْنِ السَّلُولِ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ الْأَوْثَانَ مِنَ الْأَوْسِ وَالْخَزْرَجِ، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَئِذٍ بِالْمَدِينَةِ، قَبْلَ وَقْعَةِ بَدْرٍ، يَقُولُونَ: إِنَّكُمْ آوَيْتُمْ صَاحِبَنَا، وإنَّكُمْ أَكْثَرُ أَهْلِ الْمَدِينَةِ عَدَدًا، وَإِنَّا نُقْسِمُ بِاللهِ لَتَقْتُلُنَّهُ، أَوْ لَتُخْرِجُنَّهُ، أَوْ لَنَسْتَعْدِيَنَّ عَلَيْكُمُ الْعَرَبَ، ثُمَّ لَنَسِيرَنَّ إِلَيْكُمْ بِأَجْمَعِنَا، حَتَّى نَقْتُلَ مُقَاتِلَتَكُمْ، وَنَسْتَبِيحَ نِسَاءَكُمْ، فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ ذَلِكَ ابْنَ أُبَيٍّ وَمَنْ مَعَهُ مِنْ عَبَدَةِ الْأَوْثَانِ، تَرَاسَلُوا، فَاجْتَمَعُوا، وَأَرْسَلُوا، وَأَجْمَعُوا لِقِتَالِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابِهِ، فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ ذَلِكَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَقِيَهُمْ فِي جَمَاعَةٍ، فَقَالَ: لَقَدْ بَلَغَ وَعِيدُ قُرَيْشٍ مِنْكُمُ الْمَبَالِغَ، مَا كَانَتْ لِتَكِيدَكُمْ بِأَكْثَرَ مِمَّا تُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَكِيدُوا بِهِ أَنْفُسَكُمْ، فَأَنْتُمْ هَؤُلَاءِ تُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَقْتُلُوا أَبْنَاءَكُمْ وَإخْوَانَكُمْ، فَلَمَّا سَمِعُوا ذَلِكَ مِنَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَفَرَّقُوا، فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ كُفَّارَ قُرَيْشٍ، وَكَانَتْ وَقْعَةُ بَدْرٍ، فَكَتَبَتْ كُفَّارُ قُرَيْشٍ بَعْدَ وَقْعَةِ بَدْرٍ إِلَى الْيَهُودِ: إِنَّكُمْ أَهْلُ الْحَلْقَةِ وَالْحُصُونِ، وإنَّكُمْ لَتُقَاتِلُنَّ صَاحِبَنَا، أَوْ لَنَفْعَلَنَّ كَذَا وَكَذَا، وَلَا يَحُولُ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ خَدَمِ نِسَائِكُمْ شَيْءٌ، وَهُوَ الْخَلَاخِلُ، فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ كِتَابُهُمُ الْيَهُودَ أَجْمَعَتْ بَنُو النَّضِيرِ عَلَى الْغَدْرِ، فَأَرْسَلَتْ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اخْرُجْ إِلَيْنَا فِي ثَلَاثِينَ رَجُلًا مِنْ أَصْحَابِكَ، وَلْنَخْرُجْ فِي ثَلَاثِينَ حَبْرًا، حَتَّى نَلْتَقِيَ فِي مَكَانِ كَذَا، نِصْفٌ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ، فَيَسْمَعُوا مِنْكَ، فَإِنْ صَدَّقُوكَ، وَآمَنُوا بِكَ، آمَنَّا كُلُّنَا، فَخَرَجَ (*) النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي ثَلَاثِينَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ، وَخَرَجَ إِلَيْهِ ثَلَاثُونَ حَبْرًا مِنْ يَهُودَ، حَتَّى إِذَا بَرَزُوا فِي بَرَازٍ مِنَ الْأَرْضِ، قَالَ بَعْضُ الْيَهُودِ لِبَعْضٍ: كَيْفَ تَخْلُصُونَ إِلَيهِ، وَمَعَهُ ثَلَاثُونَ رَجُلًا مِنْ أَصحَابِهِ، كُلُّهُمْ يُحِبُّ أَنْ يَمُوتَ قَبْلَهُ، فَأَرْسِلُوا إِلَيْهِ: كَيْفَ تَفْهَمُ وَنَفْهَمُ؟ وَنَحْنُ سِتُّونَ رَجُلًا؟ اخْرُجْ فِي ثَلَاثَةٍ مِنْ أَصْحَابِكَ، وَيَخْرُجُ إِلَيْكَ ثَلَاثَةٌ مِنْ عُلَمَائِنَا، فَلْيَسْمَعُوا مِنْكَ، فَإِنْ آمَنُوا بِكَ آمَنَّا كُلُّنَا، وَصَدَّقْنَاكَ، فَخَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي ثَلَاثَةِ نَفَرٍ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ، وَاشْتَمَلُوا عَلَى الْخَنَاجِرِ، وَأَرَادُوا الْفَتْكَ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَرْسَلَتِ امْرَأَةٌ نَاصحَةٌ مِنْ بَنِي النَّضِيرِ إِلَى بَنِي أَخِيهَا، وَهُوَ رَجُلٌ مُسْلِمٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ، فَأَخْبَرَتْهُ خَبَرَ مَا أَرَادَتْ بَنُو النَّضِيرِ مِنَ الْغَدْرِ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَقْبَلَ أَخُوهَا سَرِيعًا، حَتَّى أَدْرَكَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فسَارَّهُ بِخَبَرِهِمْ، قَبْلَ أَنْ يَصِلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إلَيْهِمْ، فَرَجَعَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ مِنَ الْغَدِ، غَدَا عَلَيْهِمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْكَتَائِبِ، فَحَاصَرَهُمْ، وَقَالَ لَهُمْ: إِنَّكُمْ لَا تَأْمَنُونَ عِنْدِي إِلَّا بِعَهْدٍ تُعَاهِدُونِي عَلَيْهِ، فَأَبَوْا أَنْ يُعْطُوهُ عَهْدًا، فَقَاتَلَهُمْ يَوْمَهُمْ ذَلِكَ هُوَ وَالْمُسْلِمُونَ، ثُمَّ غَدَا الْغَدُ عَلَى بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ بِالْخَيْلِ وَالْكَتَائِبِ، وَتَرَكَ بَنِي النَّضِيرِ، وَدَعَاهُمْ إِلَى أَنْ يُعَاهِدُوهُ، فَعَاهَدُوهُ، فَانْصَرَفَ عَنْهُمْ، وَغَدَا إِلَى بَنِي النَّضيرِ بِالْكَتَائِبِ، فَقَاتَلَهُمْ حَتَّى نَزَلُوا عَلَى الْجَلَاءِ، وَعَلَى أَنَّ لَهُمْ مَا أَقَلَّتِ الْإِبِلُ إِلَّا الْحَلْقَةَ، وَالْحَلْقَةُ: السِّلَاحُ، فَجَاءَتْ بَنُو النَّضِيرِ، وَاحْتَمَلُوا مَا أَقَلَّتِ إِبِلٌ مِنْ أَمْتِعَتِهِمْ، وَأَبْوَابِ بُيُوتِهِمْ، وَخَشَبِهَا، فَكَانُوا يُخْرِبُونَ بُيُوتَهُمْ، فَيَهْدِمُونَهَا فَيَحْمِلُونَ مَا وَافَقَهُمْ مِنْ خَشَبِهَا، وَكَانَ جَلَاؤُهُمْ ذَلِكَ أَوَّلَ حَشْرِ النَّاسِ إِلَى الشَّامِ وَكَانَ بَنُو النَّضِيرِ مِنْ سِبْطٍ مِنْ أَسْبَاطِ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ، لَمْ يُصِبْهُمْ جَلَاءٌ مُنْذُ كَتَبَ اللهُ عَلَى بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ الْجَلَاءَ، فَلِذَلِكَ أَجْلَاهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَوْلَا مَا كَتَبَ اللهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنَ الْجَلَاءِ لَعَذَّبَهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيَا كَمَا عُذِّبَتْ بَنُو قُرَيْظَةَ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ: ﴿سَبَّحَ لِلَّهِ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ﴾ حَتَّى بَلَغَ ﴿وَاللَّهُ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ﴾ [الحشر: ١ - ٦]، وَكَانَتْ نَخْلُ بَنِي النَّضِيرِ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَاصَّةً، فَأَعْطَاهُ اللهُ إِيَّاهَا وَخَصَّهُ بِهَا، فَقَالَ: ﴿وَمَا أَفَاءَ اللَّهُ عَلَى رَسُولِهِ مِنْهُمْ فَمَا أَوْجَفْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ خَيْلٍ وَلَا رِكَابٍ﴾ [الحشر: ٦]، يَقُولُ: بِغَيْرِ قِتَالٍ، قَالَ: فَأَعْطَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَكْثَرَهَا لِلْمُهَاجِرِينَ، وَقَسَمَهَا بَيْنَهُمْ، وَقَسَمَ مِنْهَا لِرَجُلَيْنِ مِنَ الْأَنْصارِ كَانَا ذَوَيْ حَاجَةٍ، لَمْ يَقْسِمْ لِرَجُلٍ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ غَيْرَهُمَا، وَبَقِيَ مِنْهَا صدَقَةُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي يَدِ بَنِي فَاطِمَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه عبد الرزاق (9733) عن معمر، عن الزهري، عن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن كعب بن مالك، عن رجل من أصحاب النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني النضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (9733).","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū al-Naḍīr","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع في الأحداث التي بين غزوة أحد والأحزاب","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Events Between the Battle of Uhud and the Battle of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["A man among the Prophet’s Companions reported that, before the Battle of Badr, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in Madinah, the disbelievers of Quraysh wrote to ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl and the idolaters among the Aws and Khazraj, saying: “You have given refuge to our man. We swear by Allah that you must fight him or expel him; otherwise, we shall march against you in our entirety, kill your fighting men, and violate your women.” When this reached ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy and the idolaters with him, they assembled to fight the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions. When the Prophet ﷺ learned of this, he met them and said: “The threat of Quraysh has profoundly affected you. They could not harm you more than you intend to harm yourselves. Do you mean to fight your own sons and brothers?” When they heard this from the Prophet ﷺ, they dispersed. News of this reached the disbelievers of Quraysh. After the Battle of Badr, they wrote to the Jews: “You possess weapons, armor, and fortresses. You must fight our man, or we shall do such-and-such to you, and nothing will stand between us and the anklets of your women.” When news of their letter reached the Prophet ﷺ, Banū al-Naḍīr resolved upon treachery. They sent word to the Prophet ﷺ: “Come out to us with thirty of your Companions, and we shall come out with thirty of our rabbis. We shall meet at a place midway between us so that they may hear from you. If they affirm your truthfulness and believe in you, we shall all believe.” The Prophet ﷺ set out with thirty of his Companions, and thirty Jewish rabbis came out to meet him. When they reached an open tract of land, some of the Jews said to the others, “How can you get to him when thirty of his Companions are with him, every one of whom would love to die before him?” They therefore sent word to him: “How can we understand one another while we are sixty men? Come out with three of your Companions, and three of our scholars will come to you. Let them listen to you; if they believe in you, we shall all believe and affirm your truthfulness.” The Prophet ﷺ set out with three of his Companions, while three Jews came out with daggers concealed beneath their garments, intending to assassinate the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A sincere woman from Banū al-Naḍīr sent word to her brother, a Muslim man of the Anṣār, and informed him of Banū al-Naḍīr’s intended betrayal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Her brother hurried forward until he caught up with the Prophet ﷺ. He privately informed him of their plot before the Prophet ﷺ reached them, so the Prophet ﷺ returned. The following morning, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marched against them with military detachments and besieged them. He said: “By Allah, you will have no security with me unless you enter into a covenant with me.” They refused to give him a covenant, so he and the Muslims fought them that day. The following morning, he marched with cavalry and military detachments against Banū Qurayẓah, leaving Banū al-Naḍīr. He called upon Qurayẓah to enter into a covenant with him, and they did so. He then withdrew from them and marched against Banū al-Naḍīr with his detachments. He fought them until they agreed to depart, with permission to take whatever their camels could carry except weapons. Banū al-Naḍīr departed, carrying whatever their camels could bear of their belongings, the doors of their houses, and their timber. They demolished their own houses and carried away whatever timber suited them. Their expulsion was the first gathering and removal of people toward Syria. Banū al-Naḍīr belonged to one of the tribes of the Children of Israel and had not suffered expulsion since Allah decreed exile upon the Children of Israel. For this reason, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ expelled them. Had Allah not decreed exile for them, He would have punished them in this world as Banū Qurayẓah were punished. Allah then revealed: “Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies Allah, and He is the Almighty, the All-Wise,” continuing until: “And Allah has power over all things.” [Al-Ḥashr 59:1–6] The palm groves of Banū al-Naḍīr belonged exclusively to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; Allah bestowed them upon him and reserved them for him. He said: “Whatever Allah bestowed upon His Messenger from them—you spurred neither horses nor riding camels for it.” [Al-Ḥashr 59:6] That is, they were acquired without battle. The narrator said: The Prophet ﷺ gave most of it to the Emigrants and divided it among them. He also gave a share to two needy men of the Anṣār but to no other Anṣārī. The remainder became the charitable endowment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that remained in the hands of the descendants of Fāṭimah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",493],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13513],"tks":"صحيح: رواه عبد الرزاق (9733)."},{"num":8896,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَوْنٍ قَالَ:  كَتَبْتُ إِلَى نَافِعٍ أَسْأَلُهُ عَنِ الدُّعَاءِ قَبْلَ الْقِتَالِ. قَالَ: فَكَتَبَ إِلَيَّ: إِنَّمَا كَانَ ذَلِكَ فِي أَوَّلِ الْإِسْلَامِ، قَدْ أَغَارَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى بَنِي الْمُصْطَلِقِ وَهُمْ غَارُّونَ، وَأَنْعَامُهُمْ تُسْقَى عَلَى الْمَاءِ، فَقَتَلَ مُقَاتِلَتَهُمْ وَسَبَى سَبْيَهُمْ، وَأَصَابَ يَوْمَئِذٍ، (قَالَ يَحْيَى: أَحْسِبُهُ قَالَ:) جُوَيْرِيَةَ، (أَوْ قَالَ: الْبَتَّةَ) ابْنَةَ الْحَارِثِ. وَحَدَّثَنِي هَذَا الْحَدِيثَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عُمَرَ، وَكَانَ فِي ذَاكَ الْجَيْشِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في العتق (2541) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (1730) كلاهما من هذا الوجه واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب غزوة بني المصطلق، وهي غزوة المريسيع، وكانت سنة خمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2541) and Muslim (1730). This wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"The Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq, Also Known as al-Muraysīʿ, in the Fifth Year","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAwn reported: I wrote to Nāfiʿ asking him about calling people to Islam before fighting them. He wrote back: “That was only during the early period of Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided Banū al-Muṣṭaliq while they were unaware, as their livestock were being watered. He killed their fighting men and took their captives. Juwayriyyah bint al-Ḥārith was captured that day. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who was present with that army, related this to me.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال موسى بن عقبة، عن ابن شهاب: ثم قاتل رسول الله ﷺ بني المصطلق وبني لحيان في شعبان سنة خمس.","والذي ذكره البخاري عن موسى بن عقبة أنها سنة أربع، فهو سبق قلم؛ أراد أن يكتب سنة خمس فكتب سنة أربع، لأن الذي في مغازي موسى بن عقبة، من عدة طرق أخرجها الحاكم وأبو سعيد النيسابوري والبيهقي في «الدلائل» وغيرهم، سنة خمس. ذكره الحافظ ابن حجر في «الفتح» (٧/٤٣٠). وأما ابن إسحاق فذهب إلى أنها كانت سنة ست، والأول أصح.","سبب غزو رسول الله ﷺ لهم","قال ابن إسحاق: فحدثني عاصم بن عمر بن قتادة، وعبد الله بن أبي بكر، ومحمد بن يحيى بن حبان، كلٌّ قد حدثني بعض حديث بني المصطلق، قالوا: بلغ رسول الله ﷺ أن بني المصطلق يجمعون له، وقائدهم الحارث بن أبي ضرار، أبو جويرية بنت الحارث، زوج رسول الله ﷺ.","فلما سمع رسول الله ﷺ بهم خرج إليهم، حتى لقيهم على ماء لهم يقال له المريسيع، من ناحية قديد إلى الساحل. فتزاحف الناس واقتتلوا، فهزم الله بني المصطلق، وقتل من قتل منهم، ونفَّل رسول الله ﷺ أبناءهم ونساءهم وأموالهم، فأفاءهم عليه."],"en":["Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah related from Ibn Shihāb: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then fought Banū al-Muṣṭaliq and Banū Liḥyān in Shaʿbān of the fifth year.","Al-Bukhārī’s statement, related from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, that it occurred in the fourth year is a slip of the pen: he intended to write “the fifth year” but wrote “the fourth year.” The accounts in the Maghāzī of Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah—transmitted through several routes by al-Ḥākim, Abū Saʿīd al-Naysābūrī, al-Bayhaqī in Al-Dalā’il, and others—place it in the fifth year. Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar mentioned this in Fatḥ al-Bārī (7/430). Ibn Isḥāq held that it occurred in the sixth year, but the first view is more correct.","The Reason the Messenger of Allah ﷺ Campaigned Against Them","Ibn Isḥāq said: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah, ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr, and Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥibbān each related to me part of the account of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq. They said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ learned that Banū al-Muṣṭaliq were assembling forces against him under the command of al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Ḍirār, the father of Juwayriyyah bint al-Ḥārith, who later became the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard about them, he marched against them until he met them at one of their watering places called al-Muraysīʿ, near Qudayd toward the coast. The two forces advanced against each other and fought. Allah defeated Banū al-Muṣṭaliq; some of them were killed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took their children, women, and property as spoils bestowed upon him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",496],"full":1,"rep":[7854],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2541)، ومسلم (1730)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":8897,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ مُحَيْرِيزٍ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: دَخَلْتُ المَسْجِدَ فَرَأَيْتُ أَبَا سَعِيدٍ الخُدْرِيَّ فَجَلَسْتُ إِلَيْهِ فَسَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ الْعَزْلِ،، قَالَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزْوَةِ بَنِي المُصْطَلِقِ، فَأَصَبْنَا سَبْيًا مِنْ سَبْىِ الْعَرَبِ، فَاشْتَهَيْنَا النِّسَاءَ وَاشْتَدَّتْ عَلَيْنَا الْعُزْبَةُ، وَأَحْبَبْنَا الْعَزْلَ، فَأَرَدْنَا أَنْ نَعْزِلَ، وَقُلْنَا نَعْزِلُ وَرَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَ أَظْهُرِنَا قَبْلَ أَنْ نَسْأَلَهُ فَسَأَلْنَاهُ عَنْ ذَلِكَ فَقَالَ: مَا عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْ لاَ تَفْعَلُوا، مَا مِنْ نَسَمَةٍ كَائِنَةٍ إِلَى يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ إِلاَّ وَهِيَ كَائِنَةٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4138) ومسلم في النكاح (125:1438) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، أخبرنا إسماعيل بن جعفر، عن ربيعة بن أبي عبد الرحمن، عن محمد بن يحيى بن حبان، عن ابن محيريز أنه قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب العزل في غزوة بني المصطلق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4138) and Muslim (1438/125).","chapter_en":"Coitus Interruptus During the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Muḥayrīz reported: I entered the mosque and saw Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, so I sat with him and asked him about coitus interruptus. Abū Saʿīd said: We accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq and captured some Arab women. We desired women, celibacy had become difficult for us, and we wished to practice coitus interruptus. We intended to do so but said, “Shall we practice it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among us without first asking him?” We therefore asked him, and he replied: “There is no harm if you do not do so, for every soul destined to exist until the Day of Resurrection will inevitably come into existence.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",497],"full":1,"rep":[6370],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4138)، ومسلم (125:1438)."},{"num":8898,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَة قالت: كَانَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا أَرَادَ سَفَرًا أَقْرَعَ بَيْنَ أَزْوَاجِهِ، فَأَيُّهُنَّ خَرَجَ سَهْمُهَا، خَرَجَ بِهَا رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَعَهُ، قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: فَأَقْرَعَ بَيْنَنَا فِي غَزْوَةٍ غَزَاهَا فَخَرَجَ فِيهَا سَهْمِي، فَخَرَجْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدَ مَا أُنْزِلَ الْحِجَابُ، فَكُنْتُ أُحْمَلُ فِي هَوْدَجِي وَأُنْزَلُ فِيهِ، فَسِرْنَا حَتَّى إِذَا فَرَغَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ غَزْوَتِهِ تِلْكَ وَقَفَلَ ودَنَوْنَا مِنَ المَدِينَةِ قَافِلِينَ، آذَنَ لَيْلَةً بِالرَّحِيلِ، فَقُمْتُ حِينَ آذَنُوا بِالرَّحِيلِ فَمَشَيْتُ حَتَّى جَاوَزْتُ الجَيْشَ، فَلَمَّا قَضَيْتُ شَأْنِي أَقْبَلْتُ إِلَى رَحْلِي، فَلَمَسْتُ صَدْرِي، فَإِذَا عِقْدٌ لِي مِنْ جَزْعِ ظَفَارِ قَدِ انْقَطَعَ، فَرَجَعْتُ فَالْتَمَسْتُ عِقْدِي، فَحَبَسَنِي ابْتِغَاؤُهُ، قَالَتْ: وَأَقْبَلَ الرَّهْطُ الَّذِينَ كَانُوا يُرَحِّلُونِي فَاحْتَمَلُوا هَوْدَجِي، فَرَحَلُوهُ عَلَى بَعِيرِي الَّذِي كُنْتُ أَرْكَبُ عَلَيْهِ، وَهُمْ يَحْسِبُونَ أَنِّي فِيهِ، وَكَانَ النِّسَاءُ إِذْ ذَاكَ خِفَافًا لَمْ يَهْبُلْنَ وَلَمْ يَغْشَهُنَّ اللَّحْمُ، إِنَّمَا يَأْكُلْنَ الْعُلْقَةَ مِنَ الطَّعَامِ، فَلَمْ يَسْتَنْكِرِ الْقَوْمُ خِفَّةَ الهَوْدَجِ حِينَ رَفَعُوهُ وَحَمَلُوهُ، وَكُنْتُ جَارِيَةً حَدِيثَةَ السِّنِّ، فَبَعَثُوا الجَمَلَ فَسَارُوا، وَوَجَدْتُ عِقْدِي بَعْدَ مَا اسْتَمَرَّ الجَيْشُ، فَجِئْتُ مَنَازِلهُمْ وَلَيْسَ بِهَا مِنْهُمْ دَاعٍ وَلاَ مُجِيبٌ، فَتَيَمَّمْتُ مَنْزِلِي الَّذِي كُنْتُ بِهِ، وَظَنَنْتُ أَنَّهُمْ سَيَفْقِدُونِي فَيَرْجِعُونَ إِلَيَّ، فَبَيْنَا أَنَا جَالِسَةٌ فِي مَنْزِلِي غَلَبَتْنِي عَيْنِي فَنِمْتُ، وَكَانَ صَفْوَانُ بْنُ المُعَطَّلِ السُّلَمِيُّ ثُمَّ الذَّكْوَانِيُّ مِنْ وَرَاءِ الجَيْشِ، فَأَصْبَحَ عِنْدَ مَنْزِلِي فَرَأَى سَوَادَ إِنْسَانٍ نَائِمٍ، فَعَرَفَنِي حِينَ رَآنِي، وَكَانَ رَآنِي قَبْلَ الْحِجَابِ، فَاسْتَيْقَظْتُ بِاسْتِرْجَاعِهِ حِينَ عَرَفَنِي، فَخَمَّرْتُ وَجْهِي بِجِلْبَابِي، والله مَا تَكَلَّمْنَا بِكَلِمَةٍ وَلاَ سَمِعْتُ مِنْهُ كَلِمَةً غَيْرَ اسْتِرْجَاعِهِ، وَهَوَى حَتَّى أَنَاخَ رَاحِلَتَهُ، فَوَطِئَ عَلَى يَدِهَا، فَقُمْتُ إِلَيْهَا فَرَكِبْتُهَا، فَانْطَلَقَ يَقُودُ بِي الرَّاحِلَةَ حَتَّى أَتَيْنَا الجَيْشَ مُوغِرِينَ فِي نَحْرِ الظَّهِيرَةِ، وَهُمْ نُزُولٌ ـ قَالَتْ: ـ فَهَلَكَ فِيَّ مَنْ هَلَكَ، وَكَانَ الَّذِي تَوَلَّى كِبْرَ الإِفْكِ عَبْدَ الله بْنَ أُبَىٍّ ابْنَ سَلُولَ. قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: أُخْبِرْتُ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يُشَاعُ وَيُتَحَدَّثُ بِهِ عِنْدَهُ، فَيُقِرُّهُ وَيَسْتَمِعُهُ وَيَسْتَوْشِيهِ. وَقَالَ عُرْوَةُ أَيْضًا: لَمْ يُسَمَّ مِنْ أَهْلِ الإِفْكِ أَيْضًا إِلاَّ حَسَّانُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ، وَمِسْطَحُ بْنُ أُثَاثَةَ، وَحَمْنَةُ بِنْتُ جَحْشٍ فِي نَاسٍ آخَرِينَ، لاَ عِلْمَ لِي بِهِمْ، غَيْرَ أَنَّهُمْ عُصْبَةٌ ـ كَمَا قَالَ الله تَعَالَى ـ وَإِنَّ كُبْرَ ذَلِكَ يُقَالُ عَبْدُ الله بْنُ أُبَىٍّ ابْنُ سَلُولَ. قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: كَانَتْ عَائِشَةُ تَكْرَهُ أَنْ يُسَبَّ عِنْدَهَا حَسَّانُ، وَتَقُولُ: إِنَّهُ الَّذِي قَالَ:","فَإِنَّ أَبِي وَوَالِدَهُ وَعِرْضِي لِعِرْضِ مُحَمَّدٍ مِنْكُمْ وِقَاءُ.","قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: فَقَدِمْنَا المَدِينَةَ فَاشْتَكَيْتُ حِينَ قَدِمْتُ شَهْرًا، وَالنَّاسُ يُفِيضُونَ فِي قَوْلِ أَصْحَابِ الإِفْكِ، لاَ أَشْعُرُ بِشَىْءٍ مِنْ ذَلِكَ، وَهْوَ يَرِيبُنِي فِي وَجَعِي أَنِّي لاَ أَعْرِفُ مِنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ اللُّطْفَ الَّذِي كُنْتُ أَرَى مِنْهُ حِينَ أَشْتَكِي، إِنَّمَا يَدْخُلُ عَلَىَّ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَيُسَلِّمُ ثُمَّ يَقُولُ: كَيْفَ تِيكُمْ؟ ثُمَّ يَنْصَرِفُ، فَذَلِكَ يَرِيبُنِي وَلاَ أَشْعُرُ بِالشَّرِّ، حَتَّى خَرَجْتُ حِينَ نَقَهْتُ، فَخَرَجْتُ مَعَ أُمِّ مِسْطَحٍ قِبَلَ المَنَاصِعِ، وَكَانَ مُتَبَرَّزَنَا، وَكُنَّا لاَ نَخْرُجُ إِلاَّ لَيْلاً إِلَى لَيْلٍ، وَذَلِكَ قَبْلَ أَنْ نَتَّخِذَ الْكُنُفَ قَرِيبًا مِنْ بُيُوتِنَا. قَالَتْ: وَأَمْرُنَا أَمْرُ الْعَرَبِ الأُوَلِ فِي الْبَرِّيَّةِ قِبَلَ الْغَائِطِ، وَكُنَّا نَتَأَذَّى بِالْكُنُفِ أَنْ نَتَّخِذَهَا عِنْدَ بُيُوتِنَا، قَالَتْ: فَانْطَلَقْتُ أَنَا وَأُمُّ مِسْطَحٍ وَهْىَ ابْنَةُ أَبِي رُهْمِ بْنِ المُطَّلِبِ بْنِ عَبْدِ مَنَافٍ، وَأُمُّهَا بِنْتُ صَخْرِ بْنِ عَامِرٍ خَالَةُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقِ، وَابْنُهَا مِسْطَحُ بْنُ أُثَاثَةَ بْنِ عَبَّادِ بْنِ المُطَّلِبِ، فَأَقْبَلْتُ أَنَا وَأُمُّ مِسْطَحٍ قِبَلَ بَيْتِي حِينَ فَرَغْنَا مِنْ شَأْنِنَا، فَعَثَرَتْ أُمُّ مِسْطَحٍ فِي مِرْطِهَا فَقَالَتْ: تَعِسَ مِسْطَحٌ. فَقُلْتُ لَهَا: بِئْسَ مَا قُلْتِ، أَتَسُبِّينَ رَجُلاً شَهِدَ بَدْرًا؟ فَقَالَتْ: أَيْ هَنْتَاهْ أوَلَمْ تَسْمَعِي مَا قَالَ؟ قَالَتْ: وَقُلْتُ: مَا قَالَ؟ فَأَخْبَرَتْنِي بِقَوْلِ أَهْلِ الإِفْكِ ـ قَالَتْ: فَازْدَدْتُ مَرَضًا عَلَى مَرَضِي، فَلَمَّا رَجَعْتُ إِلَى بَيْتِي دَخَلَ عَلَىَّ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَسَلَّمَ ثُمَّ قَالَ: كَيْفَ تِيكُمْ؟ فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: أَتَأْذَنُ لِي أَنْ آتِيَ أَبَوَيَّ؟ قَالَتْ: وَأُرِيدُ أَنْ أَسْتَيْقِنَ الخَبَرَ مِنْ قِبَلِهِمَا، قَالَتْ فَأَذِنَ لِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ لأُمِّي: يَا أُمَّتَاهُ مَاذَا يَتَحَدَّثُ النَّاسُ؟ قَالَتْ: يَا بُنَيَّةُ هَوِّنِي عَلَيْكِ، فَوَالله لَقَلَّمَا كَانَتِ امْرَأَةٌ قَطُّ وَضِيئَةً عِنْدَ رَجُلٍ يُحِبُّهَا لَهَا ضَرَائِرُ إِلاَّ كَثَّرْنَ عَلَيْهَا. قَالَتْ: فَقُلْتُ: سُبْحَانَ الله، أَوَلَقَدْ تَحَدَّثَ النَّاسُ بِهَذَا؟ قَالَتْ: فَبَكَيْتُ تِلْكَ اللَّيْلَةَ، حَتَّى أَصْبَحْتُ لاَ يَرْقَأُ لِي دَمْعٌ وَلاَ أَكْتَحِلُ بِنَوْمٍ، ثُمَّ أَصْبَحْتُ أَبْكِي ـ قَالَتْ: وَدَعَا رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلِيَّ بْنَ أَبِي طَالِبٍ وَأُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ حِينَ اسْتَلْبَثَ الْوَحْىُ، يَسْأَلُهُمَا وَيَسْتَشِيرُهُمَا فِي فِرَاقِ أَهْلِهِ، قَالَتْ: فَأَمَّا أُسَامَةُ فَأَشَارَ عَلَى رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالَّذِي يَعْلَمُ مِنْ بَرَاءَةِ أَهْلِهِ، وَبِالَّذِي يَعْلَمُ لهُمْ فِي نَفْسِهِ، فَقَالَ أُسَامَةُ: أَهْلَكَ، وَلاَ نَعْلَمُ إِلاَّ خَيْرًا. وَأَمَّا عَلِيٌّ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ الله لَمْ يُضَيِّقِ الله عَلَيْكَ، وَالنِّسَاءُ سِوَاهَا كَثِيرٌ، وَسَلِ الجَارِيَةَ تَصْدُقْكَ. قَالَتْ: فَدَعَا رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَرِيرَةَ، فَقَالَ: أَىْ بَرِيرَةُ هَلْ رَأَيْتِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ يَرِيبُكِ؟. قَالَتْ لَهُ بَرِيرَةُ: وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالحَقِّ مَا رَأَيْتُ عَلَيْهَا أَمْرًا قَطُّ أَغْمِصُهُ، غَيْرَ أَنَّهَا جَارِيَةٌ حَدِيثَةُ السِّنِّ تَنَامُ عَنْ عَجِينِ أَهْلِهَا، فَتَأْتِي الدَّاجِنُ فَتَأْكُلُهُ ـ قَالَتْ: فَقَامَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ يَوْمِهِ، فَاسْتَعْذَرَ مِنْ عَبْدِ الله بْنِ أُبَىٍّ وَهُوَ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ، فَقَالَ: يَا مَعْشَرَ المُسْلِمِينَ مَنْ يَعْذِرُنِي مِنْ رَجُلٍ قَدْ بَلَغَنِي عَنْهُ أَذَاهُ فِي أَهْلِي، والله مَا عَلِمْتُ عَلَى أَهْلِي إِلاَّ خَيْرًا، وَلَقَدْ ذَكَرُوا رَجُلاً مَا عَلِمْتُ عَلَيْهِ إِلاَّ خَيْرًا، وَمَا يَدْخُلُ عَلَى أَهْلِي إِلاَّ مَعِي قَالَتْ: فَقَامَ سَعْدُ بْنُ مُعَاذٍ أَخُو بَنِي عَبْدِ الأَشْهَلِ فَقَالَ: أَنَا يَا رَسُولَ الله أَعْذِرُكَ، فَإِنْ كَانَ مِنَ الأَوْسِ ضَرَبْتُ عُنُقَهُ، وَإِنْ كَانَ مِنْ إِخْوَانِنَا مِنَ الخَزْرَجِ أَمَرْتَنَا فَفَعَلْنَا أَمْرَكَ. قَالَتْ: فَقَامَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الخَزْرَجِ، وَكَانَتْ أُمُّ حَسَّانَ بِنْتَ عَمِّهِ مِنْ فَخِذِهِ، وَهْوَ سَعْدُ بْنُ عُبَادَةَ، وَهْوَ سَيِّدُ الخَزْرَجِ، قَالَتْ: وَكَانَ قَبْلَ ذَلِكَ رَجُلاً صَالِحًا، وَلَكِنِ احْتَمَلَتْهُ الحَمِيَّةُ فَقَالَ لِسَعْدٍ: كَذَبْتَ لَعَمْرُ الله لاَ تَقْتُلُهُ، وَلاَ تَقْدِرُ عَلَى قَتْلِهِ، وَلَوْ كَانَ مِنْ رَهْطِكَ مَا أَحْبَبْتَ أَنْ يُقْتَلَ. فَقَامَ أُسَيْدُ بْنُ حُضَيْرٍ ، وَهْوَ ابْنُ عَمِّ سَعْدٍ، فَقَالَ لِسَعْدِ بْنِ عُبَادَةَ: كَذَبْتَ لَعَمْرُ الله لَنَقْتُلَنَّهُ، فَإِنَّكَ مُنَافِقٌ تُجَادِلُ عَنِ المُنَافِقِينَ. قَالَتْ فَثَارَ الحَيَّانِ الأَوْسُ وَالخَزْرَجُ حَتَّى هَمُّوا أَنْ يَقْتَتِلُوا، وَرَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَائِمٌ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ، قَالَتْ: فَلَمْ يَزَلْ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُخَفِّضُهُمْ حَتَّى سَكَتُوا وَسَكَتَ، قَالَتْ: فَبَكَيْتُ يَوْمِي ذَلِكَ كُلَّهُ، لاَ يَرْقَأُ لِي دَمْعٌ وَلاَ أَكْتَحِلُ بِنَوْمٍ، قَالَتْ: وَأَصْبَحَ أَبَوَايَ عنْدِي، وَقَدْ بَكَيْتُ لَيْلَتَيْنِ وَيَوْمًا، لاَ يَرْقَأُ لِي دَمْعٌ وَلاَ أَكْتَحِلُ بِنَوْمٍ، حَتَّى إِنِّي لأَظُنُّ أَنَّ الْبُكَاءَ فَالِقٌ كَبِدِي، فَبَيْنَا أَبَوَاي جالِسَانِ عِنْدِي وَأَنَا أَبْكِي فَاسْتَأْذَنَتْ عَلَيَّ امْرَأَةٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، فَأَذِنْتُ لَهَا، فَجَلَسَتْ تَبْكِي مَعِي، قَالَتْ: فَبَيْنَا نَحْنُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ دَخَلَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْنَا، فَسَلَّمَ ثُمَّ جَلَسَ، قَالَتْ: وَلَمْ يَجْلِسْ عِنْدِي مُنْذُ قِيلَ مَا قِيلَ قَبْلَهَا، وَقَدْ لَبِثَ شَهْرًا لاَ يُوحَى إِلَيْهِ فِي شَأْنِي بِشَىْءٍ، قَالَتْ: فَتَشَهَّدَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ جَلَسَ ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَمَّا بَعْدُ، يَا عَائِشَةُ إِنَّهُ بَلَغَنِي عَنْكِ كَذَا وَكَذَا، فَإِنْ كُنْتِ بَرِيئَةً، فَسَيُبَرِّئُكِ الله، وَإِنْ كُنْتِ أَلمَمْتِ بِذَنْبٍ، فَاسْتَغْفِرِي الله وَتُوبِي إِلَيْهِ، فَإِنَّ الْعَبْدَ إِذَا اعْتَرَفَ ثُمَّ تَابَ تَابَ الله عَلَيْهِ. قَالَتْ: فَلَمَّا قَضَى رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَقَالَتَهُ قَلَصَ دَمْعِي حَتَّى مَا أُحِسُّ مِنْهُ قَطْرَةً، فَقُلْتُ لأَبِي: أَجِبْ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنِّي فِيمَا قَالَ، فَقَالَ أَبِي: ولله مَا أَدْرِي مَا أَقُولُ لِرَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. فَقُلْتُ لأُمِّي: أَجِيبِي رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِيمَا قَالَ. قَالَتْ أُمِّي: والله مَا أَدْرِي مَا أَقُولُ لِرَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. فَقُلْتُ: - وَأَنَا جَارِيَةٌ حَدِيثَةُ السِّنِّ لاَ أَقْرَأُ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ كَثِيرًا - إِنِّي والله لَقَدْ عَلِمْتُ لَقَدْ سَمِعْتُمْ هَذَا الحَدِيثَ حَتَّى اسْتَقَرَّ فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ وَصَدَّقْتُمْ بِهِ، فَلَئِنْ قُلْتُ لَكُمْ إِنِّي بَرِيئَةٌ لاَتُصَدِّقُونِي، وَلَئِنِ اعْتَرَفْتُ لَكُمْ بِأَمْرٍ، والله يَعْلَمُ أَنِّي مِنْهُ بَرِيئَةٌ لَتُصَدِّقُنِّي، فوالله لاَ أَجِدُ لِي وَلَكُمْ مَثَلاً إِلاَّ أَبَا يُوسُفَ حِينَ قَالَ: ﴿فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيلٌ وَاللَّهُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلَى مَا تَصِفُونَ﴾ [يوسف:١٨] ثُمَّ تَحَوَّلْتُ وَاضْطَجَعْتُ عَلَى فِرَاشِي، والله يَعْلَمُ أَنِّي حِينَئِذٍ بَرِيئَةٌ، وَأَنَّ الله مُبَرِّئِي بِبَرَاءَتِي- وَلَكِنْ والله مَا كُنْتُ أَظُنُّ أَنَّ الله مُنْزِلٌ فِي شَأْنِي وَحْيًا يُتْلَى، لَشَأْنِي فِي نَفْسِي كَانَ أَحْقَرَ مِنْ أَنْ يَتَكَلَّمَ الله فِيَّ بِأَمْرٍ، وَلَكِنْ كُنْتُ أَرْجُو أَنْ يَرَى رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي النَّوْمِ رُؤْيَا يُبَرِّئُنِي الله بِهَا- فوالله مَا رَامَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَجْلِسَهُ، وَلاَ خَرَجَ أَحَدٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْبَيْتِ، حَتَّى أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ، فَأَخَذَهُ مَا كَانَ يَأْخُذُهُ مِنَ الْبُرَحَاءِ، حَتَّى إِنَّهُ لَيَتَحَدَّرُ مِنْهُ مِنَ الْعَرَقِ مِثْلُ الجُمَانِ وَهْوَ فِي يَوْمٍ شَاتٍ؛ مِنْ ثِقَلِ الْقَوْلِ الَّذِي أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ، قَالَتْ: فَسُرِّيَ عَنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهْوَ يَضْحَكُ، فَكَانَتْ أَوَّلَ كَلِمَةٍ تَكَلَّمَ بِهَا أَنْ قَالَ: يَا عَائِشَةُ أَمَّا الله فَقَدْ بَرَّأَكِ قَالَتْ: فَقَالَتْ لِي أُمِّي: قُومِي إِلَيْهِ. فَقُلْتُ: والله لاَ أَقُومُ إِلَيْهِ، فَإِنِّي لاَ أَحْمَدُ إِلاَّ الله عَزَّ وَجَلَّ، قَالَتْ: وَأَنْزَلَ الله تَعَالَى: ﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ جَاءُوا بِالْإِفْكِ عُصْبَةٌ مِنْكُمْ﴾ [النور: ١١] الْعَشْرَ الآيَاتِ، ثُمَّ أَنْزَلَ الله هَذَا فِي بَرَاءَتِي. قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقُ: وَكَانَ يُنْفِقُ عَلَى مِسْطَحِ بْنِ أُثَاثَةَ لِقَرَابَتِهِ مِنْهُ وَفَقْرِهِ: والله لاَ أُنْفِقُ عَلَى مِسْطَحٍ شَيْئًا أَبَدًا، بَعْدَ الَّذِي قَالَ لِعَائِشَةَ مَا قَالَ. فَأَنْزَلَ الله: وَلَا يَأْتَلِ أُولُو الْفَضْلِ مِنْكُمْ -إِلَى قَوْلِهِ- وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ [النور: ٢٢]قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقُ: بَلَى والله إِنِّي لأُحِبُّ أَنْ يَغْفِرَ الله لِي، فَرَجَعَ إِلَى مِسْطَحٍ النَّفَقَةَ الَّتِي كَانَ يُنْفِقُ عَلَيْهِ، وَقَالَ: والله لاَ أَنْزِعُهَا مِنْهُ أَبَدًا، قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: وَكَانَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَأَلَ زَيْنَبَ بِنْتَ جَحْشٍ عَنْ أَمْرِي، فَقَالَ لِزَيْنَبَ: مَاذَا عَلِمْتِ أَوْ رَأَيْتِ؟ فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ الله أَحْمِي سَمْعِي وَبَصَرِي، والله مَا عَلِمْتُ إِلاَّ خَيْرًا. قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: وَهْىَ الَّتِي كَانَتْ تُسَامِينِي مِنْ أَزْوَاجِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. فَعَصَمَهَا الله بِالْوَرَعِ ـ قَالَتْ: وَطَفِقَتْ أُخْتُهَا حَمْنَةُ تُحَارِبُ لَهَا، فَهَلَكَتْ فِيمَنْ هَلَكَ.","قَالَ ابْنُ شِهَابٍ: فَهَذَا الَّذِي بَلَغَنِي مِنْ حَدِيثِ هَؤُلاَءِ الرَّهْطِ.","ثُمَّ قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: والله إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ الَّذِي قِيلَ لَهُ ما قِيلَ لَيَقُولُ: سُبْحَانَ الله فَوَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ مَا كَشَفْتُ مِنْ كَنَفِ أُنْثَى قَطُّ. قَالَتْ: ثُمَّ قُتِلَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ فِي سَبِيلِ الله."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4141) ومسلم في التوبة (2770) كلاهما من طرق عن الزهري قال: حدثني عروة بن الزبير، وسعيد بن المسيب، وعلقمة بن وقاص، وعبيد الله بن عبد الله بن عتبة بن مسعود، عن عائشة زوج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قالت: فذكرت الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حديث الإفك في غزوة بني المصطلق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4141) and Muslim (2770).","chapter_en":"The Incident of the Slander During the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. Whichever wife’s lot was drawn would accompany him. On one campaign he drew lots among us, and my lot was selected. I therefore accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the command of veiling had been revealed. I was carried inside my litter and would remain in it when it was set down. We traveled until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ completed that campaign and began the return journey. When we had drawn close to Madinah, orders were given one night to depart. I rose when the departure was announced and walked beyond the army to relieve myself. When I had finished, I returned toward my mount and touched my chest, only to discover that a necklace of black onyx from Ẓafār had broken and fallen. I went back to search for it, and the search delayed me. The men responsible for preparing my mount came and lifted my litter onto the camel I had been riding, assuming that I was inside it. Women at that time were light and had not become heavy with flesh, since they ate only small amounts of food. The men therefore did not find the litter’s lightness unusual when they raised and carried it. I was also a young girl. They sent the camel forward and departed. I found my necklace after the army had moved on. I returned to their campsite, but there was no one there to call or answer. I remained at the place where I had been, thinking that when they discovered my absence they would return for me. While I was sitting there, sleep overcame me. Ṣafwān ibn al-Muʿaṭṭal al-Sulamī, of Dhakwān, had remained behind the army. In the morning he reached my stopping place and saw the dark figure of a sleeping person. When he saw me, he recognized me, for he had seen me before the command of veiling. I awoke when he recognized me and said, “Indeed, we belong to Allah, and to Him we shall return.” I covered my face with my outer garment. By Allah, we did not speak a single word, nor did I hear anything from him other than his words of return to Allah. He lowered himself, made his camel kneel, and placed his foot upon its foreleg. I rose and mounted it. He then led the camel on foot until we reached the army during the intense heat of midday, while they were encamped. Some people were ruined by what followed, and the one who assumed the greatest share of the slander was ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl. ʿUrwah said: I was informed that the slander would be circulated and discussed in his presence, and he would approve of it, listen to it, and encourage its spread. ʿUrwah also said: Among those involved in the slander, no one was specifically named except Ḥassān ibn Thābit, Misṭaḥ ibn Uthāthah, and Ḥamnah bint Jaḥsh, together with others whose names I do not know. They were a group, as Allah Most High stated. The man said to have borne its greatest share was ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl.","ʿUrwah said: ʿĀ’ishah disliked anyone insulting Ḥassān in her presence, and would say that he was the one who composed: My father, his father, and my honor are a shield protecting Muhammad’s honor from you. ʿĀ’ishah continued: When we reached Madinah, I fell ill for a month. The people were engrossed in circulating the slander, but I knew nothing of it. What made me uneasy during my illness was that I did not see from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the tenderness he usually showed me when I was ill. He would enter, greet me, and merely ask, “How is that one?” He would then leave. This made me uneasy, though I still knew nothing of the evil being said.","When I had begun to recover, I went out with Umm Misṭaḥ toward al-Manāṣiʿ, which was where we relieved ourselves. We would go out only from night to night. This was before privies were constructed close to our houses. We followed the custom of the early Arabs of going into open country to relieve ourselves, and we disliked having privies beside our homes. I went with Umm Misṭaḥ, who was the daughter of Abū Ruhm ibn al-Muṭṭalib ibn ʿAbd Manāf. Her mother was the daughter of Ṣakhr ibn ʿĀmir and the maternal aunt of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq. Her son was Misṭaḥ ibn Uthāthah ibn ʿAbbād ibn al-Muṭṭalib. When Umm Misṭaḥ and I had finished and were returning toward my house, she stumbled over her cloak and exclaimed, “May Misṭaḥ perish!” I said to her, “What a terrible thing you have said! Are you insulting a man who witnessed Badr?” She replied, “My dear girl, have you not heard what he said?” I asked, “What did he say?” She then told me what the slanderers were saying, and my illness became even worse. When I returned home, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, greeted me, and asked, “How is that one?” I said, “Will you permit me to go to my parents?” I wanted to verify the news through them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted me permission. I asked my mother, “Mother, what are the people saying?” She replied, “My daughter, take it easy. By Allah, there is hardly ever a beautiful woman beloved by her husband who has co-wives without them speaking much against her.” I exclaimed, “Glory be to Allah! Have the people truly been saying this?” I wept throughout that night until morning. My tears did not cease, nor did I taste sleep. When morning came, I continued weeping. As revelation had been delayed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Usāmah ibn Zayd to ask their opinion about separating from his wife. Usāmah advised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ according to what he knew of his wife’s innocence and the affection he knew the Prophet ﷺ had for her. He said, “They are your family, and we know nothing but good about them.” ʿAlī said, “Messenger of Allah, Allah has not restricted matters for you, and there are many women besides her. Ask the maidservant, and she will tell you the truth.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned Barīrah and asked: “Barīrah, have you ever seen anything about her that made you suspicious?” Barīrah replied: “By Him who sent you with the truth, I have never seen anything in her that I could fault, except that she is a young girl who sometimes falls asleep while watching her family’s dough, so a domestic animal comes and eats it.” That same day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood upon the pulpit and publicly sought support against ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy. He said: “Muslims, who will excuse me in dealing with a man whose abuse of my family has reached me? By Allah, I know nothing but good concerning my family. They have also mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good and who never entered upon my family except in my company.” Saʿd ibn Muʿādh of Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal rose and said, “Messenger of Allah, I shall excuse you and deal with him. If he belongs to the Aws, I will strike off his head; and if he belongs to our brothers of the Khazraj, command us and we shall carry out your order.” A man of the Khazraj then stood up. He was Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, the leader of the Khazraj, and Umm Ḥassān was his cousin from the same clan. He had previously been a righteous man, but tribal zeal overcame him. He said to Saʿd, “You have lied! By Allah, you will not kill him and cannot kill him. Had he belonged to your own clan, you would not have wanted him killed.” Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr, Saʿd ibn Muʿādh’s cousin, then rose and said to Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, “You have lied! By Allah, we shall certainly kill him. You are behaving like a hypocrite, arguing in defense of the hypocrites.” The two tribes, the Aws and Khazraj, became inflamed until they nearly fought one another, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained standing upon the pulpit. He continued calming them until they settled down and fell silent. I wept throughout that entire day. My tears did not stop, nor did I taste sleep. My parents remained with me the next morning. I had wept for two nights and a day without my tears ceasing or tasting sleep, until I thought that my weeping would split my liver. While my parents were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Anṣār sought permission to enter. I allowed her in, and she sat and wept with me. While we were in that state, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, greeted us, and sat down. He had not sat with me since the rumors began, and a month had passed without any revelation concerning me. After sitting down, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praised Allah and recited the testimony of faith, then said: “To proceed: ʿĀ’ishah, such-and-such has reached me concerning you. If you are innocent, Allah will declare your innocence. If you have committed a sin, seek Allah’s forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant acknowledges a sin and repents, Allah accepts the servant’s repentance.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished speaking, my tears stopped so completely that I could not feel a single drop. I said to my father, “Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf.” My father replied, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said to my mother, “Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning what he has said.” She replied, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Being a young girl who had not memorized much of the Qur’an, I said: “By Allah, I know that you have heard this story until it has settled in your minds and you have believed it. If I tell you that I am innocent, you will not believe me; but if I confess to something—and Allah knows that I am innocent of it—you will believe me. “By Allah, I can find no comparison for my situation with you except the father of Yūsuf when he said: ‘So beautiful patience is most fitting, and Allah alone is whose help is sought against what you describe.’” [Yūsuf 12:18] I turned away and lay down upon my bed. Allah knew that I was innocent and that He would declare my innocence. Yet, by Allah, I never imagined that Allah would reveal recited revelation concerning me. In my own estimation, my affair was too insignificant for Allah to speak about me in revelation. I merely hoped that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see a dream through which Allah would declare my innocence. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not left his seat, nor had anyone departed from the house, when revelation descended upon him. The severe condition that accompanied revelation overtook him, and drops of perspiration like pearls streamed from him despite the coldness of the day, because of the weight of the words being revealed. When the revelation ended, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was smiling. His first words were: “ʿĀ’ishah, Allah has declared you innocent.” My mother said, “Rise and go to him.” I replied, “By Allah, I will not rise to go to him. I shall praise none but Allah Almighty.” Allah Most High revealed: “Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group from among you.” [Al-Nūr 24:11] He revealed the ten verses declaring my innocence. Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, who used to support Misṭaḥ ibn Uthāthah because of their kinship and Misṭaḥ’s poverty, said: “By Allah, I shall never again spend anything upon Misṭaḥ after what he said about ʿĀ’ishah.” Allah then revealed: “Let not those among you who possess virtue and wealth swear not to give…” through His words: “…and Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.” [Al-Nūr 24:22] Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said: “Yes, by Allah, I certainly love that Allah should forgive me.” He resumed the support he had provided to Misṭaḥ and said: “By Allah, I shall never withdraw it from him.” ʿĀ’ishah continued: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had asked Zaynab bint Jaḥsh concerning me, saying: “What do you know or what have you seen?” She replied: “Messenger of Allah, I guard my hearing and sight from speaking without knowledge. By Allah, I know nothing but good.” ʿĀ’ishah said: Among the Prophet’s wives, she was the one who competed with me in status, but Allah protected her through piety. Her sister Ḥamnah, however, began defending her and became ruined among those who were ruined by the slander. Ibn Shihāb said: This is what reached me from the reports of those narrators. ʿUrwah then related that ʿĀ’ishah said: By Allah, the man about whom those things were said used to declare: “Glory be to Allah! By Him in whose hand is my soul, I have never uncovered the garment of any woman.” She said: He was later killed in the cause of Allah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",498],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4141)، ومسلم (2770)."},{"num":8899,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أم رومان – وَهْىَ أُمُّ عَائِشَةَ ـ قَالَتْ: بَيْنَا أَنَا قَاعِدَةٌ أَنَا وَعَائِشَةُ إِذْ وَلَجَتِ امْرَأَةٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ فَقَالَتْ: فَعَلَ الله بِفُلاَنٍ وَفَعَلَ. فَقَالَتْ أُمُّ رُومَانَ: وَمَا ذَاكَ؟ قَالَتْ: ابْنِي فِيمَنْ حَدَّثَ الحَدِيثَ. قَالَتْ: وَمَا ذَاكَ؟ قَالَتْ: كَذَا وَكَذَا. قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: سَمِعَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ. قَالَتْ: وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ؟ قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ. فَخَرَّتْ مَغْشِيًّا عَلَيْهَا، فَمَا أَفَاقَتْ إِلاَّ وَعَلَيْهَا حُمَّى بِنَافِضٍ، فَطَرَحْتُ عَلَيْهَا ثِيَابَهَا فَغَطَّيْتُهَا. فَجَاءَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: مَا شَأْنُ هَذِهِ؟ . قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله أَخَذَتْهَا الحُمَّى بِنَافِضٍ. قَالَ: فَلَعَلَّ فِي حَدِيثٍ تُحُدِّثَ بِهِ قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ. فَقَعَدَتْ عَائِشَةُ، فَقَالَتْ: والله لَئِنْ حَلَفْتُ لاَ تُصَدِّقُونِي، وَلَئِنْ قُلْتُ لاَ تَعْذِرُونِي، مَثَلِي وَمَثَلُكُمْ كَيَعْقُوبَ وَبَنِيهِ، وَاللَّهُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلَى مَا تَصِفُونَ قَالَتْ: وَانْصَرَفَ وَلَمْ يَقُلْ شَيْئًا، فَأَنْزَلَ الله عُذْرَهَا، قَالَتْ: بِحَمْدِ الله، لاَ بِحَمْدِ أَحَدٍ، وَلاَ بِحَمْدِكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4143) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، حدثنا أبو عوانة، عن حصين (هو ابن عبد الرحمن الواسطي) عن أبي وائل (هو شقيق بن سلمة الأسدي) قال: حدثني مسروق بن الأجدع، قال: حدثتني أم رومان فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حديث الإفك في غزوة بني المصطلق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4143).","chapter_en":"The Incident of the Slander During the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Rūmān, the mother of ʿĀ’ishah, reported: While ʿĀ’ishah and I were sitting together, a woman of the Anṣār entered and exclaimed, “May Allah do such-and-such to so-and-so!” Umm Rūmān asked, “What has happened?” She replied, “My son is among those who have repeated the story.” She asked, “What story?” The woman then related what had been said. ʿĀ’ishah asked, “Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard it?” She replied, “Yes.” She asked, “Has Abū Bakr heard it?” She replied, “Yes.” ʿĀ’ishah collapsed unconscious. When she regained consciousness, she had a fever accompanied by shivering, so I placed her garments over her and covered her. The Prophet ﷺ came and asked: “What is wrong with her?” I replied, “Messenger of Allah, she has been seized by a shivering fever.” He asked: “Is it perhaps because of a story being circulated?” She replied, “Yes.” ʿĀ’ishah sat up and said: “By Allah, if I swear an oath, you will not believe me, and if I offer an explanation, you will not excuse me. My situation with you is like that of Yaʿqūb with his sons: ‘Allah alone is whose help is sought against what you describe.’” The Prophet ﷺ departed without saying anything. Allah then revealed her vindication. She said: “It came by Allah’s praise, not through the praise of anyone else, nor through yours.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",499],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4143)."},{"num":8900,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مسروق قال: دَخَلْنَا عَلَى عَائِشَةَ - رضى الله عنها - وَعِنْدَهَا حَسَّانُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ يُنْشِدُهَا شِعْرًا، يُشَبِّبُ بِأَبْيَاتٍ لَهُ وَقَالَ:","حَصَانٌ رَزَانٌ مَا تُزَنُّ بِرِيبَةٍ * وَتُصْبِحُ غَرْثَى مِنْ لحُومِ الْغَوَافِلِ.","فَقَالَتْ لَهُ عَائِشَةُ: لَكِنَّكَ لَسْتَ كَذَلِكَ. قَالَ مَسْرُوقٌ: فَقُلْتُ لَهَا: لمَ تَأْذَنِينَ لَهُ أَنْ يَدْخُلَ عَلَيْكِ؟ وَقَدْ قَالَ الله تَعَالَى: ﴿وَالَّذِي تَوَلَّى كِبْرَهُ مِنْهُمْ لَهُ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ﴾ [النور: ١١] فَقَالَتْ :وَأَىُّ عَذَابٍ أَشَدُّ مِنَ الْعَمَى؟ قَالَتْ لَهُ: إِنَّهُ كَانَ يُنَافِحُ ـ أَوْ: يُهَاجِي ـ عَنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4146) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2488 :155) كلاهما عن بشر بن خالد، أخبرنا محمد بن جعفر، عن شعبة، عن سليمان، عن أبي الضحى، عن مسروق قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حديث الإفك في غزوة بني المصطلق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4146) and Muslim (2488/155).","chapter_en":"The Incident of the Slander During the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Masrūq reported: We entered upon ʿĀ’ishah, while Ḥassān ibn Thābit was with her reciting poetry and praising her in his verses. He said: Chaste and dignified, never accused of anything suspicious; she rises hungry, having never consumed the flesh of heedless women. ʿĀ’ishah said to him, “But you were not like that.” Masrūq said: I asked her, “Why do you permit him to enter upon you when Allah Most High says: ‘The one among them who assumed the greatest share of it will suffer a tremendous punishment’?”","[Al-Nūr 24:11] She replied: “What punishment could be more severe than blindness?” She also said: “He used to defend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—or engage in poetic combat on his behalf.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“Ḥaṣān” means chaste.","“Razān” means a woman of dignity and composure.","“Tuẓannu” means to be accused.","“Gharthā” means hungry: she does not backbite people and thereby fill herself with their flesh."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4146)، ومسلم (2488 :155)."},{"num":8901,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عروة بن الزبير قَالَ: ذَهَبْتُ أَسُبُّ حَسَّانَ عِنْدَ عَائِشَةَ، فَقَالَتْ: لاَ تَسُبَّهُ، فَإِنَّهُ كَانَ يُنَافِحُ عَنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. وَقَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: اسْتَأْذَنَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي هِجَاءِ المُشْرِكِينَ قَالَ: كَيْفَ بِنَسَبِي قَالَ: لأَسُلَّنَّكَ مِنْهُمْ كَمَا تُسَلُّ الشَّعْرَةُ مِنَ الْعَجِينِ.","وقال عروة: سببت حسان، وكان ممن كثر عليها."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4145) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (154:2487) كلاهما من طريق هشام بن عروة عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حديث الإفك في غزوة بني المصطلق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4145) and Muslim (2487/154).","chapter_en":"The Incident of the Slander During the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr reported: I began insulting Ḥassān in the presence of ʿĀ’ishah, but she said: “Do not insult him, for he used to defend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” ʿĀ’ishah also related: Ḥassān sought the Prophet’s ﷺ permission to satirize the polytheists. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What about my ancestry among them?” Ḥassān replied: “I shall extract you from among them as a hair is drawn out of dough.” ʿUrwah said: I insulted Ḥassān because he had been among those who spoke extensively against her."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words “he defended the Messenger of Allah ﷺ” mean that he defended him through his poetry."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",501],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4145)، ومسلم (154:2487)."},{"num":8902,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، قَالَتْ: لَمَّا قَسَمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَبَايَا بَنِي الْمُصْطَلِقِ، وَقَعَتْ جُوَيْرِيَةُ بِنْتُ الْحَارِثِ فِي السَّهْمِ لِثَابِتِ بْنِ قَيْسِ بْنِ الشَّمَّاسِ - أَوْ لِابْنِ عَمٍّ لَهُ - وَكَاتَبَتْهُ عَلَى نَفْسِهَا، وَكَانَتْ امْرَأَةً حُلْوَةً مُلَاحَةً لَا يَرَاهَا أَحَدٌ إِلَّا أَخَذَتْ بِنَفْسِهِ، فَأَتَتْ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَسْتَعِينُهُ فِي كِتَابَتِهَا، قَالَتْ: فَوَاللهِ مَا هُوَ إِلَّا أَنْ رَأَيْتُهَا عَلَى بَابِ حُجْرَتِي فَكَرِهْتُهَا، وَعَرَفْتُ أَنَّهُ سَيَرَى مِنْهَا مَا رَأَيْتُ، فَدَخَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ، فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَنَا جُوَيْرِيَةُ بِنْتُ الْحَارِثِ بْنِ أَبِي ضِرَارٍ سَيِّدِ قَوْمِهِ، وَقَدْ أَصَابَنِي مِنَ الْبَلَاءِ مَا لَمْ يَخْفَ عَلَيْكَ، فَوَقَعْتُ فِي السَّهْمِ لِثَابِتِ بْنِ قَيْسِ بْنِ الشَّمَّاسِ - أَوْ لِابْنِ عَمٍّ لَهُ - فَكَاتَبْتُهُ عَلَى نَفْسِي، فَجِئْتُكَ أَسْتَعِينُكَ عَلَى كِتَابَتِي. قَالَ: فَهَلْ لَكِ فِي خَيْرٍ مِنْ ذَلِكَ؟. قَالَتْ: وَمَا هُوَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: أَقْضِي كِتَابَتَكِ وَأَتَزَوَّجُكِ قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: قَدْ فَعَلْتُ. قَالَتْ: وَخَرَجَ الْخَبَرُ إِلَى النَّاسِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَزَوَّجَ جُوَيْرِيَةَ بِنْتَ الْحَارِثِ، فَقَالَ النَّاسُ: أَصْهَارُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ! فَأَرْسَلُوا مَا بِأَيْدِيهِمْ، قَالَتْ: فَلَقَدْ أَعْتَقَ بِتَزْوِيجِهِ إِيَّاهَا مِائَةَ أَهْلِ بَيْتٍ مِنْ بَنِي الْمُصْطَلِقِ، فَمَا أَعْلَمُ امْرَأَةً كَانَتْ أَعْظَمَ بَرَكَةً عَلَى قَوْمِهَا مِنْهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3931) وأحمد (26265) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4054) والحاكم (4/26) كلهم من طريق محمد بن إسحاق، قال: حدثني محمد بن جعفر بن الزبير، عن عروة بن الزبير، عن عائشة أم المؤمنين فذكرته. واللفظ لأحمد.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"قصة جويرية بنت الحارث وزواج النبي ﷺ بها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3931) and Aḥmad (26265); authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (4054) and al-Ḥākim (6781). This wording is Aḥmad’s.","chapter_en":"The Story of Juwayriyyah bint al-Ḥārith and Her Marriage to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, Mother of the Believers, reported: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed the captives of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq, Juwayriyyah bint al-Ḥārith fell to the share of Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās, or to one of his cousins. She concluded a contract with him to purchase her freedom. She was a beautiful and attractive woman whom no one could see without being captivated by her. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his assistance in paying her emancipation contract. ʿĀ’ishah said: By Allah, as soon as I saw her at the door of my apartment, I disliked her presence, for I knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would notice the same beauty in her that I had noticed. She entered and said: “Messenger of Allah, I am Juwayriyyah, daughter of al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Ḍirār, the chief of his people. The hardship that has befallen me is not hidden from you. I fell to the share of Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās—or one of his cousins—and entered into an emancipation contract with him. I have come to seek your assistance in paying it.” He asked: “Would you like something better than that?” She asked, “What is it, Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “I shall pay your emancipation contract and marry you.” She said, “Yes, Messenger of Allah.” He replied: “I have done so.” News spread among the people that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had married Juwayriyyah bint al-Ḥārith. The people said, “They are now the in-laws of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!” They therefore released the captives in their possession. ʿĀ’ishah said: Through his marriage to her, one hundred households of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq were set free. I know of no woman who brought a greater blessing to her people than she did."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",502],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9414],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3931)، وأحمد (26265)، وصححه ابن حبان (4054)، والحاكم (6781). واللفظ لأحمد."},{"num":8903,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: أَمَّا زَيْنَبُ ابْنَةُ جَحْشٍ فَعَصَمَهَا اللَّهُ بِدِينِهَا، فَلَمْ تَقُلْ إِلاَّ خَيْرًا، وَأَمَّا أُخْتُهَا حَمْنَةُ فَهَلَكَتْ فِيمَنْ هَلَكَ، وَكَانَ الَّذِي يَتَكَلَّمُ فِيهِ مِسْطَحٌ وَحَسَّانُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ وَالْمُنَافِقُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ أُبَىٍّ، وَهْوَ الَّذِي كَانَ يَسْتَوْشِيهِ، وَيَجْمَعُهُ، وَهْوَ الَّذِي تَوَلَّى كِبْرَهُ مِنْهُمْ هُوَ وَحَمْنَةُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في التوبة (58:2770) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة ومحمد بن العلاء قالا: حدثنا أبو أسامة، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته. ورواه الترمذي (3180) من وجه آخر عن أبي أسامة واللفظ له.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"الذي تولى كبره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (2770/58) and al-Bukhārī (4757).","chapter_en":"The One Who Assumed the Greatest Share of the Slander","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, Mother of the Believers, reported: As for Zaynab bint Jaḥsh, Allah protected her through her religion, and she said nothing but good. Her sister Ḥamnah, however, was ruined among those who were ruined. Those who spoke about the matter included Misṭaḥ, Ḥassān ibn Thābit, and the hypocrite ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl. He was the one who encouraged and gathered the slander, and he assumed its greatest share, together with Ḥamnah."]},"buhuth":{"en":["“Yastawshīhi” means that he cultivated, managed, and promoted it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",503],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (58:2770)، والبخاري (4757)."},{"num":8904,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: لَمَّا نَزَلَ عُذْرِي قَامَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ فَذَكَرَ ذَاكَ وَتَلاَ - تَعْنِي الْقُرْآنَ - فَلَمَّا نَزَلَ مِنَ الْمِنْبَرِ أَمَرَ بِالرَّجُلَيْنِ وَالْمَرْأَةِ فَضُرِبُوا حَدَّهُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4474) والترمذي (3181) وابن ماجة (2567) وأحمد (24066) والبيهقي في الدلائل (4/74) كلهم من حديث محمد بن إسحاق، عن عبد الله بن أبي بكر، عن عمرة، عن عائشة فذكرته. وصرّح ابن إسحاق عند البيهقي.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"إقامة الحد على القاذفين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4474), al-Tirmidhī (3181), Ibn Mājah (2567), and Aḥmad (24066).","chapter_en":"Carrying Out the Prescribed Punishment upon the Slanderers","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: When the revelation vindicating me descended, the Prophet ﷺ stood upon the pulpit, mentioned the matter, and recited the Qur’an concerning it. When he descended from the pulpit, he ordered that the two men and the woman receive their prescribed punishment, and it was carried out upon them."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The two men were Ḥassān ibn Thābit and Misṭaḥ ibn Uthāthah. It was also said that the woman was Ḥamnah bint Jaḥsh. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4475)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",504],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12847],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4474)، والترمذي (3181)، وابن ماجه (2567)، وأحمد (24066)."},{"num":8905,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الزُّهْرِيِّ، قَالَ: قَالَ لِي الْوَلِيدُ بْنُ عَبْدِ المَلِكِ: أَبَلَغَكَ أَنَّ عَلِيًّا، كَانَ فِيمَنْ قَذَفَ عَائِشَةَ، قُلْتُ: لاَ. وَلَكِنْ قَدْ أَخْبَرَنِي رَجُلاَنِ مِنْ قَوْمِكِ - أَبُو سَلَمَةَ بْنُ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ وَأَبُو بَكْرِ بْنُ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ الْحَارِثِ - أَنَّ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ لهُمَا :كَانَ عَلِيٌّ مُسَلِّمًا فِي شَأْنِهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4142) عن عبد الله بن محمد، قال: أملى على هشام بن يوسف من حفظه قال: أخبرنا معمر، عن الزهري قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن عائشة فهمت من قول علي بن أبي طالب أنه ممن أساء الظن بها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4142), from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad; Hishām ibn Yūsuf dictated it to him from memory, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī.","chapter_en":"ʿĀ’ishah’s Understanding That ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib’s Words Indicated an Unfavorable Opinion of Her","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في غزوة بني المصطلق","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq","part_no":48,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Zuhrī reported: Al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik asked me, “Has it reached you that ʿAlī was among those who accused ʿĀ’ishah?” I replied, “No. However, two men from your people—Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith—have informed me that ʿĀ’ishah told them that ʿAlī had remained silent and did not involve himself in the accusation concerning her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",505],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4142)."},{"num":8906,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَرَضَهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، وَهْوَ ابْنُ أَرْبَعَ عَشْرَةَ فَلَمْ يُجِزْهُ، وَعَرَضَهُ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ وَهْوَ ابْنُ خَمْسَ عَشْرَةَ فَأَجَازَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4097) ومسلم في الإمارة (91:1868) كلاهما من طريق عبيد الله (هو ابن عمر) عن نافع، عن ابن عمر قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب غزوة الأحزاب، وتسمى أيضًا غزوة الخندق، سنة خمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4097) and Muslim (1868/91).","chapter_en":"The Campaign of the Confederates, Also Called the Battle of the Trench, in the Fifth Year","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: The Prophet ﷺ inspected him for participation on the day of Uḥud, when he was fourteen years old, but did not permit him to fight. He inspected him on the day of the Trench, when he was fifteen, and permitted him."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ جَاءَتْكُمْ جُنُودٌ فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيحًا وَجُنُودًا لَمْ تَرَوْهَا وَكَانَ اللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرًا ۝ إِذْ جَاءُوكُمْ مِنْ فَوْقِكُمْ وَمِنْ أَسْفَلَ مِنْكُمْ وَإِذْ زَاغَتِ الْأَبْصَارُ وَبَلَغَتِ الْقُلُوبُ الْحَنَاجِرَ وَتَظُنُّونَ بِاللَّهِ الظُّنُونَا﴾ [الأحزاب: ٩–١٠].","قال جمهور أهل العلم: إنها كانت في شوال سنة خمس من الهجرة، وهو رأي ابن إسحاق وعروة بن الزبير وقتادة والبيهقي وغيرهم. ومن قال: إنها كانت سنة أربع، فأراد به أنه بعد مضي أربع سنين وقبل استكمال خمس."],"en":["Allah Most High says:","“Believers, remember Allah’s favor upon you when armies came against you and We sent against them a wind and forces you could not see. Allah is All-Seeing of what you do. They came upon you from above and from below; your eyes grew wild, your hearts rose into your throats, and you entertained various thoughts about Allah.”","[Al-Aḥzāb 33:9–10]","The majority of scholars held that it occurred in Shawwāl of the fifth year after the Hijrah. This was the opinion of Ibn Isḥāq, ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, Qatādah, al-Bayhaqī, and others. Those who said that it occurred in the fourth year meant that four complete years had passed, while the fifth had not yet been completed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",509],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4097)، ومسلم (91:1868)."},{"num":8907,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ دِينَارٍ، أَنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ - رضي الله عنهما - قَالَ: أَوَّلُ يَوْمٍ شَهِدْتُهُ يَوْمُ الْخَنْدَقِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4107) عن عبدة بن عبد الله، حدثنا عبد الصمد، عن عبد الرحمن هو ابن عبد الله بن دينار، عن أبيه، أن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب غزوة الأحزاب، وتسمى أيضًا غزوة الخندق، سنة خمس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4107).","chapter_en":"The Campaign of the Confederates, Also Called the Battle of the Trench, in the Fifth Year","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported: The first battle I witnessed was the Battle of the Trench."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",510],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4107)."},{"num":8908,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ: دَخَلْتُ عَلَى حَفْصَةَ وَنَسْوَاتُهَا تَنْطُفُ، قُلْتُ: قَدْ كَانَ مِنْ أَمْرِ النَّاسِ مَا تَرَيْنَ، فَلَمْ يُجْعَلْ لِي مِنَ الأَمْرِ شَىْءٌ. فَقَالَتِ: الْحَقْ فَإِنَّهُمْ يَنْتَظِرُونَكَ، وَأَخْشَى أَنْ يَكُونَ فِي احْتِبَاسِكَ عَنْهُمْ فُرْقَةٌ. فَلَمْ تَدَعْهُ حَتَّى ذَهَبَ، فَلَمَّا تَفَرَّقَ النَّاسُ خَطَبَ مُعَاوِيَةُ، قَالَ: مَنْ كَانَ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَتَكَلَّمَ فِي هَذَا الأَمْرِ فَلْيُطْلِعْ لَنَا قَرْنَهُ، فَلَنَحْنُ أَحَقُّ بِهِ مِنْهُ وَمِنْ أَبِيهِ. قَالَ حَبِيبُ بْنُ مَسْلَمَةَ: فَهَلاَّ أَجَبْتَهُ؟ قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: فَحَلَلْتُ حُبْوَتِي، وَهَمَمْتُ أَنْ أَقُولَ: أَحَقُّ بِهَذَا الأَمْرِ مِنْكَ مَنْ قَاتَلَكَ وَأَبَاكَ عَلَى الإِسْلاَمِ. فَخَشِيتُ أَنْ أَقُولَ كَلِمَةً تُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ الْجَمْعِ، وَتَسْفِكُ الدَّمَ، وَيُحْمَلُ عَنِّي غَيْرُ ذَلِكَ، فَذَكَرْتُ مَا أَعَدَّ اللَّهُ فِي الْجِنَانِ. قَالَ حَبِيبٌ: حُفِظْتَ وَعُصِمْتَ. قَالَ مَحْمُودٌ، عَنْ عَبْدِ الرَّزَّاقِ: وَنَوْسَاتُهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4108) عن إبراهيم بن موسى أخبرنا هشام، عن معمر، عن الزهري، عن سالم، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"كان أبو سفيان من رؤوس الأحزاب يوم الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4108).","chapter_en":"Abū Sufyān Was One of the Leaders of the Confederates on the Day of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: I entered upon Ḥafṣah while her braids were dripping. I said, “You see what has happened among the people, yet I have been given no part in the matter.” She replied, “Go and join them, for they are waiting for you. I fear that your remaining away from them may cause division.” She continued urging him until he went. When the people dispersed, Muʿāwiyah delivered an address and said: “Whoever wishes to speak concerning this matter should show himself to us, for we have a greater right to it than he and his father.” Ḥabīb ibn Maslamah asked Ibn ʿUmar, “Why did you not answer him?” ʿAbdullāh replied: I loosened the cloth binding my legs and was about to say, “The one who fought you and your father for the sake of Islam has a greater right to this matter than you.” But I feared uttering a statement that would divide the community, lead to bloodshed, and be interpreted as meaning something other than what I intended. I therefore remembered what Allah has prepared in Paradise. Ḥabīb said: “You were protected and preserved.” Maḥmūd related from ʿAbd al-Razzāq the wording: “her braids.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word nasawātuhā is a scribal transposition; the correct reading is nawāsātuhā, meaning her braids. “Dripping” indicates that she had apparently bathed.","The words “You see what has happened among the people” refer to the fighting between ʿAlī and Muʿāwiyah at Ṣiffīn.","The ḥibwah was a cloth placed around the back, with its ends tied around the legs after the knees were drawn together.","The words “the one who fought you and your father for the sake of Islam” refer to Muʿāwiyah’s father, Abū Sufyān ibn Ḥarb, who was one of the leaders of the Confederates at the Battle of the Trench."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",511],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4108)."},{"num":8909,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة في قوله عز وجل: ﴿إِذْ جَاءُوكُمْ مِنْ فَوْقِكُمْ وَمِنْ أَسْفَلَ مِنْكُمْ وَإِذْ زَاغَتِ الْأَبْصَارُ وَبَلَغَتِ الْقُلُوبُ الْحَنَاجِرَ وَتَظُنُّونَ بِاللَّهِ الظُّنُونَا﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: ١٠] قالت: كان ذلك يوم الخندق."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4103) ومسلم في التفسير (12:3020) كلاهما من حديث عبدة بن سليمان، عن هشام (هو ابن عروة بن الزبير) عن أبيه، عن عائشة قالت فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حال المسلمين يوم الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4103) and Muslim (3020/12).","chapter_en":"The Condition of the Muslims on the Day of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, Mother of the Believers, said concerning Allah’s words: “They came upon you from above and from below; your eyes grew wild, your hearts rose into your throats, and you entertained various thoughts about Allah.” [Al-Aḥzāb 33:10] “That occurred on the day of the Trench.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13043],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4103)، ومسلم (12:3020)."},{"num":8910,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["8910 - عَنْ يَزِيدَ بْنِ شَرِيكٍ التميمي قَالَ: كُنَّا عِنْدَ حُذَيْفَةَ فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ: لَوْ أَدْرَكْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَاتَلْتُ مَعَهُ وَأَبْلَيْتُ، فَقَالَ حُذَيْفَةُ: أَنْتَ كُنْتَ تَفْعَلُ ذَلِكَ؟ لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيْلَةَ الأحزب، وَأَخَذَتْنَا رِيحٌ شَدِيدَةٌ وَقُرٌّ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : أَلَا رَجُلٌ يَأْتِينِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ مَعِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ؟ فَسَكَتْنَا، فَلَمْ يُجِبْهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا رَجُلٌ يَأْتِينِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ مَعِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ؟ فَسَكَتْنَا، فَلَمْ يُجِبْهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا رَجُلٌ يَأْتِينِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ مَعِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ؟ فَسَكَتْنَا، فَلَمْ يُجِبْهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ. فَقَالَ: قُمْ، يَا حُذَيْفَةُ! فَأْتِنَا بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ فَلَمْ أَجِدْ بُدًّا، إِذْ دَعَانِي بِاسْمِي، أَنْ أَقُومَ، قَالَ: اذْهَبْ، فَأْتِنِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ وَلَا تَذْعَرْهُمْ عليّ فَلَمَّا وَلَّيْتُ مِنْ عِنْدِهِ جَعَلْتُ كَأَنَّمَا أَمْشِي فِي حَمَّامٍ، حَتَّى أَتَيْتُهُمْ، فَرَأَيْتُ أَبَا سُفْيَانَ يَصْلِي ظَهْرَهُ بِالنَّارِ، فَوَضَعْتُ سَهْمًا فِي كَبِدِ الْقَوْسِ، فَأَرَدْتُ أَنْ أَرْمِيَهُ، فَذَكَرْتُ قَوْلَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : وَلَا تَذْعَرْهُمْ عَلَيَّ وَلَوْ رَمَيْتُهُ لَأَصَبْتُهُ. فَرَجَعْتُ وَأَنَا أَمْشِي فِي مِثْلِ الْحَمَّامِ، فَلَمَّا أَتَيْتُهُ أخبرته بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، وَفَرَغْتُ قُرِرْتُ، فَأَلْبَسَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ فَضْلِ عَبَاءَةٍ كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِ يُصَلِّي فِيهَا، فَلَمْ أَزَلْ نَائِمًا حَتَّى أَصْبَحْتُ فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحْتُ قَالَ: قُمْ، يَا نَوْمَانُ!"],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد والسير (99:1788) عن زهير بن حرب وإسحاق بن إبراهيم جميعاً عن جرير، عن الأعمش، عن إبراهيم التميمي، عن أبيه (يزيد بن شريك) قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حال المسلمين يوم الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1788/99).","chapter_en":"The Condition of the Muslims on the Day of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd ibn Sharīk al-Tamīmī reported: We were with Ḥudhayfah when a man said, “Had I lived in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would have fought alongside him and distinguished myself.” Ḥudhayfah asked, “Would you really have done that?” “I saw us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Confederates, when we were struck by a fierce wind and bitter cold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Will any man bring me news of the enemy, so that Allah may place him with me on the Day of Resurrection?’ We remained silent, and none of us answered him. “He repeated: ‘Will any man bring me news of the enemy, so that Allah may place him with me on the Day of Resurrection?’ We remained silent, and no one answered. He said it a third time, but we remained silent and no one answered. “He then said: ‘Rise, Ḥudhayfah, and bring us news of the enemy.’ Once he had called me by name, I had no choice but to rise. He said: ‘Go and bring me news of them, but do nothing to alarm them against me.’ “When I departed from him, it was as though I were walking inside a heated bath, until I reached them. I saw Abū Sufyān warming his back at the fire. I placed an arrow at the center of my bow and intended to shoot him, but then I remembered the Messenger of Allah’s words: ‘Do nothing to alarm them against me.’ Had I shot, I would certainly have struck him. “I returned, again feeling as though I were walking in a heated bath. When I reached the Prophet ﷺ, I informed him of the enemy’s situation. Once I had finished, I became cold, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ covered me with the extra portion of a cloak in which he had been praying. I remained asleep until morning. When morning came, he said: ‘Rise, sleepyhead!’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“Fierce wind and qurr”: qurr means intense cold.","“It was as though I were walking inside a heated bath” means that he no longer felt the cold experienced by the others. The word ḥammām is derived from ḥamīm, meaning hot water."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",514],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (99:1788)."},{"num":8911,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ قَالَ:  كُنْتُ أَنَا وَعُمَرُ بْنُ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ مَعَ النِّسْوَةِ فِي أُطُمِ حَسَّانٍَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في الفضائل (2416) من طرق عن علي بن مسهر، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن الزبير فذكره في سياق أطول.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جعل النساء والذراري في الآطام الحصينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (2416) and al-Bukhārī (3720).","chapter_en":"Placing the Women and Children Inside Fortified Strongholds","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr reported: On the day of the Trench, ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah and I were with the women inside Ḥassān’s fortified tower."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn Saʿd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would dispatch Salamah ibn Aslam with two hundred men and Zayd ibn Ḥārithah with three hundred men to guard Madinah and proclaim the takbīr aloud. He feared that Banū Qurayẓah might attack the women and children. Al-Ṭabaqāt (3/67)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",515],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2416)، والبخاري (3720)."},{"num":8912,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: جَاءَ الْحَارِثُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: نَاصِفْنَا تَمْرَ الْمَدِينَةِ، وَإِلَّا مَلَأْتُهَا عَلَيْكَ خَيْلًا وَرِجَالًا، فَقَالَ: حَتَّى أَسْتَأْمِرَ السُّعُودَ: سَعْدَ بْنَ عُبَادَةَ، وَسَعْدَ بْنَ مُعَاذٍ، يَعْنِي: يُشَاوِرُهُمَا، فَقَالَا: لَا وَاللَّهِ، مَا أُعْطِينَا الدَّنِيَّةَ مِنْ أَنْفُسِنَا فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، فَكَيْفَ وَقَدْ جَاءَ اللَّهُ بِالْإِسْلَامِ؟! فَرَجَعَ إِلَى الْحَارِثِ، فَأَخْبَرَهُ، فَقَالَ: غَدَرْتَ يَا مُحَمَّدُ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ حَسَّانُ: يَا حَارِ مَنْ يَغْدِرْ بِذِمَّةِ جَارِهِ... مِنْكُمْ فَإِنَّ مُحَمَّدًا لَا يَغْدِرْ إِنْ تَغْدِرُوا فَالْغَدْرُ مِنْ عَادَاتِكُمْ... وَاللُّؤْمُ يَنْبُتُ فِي أُصُولِ السَّخْبَرِ وَأَمَانَةُ النَّهْدِيِّ حِينَ لَقِيتُهَا.","مِثْلُ الزُّجَاجَةِ صَدْعُهَا لا يُجْبَرِ.","قَالَ: فَقَالَ الْحَارِثُ: كُفَّ عَنَّا يَا مُحَمَّدُ لِسَان حَسَّان، فَلَوْ مُزِجَ بِهِ مَاءٌ الْبَحْر لِمَزِجه."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1803) عن عقبة بن سنان، ثنا عثمان بن عثمان الغطفاني، ثنا محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب همِّ الرسول ﷺ بعقد الصلح بينه وبين غطفان ثم عدل عنه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (1803).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Consideration of a Peace Agreement with Ghaṭafān and His Subsequent Decision Not to Proceed","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: Al-Ḥārith al-Ghaṭafānī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “Muhammad, give us half the dates of Madinah, or we shall fill it against you with cavalry and men.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Let me first consult the Saʿds”—meaning Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah and Saʿd ibn Muʿādh. They said: “No, by Allah! We did not accept humiliation during the pre-Islamic period, so how could we accept it now that Allah has brought Islam?” Al-Ḥārith returned and was informed of their response, so he said, “You have betrayed us, Muhammad!” Ḥassān responded: Ḥārith, whoever betrays the protection granted his neighbor is one of you—for Muhammad never betrays. If you betray, betrayal is among your customs, and baseness grows deep within the roots of al-sakhbar. The pledge of a man of Murrah, wherever you encounter it, is like shattered glass whose fracture can never be repaired. Al-Ḥārith said: “Muhammad, restrain Ḥassān’s tongue from us! If his words were mixed with the water of the sea, they would permeate it.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال ابن إسحاق: فلما اشتد على الناس البلاء، بعث رسول الله ﷺ – فيما حدثني عاصم بن عمر بن قتادة ومن لا أتهم، عن محمد بن مسلم بن عبيد الله بن شهاب الزهري – إلى عيينة بن حصن بن حذيفة بن بدر، وإلى الحارث بن عوف بن أبي حارثة المري، وهما قائدا غطفان، فأعطاهما ثلث ثمار المدينة على أن يرجعا بمن معهما عنه وعن أصحابه.","فجرى بينه وبينهما الصلح، حتى كتبوا الكتاب، ولم تقع الشهادة ولا عزيمة الصلح، إلا المراوضة في ذلك.","فلما أراد رسول الله ﷺ أن يفعل، بعث إلى سعد بن معاذ وسعد بن عبادة، فذكر ذلك لهما واستشارهما فيه. فقالا له: يا رسول الله، أمرًا تحبه فنصنعه، أم شيئًا أمرك الله به لا بد لنا من العمل به، أم شيئًا تصنعه لنا؟","قال: «بل شيء أصنعه لكم. والله ما أصنع ذلك إلا لأنني رأيت العرب قد رمتكم عن قوس واحدة، وكالبوكم من كل جانب، فأردت أن أكسر عنكم من شوكتهم إلى أمر ما».","فقال له سعد بن معاذ: يا رسول الله، قد كنا نحن وهؤلاء القوم على الشرك بالله وعبادة الأوثان، لا نعبد الله ولا نعرفه، وهم لا يطمعون أن يأكلوا منها تمرة إلا قرًى أو بيعًا. أفحين أكرمنا الله بالإسلام، وهدانا له، وأعزنا بك وبه، نعطيهم أموالنا؟ والله ما لنا بهذا من حاجة. والله لا نعطيهم إلا السيف حتى يحكم الله بيننا وبينهم.","قال رسول الله ﷺ: «فأنت وذاك». فتناول سعد بن معاذ الصحيفة، فمحا ما فيها من الكتاب، ثم قال: ليجهدوا علينا.","سيرة ابن هشام (٢/٢٢٣)."],"en":["Ibn Isḥāq said: When the hardship became severe for the people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a proposal—as related to me by ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah and other trustworthy narrators from Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī—to ʿUyaynah ibn Ḥiṣn ibn Ḥudhayfah ibn Badr and al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAwf ibn Abī Ḥārithah al-Murrī, the two commanders of Ghaṭafān. He offered them one-third of Madinah’s produce on condition that they withdraw with their forces and leave him and his Companions.","Terms were discussed between him and them, and a document was even written. It was neither witnessed nor finalized as a binding agreement; it remained only a negotiation.","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ considered proceeding, he summoned Saʿd ibn Muʿādh and Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, informed them of the proposal, and sought their counsel. They asked: “Messenger of Allah, is this something you desire and want us to carry out, something Allah has commanded and that we must obey, or something you are doing for our sake?”","He replied: “It is something I am doing for your sake. By Allah, I am considering it only because I see that all the Arabs have shot at you from a single bow and have gathered against you from every direction. I wanted to weaken some of their force against you for a time.”","Saʿd ibn Muʿādh said: “Messenger of Allah, both we and these people once followed polytheism and worshipped idols, neither worshipping nor knowing Allah. Even then, they could not hope to eat a single date from us except as hospitality or through purchase. Now that Allah has honored us with Islam, guided us to it, and strengthened us through you and through it, should we give them our property? By Allah, we have no need for this. By Allah, we shall give them nothing but the sword until Allah judges between us and them.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Then it shall be as you say.” Saʿd ibn Muʿādh took the document and erased what had been written in it, then said: “Let them exert all their strength against us.”","The Sīrah of Ibn Hishām (2/223)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",517],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في «كشف الأستار» (1803)."},{"num":8913,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَهْلِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الْخَنْدَقِ، وَهُمْ يَحْفِرُونَ، وَنَحْنُ نَنْقُلُ التُّرَابَ عَلَى أَكْتَادِنَا، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اللَّهُمَّ لاَ عَيْشَ إِلاَّ عَيْشُ الآخِرَهْ، فَاغْفِرْ لِلْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالأَنْصَارِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4098) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (126:1804) كلاهما من طريق عبد العزيز بن أبي حازم، عن أبيه، عن سهل بن سعد قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أمر النبي ﷺ بحفر الخندق حول المدينة وحث أصحابه على ذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4098) and Muslim (1804/126).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Order to Dig the Trench Around Madinah and His Encouragement of His Companions","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd reported: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the Trench. They were digging while we carried the soil upon our backs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, there is no true life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Emigrants and the Anṣār.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word aktādinā is the plural of katid, meaning the area extending from the withers toward the back. Muslim’s version reads “upon our shoulders.”","The trench was situated along the northwestern side of Madinah because that was the only exposed approach. The other sides were protected by palm groves, dense cultivated lands, mountains, and other natural barriers."]},"intro":{"ar":["ذكر أصحاب المغازي أن الذي أشار إلى حفر الخندق هو سلمان الفارسي، قائلًا: يا رسول الله، إنا كنا بفارس إذا حوصرنا خندقنا علينا. مغازي الواقدي (٢/٤٤٥)."],"en":["The historians of the campaigns stated that Salmān al-Fārisī was the one who suggested digging the trench. He said: “Messenger of Allah, when we were besieged in Persia, we would dig a trench around ourselves.” Maghāzī al-Wāqidī (2/445)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",518],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4098)، ومسلم (126:1804)."},{"num":8914,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس قَالَ: خَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى الْخَنْدَقِ فَإِذَا الْمُهَاجِرُونَ وَالأَنْصَارُ يَحْفِرُونَ فِي غَدَاةٍ بَارِدَةٍ، فَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُمْ عَبِيدٌ يَعْمَلُونَ ذَلِكَ لَهُمْ، فَلَمَّا رَأَى مَا بِهِمْ مِنَ النَّصَبِ وَالْجُوعِ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّ الْعَيْشَ عَيْشُ الآخرة، فَاغْفِرْ لِلأَنْصَارِ والمهاجرة فَقَالُوا مُجِيبِينَ لَهُ: نَحْنُ الَّذِينَ بَايَعُوا مُحَمَّدَا عَلَى الْجِهَادِ مَا بَقِينَا أَبَدَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4099) عن عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا معاوية بن عمرو، حدثنا أبو إسحاق، عن حميد (هو الطويل) عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أمر النبي ﷺ بحفر الخندق حول المدينة وحث أصحابه على ذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4099) and Muslim (1805/130).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Order to Dig the Trench Around Madinah and His Encouragement of His Companions","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the Trench and found the Emigrants and the Anṣār digging on a cold morning. They had no servants to perform that labor for them. When he saw their exhaustion and hunger, he said: “O Allah, the true life is the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Anṣār and the Emigrants.” They answered him: We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad to strive as long as we remain alive."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",519],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4099)، ومسلم (1805/130)."},{"num":8915,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: جَعَلَ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ وَالأَنْصَارُ يَحْفِرُونَ الْخَنْدَقَ حَوْلَ الْمَدِينَةِ، وَيَنْقُلُونَ التُّرَابَ عَلَى مُتُونِهِمْ وَهُمْ يَقُولُونَ: نَحْنُ الَّذِينَ بَايَعُوا مُحَمَّدَا عَلَى الإِسْلاَمِ مَا بَقِينَا أَبَدَا.","قَالَ: يَقُولُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ يُجِيبُهُمْ:","اللهُمَّ إِنَّهُ لَا خَيْرَ إِلَّا خَيْرُ الْآخِرَهْ.","فَبَارِكْ فِي الْأَنْصَارِ وَالْمُهَاجِرَهْ.","قَالَ: يُؤْتَوْنَ بِمِلْءِ كَفَّى مِنَ الشَّعِيرِ، فَيُصْنَعُ لَهُمْ بِإِهَالَةٍ سَنِخَةٍ تُوضَعُ بَيْنَ يَدَىِ الْقَوْمِ، وَالْقَوْمُ جِيَاعٌ، وَهْىَ بَشِعَةٌ فِي الْحَلْقِ وَلَهَا رِيحٌ مُنْتِنٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4100) عن أبي معمر، حدثنا عبد الوارث، عن عبد العزيز (هو ابن صهيب) عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أمر النبي ﷺ بحفر الخندق حول المدينة وحث أصحابه على ذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4100).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Order to Dig the Trench Around Madinah and His Encouragement of His Companions","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: The Emigrants and the Anṣār began digging the trench around Madinah and carrying soil upon their backs while chanting: We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad to remain upon Islam for as long as we live. The Prophet ﷺ answered them: “O Allah, there is no true good except the good of the Hereafter, so bless the Anṣār and the Emigrants.” A quantity of barley filling two cupped hands would be brought and prepared for them with rancid fat. It would be placed before the men while they were hungry, though it tasted repulsive in the throat and had a foul odor."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ihālah means fat used as a condiment, whether oil, clarified butter, or animal fat.","Sanikhah means that its taste and color had changed because of age.","Bashiʿah means foul-tasting and unpleasant in the throat."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",520],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7380],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4100)."},{"num":8916,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَنَّهُ قَالَ:  اللَّهُمَّ لَا عَيْشَ إِلَّا عَيْشُ الْآخِرَهْ … فَاغْفِرْ لِلْأَنْصَارِ وَالْمُهَاجِرَهْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3795) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (127:1805) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، حدثنا أبو إياس معاوية بن قرة، عن أنس بن مالك قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أمر النبي ﷺ بحفر الخندق حول المدينة وحث أصحابه على ذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3795) and Muslim (1805/127).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Order to Dig the Trench Around Madinah and His Encouragement of His Companions","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, there is no true life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Anṣār and the Emigrants.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",521],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3795)، ومسلم (127:1805)."},{"num":8917,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ: والله لَوْلَا اللَّهِ مَا اهْتَدَيْنَا وَلَا تصدقنا وَلَا صَلَّيْنَا فَأَنْزِلَنْ سَكِينَةً عَلَيْنَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1804) وأبو يعلى (3395) كلاهما من حديث محمد بن المثنى، ثنا زكريا بن يحيى، قال: سمعت ثابتا البناني، يحدث عن أنس بن مالك فذكره. وإسناده حسن من أجل زكريا بن يحيى وهو ابن عمارة الأنصاري، وقد ينسب إلى جده مختلف فيه غير أنه حسن الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أمر النبي ﷺ بحفر الخندق حول المدينة وحث أصحابه على ذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (1804) and Abū Yaʿlā (3395).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Order to Dig the Trench Around Madinah and His Encouragement of His Companions","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: On the day of the Trench, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: By Allah, had Allah not guided us, we would never have found guidance, nor given charity, nor performed prayer. So send tranquility down upon us."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",522],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في «كشف الأستار» (1804)، وأبو يعلى (3395)."},{"num":8918,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ سَلَمَةَ، قَالَتْ: مَا نَسِيتُ قَوْلَهُ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ وَهُوَ يُعَاطِيهِمُ اللَّبَنَ، وَقَدْ اغْبَرَّ شَعْرُ صَدْرِهِ، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: اللهُمَّ إِنَّ الْخَيْرَ خَيْرُ الْآخِرَهْ فَاغْفِرْ لِلْأَنْصَارِ وَالْمُهَاجِرَهْ.","قَالَ: فَرَأَى عَمَّارًا فَقَالَ: وَيْحَكَ ابْنَ سُمَيَّةَ تَقْتُلُهُ الْفِئَةُ الْبَاغِيَةُ.","قَالَ: فَذَكَرْتُهُ لِمُحَمَّدٍ –– يَعْنِي ابْنَ سِيرِينَ –– فَقَالَ: عَنْ أُمِّهِ؟ قُلْت: نَعَمْ، أَمَا إِنَّهَا كَانَتْ تُخَالِطُهَا تَلِجُ عَلَيْهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (26482) وأبو يعلى (1645) كلاهما من حديث ابن عون، عن الحسن، عن أمه، عن أم سلمة فذكرته، واللفظ لأحمد،","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أمر النبي ﷺ بحفر الخندق حول المدينة وحث أصحابه على ذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (26482) and Abū Yaʿlā (1645). This wording is Aḥmad’s.","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Order to Dig the Trench Around Madinah and His Encouragement of His Companions","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah reported: I have never forgotten what he said on the day of the Trench as he handed the workers bricks, while the hair upon his chest had become covered with dust. He was saying: “O Allah, the true good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Anṣār and the Emigrants.” He then saw ʿAmmār and said: “Alas for you, son of Sumayyah! The rebellious faction will kill you.” The narrator said: I mentioned this report to Muḥammad—meaning Ibn Sīrīn—and he asked, “Did he narrate it from his mother?” I replied, “Yes. She used to associate closely with Umm Salamah and enter upon her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",523],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (26482)، وأبو يعلى (1645)، واللفظ لأحمد."},{"num":8919,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ وَهُوَ يَنْقُلُ التُّرَابَ حَتَّى وَارَى التُّرَابُ شَعَرَ صَدْرِهِ، وَكَانَ رَجُلاً كَثِيرَ الشَّعَرِ وَهْوَ يَرْتَجِزُ بِرَجَزِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ اللَّهُمَّ لَوْلاَ أَنْتَ مَا اهْتَدَيْنَا وَلاَ تَصَدَّقْنَا وَلاَ صَلَّيْنَا فَأَنْزِلَنْ سَكِينَةً عَلَيْنَا وَثَبِّتِ الأَقْدَامَ إِنْ لاَقَيْنَا إِنَّ الأَعْدَاءَ قَدْ بَغَوْا عَلَيْنَا.","إِذَا أَرَادُوا فِتْنَةً أَبَيْنَا.","يرفع بها صوته.،في رواية : إن الألى قد بغوا علينا ..."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (3034) من طريق أبي الأحوص، ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (125:1803) من طريق شعبة – كلاهما عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء، فذكره واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إنشاد الشعر والرجز في غزوة الخندق لأجل العمل والتنشيط","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3034) and Muslim (1803/125). This wording is al-Bukhārī’s.","chapter_en":"Reciting Poetry and Martial Verse During the Campaign of the Trench to Encourage the Workers","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ reported: I saw the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the Trench carrying soil until the dust covered the hair of his chest—and he was a man with abundant body hair. He was chanting the martial verses of ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah: O Allah, had it not been for You, we would never have found guidance, nor given charity, nor performed prayer. So send tranquility down upon us, and make our feet firm when we meet the enemy. The enemies have indeed transgressed against us; whenever they desire sedition, we refuse. He raised his voice while reciting it. Another narration reads: “Those people have indeed transgressed against us.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",524],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3034)، ومسلم (125:1803)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":8920,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: لَمَّا حُفِرَ الْخَنْدَقُ رَأَيْتُ بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَمَصًا شَدِيدًا، فَانْكَفَأْتُ إِلَى امْرَأَتِي، فَقُلْتُ: هَلْ عِنْدَكِ شَىْءٌ؟ فَإِنِّي رَأَيْتُ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَمَصًا شَدِيدًا. فَأَخْرَجَتْ إِلَىَّ جِرَابًا فِيهِ صَاعٌ مِنْ شَعِيرٍ، وَلَنَا بُهَيْمَةٌ دَاجِنٌ فَذَبَحْتُهَا، وَطَحَنَتِ الشَّعِيرَ، فَفَرَغَتْ إِلَى فَرَاغِي، وَقَطَّعْتُهَا فِي بُرْمَتِهَا، ثُمَّ وَلَّيْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ: لاَ تَفْضَحْنِي بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَبِمَنْ مَعَهُ. فَجِئْتُهُ فَسَارَرْتُهُ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ذَبَحْنَا بُهَيْمَةً لَنَا وَطَحَنَّا صَاعًا مِنْ شَعِيرٍ كَانَ عِنْدَنَا، فَتَعَالَ أَنْتَ وَنَفَرٌ مَعَكَ. فَصَاحَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا أَهْلَ الْخَنْدَقِ، إِنَّ جَابِرًا قَدْ صَنَعَ سُورًا، فَحَىَّ هَلاً بِكُمْ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لاَ تُنْزِلُنَّ بُرْمَتَكُمْ، وَلاَ تَخْبِزُنَّ عَجِينَكُمْ حَتَّى أَجِيءَ. فَجِئْتُ وَجَاءَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقْدُمُ النَّاسَ حَتَّى جِئْتُ امْرَأَتِي، فَقَالَتْ: بِكَ وَبِكَ. فَقُلْتُ: قَدْ فَعَلْتُ الَّذِي قُلْتِ. فَأَخْرَجَتْ لَهُ عَجِينًا، فَبَصَقَ فِيهِ وَبَارَكَ، ثُمَّ عَمَدَ إِلَى بُرْمَتِنَا فَبَصَقَ وَبَارَكَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: ادْعُ خَابِزَةً فَلْتَخْبِزْ مَعِي، وَاقْدَحِي مِنْ بُرْمَتِكُمْ وَلاَ تُنْزِلُوهَا، وَهُمْ أَلْفٌ، فَأُقْسِمُ بِاللَّهِ لَقَدْ أَكَلُوا حَتَّى تَرَكُوهُ وَانْحَرَفُوا، وَإِنَّ بُرْمَتَنَا لَتَغِطُّ كَمَا هِيَ، وَإِنَّ عَجِينَنَا لَيُخْبَزُ كَمَا هُوَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4102) ومسلم في الأشربة (141:2039) كلاهما من طريق أبي عاصم الضحاك بن مخلد بن حنظلة بن أبي سفيان، أخبرنا سعيد بن ميناء، قال: سمعت جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"المعجزات التي ظهرت أثناء حفر الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4102) and Muslim (2039/141).","chapter_en":"Miracles That Appeared During the Digging of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: While the trench was being dug, I noticed that the Prophet ﷺ was suffering from severe hunger. I returned to my wife and asked, “Do you have anything? I have seen that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is suffering from intense hunger.” She brought out a leather bag containing one ṣāʿ of barley. We also had a young domesticated animal, so I slaughtered it while she ground the barley. She finished at the same time as I did, and I cut the meat and placed it in a cooking pot. When I was about to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, my wife said: “Do not disgrace me before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those with him by bringing more people than the food can feed.” I went to him and spoke privately, saying: “Messenger of Allah, we have slaughtered a young animal and ground a ṣāʿ of barley that we had. Come with a few people.” The Prophet ﷺ called aloud: “People of the Trench! Jābir has prepared a meal, so come along quickly!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then instructed me: “Do not remove your pot from the fire, and do not bake your dough until I arrive.” I returned home while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came leading the people. When I reached my wife, she rebuked me, saying, “What have you done!” I replied, “I did exactly what you told me: I spoke to him privately.” She brought the dough to the Prophet ﷺ. He spat lightly into it and invoked Allah’s blessing. He then went to the cooking pot, spat lightly into it, and invoked Allah’s blessing. He said: “Call another woman to help you bake. Ladle food from your pot, but do not take it off the fire.” They numbered one thousand. By Allah, they continued eating until they were satisfied and departed. Our pot continued bubbling as before, and our dough continued being baked as though none had been taken from it."]},"buhuth":{"en":["“Khamaṣ” means hunger—the emptiness of the stomach from food.","A jirāb is a leather container in which provisions and similar things are stored.","“Ḥayyahala bikum” is an expression of invitation and encouragement, meaning: “Come quickly.”","The statement that they numbered one thousand is the correct version because it contains additional information. The differing numbers cannot be understood as referring to separate incidents, since this event occurred only once."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",526],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4102)، ومسلم (141:2039)."},{"num":8921,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر قَالَ: إِنَّا يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ نَحْفِرُ، فَعَرَضَتْ كُدْيَةٌ شَدِيدَةٌ، فجاؤوا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالُوا: هَذِهِ كُدْيَةٌ عَرَضَتْ فِي الْخَنْدَقِ، فَقَالَ: أَنَا نَازِلٌ. ثُمَّ قَامَ وَبَطْنُهُ مَعْصُوبٌ بِحَجَرٍ، وَلَبِثْنَا ثَلاَثَةَ أَيَّامٍ لاَ نَذُوقُ ذَوَاقًا، فَأَخَذَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْمِعْوَلَ فَضَرَبَ فِي الكدية، فَعَادَ كَثِيبًا أَهْيَلَ، أَوْ أَهْيَمَ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، ائْذَنْ لِي إِلَى الْبَيْتِ، فَقُلْتُ لاِمْرَأَتِي: رَأَيْتُ بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ شَيْئًا مَا كَانَ فِي ذَلِكَ صَبْرٌ، فَعِنْدَكِ شيء ؟ قَالَتْ: عِنْدِي شَعِيرٌ وَعَنَاقٌ، فَذَبَحْتُ الْعَنَاقَ، وَطَحَنَتِ الشَّعِيرَ حَتَّى جَعَلْنَا اللَّحْمَ فِي الْبُرْمَةِ، ثُمَّ جِئْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْعَجِينُ قَدِ انْكَسَرَ، وَالْبُرْمَةُ بَيْنَ الأَثَافِيِّ قَدْ كَادَتْ تَنْضَجَ، فَقُلْتُ: طُعَيِّمٌ لِي، فَقُمْ أَنْتَ يَا رَسُولَ وَرَجُلٌ أَوْ رَجُلاَنِ، قَالَ: كَمْ هُوَ؟. فَذَكَرْتُ لَهُ، قَالَ: كَثِيرٌ طَيِّبٌ، قَالَ: قُلْ لَهَا: لاَ تَنْزِعُ الْبُرْمَةَ، وَلاَ الْخُبْزَ مِنَ التَّنُّورِ حَتَّى آتِيَ، فَقَالَ: قُومُوا. فَقَامَ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ وَالأَنْصَارُ، فَلَمَّا دَخَلَ عَلَى امْرَأَتِهِ قَالَ: وَيْحَكِ جَاءَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالأَنْصَارِ وَمَنْ مَعَهُمْ، قَالَتْ: هَلْ سَأَلَكَ ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ، فَقَالَ: ادْخُلُوا وَلاَ تَضَاغَطُوا. فَجَعَلَ يَكْسِرُ الْخُبْزَ، وَيَجْعَلُ عَلَيْهِ اللَّحْمَ، وَيُخَمِّرُ الْبُرْمَةَ وَالتَّنُّورَ إِذَا أَخَذَ مِنْهُ، وَيُقَرِّبُ إِلَى أَصْحَابِهِ ثُمَّ يَنْزِعُ، فَلَمْ يَزَلْ يَكْسِرُ الْخُبْزَ، وَيَغْرِفُ حَتَّى شَبِعُوا وَبَقِيَ بَقِيَّةٌ، قَالَ: كُلِي هَذَا وَأَهْدِي، فَإِنَّ النَّاسَ أَصَابَتْهُمْ مَجَاعَةٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4101) عن خلاد بن يحيى حدثنا عبدالواحد بن أيمن، عن أبيه قال: أتيت جابراً فقال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"المعجزات التي ظهرت أثناء حفر الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4101).","chapter_en":"Miracles That Appeared During the Digging of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir reported: While we were digging on the day of the Trench, we encountered a mass of extremely hard earth. The men came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “A hard obstruction has appeared in the trench.” He replied: “I shall go down.” He rose with a stone tied against his stomach. We had remained for three days without tasting any food. The Prophet ﷺ took the pickaxe and struck the obstruction, whereupon it became a loose mound of sand that flowed apart. I said, “Messenger of Allah, permit me to go home.” I went to my wife and said, “I have seen the Prophet ﷺ in a condition that I cannot patiently bear. Do you have anything?” She replied, “I have some barley and a young goat.” I slaughtered the goat, and she ground the barley. We then placed the meat in the cooking pot. I then went to the Prophet ﷺ after the dough had become ready and the pot, set upon its three stones, was nearly cooked. I said, “I have prepared a small meal. Come, Messenger of Allah, with one or two men.” He asked: “How much is there?” I told him, and he said: “That is abundant and good.” He instructed me: “Tell her not to remove the pot from the fire or the bread from the oven until I arrive.” He then said to the people: “Rise.” The Emigrants and the Anṣār all rose. When Jābir entered upon his wife, he said, “What shall we do! The Prophet ﷺ has come with the Emigrants, the Anṣār, and those accompanying them.” She asked, “Did he ask you how much food we had?” I replied, “Yes.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Enter without crowding one another.” He began breaking the bread, placing meat upon it, and covering the pot and oven each time he took food from them. He presented it to his Companions, then returned for more. He continued breaking bread and ladling food until everyone was satisfied, and some food still remained. He then said to Jābir’s wife: “Eat from this and give some away as gifts, for the people have been afflicted by hunger.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“A loose mound of sand” means that it became flowing sand that would not hold together. Ah-yam has the same meaning as ahyal.","Jābir’s wife was Sahlah bint Masʿūd ibn Aws al-Anṣāriyyah, may Allah be pleased with her.","A burmah is a cooking pot.","Athāfī is the plural of uthfiyyah: one of the three stones erected to support a cooking pot.","“Do not press against one another” means: Do not crowd together."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",527],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4101)."},{"num":8922,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ رَجُلٍ، مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَمَّا أَمَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِحَفْرِ الْخَنْدَقِ، عَرَضَتْ لَهُمْ صَخْرَةٌ حَالَتْ بَيْنَهُمْ، وَبَيْنَ الْحَفْرِ، فَقَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَخَذَ الْمِعْوَلَ، وَوَضَعَ رِدَاءَهُ نَاحِيَةَ الْخَنْدَقِ وَقَالَ: { تَمَّتْ كَلِمَةُ رَبِّكَ صِدْقًا وَعَدْلاً لاَ مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَاتِهِ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ }. فَنَدَرَ ثُلُثُ الْحَجَرِ، وَسَلْمَانُ الْفَارِسِيُّ قَائِمٌ يَنْظُرُ، فَبَرَقَ مَعَ ضَرْبَةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَرْقَةٌ، ثُمَّ ضَرَبَ الثَّانِيَةَ وَقَالَ: { تَمَّتْ كَلِمَةُ رَبِّكَ صِدْقًا وَعَدْلاً لاَ مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَاتِهِ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ }. فَنَدَرَ الثُّلُثُ الآخَرُ، فَبَرَقَتْ بَرْقَةٌ، فَرَآهَا سَلْمَانُ، ثُمَّ ضَرَبَ الثَّالِثَةَ وَقَالَ: { تَمَّتْ كَلِمَةُ رَبِّكَ صِدْقًا وَعَدْلاً لاَ مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَاتِهِ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ }. فَنَدَرَ الثُّلُثُ الْبَاقِي، وَخَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَخَذَ رِدَاءَهُ وَجَلَسَ. قَالَ سَلْمَانُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! رَأَيْتُكَ حِينَ ضَرَبْتَ مَا تَضْرِبُ ضَرْبَةً، إِلاَّ كَانَتْ مَعَهَا بَرْقَةٌ. قَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا سَلْمَانُ، رَأَيْتَ ذَلِكَ. فَقَالَ: إِي وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: فَإِنِّي حِينَ ضَرَبْتُ الضَّرْبَةَ الْأُولَى، رُفِعَتْ لِي مَدَائِنُ كِسْرَى وَمَا حَوْلَهَا، وَمَدَائِنُ كَثِيرَةٌ، حَتَّى رَأَيْتُهَا بِعَيْنَىَّ. قَالَ لَهُ مَنْ حَضَرَهُ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! ادْعُ اللَّهَ أَنْ يَفْتَحَهَا عَلَيْنَا، وَيُغَنِّمَنَا دِيَارَهُمْ، وَيُخَرِّبَ بِأَيْدِينَا بِلاَدَهُمْ. فَدَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِذَلِكَ. ثُمَّ ضَرَبْتُ الضَّرْبَةَ الثَّانِيَةَ فَرُفِعَتْ لِي مَدَائِنُ قَيْصَرَ وَمَا حَوْلَهَا، حَتَّى رَأَيْتُهَا بِعَيْنَىَّ. قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! ادْعُ اللَّهَ أَنْ يَفْتَحَهَا عَلَيْنَا، وَيُغَنِّمَنَا دِيَارَهُمْ، وَيُخَرِّبَ بِأَيْدِينَا بِلاَدَهُمْ. فَدَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِذَلِكَ. ثُمَّ ضَرَبْتُ الثَّالِثَةَ، فَرُفِعَتْ لِي مَدَائِنُ الْحَبَشَةِ. وَمَا حَوْلَهَا مِنَ الْقُرَى، حَتَّى رَأَيْتُهَا بِعَيْنَىَّ. قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عِنْدَ ذَلِكَ: دَعُوا الْحَبَشَةَ مَا وَدَعُوكُمْ، وَاتْرُكُوا التُّرْكَ مَا تَرَكُوكُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3176) عن عيسى بن يونس، قال: حدثنا ضمرة، عن أبي زرعة السَّيباني، عن أبي سكينة رجل من المحرّرين، عن رجل من أصحاب النبيصلى الله عليه وسلم فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"المعجزات التي ظهرت أثناء حفر الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī (3176), whose wording this is, and Abū Dāwūd (4302).","chapter_en":"Miracles That Appeared During the Digging of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["A man among the Prophet’s Companions reported: When the Prophet ﷺ ordered that the trench be dug, the workers encountered a rock that prevented them from continuing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose, took the pickaxe, placed his cloak beside the trench, and recited: “The word of your Lord has been perfected in truth and justice. None can alter His words, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.” [Al-Anʿām 6:115] A third of the rock broke away. Salmān al-Fārisī was standing and watching, and a flash of light appeared with the Messenger of Allah’s blow. He struck a second time and recited: “The word of your Lord has been perfected in truth and justice. None can alter His words, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.” Another third of the rock broke away, and a flash appeared that Salmān saw. He struck a third time and recited the same verse. The remaining third broke away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed out, took his cloak, and sat down. Salmān said, “Messenger of Allah, whenever you struck, I saw a flash accompanying the blow.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Salmān, did you see that?” He replied, “Yes, by Him who sent you with the truth, Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “When I struck the first blow, the cities of Chosroes and their surroundings, along with many other cities, were displayed before me until I saw them with my own eyes.” The Companions present said: “Messenger of Allah, pray that Allah will grant us their conquest, give us their lands as spoils, and bring about the destruction of their power at our hands.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for that. He continued: “When I struck the second blow, the cities of Caesar and their surroundings were displayed before me until I saw them with my own eyes.” They said, “Messenger of Allah, pray that Allah will grant us their conquest, give us their lands as spoils, and bring about the destruction of their power at our hands.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for that. He continued: “When I struck the third blow, the cities of Abyssinia and the surrounding villages were displayed before me until I saw them with my own eyes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “Leave the Abyssinians alone as long as they leave you alone, and leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3176) واللفظ له، وأبو داود (4302)."},{"num":8923,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: أَرِقَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ لَيْلَةٍ فَقَالَ: لَيْتَ رَجُلاً صَالِحًا مِنْ أَصْحَابِي يَحْرُسُنِي اللَّيْلَةَ. إِذْ سَمِعْنَا صَوْتَ السِّلاَحِ قَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا. قِيلَ سَعْدٌ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ جِئْتُ أَحْرُسُكَ. فَنَامَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى سَمِعْنَا غَطِيطَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التمني (7231) ومسلم في الفضائل (2410) كلاهما من حديث سليمان بن بلال، حدثني يحيى بن سعيد، سمعت عبد الله بن عامر بن ربيعة قال: قالت عائشة: فذكرته. واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حراسة النبي ﷺ يوم الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7231) and Muslim (2410). This wording is al-Bukhārī’s.","chapter_en":"Guarding the Prophet ﷺ During the Battle of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: The Prophet ﷺ was unable to sleep one night and said: “If only a righteous man from among my Companions would guard me tonight.” We then heard the sound of weapons. He asked: “Who is there?” The man replied, “Saʿd, Messenger of Allah. I have come to guard you.” The Prophet ﷺ then slept until we could hear him breathing deeply in his sleep."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In Muslim’s narration, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: “What brought you here?” He replied, “I became concerned for the safety of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I came to guard him.” The Prophet ﷺ prayed for him and then went to sleep.","The Saʿd mentioned here was Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, as explicitly stated in other narrations."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",529],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9952,14648],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7231)، ومسلم (2410)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":8924,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الأَحْزَابِ: مَنْ يَأْتِينَا بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ؟ فَقَالَ الزُّبَيْرُ: أَنَا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: مَنْ يَأْتِينَا بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ؟ فَقَالَ الزُّبَيْرُ: أَنَا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: مَنْ يَأْتِينَا بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ؟ فَقَالَ الزُّبَيْرُ: أَنَا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: إِنَّ لِكُلِّ نَبِيٍّ حَوَارِيًّا، وَإِنَّ حواريي الزُّبَيْرُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4113) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (48:2415) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، عن محمد بن المنكدر، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب شجاعة الزبير يوم الأحزاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4113) and Muslim (2415/48).","chapter_en":"Al-Zubayr’s Courage on the Day of the Confederates","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: On the day of the Confederates, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who will bring us news of the people?” Al-Zubayr said, “I will.” He asked a second time: “Who will bring us news of the people?” Al-Zubayr again said, “I will.” He asked a third time, and al-Zubayr again volunteered. The Prophet ﷺ then said: “Every prophet has a devoted disciple, and my devoted disciple is al-Zubayr.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words “Who will bring us news of the people?” refer to obtaining news about Banū Qurayẓah’s breach of their covenant. Ḥudhayfah’s mission, by contrast, was to obtain news about Quraysh and took place during a bitterly cold night."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",530],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4113)، ومسلم (48:2415)."},{"num":8925,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن أَبِي أَوْفَى رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يَقُولُ دَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الأَحْزَابِ فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ مُنْزِلَ الْكِتَابِ، سَرِيعَ الْحِسَابِ، اهْزِمِ الأَحْزَابَ، اللَّهُمَّ اهْزِمْهُمْ وَزَلْزِلْهُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4115) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (21:1741) كلاهما من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن عبدالله بن أبي أوفى، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ يوم الأحزاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4115) and Muslim (1741/21).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Supplications on the Day of the Confederates","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against the Confederates, saying: “O Allah, Revealer of the Book and Swift in reckoning, defeat the Confederates. O Allah, defeat them and shake them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",531],"full":1,"rep":[7874,13051],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4115)، ومسلم (21:1741)."},{"num":8926,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ: مَلأَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ بُيُوتَهُمْ وَقُبُورَهُمْ نَارًا كَمَا شَغَلُونَا عَنْ صَلاَةِ الْوُسْطَى حَتَّى غَابَتِ الشَّمْسُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4111) ومسلم في المساجد ومواضع الصلاة (202:627) كلاهما من طريق هشام (هو الدستوائي) عن محمد (هو ابن سيرين) عن عبيدة (هو السلماني) عن علي قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ يوم الأحزاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4111) and Muslim (627/202).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Supplications on the Day of the Confederates","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib reported that the Prophet ﷺ said on the day of the Trench: “May Allah fill their houses and graves with fire, just as they kept us occupied from the middle prayer until the sun set.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",532],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4111)، ومسلم (202:627)."},{"num":8927,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، أَنَّ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ جَاءَ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ بَعْدَ مَا غَرَبَتِ الشَّمْسُ جَعَلَ يَسُبُّ كُفَّارَ قُرَيْشٍ قَالَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مَا كِدْتُ أَنْ أُصَلِّيَ حَتَّى كَادَتِ الشَّمْسُ أَنْ تَغْرُبَ. قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَاللَّهِ مَا صَلَّيْتُهَا فَنَزَلْنَا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بُطْحَانَ، فَتَوَضَّأَ لِلصَّلاَةِ وَتَوَضَّأْنَا لَهَا، فَصَلَّى الْعَصْرَ بَعْدَ مَا غَرَبَتِ الشَّمْسُ، ثُمَّ صَلَّى بَعْدَهَا الْمَغْرِبَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4112) ومسلم في المساجد ومواضع الصلاة (209:631) كلاهما من طريق هشام (هو ابن عبد الله الدستوائي) عن يحيى بن أبي كثير، حدثنا أبو سلمة بن عبد الرحمن، عن جابر بن عبد الله رضي الله عنهما قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ يوم الأحزاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4112) and Muslim (631/209).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Supplications on the Day of the Confederates","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: On the day of the Trench, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came after sunset, denouncing the disbelievers of Quraysh. He said, “Messenger of Allah, I was barely able to perform the afternoon prayer before the sun was about to set.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “By Allah, I have not yet performed it.” We went down with the Prophet ﷺ to Buṭḥān. He performed ablution for prayer, and we did likewise. He performed the afternoon prayer after sunset, then performed the sunset prayer afterward."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",533],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4112)، ومسلم (209:631)."},{"num":8928,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قُلْنَا لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ وَقَدْ بَلَغَ مِنَّا الْجَهْدُ: هَلْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ نَقُولُهُ؟ قَالَ: قُولُوا: اللَّهُمَّ اسْتُرْ عَوْرَاتِنَا، وَآمِنْ رَوْعَاتِنَا. قَالَ: فهزم اللَّهُ بِالرِّيحِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (3119) عن محمد بن المثنى، ثنا أبو عامر عبد الملك بن عمرو، ثنا الزبير بن عبد الله، ويقال: ابن رهيمة من أهل المدينة، عن ربيح بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي سعيد، عن أبيه، عن جده فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ يوم الأحزاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3119).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s Supplications on the Day of the Confederates","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported: On the day of the Trench, when hardship had reached its limit for us, we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Is there anything we should say?” He replied: “Say: O Allah, conceal our vulnerabilities and calm our fears.” Allah then defeated the enemy by means of the wind."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",534],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11150,13044],"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في «كشف الأستار» (3119)."},{"num":8929,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَقُولُ: لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ، أَعَزَّ جُنْدَهُ، وَنَصَرَ عَبْدَهُ، وَغَلَبَ الأَحْزَابَ وَحْدَهُ، فَلاَ شَىْءَ بَعْدَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4114) ومسلم في الذكر والدعاء (77:2724) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا الليث، عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد، عن أبيه (هو أبو سعيد المقبري) عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن الله هو الذي هزم الأحزاب ونصر النبي ﷺ بالصَّبا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4114) and Muslim (2724/77).","chapter_en":"Allah Alone Defeated the Confederates and Supported the Prophet ﷺ with the East Wind","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: “There is no deity except Allah alone. He strengthened His army, granted victory to His servant, and defeated the Confederates by Himself. Nothing remains after Him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words “He defeated the Confederates by Himself; nothing remains after Him” are an example of praiseworthy rhymed prose. Blameworthy rhymed prose is contrived and forced, whereas praiseworthy rhyming arises naturally and harmoniously."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",535],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13053],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4114)، ومسلم (77:2724)."},{"num":8930,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ إِذَا قَفَلَ مِنَ الْغَزْوِ، أَوِ الْحَجِّ، أَوِ الْعُمْرَةِ، يَبْدَأُ فَيُكَبِّرُ ثَلاَثَ مِرَارٍ، ثُمَّ يَقُولُ: لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ، وَحْدَهُ لاَ شَرِيكَ لَهُ، لَهُ الْمُلْكُ، وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ، وَهْوَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ، آيِبُونَ تَائِبُونَ عَابِدُونُ سَاجِدُونَ، لِرَبِّنَا حَامِدُونَ، صَدَقَ اللَّهُ وَعْدَهُ، وَنَصَرَ عَبْدَهُ، وَهَزَمَ الأَحْزَابَ وَحْدَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4116) ومسلم في الحج (428:1344) كلاهما من طريق نافع عن عبد الله بن عمر قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن الله هو الذي هزم الأحزاب ونصر النبي ﷺ بالصَّبا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4116) and Muslim (1344/428).","chapter_en":"Allah Alone Defeated the Confederates and Supported the Prophet ﷺ with the East Wind","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported: Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a military expedition, pilgrimage, or ʿumrah, he would begin by proclaiming Allah’s greatness three times and then say: “There is no deity except Allah alone, without partner. To Him belongs all sovereignty and praise, and He has power over all things. We return repentant, worshipping, prostrating, and praising our Lord. Allah fulfilled His promise, granted victory to His servant, and defeated the Confederates by Himself.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",536],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4116)، ومسلم (428:1344)."},{"num":8931,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عَبَّاسٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: نُصِرْتُ بِالصَّبَا، وَأُهْلِكَتْ عَادٌ بِالدَّبُورِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4105) ومسلم في صلاة الاستسقاء (17:900) كلاهما عن طريق شعبة، حدثني الحكم، عن مجاهد، عن ابن عباس، عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن الله هو الذي هزم الأحزاب ونصر النبي ﷺ بالصَّبا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4105) and Muslim (900/17).","chapter_en":"Allah Alone Defeated the Confederates and Supported the Prophet ﷺ with the East Wind","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was granted victory by the east wind, while ʿĀd were destroyed by the west wind.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-ṣabā is the east wind, while al-dabūr is the west wind."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8217],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4105)، ومسلم (17:900)."},{"num":8932,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نُصِرْتُ بِالصَّبَا، وَأُهْلِكَتْ عَادٌ بِالدَّبُورِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (7837) وفي الصغير sh13068(1069) عن محمود بن محمد الواسطي، حدثنا محمد بن أبان الواسطي، حدثنا أبو عوانة، عن قتادة، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن الله هو الذي هزم الأحزاب ونصر النبي ﷺ بالصَّبا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in Al-Awsaṭ (7837) and Al-Ṣaghīr (1069).","chapter_en":"Allah Alone Defeated the Confederates and Supported the Prophet ﷺ with the East Wind","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was granted victory by the east wind, while ʿĀd were destroyed by the west wind.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في «الأوسط» (7837)، وفي «الصغير» sh13068(1069)."},{"num":8933,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سُلَيْمَانَ بن صرد يَقُولُ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ حِينَ أَجْلَى الأَحْزَابُ عَنْهُ: الْآنَ نَغْزُوهُمْ، وَلاَ يَغْزُونَنَا، نَحْنُ نَسِيرُ إِلَيْهِمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4110) عن عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا يحيى بن آدم، حدثنا إسرائيل: سمعت أبا إسحاق يقول: سمعت سليمان بن صرد يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن المسلمين هم الذين يغزون المشركين بعد غزوة الأحزاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4110).","chapter_en":"After the Campaign of the Confederates, the Muslims Would Take the Initiative Against the Polytheists","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sulaymān ibn Ṣurad reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say when the Confederates had been driven away from him: “Now we shall campaign against them, and they will not campaign against us. We shall march toward them.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“When the Confederates had been driven away” means that they withdrew from him.","This was one of the signs of his prophethood. In the following year, he ﷺ set out to perform ʿumrah, but Quraysh prevented him from reaching the Sacred House. A truce was then concluded between them. When Quraysh later violated it, that became the cause of the conquest of Makkah. Events thus unfolded exactly as he ﷺ had foretold. See Fatḥ al-Bārī (7/405)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",539],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9729,13054],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4110)."},{"num":8934,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ; أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ يَوْمَ الْأَحْزَابِ وَقَدْ جَمَعُوا لَهُ جُمُوعًا كَثِيرَةً، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يَغْزُوكُمْ بَعْدَهَا أَبَدًا، وَلَكِنْ تَغْزُوهُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1810) عن محمد بن عمر بن هياج، ثنا يحيى بن عبد الرحمن الأرجي، ثنا عبيدة بن الأسود، عن مجالد، عن عامر (الشعبي) عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب بيان أن المسلمين هم الذين يغزون المشركين بعد غزوة الأحزاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (1810).","chapter_en":"After the Campaign of the Confederates, the Muslims Would Take the Initiative Against the Polytheists","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: On the day of the Confederates, after they had assembled vast forces against him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They will never campaign against you after this; rather, we shall campaign against them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",540],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في «كشف الأستار» (1810)."},{"num":8935,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: أُصِيبَ سَعْدٌ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ، رَمَاهُ رَجُلٌ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ يُقَالُ لَهُ: حِبَّانُ بْنُ الْعَرِقَةِ رَمَاهُ فِي الأَكْحَلِ فَضَرَبَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَيْمَةً فِي الْمَسْجِدِ لِيَعُودَهُ مِنْ قَرِيبٍ إِلاَّ أن جُرْحُهُ يَغْذُو دَمًا فَمَاتَ مِنْهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4122) ومسلم في الجهاد (1769) كلاهما من حديث عبد الله بن نمير، حدثنا هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته في حديث أطول كما سيأتي وأنه مات بعد انصراف الأحزاب بنحو من خمس وعشرين ليلة وبعد أن حكم في بني قريظة.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من استشهد من المسلمين يوم الخندق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4122) and Muslim (1769).","chapter_en":"Muslims Who Were Martyred on the Day of the Trench","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الأحزاب","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of the Confederates","part_no":48,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: Saʿd was wounded on the day of the Trench. A man of Quraysh named Ḥibbān ibn al-ʿAriqah shot him in the medial vein of his arm. The Prophet ﷺ had a tent erected for him inside the mosque so that he could visit him nearby. His wound continued discharging blood, and he eventually died from it."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah related from Ibn Shihāb that among the Anṣār martyred on the day of the Trench was Anas ibn Muʿādh ibn Aws ibn ʿAbd ʿAmr. It was narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in Al-Kabīr (1/238) and is a mursal report.","The authors of the biographies and campaign histories also listed the following among those martyred at the Trench: ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl al-Ashhalī; Thaʿlabah ibn Ghanamah ibn ʿAdī al-Anṣārī al-Khazrajī; Ṭufayl ibn al-Nuʿmān al-Anṣārī; Kaʿb ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī al-Najjārī; Sulayṭ ibn ʿAwf al-Aslamī; Sufyān ibn ʿAwf al-Aslamī; and Sinān ibn Ṣayfī al-Khazrajī. There is disagreement concerning some of these names."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",541],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4122)، ومسلم (1769)."},{"num":8936,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: لَمَّا رَجَعَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الْخَنْدَقِ، وَوَضَعَ السِّلاَحَ، وَاغْتَسَلَ، أَتَاهُ جِبْرِيلُ ـ عَلَيْهِ السَّلاَمُ ـ فَقَالَ: قَدْ وَضَعْتَ السِّلاَحَ، وَاللَّهِ مَا وَضَعْنَاهُ، فَاخْرُجْ إِلَيْهِمْ. قَالَ: فَإِلَى أَيْنَ. قَالَ: هَا هُنَا، وَأَشَارَ إِلَى بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ، فَخَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَيْهِمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4117) ومسلم في الجهاد (1769) كلاهما من حديث ابن نمير، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة واللفظ للبخاري. وسيأتي مطولاً.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب خروج النبي ﷺ إلى بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4117) and Muslim in al-Jihād (1769), both through Ibn Numayr, from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀ’ishah; the wording is al-Bukhārī’s. It will appear later in fuller form.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Sets Out Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: When the Prophet ﷺ returned from the Trench, laid down his weapons, and bathed, Gabriel came to him and said: “Have you laid down your weapons? By Allah, we have not laid ours down! March against them.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Where?” Gabriel replied, “Over there,” pointing toward Banū Qurayẓah. The Prophet ﷺ therefore set out against them."]},"intro_majmu":{"ar":["كانت غزوة بني قريظة في شهر ذي الحجة من السنة الخامسة عقب غزوة الأحزاب. وكان سببها نقض بني قريظة العهد الذي بينهم وبين النبي ﷺ وقت غزو قريش المدينة، فأمر الله تعالى نبيه بالتوجه إليهم لقتالهم."],"en":["The campaign against Banū Qurayẓah took place in Dhū al-Ḥijjah of the fifth year, immediately after the Campaign of the Confederates. Its cause was Banū Qurayẓah’s violation of their covenant with the Prophet ﷺ while Quraysh were attacking Madinah. Allah Most High therefore commanded His Prophet to march against them and fight them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",543],"full":1,"rep":[513,631],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4117) ومسلم (1769). وسيأتي مطولا."},{"num":8937,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: كَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَى الْغُبَارِ سَاطِعًا فِي زُقَاقِ بَنِي غَنْمٍ، مَوْكِبِ جِبْرِيلَ حِينَ سَارَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4118) عن موسى حدثنا جرير بن حازم، عن حميد بن هلال، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب خروج النبي ﷺ إلى بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4118), from Mūsā, from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim, from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from Anas.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Sets Out Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: It is as though I can still see the dust rising through the street of Banū Ghanm from Gabriel’s procession when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marched against Banū Qurayẓah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",544],"full":1,"rep":[632],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4118)."},{"num":8938,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن كَعْبِ بن مَالِكٍأَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا رَجَعَ مِنْ طَلَبِ الْأَحْزَابِ، رَجَعَ فَنَزَعَ لَأْمَتَهُ، وَاغْتَسَلَ وَاسْتَجْمَرَ. زَادَ دُحَيْمٌ فِي حَدِيثِهِ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَنَزَلَ جِبْرِيلُ - عَلَيْهِ السلام - فَقَالَ: عَذِيرُكَ مِنْ مُحَارِبٍ، أَلَا أَرَاكَ قَدْ وَضَعْتَ اللَّأْمَةَ، وَمَا وَضَعْنَاهَا بَعْدُ. فَوَثَبَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَزِعًا، فَعَزَمَ عَلَى النَّاسِ أَلَّا يُصَلُّوا الْعَصْرَ إِلَّا فِي بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ، فَلَبِسُوا السِّلَاحَ، وَخَرَجُوا فَلَمْ يَأْتُوا بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ حَتَّى غَرَبَتِ الشَّمْسُ. وَاخْتَصَمَ النَّاسُ فِي صَلَاةِ الْعَصْرِ، فَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: صَلُّوا، فَإِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمْ يُرِدْ أَنْ تَتْرُكُوا الصَّلَاةَ، وَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: عَزَمَ عَلَيْنَا أَنْ لَا نُصَلِّيَ حَتَّى نَأْتِيَ بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ، وَإِنَّمَا نَحْنُ فِي عَزِيمَةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْنَا إِثْمٌ. فَصَلَّتْ طَائِفَةٌ الْعَصْرَ إِيمَانًا وَاحْتِسَابًا، وَطَائِفَةٌ لَمْ يُصَلُّوا حَتَّى نَزَلُوا بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ بَعْدَ مَا غَرَبَتِ الشَّمْسُ فَصَلَّوْهَا إِيمَانًا وَاحْتِسَابًا، فَلَمْ يُعَنِّفْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَاحِدَةً مِنَ الطَّائِفَتَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (19/ح 160) عن إبراهيم بن دحيم الدمشقي، ثنا أبي ح وحدثنا الحسن بن إسحاق، ثنا علي بن بحر قالا: ثنا الوليد بن مسلم، ثنا مرزوق بن أبي الهذيل، عن الزهري، عن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن كعب، عن عمه عبيد الله بن كعب، عن كعب بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب خروج النبي ﷺ إلى بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr (19/79–80) through Ibrāhīm ibn Duḥaym al-Dimashqī and al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq, from al-Walīd ibn Muslim, from Marzūq ibn Abī al-Hudhayl, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allah ibn Kaʿb, from his uncle ʿUbayd Allah ibn Kaʿb, from Kaʿb ibn Mālik.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Sets Out Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Kaʿb ibn Mālik reported: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from pursuing the Confederates, laid down his armor, and perfumed himself with incense—as Duḥaym added in his narration—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gabriel descended and said: ‘What excuse can there be for laying aside battle? I see that you have removed your armor, while we have not yet laid ours down.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sprang up in alarm and firmly instructed the people not to perform the afternoon prayer until they reached Banū Qurayẓah. They put on their weapons and departed, but did not reach Banū Qurayẓah until after sunset. The people differed regarding the afternoon prayer. Some said: “Perform the prayer, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not intend that you should omit it.” Others said: “He firmly instructed us not to pray until we reached Banū Qurayẓah. We are carrying out the Messenger of Allah’s explicit command, so there is no sin upon us.” One group performed the afternoon prayer on time, acting in faith and seeking Allah’s reward. The other group did not pray until they reached Banū Qurayẓah after sunset, likewise acting in faith and seeking Allah’s reward. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not reprimand either group."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",545],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (19/79–80)."},{"num":8939,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الأَحْزَابِ: لاَ يُصَلِّيَنَّ أَحَدٌ الْعَصْرَ إِلاَّ فِي بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ. فَأَدْرَكَ بَعْضُهُمُ الْعَصْرَ فِي الطَّرِيقِ، فَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: لاَ نُصَلِّي حَتَّى نَأْتِيَهَا. وَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: بَلْ نُصَلِّي، لَمْ يُرِدْ مِنَّا ذَلِكَ، فَذُكِرَ ذَلِكَ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَلَمْ يُعَنِّفْ وَاحِدًا مِنْهُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4119) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (69:1770) كلاهما عن عبد الله بن محمد بن أسماء الضبعي، حدثنا جويرية بن أسماء، عن نافع، عن عبد الله بن عمر قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب المبادرة بغزو أهل قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4119) and Muslim in al-Jihād wa-l-Siyar (1770/69), both from ʿAbd Allah ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ al-Ḍubaʿī, from Juwayriyah ibn Asmāʾ, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar.","chapter_en":"Hastening to Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: On the day of the Confederates, the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should perform the afternoon prayer until he reaches Banū Qurayẓah.” The time of the afternoon prayer reached some of them while they were still traveling. Some said, “We shall not pray until we reach Banū Qurayẓah.” Others said, “We shall pray now; the Prophet ﷺ did not intend that we delay the prayer itself.” The matter was later mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not reprimand either group."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Their number was three thousand men accompanied by thirty-six horses, as mentioned by Ibn Saʿd (3/74).","Ibn Isḥāq said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ besieged them for twenty-five nights until the siege exhausted them and Allah cast terror into their hearts. The Sīrah of Ibn Hishām (2/235)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",546],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4119) ومسلم (69:1770)."},{"num":8940,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِحَسَّانَ: اهْجُهُمْ ـ أَوْ هَاجِهِمْ ـ وَجِبْرِيلُ مَعَكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4123) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (153:2486) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، أخبرني عدي بن ثابت، قال: سمعت البراء بن عازب قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"هجاء حسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4123) and Muslim in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (2486/153), both through Shuʿbah, from ʿAdī ibn Thābit, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib.","chapter_en":"Ḥassān’s Poetic Satire","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ reported: The Prophet ﷺ said to Ḥassān: “Satirize them—or engage them in poetic combat—for Gabriel is with you.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Bukhārī’s narration states that the Prophet ﷺ said this on the day of Banū Qurayẓah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",547],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10156,12943],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4123) ومسلم (153:2486)."},{"num":8941,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ قَالَ: نَزَلَ أَهْلُ قُرَيْظَةَ عَلَى حُكْمِ سَعْدِ بْنِ مُعَاذٍ، فَأَرْسَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى سَعْدٍ فَأَتَى عَلَى حِمَارٍ، فَلَمَّا دَنَا مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ قَالَ لِلأَنْصَارِ: قُومُوا إِلَى سَيِّدِكُمْ أَوْ خَيْرِكُمْ فَقَالَ: هَؤُلاَءِ نَزَلُوا عَلَى حُكْمِكَ، فَقَالَ: تَقْتُلُ مُقَاتِلَتَهُمْ، وَتَسْبِي ذَرَارِيَّهُمْ، قَالَ: قَضَيْتَ بِحُكْمِ اللَّهِ، وَرُبَّمَا قَالَ: بِحُكْمِ الْمَلِكِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4121) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (64:1768) كلاهما عن محمد بن بشار، حدثنا غندر (هو محمد بن جعفر) حدثنا شعبة، عن سعد بن إبراهيم، قال: سمعت أبا أمامة قال: سمعت أبا سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"حكم سعد بن معاذ في بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4121) and Muslim in al-Jihād wa-l-Siyar (1768/64), both from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār, from Ghundar (Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar), from Shuʿbah, from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm, from Abū Umāmah, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī.","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Muʿādh’s Judgment Concerning Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd reported: Banū Qurayẓah agreed to submit to the judgment of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh. The Prophet ﷺ sent for Saʿd, who arrived riding a donkey. When he drew near the mosque, the Prophet ﷺ said to the Anṣār: “Rise to receive your leader—or the best among you.” He then said to Saʿd: “These people have agreed to submit to your judgment.” Saʿd said: “Their fighting men are to be killed and their women and children taken captive.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You have judged according to Allah’s judgment.” On another occasion, the narrator said: “According to the judgment of the Sovereign.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",548],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4121) ومسلم (64:1768)."},{"num":8942,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: أُصِيبَ سَعْدٌ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ، رَمَاهُ رَجُلٌ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ، يُقَالُ لَهُ حِبَّانُ ابْنُ الْعَرِقَةِ، رَمَاهُ فِي الأَكْحَلِ، فَضَرَبَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَيْمَةً فِي الْمَسْجِدِ لِيَعُودَهُ مِنْ قَرِيبٍ، فَلَمَّا رَجَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الْخَنْدَقِ وَضَعَ السِّلاَحَ وَاغْتَسَلَ، فَأَتَاهُ جِبْرِيلُ ـ عَلَيْهِ السَّلاَمُ ـ وَهْوَ يَنْفُضُ رَأْسَهُ مِنَ الْغُبَارِ، فَقَالَ: قَدْ وَضَعْتَ السِّلاَحَ، وَاللَّهِ مَا وَضَعْتُهُ، اخْرُجْ إِلَيْهِمْ. قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَأَيْنَ. فَأَشَارَ إِلَى بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ، فَأَتَاهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَنَزَلُوا عَلَى حُكْمِهِ، فَرَدَّ الْحُكْمَ إِلَى سَعْدٍ، قَالَ: فَإِنِّي أَحْكُمُ فِيهِمْ: أَنْ تُقْتَلَ الْمُقَاتِلَةُ، وَأَنْ تُسْبَى النِّسَاءُ وَالذُّرِّيَّةُ، وَأَنْ تُقْسَمَ أَمْوَالُهُمْ.","قَالَ هِشَامٌ: فَأَخْبَرَنِي أَبِي، عَنْ عَائِشَةَ: أَنَّ سَعْدًا قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّكَ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ لَيْسَ أَحَدٌ أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ أَنْ أُجَاهِدَهُمْ فِيكَ، مِنْ قَوْمٍ كَذَّبُوا رَسُولَكَ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَخْرَجُوهُ، اللَّهُمَّ فَإِنِّي أَظُنُّ أَنَّكَ قَدْ وَضَعْتَ الحَرْبَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ، فَإِنْ كَانَ بَقِيَ مِنْ حَرْبِ قُرَيْشٍ شَيْءٌ فَأَبْقِنِي لَهُ، حَتَّى أُجَاهِدَهُمْ فِيكَ، وَإِنْ كُنْتَ وَضَعْتَ الحَرْبَ فَافْجُرْهَا وَاجْعَلْ مَوْتَتِي فِيهَا، فَانْفَجَرَتْ مِنْ لَبَّتِهِ، فَلَمْ يَرُعْهُمْ، وَفِي المَسْجِدِ خَيْمَةٌ مِنْ بَنِي غِفَارٍ، إِلَّا الدَّمُ يَسِيلُ إِلَيْهِمْ، فَقَالُوا: يَا أَهْلَ الخَيْمَةِ، مَا هَذَا الَّذِي يَأْتِينَا مِنْ قِبَلِكُمْ ؟ فَإِذَا سَعْدٌ يَغْذُو جُرْحُهُ دَمًا، فَمَاتَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4122) ومسلم في الجهاد والسير (65:1769) كلاهما من طريق عبد الله بن نمير، حدثنا هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"حكم سعد بن معاذ في بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4122) and Muslim (1769/65).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Muʿādh’s Judgment Concerning Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, Mother of the Believers, reported: Saʿd was wounded on the day of the Trench. A man of Quraysh named Ḥibbān ibn al-ʿAriqah shot him in the medial vein of his arm. The Prophet ﷺ had a tent erected for him inside the mosque so that he could visit him nearby. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Trench, he laid down his weapons and bathed. Gabriel came to him, shaking dust from his head, and said: “Have you laid down your weapons? By Allah, I have not laid mine down! March against them.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Where?” Gabriel pointed toward Banū Qurayẓah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to them, and they agreed to submit to his judgment. He referred the judgment to Saʿd, who said: “My judgment is that their fighting men be killed, their women and children taken captive, and their property divided.” Hishām said: My father related to me from ʿĀ’ishah that Saʿd prayed: “O Allah, You know that there are no people whom I would rather strive against for Your sake than those who rejected Your Messenger ﷺ and drove him out. O Allah, I believe that You have brought the warfare between us and them to an end. If any fighting against Quraysh remains, preserve me so that I may strive against them for Your sake. But if You have ended the war, cause my wound to burst and make my death result from it.”","The wound burst open near his upper chest. The people in a tent belonging to Banū Ghifār inside the mosque were suddenly startled by blood flowing toward them. They asked, “People of the tent, what is this coming toward us from your direction?” They discovered that Saʿd’s wound was pouring blood, and he died from it."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim added the statement of ʿUrwah: I was informed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have judged them according to the judgment of Allah Almighty.”","Muslim also added (1769/68), through another route from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah with this chain: His wound burst open that night and continued bleeding until he died."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",549],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4122)، ومسلم (65:1769)."},{"num":8943,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: خَرَجْتُ يَوْمَ الْخَنْدَقِ أَقْفُو آثَارَ النَّاسِ. قَالَتْ: فَسَمِعْتُ وَئِيدَ الْأَرْضِ وَرَائِي، - يَعْنِي حِسَّ الْأَرْضِ، - قَالَتْ: فَالْتَفَتُّ، فَإِذَا أَنَا بِسَعْدِ بْنِ مُعَاذٍ وَمَعَهُ ابْنُ أَخِيهِ الْحَارِثُ بْنُ أَوْسٍ، يَحْمِلُ مِجَنَّهُ. قَالَتْ: فَجَلَسْتُ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ، فَمَرَّ سَعْدٌ وَعَلَيْهِ دِرْعٌ مِنْ حَدِيدٍ، قَدْ خَرَجَتْ مِنْهَا أَطْرَافُهُ، فَأَنَا أَتَخَوَّفُ عَلَى أَطْرَافِ سَعْدٍ. قَالَتْ: وَكَانَ سَعْدٌ مِنْ أَعْظَمِ النَّاسِ وَأَطْوَلِهِمْ. قَالَتْ: فَمَرَّ وَهُوَ يَرْتَجِزُ وَيَقُولُ: [البحر الرجز] لَبَّثْ قَلِيلًا يُدْرِكُ الْهَيْجَا حَمَلْ... مَا أَحْسَنَ الْمَوْتَ إِذَا حَانَ الْأَجَلْ.","قَالَتْ : فَقُمْتُ، فَاقْتَحَمْتُ حَدِيقَةً، فَإِذَا فيها نَفَرٌ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ، وَإِذَا فِيهِمْ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ وَفِيهِمْ رَجُلٌ عَلَيْهِ تَسْبِغَةٌ لَهُ - يعنى مغفرا - فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: مَا جَاءَ بِكِ؟! لعمري وَاللَّهِ إِنَّكِ لَجَرِيئَةٌ، وَمَا يُؤْمِنُكِ أَنْ يَكُونَ بَلَاءٌ، أَوْ يَكُونَ تَحَوُّزٌ؟ قالت : فَمَا زَالَ يَلُومُنِي حَتَّى تَمَنَّيْتُ أَنَّ الْأَرْضَ انْشَقَّتْ لِي سَاعَتَئِذٍ، فَدَخَلْتُ فِيهَا، قالت: فَرَفَعَ الرَّجُلُ التَّسْبِغَةَ عَنْ وَجْهِهِ، فَإِذَا طَلْحَةُ بْنُ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ، فَقَالَ: يَا عُمَرُ، إِنَّكَ قَدْ أَكْثَرْتَ مُنْذُ الْيَوْمِ، وَأَيْنَ التَّحَوُّزُ أَوِ الْفِرَارُ إِلَّا إِلَى اللَّهِ عز وجل؟!","قَالَتْ: وَيَرْمِي سَعْدًا رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ - يُقَالُ لَهُ: ابْنُ الْعَرِقَةِ- بِسَهْمٍ لَهُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ: خُذْهَا وَأَنَا ابْنُ الْعَرَقَةِ، فَأَصَابَ أَكْحَلَهُ، فَقَطَعَهُ، فَدَعَا اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ سَعْدٌ، فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ لَا تُمِتْنِي حَتَّى تُقِرَّ عَيْنِي مِنْ قُرَيْظَةَ. قَالَتْ: وَكَانُوا حلفاء وَمَوَالِيَهُ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ.","قَالَتْ: فَرَقَأ كَلْمُهُ، وَبَعَثَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ الرِّيحَ عَلَى الْمُشْرِكِينَ، فَكَفَى اللَّهُ عزوجل ﴿الْمُؤْمِنِينَ الْقِتَالَ، وَكَانَ اللَّهُ قَوِيًّا عَزِيزًا﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: 25]، فَلَحِقَ أَبُو سُفْيَانَ وَمَنْ مَعَهُ بِتِهَامَةَ، وَلَحِقَ عُيَيْنَةُ بْنُ بَدْرٍ وَمَنْ مَعَهُ بِنَجْدٍ، وَرَجَعَتْ بَنُو قُرَيْظَةَ، فَتَحَصَّنُوا فِي صَيَاصِيهِمْ، وَرَجَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ، فَوَضَعَ السِّلَاحَ، وَأَمَرَ بِقُبَّةٍ مِنْ أَدَمٍ، فَضُرِبَتْ عَلَى سَعْدٍ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ.","قالت: فجاء جبريل عليه السلام، وإن على ثناياه لنقع الغبار فقال: أقد وضعت السلاح؟ والله ما وضعت الملائكة بعد السلاح، اخرج إلى بني قريظة فقاتلهم، قالت: فلبس رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم لأمته، وأذن في الناس بالرحيل أن يخرجوا، فخرج رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فمر على بني غنم، وهم جيران المسجـد حولـه، فقال: من مر بكم؟ قالوا: مر بنا دحية الكلبي، وكان دحية الكلبي تشبه لحيته وسنة وجهه جبريل عليه السلام.","فَقَالَتْ: فَأَتَاهُمْ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَحَاصَرَهُمْ خَمْسًا وَعِشْرِينَ لَيْلَةً، فَلَمَّا اشْتَدَّ حَصْرُهُمْ وَاشْتَدَّ الْبَلَاءُ، قِيلَ لَهُمْ: انْزِلُوا عَلَى حُكْمِ رَسُولِ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم، فَاسْتَشَارُوا أَبَا لُبَابَةَ بْنَ عَبْدِ الْمُنْذِرِ، فَأَشَارَ إِلَيْهِمْ أَنَّهُ الذَّبْحُ قَالُوا: نَنْزِلُ عَلَى حُكْمِ سَعْدِ بْنِ مُعَاذٍ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم: انْزِلُوا عَلَى حُكْمِ سَعْدِ بْنِ مُعَاذٍ فَنَزَلُوا وَبَعَثَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلَى سَعْدِ بْنِ مُعَاذٍ، فَأُتِيَ بِهِ عَلَى حِمَارٍ عَلَيْهِ إِكَافٌ مِنْ لِيفٍ، قَدْ حُمِلَ عَلَيْهِ، وَحَفَّ بِهِ قَوْمُهُ، فَقَالُوا: يَا أَبَا عَمْرٍو، حُلَفَاؤُكَ وَمَوَالِيكَ وَأَهْلُ النِّكَايَةِ وَمَنْ قَدْ عَلِمْتَ. قَالَتْ: لَا يُرْجِعُ إِلَيْهِمْ شَيْئًا، وَلَا يَلْتَفِتُ إِلَيْهِمْ حَتَّى إِذَا دَنَا مِنْ دُورِهِمْ، الْتَفَتَ إِلَى قَوْمِهِ، فَقَالَ: قَدْ أَنَى لِي أَنْ لَا أُبَالِيَ فِي اللهِ لَوْمَةَ لَائِمٍ.","قَالَ: قَالَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ: فَلَمَّا طَلَعَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَالَ: قُومُوا إِلَى سَيِّدِكُمْ فَأَنْزَلُوهُ فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: سَيِّدُنَا اللهُ عز وجل. قَالَ: أَنْزِلُوهُ، فَأَنْزَلُوهُ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم: احْكُمْ فِيهِمْ قَالَ سَعْدٌ : فَإِنِّي أَحْكُمُ فِيهِمْ، أَنْ تُقْتَلَ مُقَاتِلَتُهُمْ، وَتُسْبَى ذَرَارِيُّهُمْ، وَتُقْسَمَ أَمْوَالُهُمْ –– وَقَالَ يَزِيدُ بِبَغْدَادَ: وَيُقْسَمُ -- فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم: لَقَدْ حَكَمْتَ بِحُكْمِ اللهِ عز وجل وَحُكْمِ رَسُولِهِ.","قَالَتْ: ثُمَّ دَعَا سَعْدٌ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ كُنْتَ أَبْقَيْتَ عَلَى نَبِيِّكَ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ حَرْبِ قُرَيْشٍ شَيْئًا، فَأَبْقِنِي لَهَا، وَإِنْ كُنْتَ قَطَعْتَ الْحَرْبَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهُمْ، فَاقْبِضْنِي إِلَيْكَ. قَالَتْ: فَانْفَجَرَ كَلْمُهُ، وَكَانَ قَدْ بَرِئَ حَتَّى مَا يُرَى مِنْهُ إِلَّا مِثْلُ الْخُرْصِ، وَرَجَعَ إِلَى قُبَّتِهِ الَّتِي ضَرَبَ عَلَيْهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ.","قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: فَحَضَرَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ. قَالَتْ: فَوَالَّذِي نَفْسُ مُحَمَّدٍ بِيَدِهِ، إِنِّي لَأَعْرِفُ بُكَاءَ عُمَرَ مِنْ بُكَاءِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، وَأَنَا فِي حُجْرَتِي، وَكَانُوا كَمَا قَالَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: رُحَمَآءُ بَيْنَهُمْ [الفتح: ٢٩]٢٩] قَالَ عَلْقَمَةُ: قُلْتُ: أَيْ أُمَّهْ، فَكَيْفَ كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَصْنَعُ؟ قَالَتْ: كَانَتْ عَيْنُهُ لَا تَدْمَعُ عَلَى أَحَدٍ، وَلَكِنَّهُ كَانَ إِذَا وَجِدَ، فَإِنَّمَا هُوَ آخِذٌ بِلِحْيَتِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (25097) وابن سعد (1057) وابن حبان (7028) كلهم من حديث يزيد، قال: أخبرنا محمد بن عمرو، عن أبيه، عن جده علقمة بن وقاص، قال: أخبرتني عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"حكم سعد بن معاذ في بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (25097), Ibn Saʿd (3/421), and Ibn Ḥibbān (7028).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Muʿādh’s Judgment Concerning Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: On the day of the Trench, I went out following the people’s tracks. I heard the heavy sound of the ground behind me—that is, the sound of someone walking. I turned and saw Saʿd ibn Muʿādh accompanied by his nephew al-Ḥārith ibn Aws, who was carrying Saʿd’s shield. I sat down upon the ground. Saʿd passed wearing an iron coat of armor from which his limbs protruded, and I feared that his exposed limbs might be struck. Saʿd was among the largest and tallest of men. As he passed, he chanted: Wait but a little—Ḥamal will reach the raging battle; how beautiful death is when the appointed time has come. I rose and entered an enclosed garden. A group of Muslims was inside, including ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and a man wearing a helmet that covered his face. ʿUmar asked: “What brought you here? By my life, you are certainly bold! What makes you feel safe from a calamity or a forced retreat?” He continued reproaching me until I wished that the ground would split open at that moment and swallow me. The man lifted the helmet from his face, and it was Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh. He said: “ʿUmar, you have gone too far today! Where can anyone seek refuge or flee except to Allah Almighty?”","A polytheist of Quraysh known as Ibn al-ʿAriqah shot an arrow at Saʿd, saying, “Take that! I am Ibn al-ʿAriqah.” It struck and severed the medial vein in Saʿd’s arm. Saʿd prayed: “O Allah, do not cause me to die until You grant me satisfaction concerning Banū Qurayẓah.” They had been his allies and confederates during the pre-Islamic period. His wound stopped bleeding. Allah Almighty sent the wind against the polytheists and spared the believers from fighting; Allah is All-Strong, Almighty. Abū Sufyān and those with him withdrew toward Tihāmah, while ʿUyaynah ibn Badr and his forces returned to Najd. Banū Qurayẓah returned and fortified themselves inside their strongholds.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to Madinah and laid down his weapons. He ordered that a leather tent be erected for Saʿd inside the mosque. Gabriel came with dust visible upon his front teeth and said: “Have you laid down your weapons? By Allah, the angels have not yet laid down theirs! March against Banū Qurayẓah and fight them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ put on his armor and announced to the people that they were to depart. He set out and passed by Banū Ghanm, who lived around the mosque. He asked: “Who passed by you?” They replied, “Diḥyah al-Kalbī passed us.” Gabriel resembled Diḥyah al-Kalbī in his beard, teeth, and facial appearance.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached Banū Qurayẓah and besieged them for twenty-five nights. When the siege and hardship became severe, they were told: “Submit to the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” They consulted Abū Lubābah ibn ʿAbd al-Mundhir, who gestured toward his throat to indicate slaughter. They said, “We shall submit to the judgment of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told them: “Then submit to the judgment of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh,” and they did so.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Saʿd ibn Muʿādh. He was brought riding a donkey fitted with a saddle made of palm fiber, having been helped onto it. His people surrounded him and said: “Abū ʿAmr, consider your allies and confederates—people who have fought alongside you and whose position you know.” He gave them no answer and did not turn toward them. When he approached the dwellings of Banū Qurayẓah, he turned to his people and said: “The time has come for me not to care, for Allah’s sake, about the criticism of any critic.”","Abū Saʿīd said: When Saʿd came into view, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rise to receive your leader and help him dismount.” ʿUmar said, “Our Master is Allah Almighty.” The Prophet ﷺ repeated: “Help him dismount,” so they did. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Pass judgment concerning them.” Saʿd replied: “My judgment is that their fighting men be killed, their women and children taken captive, and their property divided.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have judged according to the judgment of Allah Almighty and the judgment of His Messenger.”","Saʿd then prayed: “O Allah, if any warfare against Quraysh remains for Your Prophet ﷺ, preserve me for it. But if You have ended the war between him and them, then take me to Yourself.” His wound burst open after having healed until only a ring-like scar could be seen. He was returned to the tent that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had erected for him. ʿĀ’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar were present with him. By Him in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, I could distinguish ʿUmar’s weeping from Abū Bakr’s while I was inside my apartment. They were as Allah Almighty described them: “Compassionate among themselves.”","[Al-Fatḥ 48:29] ʿAlqamah said: I asked, “Mother, what would the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do?” She replied: “His eyes would not shed tears over anyone, but when grief affected him, he would grasp his beard.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",550],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (25097)، وابن سعد (1057)، وابن حبان (7028)."},{"num":8944,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ:  رُمِيَ سَعْدُ بْنُ مُعَاذٍ فِي أَكْحَلِهِ، قَالَ: فَحَسَمَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِيَدِهِ بِمِشْقَصٍ، ثُمَّ وَرِمَتْ، فَحَسَمَهُ الثَّانِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في السلام (2208: 75) من طرق عن أبي خيثمة زهير بن حرب، حدثنا أبو الزبير، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"حكم سعد بن معاذ في بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2208/75).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Muʿādh’s Judgment Concerning Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: Saʿd ibn Muʿādh was shot in the medial vein of his arm. The Prophet ﷺ cauterized it with his own hand using a broad-headed arrowhead. When the arm swelled, he cauterized it a second time."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",551],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10213,11574],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2208: 75)."},{"num":8945,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: رُمِيَ يَوْمَ الأَحْزَابِ سَعْدُ بْنُ مُعَاذٍ فَقَطَعُوا أَكْحَلَهُ أَوْ أَبْجَلَهُ فَحَسَمَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالنَّارِ، فَانْتَفَخَتْ يَدُهُ، فَتَرَكَهُ فَنَزَفَهُ الدَّمُ، فَحَسَمَهُ أُخْرَى فَانْتَفَخَتْ يَدُهُ، فَلَمَّا رَأَى ذَلِكَ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ لاَ تُخْرِجْ نَفْسِي حَتَّى تُقِرَّ عَيْنِي مِنْ بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ. فَاسْتَمْسَكَ عِرْقُهُ، فَمَا قَطَرَ قَطْرَةً، حَتَّى نَزَلُوا عَلَى حُكْمِ سَعْدِ بْنِ مُعَاذٍ. فَأَرْسَلَ إِلَيْهِ، فَحَكَمَ أَنْ يُقْتَلَ رِجَالُهُمْ وَيُسْتَحْيَى نِسَاؤُهُمْ، يَسْتَعِينُ بِهِنَّ الْمُسْلِمُونَ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَصَبْتَ حُكْمَ اللَّهِ فِيهِمْ. وَكَانُوا أَرْبَعَمِائَةٍ، فَلَمَّا فَرَغَ مِنْ قَتْلِهِمُ انْفَتَقَ عِرْقُهُ فَمَاتَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1582) وأحمد (14773) وابن حبان (4784) كلهم من طرق عن الليث بن سعد، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"حكم سعد بن معاذ في بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1582), Aḥmad (14773), and Ibn Ḥibbān (4784).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Muʿādh’s Judgment Concerning Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir reported: On the day of the Confederates, Saʿd ibn Muʿādh was shot and the medial vein of his arm—or another major vein—was severed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized it with fire. His arm swelled, so he left it untreated for a time, but when the bleeding resumed, he cauterized it again, and the arm swelled once more. When Saʿd saw this, he prayed: “O Allah, do not take my soul until You grant me satisfaction concerning Banū Qurayẓah.” His vein then closed and did not release another drop until they submitted to the judgment of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh. The Prophet ﷺ sent for him. Saʿd judged that their men should be killed and their women kept alive so that the Muslims could benefit from their service. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have reached Allah’s judgment concerning them.” They numbered four hundred. When their execution was completed, Saʿd’s vein opened again and he died."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",552],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10214],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1582)، وأحمد (14773)، وابن حبان (4784)."},{"num":8946,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عطية القرظي قَالَ: كُنْتُ مِنْ سَبْىِ بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ، فَكَانُوا يَنْظُرُونَ، فَمَنْ أَنْبَتَ الشَّعْرَ قُتِلَ، وَمَنْ لَمْ يُنْبِتْ لَمْ يُقْتَلْ، فَكُنْتُ فِيمَنْ لَمْ يُنْبِتْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4404، 4405)، والترمذي (1584)، والنسائي (4981، 3430)، وابن ماجه (2541، 2542)، وأحمد (18766)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (4780، 4783، 4788)، والحاكم (2/123 و3/135) كلهم من طرق عن عبد الملك بن عمير، حدثني عطية القرظي فذكره. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"حكم سعد بن معاذ في بني قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4404, 4405), al-Tirmidhī (1584), and al-Nasā’ī (3430, 4981).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Muʿādh’s Judgment Concerning Banū Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAṭiyyah al-Quraẓī reported: I was among the captives of Banū Qurayẓah. They examined the captives: anyone whose pubic hair had grown was killed, while anyone whose hair had not grown was not killed. I was among those whose hair had not grown."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",553],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4404، 4405)، والترمذي (1584)، والنسائي (3430، 4981)."},{"num":8947,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: لَمْ يُقْتَلْ مِنْ نِسَائِهِمْ - تَعْنِي بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ - إِلاَّ امْرَأَةً، إِنَّهَا لَعِنْدِي تُحَدِّثُ تَضْحَكُ ظَهْرًا وَبَطْنًا، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقْتُلُ رِجَالَهُمْ بِالسُّيُوفِ، إِذْ هَتَفَ هَاتِفٌ بِاسْمِهَا: أَيْنَ فُلاَنَةُ؟ قَالَتْ: أَنَا. قُلْتُ: وَمَا شَأْنُكِ؟ قَالَتْ: حَدَثٌ أَحْدَثْتُهُ. قَالَتْ: فَانْطَلَقَ بِهَا، فَضُرِبَتْ عُنُقُهَا، فَمَا أَنْسَى عَجَبًا مِنْهَا أَنَّهَا تَضْحَكُ ظَهْرًا وَبَطْنًا، وَقَدْ عَلِمَتْ أَنَّهَا تُقْتَلُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2671) وأحمد (26364) وصحّحه الحاكم (3/35-36) وعنه البيهقي (9/82) كلهم من طرق عن محمد بن إسحاق قال: حدثني محمد بن جعفر بن الزبير، عن عروة بن الزبير، عن عائشة فذكرته. وهو في سيرة ابن هشام (1646)","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"لم يُقتل من النساء إلا امرأة واحدة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (2671) and Aḥmad (26364); authenticated by al-Ḥākim (3/35–36).","chapter_en":"Only One Woman Was Executed","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: Only one of their women—meaning the women of Banū Qurayẓah—was killed. She was sitting with me, speaking and laughing heartily, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was having their men put to the sword. Then someone called out her name: “Where is so-and-so?” She replied, “Here I am.” I asked, “What is the matter with you?” She replied, “It is because of something I did.” She was taken away and beheaded. I shall never forget my astonishment at her: she was laughing heartily despite knowing that she was going to be killed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",554],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2671)، وأحمد (26364)، وصححه الحاكم (3/35–36)."},{"num":8948,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: حَارَبَتِ النَّضِيرُ وَقُرَيْظَةُ، فَأَجْلَى بَنِي النَّضِيرِ، وَأَقَرَّ قُرَيْظَةَ، وَمَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ، حَتَّى حَارَبَتْ قُرَيْظَةُ، فَقَتَلَ رِجَالَهُمْ، وَقَسَمَ نِسَاءَهُمْ، وَأَوْلاَدَهُمْ، وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ بَيْنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ إِلاَّ بَعْضَهُمْ لَحِقُوا بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَآمَنَهُمْ وَأَسْلَمُوا، وَأَجْلَى يَهُودَ الْمَدِينَةِ كُلَّهُمْ: بَنِي قَيْنُقَاعَ، وَهُمْ رَهْطُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ سَلاَمٍ، وَيَهُودَ بَنِي حَارِثَةَ، وَكُلَّ يَهُودِ الْمَدِينَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4028) ومسلم في الجهاد (1766) كلاهما من حديث عبدالرزاق، أخبرنا ابن جريج، عن موسى بن عقبة، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر، قال:فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إجلاء يهود المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4028) and Muslim (1766).","chapter_en":"The Expulsion of the Jews of Madinah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported: The Prophet ﷺ fought Banū al-Naḍīr and Banū Qurayẓah. He expelled Banū al-Naḍīr but allowed Qurayẓah to remain and showed them favor. Later, when Qurayẓah fought, he had their men killed and divided their women, children, and property among the Muslims. Some of them, however, joined the Prophet ﷺ, who granted them safety, and they embraced Islam. He expelled all the Jews of Madinah: Banū Qaynuqāʿ—the clan of ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām—the Jews of Banū Ḥārithah, and all the other Jews of Madinah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",555],"full":1,"rep":[8544,8891,13056],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4028)، ومسلم (1766)."},{"num":8949,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: إن الرَّجُلَ كَانَ يَجْعَلُ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ النَّخَلَاتِ مِنْ أَرْضِهِ، حَتَّى فُتِحَتْ عَلَيْهِ قُرَيْظَةُ وَالنَّضِيرُ، فَجَعَلَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ يردّ عَلَيْهِ مَا كَانَ أَعْطَاهُ.","قَالَ أَنَسٌ: وَإِنَّ أَهْلِي أَمَرُونِي أَنْ آتِيَ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَأَسْأَلَهُ مَا كَانَ أَهْلُهُ أَعْطَوْهُ أَوْ بَعْضَهُ، وَكَانَ نَبِيُّ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَدْ أَعْطَاهُ أُمَّ أَيْمَنَ، فَأَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَأَعْطَانِيهِنَّ، فَجَاءَتْ أُمُّ أَيْمَنَ فَجَعَلَتِ الثَّوْبَ فِي عُنُقِي، وَقَالَتْ: لا وَاللهِ لَا نُعْطِيكَهُنَّ وَقَدْ أَعْطَانِيهِنَّ، فَقَالَ نَبِيُّ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم: يَا أُمَّ أَيْمَنَ اتْرُكِيهِ وَلَكِ كَذَا وَكَذَا وَتَقُولُ: كَلَّا، وَالَّذِي لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا هُوَ! فَجَعَلَ يَقُولُ: كَذَا حَتَّى أَعْطَاهَا عَشَرَةَ أَمْثَالِهِ، أَوْ قَرِيبًا مِنْ عَشَرَةِ أَمْثَالِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4120) ومسلم في الجهاد (71:1771) كلاهما من طريق معتمر بن سليمان، عن أبيه، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استغناء النبي ﷺ عن منائح الأنصار بعد فتح قريظة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4120) and Muslim (1771/71).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ No Longer Needing the Anṣār’s Grants After the Conquest of Qurayẓah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة بني قريظة","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign Against Banū Qurayẓah","part_no":48,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: A man would assign some palm trees from his land to the Prophet ﷺ. When the lands of Qurayẓah and al-Naḍīr were conquered for him, the Prophet ﷺ began returning to each person what he had given. Anas said: My family instructed me to go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him to return what they had given him, or part of it. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ had given it to Umm Ayman. I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave the palm trees back to me.","Umm Ayman came, placed a cloth around my neck, and said: “No, by Allah! We shall not give them to you after he has given them to me.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Umm Ayman, let him go, and you shall receive such-and-such.” She replied: “No, by Him besides whom there is no deity!” He continued increasing his offer until he gave her ten times their value, or nearly ten times their value."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",556],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4120)، ومسلم (71:1771)."},{"num":8950,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: بَعَثَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَيْلاً قِبَلَ نَجْدٍ، فَجَاءَتْ بِرَجُلٍ مِنْ بَنِي حَنِيفَةَ يُقَالُ لَهُ: ثُمَامَةُ بْنُ أُثَالٍ، فَرَبَطُوهُ بِسَارِيَةٍ مِنْ سَوَارِي المَسْجِدِ، فَخَرَجَ إِلَيْهِ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: مَا عِنْدَكَ يَا ثُمَامَةُ؟ فَقَالَ عِنْدِي خَيْرٌ يَا مُحَمَّدُ، إِنْ تَقْتُلْنِي تَقْتُلْ ذَا دَمٍ، وَإِنْ تُنْعِمْ تُنْعِمْ عَلَى شَاكِرٍ، وَإِنْ كُنْتَ تُرِيدُ المَالَ فَسَلْ مِنْهُ مَا شِئْتَ. فترك حَتَّى كَانَ الْغَدُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ لَهُ: مَا عِنْدَكَ يَا ثُمَامَةُ؟ قَالَ: مَا قُلْتُ لَكَ: إِنْ تُنْعِمْ تُنْعِمْ عَلَى شَاكِرٍ. فَتَرَكَهُ حَتَّى كَانَ بَعْدَ الْغَدِ، فَقَالَ: مَا عِنْدَكَ يَا ثُمَامَةُ؟ فَقَالَ عِنْدِي مَا قُلْتُ لَكَ. فَقَالَ: أَطْلِقُوا ثُمَامَةَ فَانْطَلَقَ إِلَى نَخْلٍ قَرِيبٍ مِنَ المَسْجِدِ فَاغْتَسَلَ ثُمَّ دَخَلَ المَسْجِدَ، فَقَالَ: أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ الله، وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ الله، يَا مُحَمَّدُ، والله مَا كَانَ عَلَى الأَرْضِ وَجْهٌ أَبْغَضَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ وَجْهِكَ، فَقَدْ أَصْبَحَ وَجْهُكَ أَحَبَّ الْوُجُوهِ إِلَيَّ، والله مَا كَانَ مِنْ دِينٍ أَبْغَضَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ دِينِكَ، فَأَصْبَحَ دِينُكَ أَحَبَّ الدِّينِ إِلَيَّ، والله مَا كَانَ مِنْ بَلَدٍ أَبْغَضُ إِلَيَّ مِنْ بَلَدِكَ، فَأَصْبَحَ بَلَدُكَ أَحَبَّ الْبِلاَدِ إِلَيَّ، وَإِنَّ خَيْلَكَ أَخَذَتْنِي وَأَنَا أُرِيدُ الْعُمْرَةَ، فَمَاذَا تَرَى؟ فَبَشَّرَهُ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَمَرَهُ أَنْ يَعْتَمِرَ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمَ مَكَّةَ قَالَ لَهُ قَائِلٌ: صَبَوْتَ. قَالَ: لاَ، وَلَكِنْ أَسْلَمْتُ مَعَ مُحَمَّدٍ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَلاَ والله لاَ يَأْتِيكُمْ مِنَ الْيَمَامَةِ حَبَّةُ حِنْطَةٍ حَتَّى يَأْذَنَ فِيهَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4372) ومسلم في الجهاد (59:1764) كلاهما من طريق الليث، عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد أنه سمع أبا هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"سرية محمد بن مسلمة إلى القرطاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4372) and Muslim in al-Jihād (1764/59), both through al-Layth, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd, who heard Abū Hurayrah.","chapter_en":"The Expedition of Muḥammad ibn Maslamah to al-Quraṭāʾ","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: The Prophet ﷺ sent a cavalry detachment toward Najd. They returned with a man from Banū Ḥanīfah named Thumāmah ibn Uthāl and tied him to one of the pillars of the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ came to him and asked: “What do you have to say, Thumāmah?” He replied: “I have good to say, Muhammad. If you kill me, you will kill a man whose blood will be avenged. If you show me favor, you will show favor to one who is grateful. If you desire wealth, ask for whatever amount you wish.” The Prophet ﷺ left him until the following day, then asked: “What do you have to say, Thumāmah?” He replied: “What I told you: if you show me favor, you will show favor to one who is grateful.” He left him until the next day and again asked: “What do you have to say, Thumāmah?” He replied: “I have what I already told you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Release Thumāmah.” Thumāmah went to a grove near the mosque and bathed. He then entered the mosque and declared: “I testify that there is no deity except Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.” He continued: “Muhammad, by Allah, there was no face upon the earth more hateful to me than yours, but now your face has become the most beloved of all faces to me. By Allah, no religion was more hateful to me than your religion, but now your religion has become the most beloved religion to me. By Allah, no land was more hateful to me than your land, but now your land has become the most beloved land to me.” “Your cavalry captured me while I was intending to perform ʿumrah. What do you advise?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him glad tidings and instructed him to perform his ʿumrah. When he reached Makkah, someone asked him, “Have you abandoned your religion?” He replied: “No, but I have embraced Islam with Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, not a single grain of wheat will come to you from al-Yamāmah until the Prophet ﷺ permits it.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["كانت في شهر المحرم سنة ست. بعث رسول الله ﷺ محمد بن مسلمة في ثلاثين راكبًا إلى القرطاء، وهم بطن من بني بكر بن كلاب، وكانوا ينزلون البكرات بناحية ضرية، وبين ضرية والمدينة سبع ليال.","وأمره أن يشن عليهم الغارة، فسار الليل وكمن النهار، وأغار عليهم، فقتل نفرًا منهم وهرب سائرهم، واستاق نعمًا وشاءً، ولم يعرض للظعن، وانحدر إلى المدينة.","فخمَّس رسول الله ﷺ ما جاء به، وفضَّ على أصحابه ما بقي، وعدلوا الجزور بعشر من الغنم. وكانت النعم مائة وخمسين بعيرًا، والغنم ثلاثة آلاف شاة. وغاب تسع عشرة ليلة، وقدم لليلة بقيت من المحرم. ذكره ابن سعد في «الطبقات» (٢/٧٨).","وفي هذه السرية أُسر ثمامة بن أثال – سيد أهل اليمامة – كما نص ابن حبان في «الثقات» (١/٢٨١) أن محمد بن مسلمة أخذه في بعثه إلى القرطاء. وتفصيل قصة ثمامة في الحديث الآتي:"],"en":["It took place in Muḥarram of the sixth year. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muḥammad ibn Maslamah with thirty horsemen against al-Quraṭāʾ, a branch of Banū Bakr ibn Kilāb. They lived at al-Bakarāt in the region of Ḍariyyah, a seven-night journey from Madinah.","He ordered him to launch a surprise attack against them. Muḥammad traveled by night and concealed himself by day. He raided them, killed several men, and the rest fled. He drove away camels and sheep without interfering with the women, then returned to Madinah.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took one-fifth of what he brought and distributed the remainder among his Companions. They valued one camel as equivalent to ten sheep. The spoils consisted of one hundred and fifty camels and three thousand sheep. Muḥammad ibn Maslamah was absent for nineteen nights and returned when one night remained of Muḥarram. Ibn Saʿd mentioned it in Al-Ṭabaqāt (2/78).","During this expedition, Thumāmah ibn Uthāl, the leader of the people of al-Yamāmah, was captured. Ibn Ḥibbān expressly stated in Al-Thiqāt (1/281) that Muḥammad ibn Maslamah captured him during his expedition to al-Quraṭāʾ. The details of Thumāmah’s story appear in the following hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",558],"full":1,"rep":[8003],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4372) ومسلم (59:1764)."},{"num":8951,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي عَيَّاشٍ الزُّرَقِيِّ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِعُسْفَانَ، فَاسْتَقْبَلَنَا الْمُشْرِكُونَ، عَلَيْهِمْ خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ، وَهُمْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ الْقِبْلَةِ، فَصَلَّى بِنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الظُّهْرَ، فَقَالُوا: قَدْ كَانُوا عَلَى حَالٍ لَوْ أَصَبْنَا غِرَّتَهُمْ، ثُمَّ قَالُوا: تَأْتِي عَلَيْهِمُ الْآنَ صَلَاةٌ هِيَ أَحَبُّ إِلَيْهِمْ مِنْ أَبْنَائِهِمْ وَأَنْفُسِهِمْ، قَالَ: فَنَزَلَ جِبْرِيلُ عَلَيْهِ السلام بِهَذِهِ الْآيَاتِ بَيْنَ الظُّهْرِ وَالْعَصْرِ: ﴿وَإِذَا كُنْتَ فِيهِمْ فَأَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلَاةَ﴾ [النساء: ١٠٢]، قَالَ: فَحَضَرَتْ فَأَمَرَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخَذُوا السِّلَاحَ، قَالَ: فَصَفَفْنَا خَلْفَهُ صَفَّيْنِ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ رَكَعَ، فَرَكَعْنَا جَمِيعًا، ثُمَّ رَفَعَ، فَرَفَعْنَا جَمِيعًا، ثُمَّ سَجَدَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالصَّفِّ الَّذِي يَلِيهِ، وَالْآخَرُونَ قِيَامٌ يَحْرُسُونَهُمْ، فَلَمَّا سَجَدُوا وَقَامُوا، جَلَسَ الْآخَرُونَ، فَسَجَدُوا فِي مَكَانِهِمْ، ثُمَّ تَقَدَّمَ هَؤُلَاءِ إِلَى مَصَافِّ هَؤُلَاءِ، وَجَاءَ هَؤُلَاءِ إِلَى مَصَافِّ هَؤُلَاءِ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ رَكَعَ، فَرَكَعُوا جَمِيعًا، ثُمَّ رَفَعَ، فَرَفَعُوا جَمِيعًا، ثُمَّ سَجَدَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالصَّفُّ الَّذِي يَلِيهِ، وَالْآخَرُونَ قِيَامٌ يَحْرُسُونَهُمْ، فَلَمَّا جَلَسَ، جَلَسَ الْآخَرُونَ، فَسَجَدُوا، ثُمَّ سَلَّمَ عَلَيْهِمْ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ، قَالَ: فَصَلَّاهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَرَّتَيْنِ: مَرَّةً بِعُسْفَانَ، وَمَرَّةً بِأَرْضِ بَنِي سُلَيْمٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1236) وأحمد (16580) وصحّحه ابن حبان (2876) والحاكم (1/337-338) كلهم من حديث منصور بن معتمر، عن مجاهد، عن أبي عياش الزرقي فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني لحيان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1236) and Aḥmad (16580), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (2876) and al-Ḥākim (1/337–338), all through Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir, from Mujāhid, from Abū ʿAyyāsh al-Zuraqī.","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū Liḥyān","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū ʿAyyāsh al-Zuraqī reported: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at ʿUsfān when the polytheists confronted us under the command of Khālid ibn al-Walīd. They were positioned between us and the direction of prayer. The Prophet ﷺ led us in the noon prayer. They said: “They were in a position in which we could have taken them by surprise.” They then said: “A prayer is now approaching that is dearer to them than their children and their own lives.” Gabriel descended between the noon and afternoon prayers with the verses beginning: “When you are among them and lead them in prayer…” [Al-Nisāʾ 4:102] When the afternoon prayer arrived, the Prophet ﷺ instructed them to take up their weapons. We formed two rows behind him. He bowed and we all bowed; he rose and we all rose. The Prophet ﷺ prostrated together with the row immediately behind him, while the other row remained standing on guard. When the first row had prostrated and stood, the other row prostrated in its place. The two rows then exchanged positions. The Prophet ﷺ then bowed and they all bowed; he rose and they all rose. He prostrated with the row directly behind him while the others remained standing on guard. When he sat, the others sat and prostrated. He then pronounced the salutation to all of them and completed the prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the fear prayer in this manner twice: once at ʿUsfān and once in the territory of Banū Sulaym."]},"intro":{"ar":["كانت في السنة السادسة، بعد ستة أشهر من فتح قريظة. قال ابن إسحاق: خرج رسول الله ﷺ إلى بني لحيان يطلب بأصحاب الرجيع: خبيب بن عدي وأصحابه، وأظهر أنه يريد الشام ليصيب من القوم غِرَّة. سيرة ابن هشام (٢/٢٧٩).","وبنو لحيان هم الذين غدروا بخبيب وأصحابه يوم الرجيع، فخرج إليهم في مائتين من أصحابه. فلما سمعت به بنو لحيان هربوا إلى رؤوس الجبال، فلم يقدر منهم على أحد.","فسار إلى عسفان، فبعث عشرة فوارس إلى كراع الغميم، ليرى أهل مكة أنا قد جئنا مكة، ثم رجعوا إلى المدينة، وكانت غيبته عنها أربع عشرة ليلة. انظر «زاد المعاد» (٣/٢٧٦).","وفي عسفان استقبلهم جمع من المشركين، على رأسهم خالد بن الوليد، فقال المشركون: قد كانوا على حال لو أصبنا غرتهم. ثم قالوا: تأتي عليهم الآن صلاة هي أحب إليهم من أبنائهم وأنفسهم. فنزل جبريل عليه السلام بهذه الآيات بين الظهر والعصر:","﴿وَإِذَا كُنْتَ فِيهِمْ فَأَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلَاةَ﴾ [النساء: ١٠٢].","كما يرويه أبو عياش الزرقي وأبو هريرة في الحديثين التاليين."],"en":["It took place in the sixth year, six months after the conquest of Banū Qurayẓah. Ibn Isḥāq said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marched against Banū Liḥyān to avenge the companions of al-Rajīʿ—Khubayb ibn ʿAdī and his companions. He gave the appearance that he intended to travel toward Syria so that he might take the enemy by surprise. The Sīrah of Ibn Hishām (2/279).","Banū Liḥyān were the people who had betrayed Khubayb and his companions at al-Rajīʿ. The Prophet ﷺ marched against them with two hundred of his Companions. When Banū Liḥyān learned of his advance, they fled to the mountain peaks, and he was unable to reach any of them.","He proceeded to ʿUsfān and sent ten horsemen to Kurāʿ al-Ghamīm so that the people of Makkah would know that the Muslims had approached. They then returned to Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ had been absent from it for fourteen nights. See Zād al-Maʿād (3/276).","At ʿUsfān, a force of polytheists led by Khālid ibn al-Walīd confronted them. The polytheists said: “They were in a position in which we could have taken them by surprise.” They then said: “A prayer is now approaching that is dearer to them than their children and their own lives.” Between the noon and afternoon prayers, Gabriel brought down the verses beginning:","“When you are among them and lead them in prayer…”","[Al-Nisāʾ 4:102]","This is related by Abū ʿAyyāsh al-Zuraqī and Abū Hurayrah in the following two hadiths."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",560],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1236) وأحمد (16580)، وصححه ابن حبان (2876) والحاكم (1/337–338)."},{"num":8952,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَزَلَ بَيْنَ ضَجَنَانِ وَعُسْفَانَ، فَقَالَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ: إِنَّ لِهَؤُلَاءِ صَلَاةً هِيَ أَحَبُّ إِلَيْهِمْ مِنْ آبَائِهِمْ وَأَبْكَارِهِمْ - وَهِيَ الْعَصْرُ - فَأَجْمِعُوا أَمْرَكُمْ، فَمِيلُوا عَلَيْهِمْ مَيْلَةً وَاحِدَةً، وَإِنَّ جِبْرِيلَ عَلَيْهِ السلام أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَمَرَهُ أَنْ يَقْسِمَ أَصْحَابَهُ شَطْرَيْنِ فَيُصَلِّيَ بِبَعْضِهِمْ، وَتَقُومَ الطَّائِفَةُ الْأُخْرَى وَرَاءَهُمْ، وَلْيَأْخُذُوا حِذْرَهُمْ وَأَسْلِحَتَهُمْ، ثُمَّ تَأْتِي الْأُخْرَى فَيُصَلُّونَ مَعَهُ، وَيَأْخُذُ هَؤُلَاءِ حِذْرَهُمْ وَأَسْلِحَتَهُمْ لِتَكُونَ لَهُمْ رَكْعَةً رَكْعَةٌ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَلِرَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَكْعَتَانِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3035) والنسائي (1544) وأحمد (10765) كلاهما من حديث عبد الصمد بن عبد الوراث، قال: حدثنا سعيد بن عبيد الهنّائي، حدثنا عبد الله بن شقيق، قال: حدثنا أبو هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"غزوة بني لحيان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3035), al-Nasā’ī (1544), and Aḥmad (10765), through ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith, from Saʿīd ibn ʿUbayd al-Hannāʾī, from ʿAbd Allah ibn Shaqīq, from Abū Hurayrah.","chapter_en":"The Campaign Against Banū Liḥyān","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped between Ḍajnān and ʿUsfān. The polytheists said: “These people have a prayer that is dearer to them than their fathers and children—the afternoon prayer. Unite upon your plan and attack them in one concerted assault.” Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and instructed him to divide his Companions into two groups. He was to pray with one group while the other stood behind them on guard, taking their precautions and carrying their weapons. The second group would then come and pray with him while the first took its precautions and weapons. In this way, each group would perform one unit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while he would perform two units."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",561],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3035) والنسائي (1544) وأحمد (10765)."},{"num":8953,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّهُ قَالَ: بَعَثَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْثًا قِبَلَ السَّاحِلِ، فَأَمَّرَ عَلَيْهِمْ أَبَا عُبَيْدَةَ بْنَ الْجَرَّاحِ، وَهُمْ ثَلاَثُمِائَةٍ وَأَنَا فِيهِمْ، فَخَرَجْنَا حَتَّى إِذَا كُنَّا بِبَعْضِ الطَّرِيقِ، فَنِيَ الزَّادُ، فَأَمَرَ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بِأَزْوَادِ ذَلِكَ الْجَيْشِ، فَجُمِعَ ذَلِكَ كُلُّهُ فَكَانَ مِزْوَدَىْ تَمْرٍ، فَكَانَ يُقَوِّتُنَا كُلَّ يَوْمٍ قَلِيلاً قَلِيلاً، حَتَّى فَنِيَ، فَلَمْ يَكُنْ يُصِيبُنَا إِلاَّ تَمْرَةٌ تَمْرَةٌ. فَقُلْتُ: وَمَا تُغْنِي تَمْرَةٌ فَقَالَ: لَقَدْ وَجَدْنَا فَقْدَهَا حِينَ فَنِيَتْ. قَالَ: ثُمَّ انْتَهَيْنَا إِلَى الْبَحْرِ، فَإِذَا حُوتٌ مِثْلُ الظَّرِبِ، فَأَكَلَ مِنْهُ ذَلِكَ الْجَيْشُ ثَمَانِيَ عَشْرَةَ لَيْلَةً، ثُمَّ أَمَرَ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بِضِلَعَيْنِ مِنْ أَضْلاَعِهِ فَنُصِبَا، ثُمَّ أَمَرَ بِرَاحِلَةٍ، فَرُحِلَتْ ثُمَّ مَرَّتْ تَحْتَهُمَا، فَلَمْ تُصِبْهُمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في صفة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم (23) عن وهب بن كيسان، عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"سرية أبي عبيدة بن الجراح إلى سيف البحر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (23), al-Bukhārī (4360), and Muslim (1935/21).","chapter_en":"The Expedition of Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ Along the Seacoast","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition toward the coast, appointing Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ as its commander. They numbered three hundred men, and I was among them. We set out, but while we were partway through the journey, our provisions ran out. Abū ʿUbaydah ordered that all the army’s remaining provisions be gathered together. They amounted to two provision bags of dates. He rationed them to us little by little each day until they were exhausted, and eventually each man received only one date. I asked, “What benefit could a single date provide?” Jābir replied: “We certainly felt its loss when even that ran out.” We eventually reached the sea and found an enormous fish resembling a hill. The army ate from it for eighteen nights. Abū ʿUbaydah ordered that two of its ribs be erected, then had a camel saddled and led beneath them without touching them."]},"intro":{"ar":["وكانت في السنة السادسة، أو قبلها، قبل صلح الحديبية؛ وذلك لأنه ورد في الحديث أنهم خرجوا «يتلقون عير قريش»، ولا يُتصور هذا في الوقت الذي ذكره ابن سعد، يعني رجب سنة ثمان؛ لأنهم كانوا حينئذ في الهدنة.","وقد أنكر ذلك ابن القيم وابن حجر، ورجح ابن حجر أنه كان في السنة السادسة. انظر «الفتح» (٨/٧٨)."],"en":["It occurred in the sixth year or earlier, before the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. The hadith states that they went out “to intercept a caravan of Quraysh,” which could not have occurred at the time stated by Ibn Saʿd—Rajab of the eighth year—because the Muslims and Quraysh were then under a truce.","Ibn al-Qayyim and Ibn Ḥajar rejected that dating. Ibn Ḥajar considered it more likely that the expedition occurred in the sixth year. See Fatḥ al-Bārī (8/78)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",569],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[5652],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (23)، والبخاري (4360)، ومسلم (1935/21)."},{"num":8954,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ:  بَعَثَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَمَّرَ عَلَيْنَا أَبَا عُبَيْدَةَ نَتَلَقَّى عِيرًا لِقُرَيْشٍ، وَزَوَّدَنَا جِرَابًا مِنْ تَمْرٍ، لَمْ يَجِدْ لَنَا غَيْرَهُ، فَكَانَ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ يُعْطِينَا تَمْرَةً تَمْرَةً. قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ: كَيْفَ كُنْتُمْ تَصْنَعُونَ بِهَا؟ قَالَ: نَمَصُّهَا كَمَا يَمَصُّ الصَّبِيُّ، ثُمَّ نَشْرَبُ عَلَيْهَا مِنَ الْمَاءِ، فَتَكْفِينَا يَوْمَنَا إِلَى اللَّيْلِ، وَكُنَّا نَضْرِبُ بِعِصِيِّنَا الْخَبَطَ، ثُمَّ نَبُلُّهُ بِالْمَاءِ فَنَأْكُلُهُ. قَالَ: وَانْطَلَقْنَا عَلَى سَاحِلِ الْبَحْرِ، فَرُفِعَ لَنَا عَلَى سَاحِلِ الْبَحْرِ كَهَيْئَةِ الْكَثِيبِ الضَّخْمِ، فَأَتَيْنَاهُ فَإِذَا هِيَ دَابَّةٌ تُدْعَى الْعَنْبَرَ، قَالَ: قَالَ: أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ: مَيْتَةٌ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: لَا بَلْ نَحْنُ رُسُلُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَفِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، وَقَدِ اضْطُرِرْتُمْ فَكُلُوا. قَالَ: فَأَقَمْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَهْرًا، وَنَحْنُ ثَلَاثُ مِائَةٍ حَتَّى سَمِنَّا. قَالَ: وَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنَا نَغْتَرِفُ مِنْ وَقْبِ عَيْنِهِ بِالْقِلَالِ الدُّهْنَ، وَنَقْتَطِعُ مِنْهُ الْفِدَرَ كَالثَّوْرِ، أَوْ كَقَدْرِ الثَّوْرِ، فَلَقَدْ أَخَذَ مِنَّا أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ ثَلَاثَةَ عَشَرَ رَجُلًا، فَأَقْعَدَهُمْ فِي وَقْبِ عَيْنِهِ، وَأَخَذَ ضِلَعًا مِنْ أَضْلَاعِهِ، فَأَقَامَهَا، ثُمَّ رَحَلَ أَعْظَمَ بَعِيرٍ مَعَنَا، فَمَرَّ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا، وَتَزَوَّدْنَا مِنْ لَحْمِهِ وَشَائِقَ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا الْمَدِينَةَ أَتَيْنَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَذَكَرْنَا ذَلِكَ لَهُ فَقَالَ: هُوَ رِزْقٌ أَخْرَجَهُ اللهُ لَكُمْ، فَهَلْ مَعَكُمْ مِنْ لَحْمِهِ شَيْءٌ فَتُطْعِمُونَا؟. قَالَ: فَأَرْسَلْنَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْهُ فَأَكَلَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في الصيد (1935: 17) من طريقين عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر، ورواه البخاري في المغازي (4362)عن ابن جريج قال: أخبرني عمرو أنه سمع جابرا ثم قال: فأخبرني أبو الزبير أنه سمع جابرًا يقول: فذكر المرفوع: \"كلوا رزقًا أخرجه الله\".","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"سرية أبي عبيدة بن الجراح إلى سيف البحر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (1935/17) and al-Bukhārī (4362).","chapter_en":"The Expedition of Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ Along the Seacoast","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to intercept a caravan of Quraysh and appointed Abū ʿUbaydah as our commander. He supplied us with one leather bag of dates, having nothing else to give us. Abū ʿUbaydah distributed them one date at a time. I asked, “What did you do with a single date?” He replied: “We sucked it as a child sucks something, then drank water afterward. It sustained us from morning until night. We would also beat the leaves from the trees with our staffs, soak them in water, and eat them.” We continued along the seacoast until something resembling an enormous sandhill appeared before us on the shore. When we approached it, we found that it was a sea creature called al-ʿAnbar. Abū ʿUbaydah initially said: “It is carrion.” He then said: “No; we are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, traveling in Allah’s cause, and necessity has overtaken you, so eat.” We remained there for a month, although we numbered three hundred, until we regained our weight. I saw us scooping fat from its eye socket with large pitchers and cutting pieces of its flesh as large as an ox. Abū ʿUbaydah seated thirteen of our men inside its eye socket. He erected one of its ribs, then had the largest camel with us saddled and led underneath it. We took dried strips of its flesh as provisions. When we returned to Madinah, we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him what had happened. He said: “It was provision that Allah brought forth for you. Do you have any of its flesh with you so that you may feed us?” We sent some of it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ate it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",570],"full":1,"rep":[7354],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (1935: 17)، والبخاري (4362)."},{"num":8955,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَمْرِو بْنِ دِينَارٍ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ جَابِرَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، يَقُولُ: بَعَثَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ثَلاَثَمِائَةِ رَاكِبٍ أَمِيرُنَا أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ نَرْصُدُ عِيرَ قُرَيْشٍ، فَأَقَمْنَا بِالسَّاحِلِ نِصْفَ شَهْرٍ، فَأَصَابَنَا جُوعٌ شَدِيدٌ، حَتَّى أَكَلْنَا الْخَبَطَ، فَسُمِّيَ ذَلِكَ الْجَيْشُ جَيْشَ الْخَبَطِ، فَأَلْقَى لَنَا الْبَحْرُ دَابَّةً يُقَالُ لَهَا: الْعَنْبَرُ، فَأَكَلْنَا مِنْهُ نِصْفَ شَهْرٍ، وَادَّهَنَّا مِنْ وَدَكِهِ حَتَّى ثَابَتْ إِلَيْنَا أَجْسَامُنَا، فَأَخَذَ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ ضِلَعًا مِنْ أَضْلاَعِهِ، فَنَصَبَهُ فَعَمَدَ إِلَى أَطْوَلِ رَجُلٍ مَعَهُ ـ قَالَ سُفْيَانُ مَرَّةً: ضِلَعًا مِنْ أَعْضَائِهِ فَنَصَبَهُ وَأَخَذَ رَجُلاً وَبَعِيرًا ـ فَمَرَّ تَحْتَهُ.","قَالَ جَابِرٌ: وَكَانَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ نَحَرَ ثَلاَثَ جَزَائِرَ، ثُمَّ نَحَرَ ثَلاَثَ جَزَائِرَ، ثُمَّ نَحَرَ ثَلاَثَ جَزَائِرَ، ثُمَّ إِنَّ أَبَا عُبَيْدَةَ نَهَاهُ.","كان عَمْرٌو يَقُولُ: أَخْبَرَنَا أَبُو صَالِحٍ، أَنَّ قَيْسَ بْنَ سَعْدٍ قَالَ لأَبِيهِ: كُنْتُ فِي الْجَيْشِ فَجَاعُوا، قَالَ: انْحَرْ، قَالَ: نَحَرْتُ قَالَ: ثُمَّ جَاعُوا، قَالَ: انْحَرْ قَالَ: نَحَرْتُ قَالَ: ثُمَّ جَاعُوا قَالَ: انْحَرْ قَالَ: نَحَرْتُ ثُمَّ جَاعُوا قَالَ: انْحَرْ قَالَ: نُهِيتُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4361) واللفظ له، ومسلم في الصيد (1935: 18) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، عن عمرو بن دينار فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"سرية أبي عبيدة بن الجراح إلى سيف البحر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4361), whose wording this is, and Muslim (1935/18).","chapter_en":"The Expedition of Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ Along the Seacoast","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAmr ibn Dīnār reported: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent three hundred mounted men under the command of Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ to watch for a caravan of Quraysh. We remained on the coast for half a month and suffered such severe hunger that we ate leaves beaten from the trees. The expedition therefore became known as the Army of al-Khabaṭ. The sea cast out for us a creature called al-ʿAnbar. We ate from it for half a month and rubbed its fat upon our bodies until our physical strength and fullness returned. Abū ʿUbaydah took one of its ribs and erected it. He then selected the tallest man with him—Sufyān once narrated: “He erected a bone from its body”—and had the man ride a camel beneath it. Jābir said: One of the men slaughtered three camels for the army, then another three, and then another three. Abū ʿUbaydah subsequently prohibited him from slaughtering more. ʿAmr would also relate: Abū Ṣāliḥ informed us that Qays ibn Saʿd told his father: “I was with the army when they became hungry.” His father said, “Slaughter a camel.” Qays said, “I did.” He said, “Then they became hungry again.” His father said, “Slaughter another.” He replied, “I did.” He said, “Then they became hungry again.” His father said, “Slaughter another.” He replied, “I did.” He said, “Then they became hungry once more.” His father said, “Slaughter another.” Qays replied, “I was prohibited from doing so.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",571],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4361) واللفظ له، ومسلم (1935: 18)."},{"num":8956,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عُمَرَ-فِي حَدِيثِ طَوِيلٍ- أَنْ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَرَ عبدالرحمن بْنَ عَوْفٍ أَنْ يَتَجَهَّزُ لِسَرِيَّةٍ أَمَّرَهُ عَلَيْهَا، فَأَصْبَحَ قَدِ اعْتَمَّ بِعِمَامَةٍ كَرَابِيسَ سَوْدَاءَ، فَدَعَاهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَنَقَضَهَا، فعممه وَأَرْسَلَ مِنْ خَلْفِهِ أَرْبَعَ أَصَابِعَ أَوْ نحوها، ثُمَّ قَالَ: هَكَذَا يَا ابْنَ عَوْفٍ فَاعْتَمَّ، فَإِنَّهُ أعرف وَأَحْسَنُ، ثُمَّ أَمَرَ بِلَالًا، أَنْ يرفع إِلَيْهِ اللِّوَاءَ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اغْزُوا جَمِيعًا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، قَاتِلُوا مَنْ كَفَرَ بِاللَّهِ، لَا تَغُلُّوا، وَلَا تَغْدِرُوا، وَلَا تُمَثِّلُوا، ولاتقتلوا وَلِيدًا، فَهَذَا عَهْدُ اللَّهِ وَسُنَّةَ نبيكم فِيكُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (6175)، والطبراني في الأوسط (4668)، والحاكم (4/540) كلهم من طرق عن أبي الجماهر محمد بن عثمان الدمشقي، حدثنا الهيثم بن حميد، حدثني حفص بن غيلان، عن عطاء بن أبي رباح فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"سرية عبدالرحمن بن عوف إلى دومة الجندل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (6175), al-Ṭabarānī in Al-Awsaṭ (4668), and al-Ḥākim (8623).","chapter_en":"The Expedition of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf to Dūmat al-Jandal","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported in a lengthy hadith that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf to prepare for an expedition over which he had appointed him commander. He came in the morning wearing a turban made of black cotton cloth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew him close, unwrapped the turban, then wrapped it around his head himself, allowing approximately four finger-widths of it to hang down behind him. He said: “This is how you should wear your turban, Ibn ʿAwf, for it is more distinctive and more becoming.” He then instructed Bilāl to give him the banner. Bilāl handed it to him, and the Prophet ﷺ praised Allah and invoked blessings upon His Prophet. He then said: “Take it, Ibn ʿAwf. Campaign together in Allah’s cause and fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, betray anyone, mutilate the dead, or kill a child. This is Allah’s covenant and the way of your Prophet among you.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["كانت في شعبان سنة ست من مهاجر رسول الله ﷺ. دعا رسول الله ﷺ عبد الرحمن بن عوف، فأقعده بين يديه وعممه بيده، وقال: «اغز بسم الله وفي سبيل الله، فقاتل من كفر بالله، لا تغل ولا تغدر ولا تقتل وليدًا».","وبعثه إلى كلب بدومة الجندل، وقال: «إن استجابوا لك فتزوج ابنة ملكهم». فسار عبد الرحمن حتى قدم دومة الجندل، فمكث ثلاثة أيام يدعوهم إلى الإسلام.","فأسلم الأصبغ بن عمرو الكلبي، وكان نصرانيًّا وكان رأسهم، وأسلم معه ناس كثير من قومه، وأقام من أقام على إعطاء الجزية. وتزوج عبد الرحمن تماضر بنت الأصبغ، وقدم بها إلى المدينة، وهي أم أبي سلمة بن عبد الرحمن. ذكره الواقدي في «مغازيه» (٢/٥٦٠–٥٦٢)."],"en":["It took place in Shaʿbān of the sixth year after the Messenger of Allah’s emigration. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, seated him before him, and wrapped a turban around his head with his own hands. He said: “Campaign in Allah’s name and in Allah’s cause. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, betray anyone, or kill a child.”","He sent him against the tribe of Kalb at Dūmat al-Jandal and said: “If they respond favorably to you, marry the daughter of their leader.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān traveled until he reached Dūmat al-Jandal and remained there for three days, inviting them to Islam.","Al-Aṣbagh ibn ʿAmr al-Kalbī embraced Islam. He had been a Christian and was their leader. Many of his people embraced Islam with him, while those who remained upon their religion agreed to pay the jizyah. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān married Tumāḍir bint al-Aṣbagh and brought her to Madinah. She became the mother of Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Al-Wāqidī mentioned it in his Maghāzī (2/560–562)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",573],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (6175)، والطبراني في «الأوسط» (4668)، والحاكم (8623)."},{"num":8957,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ: أَنَّ نَاسًا مِنْ عُكْلٍ وَعُرَيْنَةَ قَدِمُوا الْمَدِينَةَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَتَكَلَّمُوا بِالإِسْلاَمِ، فَقَالُوا: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ إِنَّا كُنَّا أَهْلَ ضَرْعٍ، وَلَمْ نَكُنْ أَهْلَ رِيفٍ، وَاسْتَوْخَمُوا الْمَدِينَةَ، فَأَمَرَ لَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِذَوْدٍ وَرَاعٍ، وَأَمَرَهُمْ أَنْ يَخْرُجُوا فِيهِ، فَيَشْرَبُوا مِنْ أَلْبَانِهَا وَأَبْوَالِهَا، فَانْطَلَقُوا حَتَّى إِذَا كَانُوا نَاحِيَةَ الْحَرَّةِ، كَفَرُوا بَعْدَ إِسْلاَمِهِمْ، وَقَتَلُوا رَاعِيَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَاسْتَاقُوا الذَّوْدَ، فَبَلَغَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَبَعَثَ الطَّلَبَ فِي آثَارِهِمْ، فَأَمَرَ بِهِمْ، فَسَمَرُوا أَعْيُنَهُمْ، وَقَطَعُوا أَيْدِيَهُمْ، وَتُرِكُوا فِي نَاحِيَةِ الْحَرَّةِ حَتَّى مَاتُوا عَلَى حَالِهِمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4192) واللفظ له، ومسلم في القسامة (1671: 14) كلاهما من طريق سعيد، عن قتادة، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"سرية كرز بن جابر الفهري إلى العرنيين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4192), whose wording this is, and Muslim (1671/14).","chapter_en":"The Expedition of Kurz ibn Jābir al-Fihrī Against the ʿUrayniyyūn","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء من الأحداث التي بين غزوة بني قريظة وصلح الحديبية","group_en":"Events Between the Campaign of Banū Qurayẓah and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_no":48,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: Some men from ʿUkl and ʿUraynah came to the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah and professed Islam. They said: “Prophet of Allah, we are people accustomed to livestock, not agricultural settlements.” They found the climate of Madinah unhealthy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ provided them with a herd of camels and a shepherd, instructing them to go out with the herd and drink from its milk and urine. They departed, but when they reached the region of al-Ḥarrah, they renounced Islam, killed the Prophet’s shepherd, and drove away the camels. When the Prophet ﷺ learned of this, he sent men in pursuit. After they were captured, he ordered that their eyes be seared and their hands cut off. They were left in the region of al-Ḥarrah until they died in that state."]},"intro":{"ar":["كانت في شوال سنة ست من مهاجر رسول الله ﷺ. قالوا: قدم نفر من عرينة، ثمانية، على رسول الله ﷺ، فأسلموا واستوبؤوا المدينة.","فأمر بهم رسول الله ﷺ إلى لقاحه، وكانت ترعى بذي الجدر ناحية قباء، قريبًا من عير، على ستة أميال من المدينة. فكانوا فيها حتى صحوا وسمنوا.","فغدوا على اللقاح فاستاقوها، فأدركهم يسار مولى رسول الله ﷺ ومعه نفر، فقاتلهم، فقطعوا يده ورجله، وغرزوا الشوك في لسانه وعينيه حتى مات.","وبلغ رسول الله ﷺ الخبر، فبعث في أثرهم عشرين فارسًا، واستعمل عليهم كرز بن جابر الفهري. فأدركوهم، فأحاطوا بهم وأسروهم وربطوهم، وأردفوهم على الخيل حتى قدموا بهم المدينة.","وكان رسول الله ﷺ بالغابة، فخرجوا بهم نحوه، فلقوه بالزغابة عند مجتمع السيول. فأمر بهم، فقُطعت أيديهم وأرجلهم، وسُملت أعينهم، وصُلبوا هناك.","وأنزل على رسول الله ﷺ:","﴿إِنَّمَا جَزَاءُ الَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَسَادًا﴾ الآية [المائدة: ٣٣].","فلم يسمل بعد ذلك عينًا.","وكانت اللقاح خمس عشرة لقحة غزارًا، فردوها إلى المدينة. ففقد رسول الله ﷺ منها لقحة تدعى الحناء، فسأل عنها، فقيل: نحروها. «الطبقات» (٢/٩٣)، و«مغازي الواقدي» (٢/٥٦٨–٥٧٠)."],"en":["It took place in Shawwāl of the sixth year after the Messenger of Allah’s emigration. Eight men from ʿUraynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, embraced Islam, and found the climate of Madinah unhealthy.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them to his milch camels, which grazed at Dhū al-Jadr near Qubāʾ, close to Mount ʿAyr, six miles from Madinah. They remained there until they recovered and gained weight.","They then attacked the camels and drove them away. Yasār, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, caught up with them accompanied by several men and fought them. They cut off his hand and foot and thrust thorns into his tongue and eyes until he died.","When the news reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he sent twenty horsemen in pursuit under the command of Kurz ibn Jābir al-Fihrī. They overtook the men, surrounded and captured them, bound them, and carried them behind the riders on their horses to Madinah.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Ghābah, so they took the prisoners toward him and met him at al-Zaghābah, near the place where floodwaters converged. He ordered that their hands and feet be cut off, their eyes seared, and that they be left there suspended.","The following verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ:","“The penalty for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and spread corruption in the land…”","[Al-Māʾidah 5:33]","After that, he did not sear anyone’s eyes.","The herd consisted of fifteen milk-rich she-camels, which were returned to Madinah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ found one she-camel named al-Ḥannāʾ missing. When he asked about her, he was told that the raiders had slaughtered her. Al-Ṭabaqāt (2/93) and Maghāzī al-Wāqidī (2/568–570)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",577],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4192) واللفظ له، ومسلم (1671: 14)."},{"num":8958,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس قَالَ: اعْتَمَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَرْبَعَ عُمَرٍ، كُلُّهُنَّ فِي ذِي الْقَعْدَةِ، إِلاَّ الَّتِي كَانَتْ مَعَ حَجَّتِهِ: عُمْرَةً مِنَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ فِي ذِي الْقَعْدَةِ، وَعُمْرَةً مِنَ الْعَامِ الْمُقْبِلِ فِي ذِي الْقَعْدَةِ، وَعُمْرَةً مِنَ الْجِعْرَانَةِ، حَيْثُ قَسَمَ غَنَائِمَ حُنَيْنٍ فِي ذِي الْقَعْدَةِ، وَعُمْرَةً مَعَ حَجَّتِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4148) ومسلم في الحج (217:1253) كلاهما عن هدبة وقيل: هداب – بن خالد، حدثنا همام، حدثنا قتادة، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4148) and Muslim in al-Ḥajj (1253/217), both from Hudbah—or Hudāb—ibn Khālid, from Hammām, from Qatādah, from Anas.","chapter_en":"The Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed four ʿumrahs, all of them in Dhū al-Qaʿdah except the one performed together with his pilgrimage: the ʿumrah of al-Ḥudaybiyyah in Dhū al-Qaʿdah; the ʿumrah of the following year in Dhū al-Qaʿdah; the ʿumrah from al-Jiʿrānah, where he distributed the spoils of Ḥunayn, in Dhū al-Qaʿdah; and the ʿumrah performed with his pilgrimage."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿لَقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ﴾ [الفتح: ١٨].","اتفق معظم أهل السير والمغازي أنها كانت في شهر ذي القعدة سنة ست.","وقال الله تعالى:","﴿لَقَدْ صَدَقَ اللَّهُ رَسُولَهُ الرُّؤْيَا بِالْحَقِّ لَتَدْخُلُنَّ الْمَسْجِدَ الْحَرَامَ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ آمِنِينَ مُحَلِّقِينَ رُءُوسَكُمْ وَمُقَصِّرِينَ لَا تَخَافُونَ فَعَلِمَ مَا لَمْ تَعْلَمُوا فَجَعَلَ مِنْ دُونِ ذَلِكَ فَتْحًا قَرِيبًا﴾ [الفتح: ٢٧].","ذكر المفسرون أن خروج النبي ﷺ إلى الحديبية كان للرؤيا التي رآها وهو بالمدينة. فلما ساروا عام الحديبية لم يشك جماعة منهم أن هذه الرؤيا ستتحقق في ذلك العام.","ولكن لما منعته قريش من دخول مكة وقع في نفوس بعض الصحابة من ذلك شيء، حتى سأل عمر بن الخطاب فقال له: أفلم تكن تخبرنا أنا سنأتي البيت ونطوف به؟","فقال له: «بلى. أخبرتك أنك تأتيه عامك هذا؟» قال: لا. قال: «فإنك آتيه ومطوف به».","ولذا أكد الله سبحانه وتعالى:","﴿لَقَدْ صَدَقَ اللَّهُ رَسُولَهُ الرُّؤْيَا بِالْحَقِّ﴾","لتحقيق الخبر وتوكيده، وقد حصل ذلك في العام المقبل."],"en":["Allah Most High says:","“Allah was certainly pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you beneath the tree.”","[Al-Fatḥ 48:18]","Most scholars of the Prophet’s biography and military campaigns agreed that it took place in Dhū al-Qaʿdah of the sixth year.","Allah Most High also says:","“Allah has certainly fulfilled His Messenger’s vision in truth: Allah willing, you will surely enter the Sacred Mosque in safety, with your heads shaved or your hair shortened, without fear. He knew what you did not know, so He granted before that a near victory.”","[Al-Fatḥ 48:27]","The commentators stated that the Prophet ﷺ set out for al-Ḥudaybiyyah because of a vision he had seen while in Madinah. When the Muslims departed in the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, a group of them had no doubt that the vision would be fulfilled during that same year.","When Quraysh prevented him from entering Makkah, however, some of the Companions experienced uncertainty. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb asked him: “Did you not tell us that we would reach the Sacred House and circumambulate it?”","The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Yes. But did I tell you that you would reach it this year?” ʿUmar answered, “No.” He said: “You will certainly reach it and circumambulate it.”","Allah therefore emphatically declared:","“Allah has certainly fulfilled His Messenger’s vision in truth,”","confirming and emphasizing the promise. It was fulfilled the following year."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",581],"full":1,"rep":[9104],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4148) ومسلم (217:1253)."},{"num":8959,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَرْوَانَ، وَالْمِسْوَرِ بْنِ مَخْرَمَةَ، قَالاَ: خَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَامَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ فِي بِضْعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ بِذِي الْحُلَيْفَةِ قَلَّدَ الْهَدْىَ وَأَشْعَرَ وَأَحْرَمَ مِنْهَا. لاَ أُحْصِي كَمْ سَمِعْتُهُ مِنْ سُفْيَانَ حَتَّى سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ: لاَ أَحْفَظُ مِنَ الزُّهْرِيِّ الإِشْعَارَ، وَالتَّقْلِيدَ، فَلاَ أَدْرِي ـ يَعْنِي ـ مَوْضِعَ الإِشْعَارِ وَالتَّقْلِيدِ، أَوِ الْحَدِيثَ كُلَّهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4158،4157) عن علي بن عبد الله، حدثنا سفيان، عن الزهري، عن عروة، عن مروان والمسور بن مخرمة قالا فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"إحرام النبي ﷺ من ذي الحليفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4157, 4158).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Enters the State of Iḥrām at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Marwān and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah reported: In the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, the Prophet ﷺ set out with between thirteen and fifteen hundred of his Companions. When he reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, he placed identifying garlands upon the sacrificial animals, marked them, and entered the state of iḥrām from there. The narrator said: I cannot count how many times I heard it from Sufyān until I heard him say: “I do not reliably remember the words concerning marking and garlanding the sacrificial animals from al-Zuhrī.” The narrator was unsure whether Sufyān meant only the passage concerning marking and garlanding or the entire hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",582],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4157، 4158)."},{"num":8960,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ نَافِعٍ، أَنَّ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا خَرَجَ مُعْتَمِرًا فِي الْفِتْنَةِ، فَقَالَ: إِنْ صُدِدْتُ عَنِ الْبَيْتِ، صَنَعْنَا كَمَا صَنَعْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. فَأَهَلَّ بِعُمْرَةٍ مِنْ أَجْلِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ أَهَلَّ بِعُمْرَةٍ عَامَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الحج (103) عن نافع قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"إحرام النبي ﷺ من ذي الحليفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (103), al-Bukhārī (4183), and Muslim (1230/180).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Enters the State of Iḥrām at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Nāfiʿ reported: During the period of civil strife, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar set out intending to perform ʿumrah. He said: “If I am prevented from reaching the Sacred House, we shall do as we did with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He therefore entered iḥrām for ʿumrah because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had entered iḥrām for ʿumrah in the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",583],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (103)، والبخاري (4183)، ومسلم (1230/180)."},{"num":8961,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ نَافِعٍ أَنَّ عُبَيْدَ اللَّهِ بن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، وَسَالِمَ بن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ أَخْبَرَاهُ أَنَّهُمَا كَلَّمَا عبد اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ وَقَالَ لَهُ: لَوْ أَقَمْتَ الْعَامَ، فَإِنِّي أَخَافُ أَنْ لاَ تَصِلَ إِلَى الْبَيْتِ، قَالَ: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَحَالَ كُفَّارُ قُرَيْشٍ دُونَ الْبَيْتِ، فَنَحَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هَدَايَاهُ، وَحَلَقَ وَقَصَّرَ أَصْحَابُهُ. وَقَالَ: أُشْهِدُكُمْ أَنِّي أَوْجَبْتُ عُمْرَةً، فَإِنْ خُلِّيَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ الْبَيْتِ طُفْتُ، وَإِنْ حِيلَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ الْبَيْتِ صَنَعْتُ كَمَا صَنَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَسَارَ سَاعَةً، ثُمَّ قَالَ: مَا أُرَى شَأْنَهُمَا إِلاَّ وَاحِدًا، أُشْهِدُكُمْ أَنِّي قَدْ أَوْجَبْتُ حَجَّةً مَعَ عُمْرَتِي، فَطَافَ طَوَافًا وَاحِدًا، وَسَعْيًا وَاحِدًا، حَتَّى حَلَّ مِنْهُمَا جَمِيعًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4185) ومسلم في الحج (181:1230) كلاهما من طريق نافع به، والسياق للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"إحرام النبي ﷺ من ذي الحليفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4185) and Muslim (1230:181).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Enters the State of Iḥrām at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Nāfiʿ reported that ʿUbayd Allah ibn ʿAbd Allah and Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allah told him that they spoke to ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar and said, “If only you would remain here this year, for we fear that you may not reach the Sacred House.” He replied, “We set out with the Prophet ﷺ, but the disbelievers of Quraysh prevented him from reaching the House. The Prophet ﷺ therefore slaughtered his sacrificial animals and shaved his head, while his Companions shortened their hair.” He then said, “I call you to witness that I have entered into ʿumrah. If I am allowed to reach the House, I shall circumambulate it; but if I am prevented from reaching it, I shall do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did.” After travelling for a while, he said, “I consider the matter of the two rites to be the same. I call you to witness that I have entered into ḥajj together with my ʿumrah.” He performed one circumambulation and one saʿy, and did not leave the state of consecration until he had completed both rites."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",584],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4185)، ومسلم (181:1230)."},{"num":8962,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  مَنْ يَصْعَدُ الثَّنِيَّةَ، ثَنِيَّةَ الْمُرَارِ، فَإِنَّهُ يُحَطُّ عَنْهُ مَا حُطَّ عَنْ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ.","قَالَ: فَكَانَ أَوَّلَ مَنْ صَعِدَهَا خَيْلُنَا خَيْلُ بَنِي الْخَزْرَجِ، ثُمَّ نام النَّاسُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: أخرجه مسلم في صفات المنافقين (12:2880) عن عبيد الله بن معاذ العنبري، حدثنا أبي، حدثنا قرة بن خالد، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"طريق المسلمين إلى الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by Muslim (2880:12).","chapter_en":"The Route Taken by the Muslims to al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever ascends the mountain pass—the Pass of al-Marār—will have his sins removed as they were removed from the Children of Israel.” He said: “The first to ascend it were our horsemen, the horsemen of Banū al-Khazraj, and then the people followed one after another.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn Shihāb said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed the people, saying: “Take the road to the right, through the middle of al-Ḥumush, along a route that will bring you out at the Pass of al-Marār, descending toward al-Ḥudaybiyyah from below Makkah.” Ibn Isḥāq mentioned it, as recorded in Ibn Hishām’s Sīrah (2/310). This route was taken to avoid the polytheists’ cavalry."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: أخرجه مسلم (12:2880)."},{"num":8963,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  مَنْ يَصْعَدُ ثَنِيَّةَ الْمُرَارِ. أَوِ: الْمَرَارِ بِمِثْلِ حَدِيثِ مُعَاذٍ، غَيْرَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: وَإِذَا هُوَ أَعْرَابِيٌّ جَاءَ يَنْشُدُ ضَالَّةً لَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في صفات المنافقين (13:2880) عن يحيى بن حبيب الحارثي، حدثنا خالد بن الحارث، حدثنا قرة، حدثنا أبو الزبير، عن جابر بن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"طريق المسلمين إلى الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by Muslim (2880:13).","chapter_en":"The Route Taken by the Muslims to al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever climbs the Pass of al-Marār—or al-Marār…” He then related a report similar to the narration of Muʿādh, except that he said: “There was a Bedouin who had come looking for a lost animal.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (13:2880)."},{"num":8964,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى إِذَا كُنَّا بَعَسَفَانَ قَالَ لَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ عُيُونَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ الْآنَ عَلَى ضَجْنَانَ، فَأَيُّكُمْ يَعْرِفُ طَرِيقَ ذَاتِ الْحَنْظَلِ؟. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ أَمْسَى: هَلْ مِنْ رَجُلٍ يَنْزِلُ فَيَسْعَى بَيْنَ يَدَيِ الرِّكَابِ؟ فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ: أَنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَنَزَلْتُ، فَجَعَلَتِ الْحِجَارَةُ تَنْكُبُهُ، وَالشَّجَرُ يَتَعَلَّقُ بِثِيَابِهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ارْكَبْ، ثُمَّ نَزَلَ آخَرُ، فَجَعَلَتِ الْحِجَارَةُ [تَنْكُبُهُ] وَالشَّجَرُ يَتَعَلَّقُ بِثِيَابِهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ارْكَبْ. ثُمَّ وَقَعْنَا عَلَى الطَّرِيقِ، حَتَّى سِرْنَا فِي ثَنِيَّةٍ، يُقَالُ لَهَا: الْحَنْظَلُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا مَثَلُ هَذِهِ الثَّلَاثَةِ إِلَّا كَمَثَلِ الْبَابِ الَّذِي دَخَلَ فِيهِ بَنُو إِسْرَائِيلَ، ﴿.. ادْخُلُوا الْبَابَ سُجَّدًا وَقُولُوا حِطَّةٌ نَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ خَطَايَاكُمْ..﴾ [البقرة: ٥٨] لَا يَجُوزُ أَحَدٌ اللَّيْلَةَ هَذِهِ الثَّنِيَّةَ إِلَّا غُفِرَ لَهُ. فَجَعَلَ النَّاسُ يُسْرِعُونَ وَيَجُوزُونَ، وَكَانَ آخِرَ مَنْ جَازَ قَتَادَةُ بْنُ النُّعْمَانِ فِي آخِرِ الْقَوْمِ، قَالَ: فَجَعَلَ النَّاسُ يُرْكِبُ بَعْضُهُمْ بَعْضًا حَتَّى تَلَاحَقْنَا، قَالَ: فَنَزَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَزَلْنَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار –كشف الأستار (1812) عن إسحاق بن بهلول الأنباري، ثنا محمد بن إسماعيل بن أبي فديك، ثنا هشام بن سعد، عن زيد بن أسلم، عن عطاء بن يسار، عن أبي سعيد فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"طريق المسلمين إلى الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Related by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (1812).","chapter_en":"The Route Taken by the Muslims to al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd reported: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we reached ʿUsfān, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “The scouts of Quraysh are now at Ḍajnān. Which of you knows the road of Dhāt al-Ḥanẓal?” When evening came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Is there a man who will dismount and go ahead of the mounted party?” A man said, “I will, Messenger of Allah.” He dismounted, but the stones kept striking him and the branches caught his clothing, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Mount again.” Another man then dismounted, but the stones struck him and the branches caught his clothing, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told him: “Mount again.” We eventually found the road and travelled through a pass called al-Ḥanẓal. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The likeness of this pass is that of the gate through which the Children of Israel entered. They were told: ‘Enter the gate prostrating and say, “Relieve us of our burdens,” and We shall forgive you your sins’ [al-Baqarah 2:58]. No one will cross this pass tonight without being forgiven.” The people began hurrying across it. The last to cross was Qatādah ibn al-Nuʿmān, who was at the rear of the company. The people crowded upon one another until we had all caught up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then dismounted, and we dismounted."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في «كشف الأستار» (1812)."},{"num":8965,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ خَالِدٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَامَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ، فَأَصَابَنَا مَطَرٌ ذَاتَ لَيْلَةٍ، فَصَلَّى لَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الصُّبْحَ، ثُمَّ أَقْبَلَ عَلَيْنَا فَقَالَ: أَتَدْرُونَ مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ. قُلْنَا: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ. فَقَالَ: قَالَ اللَّهُ: أَصْبَحَ مِنْ عِبَادِي مُؤْمِنٌ بِي وَكَافِرٌ بِي، فَأَمَّا مَنْ قَالَ: مُطِرْنَا بِرَحْمَةِ اللَّهِ وَبِرِزْقِ اللَّهِ وَبِفَضْلِ اللَّهِ. فَهْوَ مُؤْمِنٌ بِي، كَافِرٌ بِالْكَوْكَبِ. وَأَمَّا مَنْ قَالَ: مُطِرْنَا بِنَجْمِ كَذَا. فَهْوَ مُؤْمِنٌ بِالْكَوْكَبِ، كَافِرٌ بِي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4147) ومسلم في الإيمان (125:71) كلاهما من طريق صالح بن كيسان، عن عبيد الله بن عبد الله، عن زيد بن خالد رضي الله عنه قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب نزول المطر في الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4147) and Muslim (71:125).","chapter_en":"Rainfall at al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Khālid reported: We accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, and rain fell upon us one night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer and then turned toward us and said: “Do you know what your Lord has said?” We replied, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Allah said: ‘This morning some of My servants became believers in Me and others became disbelievers in Me. Whoever said, “We were given rain through Allah’s mercy, provision and grace,” is a believer in Me and a disbeliever in the stars. But whoever said, “We were given rain because of such-and-such a star,” is a believer in the stars and a disbeliever in Me.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4147)، ومسلم (125:71)."},{"num":8966,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: تَعُدُّونَ أَنْتُمُ الْفَتْحَ فَتْحَ مَكَّةَ، وَقَدْ كَانَ فَتْحُ مَكَّةَ فَتْحًا، وَنَحْنُ نَعُدُّ الْفَتْحَ بَيْعَةَ الرُّضْوَانِ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ. كُنَّا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَرْبَعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً، وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةُ بِئْرٌ، فَنَزَحْنَاهَا، فَلَمْ نَتْرُكْ فِيهَا قَطْرَةً، فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَتَاهَا، فَجَلَسَ عَلَى شَفِيرِهَا، ثُمَّ دَعَا بِإِنَاءٍ مِنْ مَاءٍ فَتَوَضَّأَ، ثُمَّ مَضْمَضَ وَدَعَا، ثُمَّ صَبَّهُ فِيهَا، فَتَرَكْنَاهَا غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍ، ثُمَّ إِنَّهَا أَصْدَرَتْنَا مَا شِئْنَا نَحْنُ وَرِكَابَنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4150) عن عبيد الله بن موسى، عن إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء رضي الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن بيعة الرضوان يوم الحديبية هي الفتح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4150).","chapter_en":"The Pledge of al-Riḍwān at al-Ḥudaybiyyah Was the Conquest","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ said: You consider the conquest to be the conquest of Makkah. The conquest of Makkah was indeed a conquest, but we considered the Pledge of al-Riḍwān on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah to be the conquest. We were fourteen hundred men with the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Ḥudaybiyyah had a well, and we drew out all its water until not a single drop remained. When this reached the Prophet ﷺ, he came to the well and sat at its edge. He called for a vessel of water, performed ablution, rinsed his mouth, supplicated, and then poured the water into the well. We left it for a short while, after which it supplied all the water that we and our riding animals required."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",589],"full":1,"rep":[9671,13310],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4150)."},{"num":8967,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مِرْدَاسٍ الأَسْلَمِيِّ، قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَذْهَبُ الصَّالِحُونَ الأَوَّلُ فَالأَوَّلُ، وَيَبْقَى حُفَالَةٌ كَحُفَالَةِ الشَّعِيرِ أَوِ التَّمْرِ، لاَ يُبَالِيهِمُ اللَّهُ بَالَةً."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الرقاق (6434) عن يحيى بن حماد، حدثنا أبو عوانة، عن بيان، عن قيس بن أبي حازم، عن مرداس الأسلمي قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (6434). A narration in al-Bukhārī (4156) states that Mirdās was one of the Companions of the Tree.","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Mirdās al-Aslamī reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The righteous will depart, one after another, and there will remain only dregs like the husks of barley or the refuse of dates. Allah will give them no consideration.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[16016],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6434). وجاء في الرواية عند البخاري (4156) أن مرداسا كان من أصحاب الشجرة."},{"num":8968,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ أَسْلَمَ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: خَرَجْتُ مَعَ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ إِلَى السُّوقِ، فَلَحِقَتْ عُمَرَ امْرَأَةٌ شَابَّةٌ، فَقَالَتْ: يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، هَلَكَ زَوْجِي وَتَرَكَ صِبْيَةً صِغَارًا، وَاللَّهِ مَا يُنْضِجُونَ كُرَاعًا، وَلاَ لَهُمْ زَرْعٌ وَلاَ ضَرْعٌ، وَخَشِيتُ أَنْ تَأْكُلَهُمُ الضَّبُعُ، وَأَنَا بِنْتُ خُفَافِ بْنِ إِيمَاءَ الْغِفَارِيِّ، وَقَدْ شَهِدَ أَبِي الْحُدَيْبِيَةَ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَوَقَفَ مَعَهَا عُمَرُ، وَلَمْ يَمْضِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: مَرْحَبًا بِنَسَبٍ قَرِيبٍ. ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ إِلَى بَعِيرٍ ظَهِيرٍ كَانَ مَرْبُوطًا فِي الدَّارِ، فَحَمَلَ عَلَيْهِ غِرَارَتَيْنِ مَلأَهُمَا طَعَامًا، وَحَمَلَ بَيْنَهُمَا نَفَقَةً وَثِيَابًا، ثُمَّ نَاوَلَهَا بِخِطَامِهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اقْتَادِيهِ، فَلَنْ يَفْنَى حَتَّى يَأْتِيَكُمُ اللَّهُ بِخَيْرٍ. فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ: يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، أَكْثَرْتَ لَهَا. قَالَ عُمَرُ: ثَكِلَتْكَ أُمُّكَ، وَاللَّهِ إِنِّي لأَرَى أَبَا هَذِهِ وَأَخَاهَا، قَدْ حَاصَرَا حِصْنًا زَمَانًا، فَافْتَتَحَاهُ، ثُمَّ أَصْبَحْنَا نَسْتَفِيءُ سُهْمَانَهُمَا فِيهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4161،4160) عن إسماعيل بن عبد الله، قال: حدثني مالك، عن زيد بن أسلم، عن أبيه، قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4160, 4161).","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Aslam reported from his father: I went with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, to the marketplace. A young woman caught up with him and said, “Commander of the Faithful, my husband has died and left behind small children. By Allah, they cannot even cook a sheep’s trotter, and they possess neither crops nor milk-producing animals. I fear that a hyena may devour them. I am the daughter of Khafāf ibn Īmāʾ al-Ghifārī, and my father witnessed al-Ḥudaybiyyah with the Prophet ﷺ.” ʿUmar stopped and went no farther. He said, “Welcome to one of close lineage.” He then went to a strong pack camel that was tethered in the house, loaded it with two sacks filled with food, and placed money and clothing between them. He handed her its halter and said, “Lead it away. This provision will not be exhausted before Allah brings you relief.” A man said, “Commander of the Faithful, you have given her a great deal.” ʿUmar replied, “May your mother lose you! By Allah, I can still picture this woman’s father and brother besieging a fortress for a long time until they conquered it, and afterward we benefited from the shares they had earned in it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",591],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4161، 4160)."},{"num":8969,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ طَارِقِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ، قَالَ انْطَلَقْتُ حَاجًّا فَمَرَرْتُ بِقَوْمٍ يُصَلُّونَ قُلْتُ: مَا هَذَا المَسْجِدُ قَالُوا: هَذِهِ الشَّجَرَةُ، حَيْثُ بَايَعَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْعَةَ الرُّضْوَانِ. فَأَتَيْتُ سَعِيدَ بْنَ المُسَيَّبِ فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ فَقَالَ سَعِيدٌ: حَدَّثَنِي أَبِي أَنَّهُ كَانَ فِيمَنْ بَايَعَ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا خَرَجْنَا مِنَ الْعَامِ المُقْبِلِ نَسِينَاهَا، فَلَمْ نَقْدِرْ عَلَيْهَا. فَقَالَ سَعِيدٌ: إِنَّ أَصْحَابَ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمْ يَعْلَمُوهَا وَعَلِمْتُمُوهَا أَنْتُمْ، فَأَنْتُمْ أَعْلَمُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4163) ومسلم في الإمارة (77:1859) كلاهما من طريق طارق بن عبدالرحمن قال: فذكره. والسياق للبخاري. واختصره مسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4163) and Muslim (1859:77).","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I set out to perform the pilgrimage and passed by some people who were praying. I asked, “What is this place of prayer?” They replied, “This is the tree beneath which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received the Pledge of al-Riḍwān.” I went to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and told him about it. Saʿīd said: “My father told me that he was among those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ beneath the tree. When we returned the following year, however, we had forgotten its location and could not identify it.” Saʿīd then remarked: “The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ did not know where it was, but you know it—you must therefore know better!”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",592],"full":1,"rep":[8994,13322],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4163)، ومسلم (77:1859)."},{"num":8970,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن أَبِي أَوْفَى- وَكَانَ من أَصْحَابِ الشَّجَرَةِ – قَالَ: كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا أَتَاهُ قَوْمٌ بِصَدَقَةٍ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْ فَأَتَاهُ أَبِي بِصَدَقَتِهِ فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى آلِ أَبِي أَوْفَى."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4166) ومسلم في الزكاة (176:1078) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن عمرو بن مرة، حدثنا عبد الله بن أبي أوفى قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4166) and Muslim (1078:176).","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd Allah ibn Abī Awfā, who was one of the Companions of the Tree, reported: Whenever people brought their charitable contributions to the Prophet ﷺ, he would say: “O Allah, bestow Your blessings upon them.” When my father brought him his charitable contribution, he said: “O Allah, bestow Your blessings upon the family of Abū Awfā.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4166)، ومسلم (176:1078)."},{"num":8971,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْعَلاَءِ بْنِ الْمُسَيَّبِ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: لَقِيتُ الْبَرَاءَ بْنَ عَازِبٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا فَقُلْتُ: طُوبَى لَكَ، صَحِبْتَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَبَايَعْتَهُ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ. فَقَالَ: يَا ابْنَ أَخِي، إِنَّكَ لاَ تَدْرِي مَا أَحْدَثْنَا بَعْدَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4170) عن أحمد بن إشكاب، حدثنا محمد بن فضيل، عن العلاء بن المسيب، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4170).","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Musayyib reported from his father: I met al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, may Allah be pleased with him, and said, “Blessed are you! You accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him beneath the tree.” He replied, “My nephew, you do not know what we introduced after him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",594],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4170)."},{"num":8972,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي قِلاَبَةَ، أَنَّ ثَابِتَ بْنَ الضَّحَّاكِ، أَخْبَرَهُ أَنَّهُ، بَايَعَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4171) ومسلم في الإيمان (176:110) كلاهما من طريق معاوية بن سلاّم بن أبي سلام الدمشقي، عن يحيى بن أبي كثير أن أبا قلابة أخبره أن ثابت بن الضحاك أخبره: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4171) and Muslim (110:176).","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Qilābah reported that Thābit ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk told him that he had pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ beneath the tree. The remainder of the report follows."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",595],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4171)، ومسلم (176:110)."},{"num":8973,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زاهر الأسلمي – وَكَانَ مِمَّنْ شَهِدَ الشجرة قَالَ: إِنِّي لأُوقِدُ تَحْتَ الْقِدْرِ بِلُحُومِ الْحُمُرِ، إِذْ نَادَى مُنَادِي رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَنْهَاكُمْ عَنْ لُحُومِ الْحُمُرِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4173) عن عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا أبو عامر، (هو عبد الملك بن عمرو العقدي) حدثنا إسرائيل، عن مجزأة بن زاهر الأسلمي، عن أبيه، قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4173). His words, “I was tending the fire beneath a cooking pot containing donkey meat,” refer to the day of Khaybar.","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zāhir al-Aslamī, who was among those who witnessed the Pledge beneath the tree, said: I was tending the fire beneath a cooking pot containing donkey meat when the herald of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbids you to eat donkey meat.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",596],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4173). قوله: «إني لأوقد تحت القدر بلحوم الحمر» يعني يوم خيبر."},{"num":8974,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سُوَيْدِ بْنِ النُّعْمَانِ ـ وَكَانَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ الشَّجَرَةِ ـ كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابُهُ أُتُوا بِسَوِيقٍ فَلاَكُوهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4175) عن محمد بن بشار، حدثنا ابن أبي عدي، عن شعبة، عن يحيى بن سعيد، عن بشير بن يسار، عن سويد بن النعمان فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4175).","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Suwayd ibn al-Nuʿmān, who was one of the Companions of the Tree, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions were brought sawīq—a preparation of roasted grain—and they chewed and ate it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",597],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4175)."},{"num":8975,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي جَمْرَةَ، قَالَ: سَأَلْتُ عَائِذَ بْنَ عَمْرٍو رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ وَكَانَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ الشَّجَرَةِ هَلْ يُنْقَضُ الْوِتْرُ؟ قَالَ: إِذَا أَوْتَرْتَ مِنْ أَوَّلِهِ، فَلاَ تُوتِرْ مِنْ آخِرِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4176) عن محمد بن حاتم بن بزيع، حدثنا شاذان، عن شعبة، عن أبي جمرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد غزوة الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4176).","chapter_en":"Those Who Witnessed the Expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Jamrah said: I asked ʿĀʾidh ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with him, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and one of the Companions of the Tree, “Should the witr prayer be repeated?” He replied, “If you have performed witr at the beginning of the night, do not perform another witr at its end.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",598],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4176)."},{"num":8976,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُرْوَةَ بْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ، عَنِ الْمِسْوَرِ بْنِ مَخْرَمَةَ، وَمَرْوَانَ بْنِ الْحَكَمِ، يَزِيدُ أَحَدُهُمَا عَلَى صَاحِبِهِ قَالاَ: خَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  عَامَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ فِي بِضْعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ، فَلَمَّا أَتَى ذَا الْحُلَيْفَةِ، قَلَّدَ الْهَدْىَ، وَأَشْعَرَهُ، وَأَحْرَمَ مِنْهَا بِعُمْرَةٍ، وَبَعَثَ عَيْنًا لَهُ مِنْ خُزَاعَةَ، وَسَارَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  حَتَّى كَانَ بِغَدِيرِ الأَشْطَاطِ، أَتَاهُ عَيْنُهُ، قَالَ: إِنَّ قُرَيْشًا جَمَعُوا لَكَ جُمُوعًا، وَقَدْ جَمَعُوا لَكَ الأَحَابِيشَ، وَهُمْ مُقَاتِلُوكَ، وَصَادُّوكَ عَنِ الْبَيْتِ، وَمَانِعُوكَ. فَقَالَ أَشِيرُوا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ عَلَىَّ، أَتَرَوْنَ أَنْ أَمِيلَ إِلَى عِيَالِهِمْ وَذَرَارِيِّ هَؤُلاَءِ الَّذِينَ يُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يَصُدُّونَا عَنِ الْبَيْتِ، فَإِنْ يَأْتُونَا كَانَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ قَدْ قَطَعَ عَيْنًا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، وَإِلاَّ تَرَكْنَاهُمْ مَحْرُوبِينَ. قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، خَرَجْتَ عَامِدًا لِهَذَا الْبَيْتِ، لاَ تُرِيدُ قَتْلَ أَحَدٍ، وَلاَ حَرْبَ أَحَدٍ، فَتَوَجَّهْ لَهُ، فَمَنْ صَدَّنَا عَنْهُ قَاتَلْنَاهُ. قَالَ: امْضُوا عَلَى اسْمِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4179،4178) حدثنا عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا سفيان (هو ابن عيينة) قال: سمعت الزهري حين حدّث هذا الحديث حفظت بعضه، وثبتني معمر، عن عروة بن الزبير، عن المسور بن مخرمة ومروان بن الحكم، قالا: فذكراه.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تشاور النبي ﷺ عند غدير الأشطاط، وأنه لا يريد القتال","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4178, 4179), from ʿAbd Allah ibn Muḥammad, from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, who heard al-Zuhrī relate the report; Maʿmar confirmed what he had retained, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Consults His Companions at the Pond of al-Ashṭāṭ and Makes Clear That He Does Not Desire Battle","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr reported from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam, each adding details to the other’s account, that they said: The Prophet ﷺ set out during the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah with more than fourteen hundred of his Companions. When he reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, he garlanded and marked the sacrificial animals and entered into the state of consecration for ʿumrah. He also sent a scout from the tribe of Khuzāʿah. The Prophet ﷺ continued until he reached the pond of al-Ashṭāṭ, where his scout came to him and said, “Quraysh have assembled their forces against you and gathered the allied tribes. They intend to fight you, turn you away from the Sacred House and prevent you from reaching it.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Advise me, people. Do you think that I should turn against the families and children of those who intend to prevent us from reaching the House? If they come to confront us, Allah Almighty will have cut off a force from among the polytheists; and if they do not come, we shall leave them stripped and ruined.” Abū Bakr said, “Messenger of Allah, you set out intending to reach this House. You do not desire to kill or fight anyone. Proceed toward it, and we shall fight whoever prevents us from reaching it.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Proceed in the name of Allah.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words “a scout from Khuzāʿah” refer to an intelligence-gatherer. His name was Bishr ibn Sufyān al-Khuzāʿī.","“The pond of al-Ashṭāṭ” was a place near ʿUsfān, two stages from Makkah on the road to Madinah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4178، 4179)."},{"num":8977,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ قَالَ: لَا تُوقِدُوا نَارًا بِلَيْلٍ فَمَا كَانَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ قَالَ: أَوْقِدُوا، وَاصْطَنِعُوا، فَإِنَّهُ لَا يُدْرِكُ قَوْمٌ بَعْدَكُمْ صَاعَكُمْ وَلَا مُدَّكُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (11208) وأبو يعلى (984) وصحّحه الحاكم (4336) كلهم من حديث يحيى بن سعيد القطان، عن محمد بن أبي يحيى، قال: حدثني أبي، أن أبا سعيد الخدري حدثه فقال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب النهي عن إيقاد النار بالليل يوم الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (11208) and Abū Yaʿlā (984), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (4336), all through Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, from Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaḥyā, from his father, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī.","chapter_en":"The Prohibition of Lighting Fires at Night on the Day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not light a fire at night.” Later, he said: “Light your fires and prepare what you need, for no people who come after you will equal even your ṣāʿ or your mudd.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (11208) وأبو يعلى (984)، وصححه الحاكم (4336)."},{"num":8978,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَلَمَةَ بْنِ الْأَكْوَعِ قَالَ: قَدِمْنَا الْحُدَيْبِيَةَ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَحْنُ أَرْبَعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً، وَعَلَيْهَا خَمْسُونَ شَاةً لَا تُرْوِيهَا، قَالَ: فَقَعَدَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى جَبَا الرَّكِيَّةِ، فَإِمَّا دَعَا، وَإِمَّا بَصَقَ فِيهَا، قَالَ: فَجَاشَتْ، فَسَقَيْنَا وَاسْتَقَيْنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد (132:1807) من طرق عن عكرمة بن عمار قال: حدثني إياس بن سلمة، حدثني أبي قال: فذكره في حديث طويل.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بصق النبي ﷺ في بئر الحديبية فجاشَ الماءُ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in al-Jihād (1807:132) through several routes from ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār, from Iyās ibn Salamah, from his father, in a longer hadith.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Spits into the Well of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Water Surges Forth","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ reported: We arrived at al-Ḥudaybiyyah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we numbered fourteen hundred. Its well contained so little water that it could not provide enough for fifty sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat at the edge of the well and either supplicated or spat into it. The water then surged forth, so we drank and drew as much as we needed."]},"buhuth":{"en":["“Jabā al-rakiyyah” means the area surrounding the well, and rakiyy means a well."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",601],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (132:1807)."},{"num":8979,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْمِسْوَرِ بْنِ مَخْرَمَةَ وَمَرْوَانَ قَالَا: وَشُكِيَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ العَطَشُ فَانْتَزَعَ سَهْمًا مِنْ كِنَانَتِهِ، ثُمَّ أَمَرَهُمْ أَنْ يَجْعَلُوهُ فِيهِ، فو الله مَا زَالَ يَجِيشُ لَهُمْ بِالرِّيِّ حَتَّى صَدَرُوا عَنْهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الشروط (2732،2731) عن عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا عبد الرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، قال: أخبرني الزهري، قال: أخبرني عروة بن الزبير، عن المسور بن مخرمة ومروان يصدق كل واحد منهما حديث صاحبه، قالا: فذكرا الحديث بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بصق النبي ﷺ في بئر الحديبية فجاشَ الماءُ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Shurūṭ (2732, 2731), from ʿAbd Allah ibn Muḥammad, from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwān, each confirming the other’s report, in the longer narration.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Spits into the Well of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Water Surges Forth","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwān reported: The people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of thirst. He took an arrow from his quiver and instructed them to place it in the well. By Allah, it continued surging with abundant water for them until they had all finished and departed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",602],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2732، 2731)."},{"num":8980,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["أَنْبَأَنَا الْبَرَاءُ بْنُ عَازِبٍ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ أَلْفًا وَأَرْبَعَمِائَةٍ أَوْ أَكْثَرَ، فَنَزَلُوا عَلَى بِئْرٍ فَنَزَحُوهَا، فَأَتَوْا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَتَى الْبِئْرَ، وَقَعَدَ عَلَى شَفِيرِهَا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: ائْتُونِي بِدَلْوٍ مِنْ مَائِهَا. فَأُتِيَ بِهِ، فَبَصَقَ فَدَعَا ثُمَّ قَالَ: دَعُوهَا سَاعَةً. فَأَرْوَوْا أَنْفُسَهُمْ وَرِكَابَهُمْ حَتَّى ارْتَحَلُوا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4151) عن فضل بن يعقوب، حدثنا الحسن بن محمد بن أعين أبو علي الحراني، حدثنا زهير، حدثنا أبو إسحاق قال: أنبانا البراء بن عازب فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بصق النبي ﷺ في بئر الحديبية فجاشَ الماءُ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4151), from Faḍl ibn Yaʿqūb, from al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥarrānī, from Zuhayr, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Spits into the Well of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Water Surges Forth","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib reported that they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, numbering fourteen hundred or more. They stopped beside a well and drew out all its water. They went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who came to the well, sat at its edge and said: “Bring me a bucket of its water.” It was brought to him, and he spat into it and supplicated. He then said: “Leave it for a while.” Thereafter, they fully quenched themselves and their riding animals before departing."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",603],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4151)."},{"num":8981,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الْبَرَاءِ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَرْبَعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً، وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةُ بِئْرٌ، فَنَزَحْنَاهَا، فَلَمْ نَتْرُكْ فِيهَا قَطْرَةً، فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَتَاهَا، فَجَلَسَ عَلَى شَفِيرِهَا، ثُمَّ دَعَا بِإِنَاءٍ مِنْ مَاءٍ فَتَوَضَّأَ، ثُمَّ مَضْمَضَ وَدَعَا، ثُمَّ صَبَّهُ فِيهَا، فَتَرَكْنَاهَا غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍ، ثُمَّ إِنَّهَا أَصْدَرَتْنَا مَا شِئْنَا نَحْنُ وَرِكَابَنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4150) عن عبيد الله بن موسى، عن إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بصق النبي ﷺ في بئر الحديبية فجاشَ الماءُ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4150), from ʿUbayd Allah ibn Mūsā, from Isrāʾīl, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Spits into the Well of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Water Surges Forth","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ reported: We were fourteen hundred men with the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Ḥudaybiyyah had a well, and we drew out all its water until we left not a single drop in it. When this reached the Prophet ﷺ, he came to the well and sat at its edge. He called for a vessel of water, performed ablution, rinsed his mouth and supplicated, and then poured the water into it. We left it for a short while, after which it supplied all the water that we and our riding animals required."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",604],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4150) عن عبيد الله بن موسى، عن إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء فذكره."},{"num":8982,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: عَطِشَ النَّاسُ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ رَكْوَةٌ، فَتَوَضَّأَ مِنْهَا، ثُمَّ أَقْبَلَ النَّاسُ نَحْوَهُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا لَكُمْ. قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ لَيْسَ عِنْدَنَا مَاءٌ نَتَوَضَّأُ بِهِ، وَلاَ نَشْرَبُ إِلاَّ مَا فِي رَكْوَتِكَ. قَالَ: فَوَضَعَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَدَهُ فِي الرَّكْوَةِ، فَجَعَلَ الْمَاءُ يَفُورُ مِنْ بَيْنِ أَصَابِعِهِ كَأَمْثَالِ الْعُيُونِ، قَالَ: فَشَرِبْنَا وَتَوَضَّأْنَا. فَقُلْتُ لِجَابِرٍ: كَمْ كُنْتُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ قَالَ: لَوْ كُنَّا مِائَةَ أَلْفٍ لَكَفَانَا، كُنَّا خَمْسَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4152) ومسلم في الإمارة (73:1856) كلاهما من طريق حصين (هو ابن عبد الرحمن) عن سالم بن أبي الجعد، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"بصق النبي ﷺ في بئر الحديبية فجاشَ الماءُ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4152) and Muslim in al-Imārah (1856:73), both through Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from Jābir.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Spits into the Well of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Water Surges Forth","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir reported: The people became thirsty on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a small leather vessel of water before him, from which he performed ablution. The people then came toward him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What is the matter with you?” They replied, “Messenger of Allah, we have no water with which to perform ablution or drink except what is in your vessel.” The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand in the vessel, and water began gushing from between his fingers like springs. We drank and performed ablution. I asked Jābir, “How many were you that day?” He replied, “Had we been one hundred thousand, it would have sufficed us. We were fifteen hundred.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",605],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9670],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4152) ومسلم (73:1856)."},{"num":8983,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَلَمَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: خَفَّتْ أَزْوَادُ الْقَوْمِ وَأَمْلَقُوا، فَأَتَوُا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي نَحْرِ إِبِلِهِمْ فَأَذِنَ لَهُمْ، فَلَقِيَهُمْ عُمَرُ فَأَخْبَرُوهُ فَقَالَ: مَا بَقَاؤُكُمْ بَعْدَ إِبِلِكُمْ، فَدَخَلَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، مَا بَقَاؤُهُمْ بَعْدَ إِبِلِهِمْ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نَادِ فِي النَّاسِ، فَيَأْتُونَ بِفَضْلِ أَزْوَادِهِمْ. فَبُسِطَ لِذَلِكَ نِطَعٌ، وَجَعَلُوهُ عَلَى النِّطَعِ. فَقَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَدَعَا وَبَرَّكَ عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ دَعَاهُمْ بِأَوْعِيَتِهِمْ، فَاحْتَثَى النَّاسُ حَتَّى فَرَغُوا، ثُمَّ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ، وَأَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الشركة (2484) عن بشر بن محروم، حدثنا حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن يزيد بن أبي عبيد، عن سلمة بن الأكوع فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تكثير الطعام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (2484) and Muslim (1729).","chapter_en":"The Miraculous Increase of Food","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ reported: The people’s provisions became scarce and they fell into poverty, so they came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking permission to slaughter their camels, and he permitted them to do so. ʿUmar met them and they informed him, whereupon he said, “How will you survive after your camels are gone?” He went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Messenger of Allah, how will they survive after their camels are gone?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Call upon the people to bring whatever remains of their provisions.” A leather sheet was spread out, and the provisions were placed upon it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, supplicated and invoked blessings over the food. He then called upon the people to bring their containers, and they took handfuls until they had all finished. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word naṭʿ means a dining sheet made of leather, or a spread."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2484)، ومسلم (1729)."},{"num":8984,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: قَالَ لَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ: أَنْتُمْ خَيْرُ أَهْلِ الأَرْضِ. وَكُنَّا أَلْفًا وَأَرْبَعَمِائَةٍ، وَلَوْ كُنْتُ أُبْصِرُ الْيَوْمَ لأَرَيْتُكُمْ مَكَانَ الشَّجَرَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4154) ومسلم في الإمارة (71:1856) كلاهما من حديث سفيان، عن عمرو، قال: سمعت جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"بيعة الرضوان على الموت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4154) and Muslim in al-Imārah (1856:71), both through Sufyān, from ʿAmr, who heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah.","chapter_en":"The Pledge of al-Riḍwān to Face Death","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah: “You are the best people on earth.” We numbered fourteen hundred. Had I still possessed my sight today, I would have shown you the location of the tree."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال محمد بن إسحاق: حدثني عبد الله بن أبي بكر أن رسول الله ﷺ قال حين بلغه أن عثمان قد قتل: «لَا نَبْرَحُ حَتَّى نُنَاجِزَ الْقَوْمَ». فدعا رسول الله ﷺ الناس إلى البيعة، فكانت بيعة الرضوان تحت الشجرة. «سيرة ابن هشام» (٢/٣١٥).","قال ابن هشام: ذكر وكيع، عن إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن الشعبي: أن أول من بايع رسول الله ﷺ بيعة الرضوان أبو سنان الأسدي. «سيرة ابن هشام» (٢/٣١٦).","وأبو سنان اسمه: وهب بن محصن بن حرثان، وهو أخو عكاشة بن محصن.","ذكر ابن عبد البر في ترجمته (١٩١) عدة روايات عن الشعبي وزر وغيرهما أنه أول من بايع النبي ﷺ. ذكر الحلوان، عن أبي أسامة، عن إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن الشعبي قال: أول من بايع تحت الشجرة أبو سنان بن وهب الأسدي، فقال له رسول الله ﷺ: «عَلَامَ مَا تُبَايِعُ؟» قال: ما في نفسك، فبايعه، وتتابع الناس فبايعوه. فأثنى عليهم رسول الله ﷺ كما في الحديث الآتي:"],"en":["Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq said: ʿAbd Allah ibn Abī Bakr narrated to me that when news reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that ʿUthmān had been killed, he said: “We will not depart until we confront the people.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then called the people to pledge allegiance, and the Pledge of al-Riḍwān took place beneath the tree. See Sīrat Ibn Hishām (2/315).","Ibn Hishām said: Wakīʿ reported from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from al-Shaʿbī, that the first person to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Pledge of al-Riḍwān was Abū Sinān al-Asadī. See Sīrat Ibn Hishām (2/316).","Abū Sinān’s name was Wahb ibn Miḥṣan ibn Ḥirthān, and he was the brother of ʿUkāshah ibn Miḥṣan.","Ibn ʿAbd al-Barr, in his biography of him (no. 191), cited several reports from al-Shaʿbī, Zirr and others stating that he was the first to pledge to the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Ḥalwānī also reported from Abū Usāmah, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from al-Shaʿbī: the first to pledge beneath the tree was Abū Sinān ibn Wahb al-Asadī. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him, “On what do you pledge?” He replied, “On whatever is in your heart.” He pledged, and the people then followed one after another in giving their pledges. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ praised them, as in the following hadith:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4154) ومسلم (71:1856)."},{"num":8985,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ يَقُولُ: أَخْبَرَتْنِي أُمُّ مُبَشِّرٍ  أَنَّهَا سَمِعَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ عِنْدَ حَفْصَةَ: لَا يَدْخُلُ النَّارَ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ الشَّجَرَةِ أَحَدٌ الَّذِينَ بَايَعُوا تَحْتَهَا.","قالت: بلى يا رسول الله، فانتهرها فقالت حفصة: وَإِنْ مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا وَارِدُهَا [مريم: ٧١] فقال النبي صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قد قال الله عز وجل: ﴿ثُمَّ نُنَجِّي الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا وَنَذَرُ الظَّالِمِينَ فِيهَا جِثِيًّا﴾ [مريم: ٧٢]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2496) عن هارون بن عبد الله، حدثنا حجاج بن محمد، قال: قال ابن جريج: أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبد الله يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بيعة الرضوان على الموت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (2496), from Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allah, from Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, who heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah.","chapter_en":"The Pledge of al-Riḍwān to Face Death","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah reported: Umm Mubashshir informed me that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say in the presence of Ḥafṣah: “Allah willing, none of the Companions of the Tree—those who pledged allegiance beneath it—will enter the Fire.” Ḥafṣah said, “Indeed they will, Messenger of Allah.” He rebuked her, so she quoted: “There is none of you who will not pass over it” [Maryam 19:71]. The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Allah Almighty also said: ‘Then We shall save those who were mindful of Allah and leave the wrongdoers there upon their knees’ [Maryam 19:72].”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2496)."},{"num":8986,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَعْقِلِ بْنِ يَسَارٍ قَالَ: لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنِى يَوْمَ الشَّجَرَةِ، وَالنَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُبَايِعُ النَّاسَ، وَأَنَا رَافِعٌ غُصْنًا مِنْ أَغْصَانِهَا عَنْ رَأْسِهِ، وَنَحْنُ أَرْبَعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً، قَالَ: لَمْ نُبَايِعْهُ عَلَى المَوْتِ، وَلَكِنْ بَايَعْنَاهُ عَلَى أَنْ لاَ نَفِرَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإمارة (1858) عن يحيى بن يحيى، أخبرنا يزيد بن زريع، عن خالد، عن الحكم بن عبدالله بن الأعرج، عن معقل بن يسار فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بيعة الرضوان على الموت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in al-Imārah (1858), from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, from Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ, from Khālid, from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbd Allah ibn al-Aʿraj, from Maʿqil ibn Yasār.","chapter_en":"The Pledge of al-Riḍwān to Face Death","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Maʿqil ibn Yasār reported: I remember myself on the day of the Tree, while the Prophet ﷺ was receiving the people’s pledges and I was holding one of its branches above his head. We numbered fourteen hundred. He said: “We did not pledge to die; rather, we pledged that we would not flee.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",609],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1858)."},{"num":8987,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَزِيدَ بْنِ أَبِي عُبَيْدٍ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ لِسَلَمَةَ بْنِ الأَكْوَعِ: عَلَى أَىِّ شَىْءٍ بَايَعْتُمْ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ. قَالَ: عَلَى الْمَوْتِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4169) ومسلم في الإمارة (80:1860) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا حاتم (هو ابن إسماعيل) عن يزيد بن أبي عبيد فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"بيعة الرضوان على الموت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4169) and Muslim in al-Imārah (1860:80), both from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd, from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl, from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd.","chapter_en":"The Pledge of al-Riḍwān to Face Death","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd reported: I asked Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ, “For what did you pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah?” He replied, “To face death.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Regarding the words “to face death,” some narrations state: “They pledged to remain steadfast and not flee.” Whoever described it as a pledge to face death stated its necessary consequence, whereas whoever described it as a pledge to remain steadfast expressed its literal terms."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",610],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13317],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4169) ومسلم (80:1860)."},{"num":8988,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبَّادِ بْنِ تَمِيمٍ، قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ الْحَرَّةِ وَالنَّاسُ يُبَايِعُونَ لِعَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ حَنْظَلَةَ فَقَالَ ابْنُ زَيْدٍ: عَلَى مَا يُبَايِعُ ابْنُ حَنْظَلَةَ النَّاسَ؟ قِيلَ لَهُ: عَلَى الْمَوْتِ. قَالَ: لاَ أُبَايِعُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ أَحَدًا بَعْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. وَكَانَ شَهِدَ مَعَهُ الْحُدَيْبِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4167) ومسلم في الإمارة (81:1861) كلاهما من طريق عمرو بن يحيى، عن عباد بن تميم، قال: فذكره. والسياق للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"بيعة الرضوان على الموت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4167) and Muslim (1861:81).","chapter_en":"The Pledge of al-Riḍwān to Face Death","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm reported: On the day of al-Ḥarrah, when the people were pledging allegiance to ʿAbd Allah ibn Ḥanẓalah, Ibn Zayd asked, “For what is Ibn Ḥanẓalah receiving the people’s pledge?” He was told, “To face death.” He replied, “I shall never give such a pledge to anyone after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He had witnessed al-Ḥudaybiyyah with him."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The words “on the day of al-Ḥarrah” refer to the time when the people of Madinah renounced their pledge of allegiance to Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah and pledged allegiance to ʿAbd Allah ibn Ḥanẓalah al-Anṣārī."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",611],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4167)، ومسلم (81:1861)."},{"num":8989,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ نَافِعٍ، قَالَ: إِنَّ النَّاسَ يَتَحَدَّثُونَ أَنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ، أَسْلَمَ قَبْلَ عُمَرَ، وَلَيْسَ كَذَلِكَ، وَلَكِنْ عُمَرُ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ أَرْسَلَ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ إِلَى فَرَسٍ لَهُ عِنْدَ رَجُلٍ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، يَأْتِي بِهِ لِيُقَاتِلَ عَلَيْهِ، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُبَايِعُ عِنْدَ الشَّجَرَةِ، وَعُمَرُ لاَ يَدْرِي بِذَلِكَ، فَبَايَعَهُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ، ثُمَّ ذَهَبَ إِلَى الْفَرَسِ، فَجَاءَ بِهِ إِلَى عُمَرَ، وَعُمَرُ يَسْتَلْئِمُ لِلْقِتَالِ، فَأَخْبَرَهُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُبَايِعُ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ، ـ قَالَ ـ فَانْطَلَقَ، فَذَهَبَ مَعَهُ حَتَّى بَايَعَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَهِيَ الَّتِي يَتَحَدَّثُ النَّاسُ أَنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ أَسْلَمَ قَبْلَ عُمَرَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4186) عن شجاع بن الوليد (هو المؤدب أبو الليث) سمع النضر بن محمد، حدثنا صخر، عن نافع قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"بيعة عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4186, 4187).","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Pledge","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Nāfiʿ reported: People say that Ibn ʿUmar embraced Islam before ʿUmar, but that is not so. On the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, ʿUmar sent ʿAbd Allah to retrieve a horse of his that was being kept by a man of the Anṣār, so that he could ride it in battle. Meanwhile, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was receiving the people’s pledges beneath the tree, though ʿUmar was unaware of it. ʿAbd Allah pledged allegiance to him and then went to retrieve the horse. He brought it to ʿUmar, who was putting on his armour for battle, and informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was receiving pledges beneath the tree. ʿUmar immediately set out with him and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. This is the incident that people misconstrued when they said that Ibn ʿUmar embraced Islam before ʿUmar."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression “putting on his armour for battle” means that he was donning his la’mah, namely his weapons and armour."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",612],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4186، 4187)."},{"num":8990,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّ النَّاسَ، كَانُوا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ، تَفَرَّقُوا فِي ظِلاَلِ الشَّجَرِ، فَإِذَا النَّاسُ مُحْدِقُونَ بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ، انْظُرْ مَا شَأْنُ النَّاسِ قَدْ أَحْدَقُوا بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَوَجَدَهُمْ يُبَايِعُونَ، فَبَايَعَ ثُمَّ رَجَعَ إِلَى عُمَرَ فَخَرَجَ فَبَايَعَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4187) عن هشام بن عمار، حدثنا الوليد بن مسلم، حدثنا عمر بن محمد العمري، أخبرني نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بيعة عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (4187).","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Pledge","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that the people were with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and had dispersed beneath the shade of the trees. They then gathered closely around the Prophet ﷺ. ʿUmar said, “ʿAbd Allah, go and see what has happened to the people, for they have gathered around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He found them pledging allegiance, so he gave his pledge and then returned to ʿUmar. ʿUmar subsequently went out and pledged allegiance as well."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",613],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4187)."},{"num":8991,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عثمان بن موهب قال: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ فَرَأَى قَوْمًا جُلُوسًا فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَؤُلاَءِ الْقُعُودُ قَالُوا: هَؤُلاَءِ قُرَيْشٌ. قَالَ: مَنِ الشَّيْخُ؟ قَالُوا: ابْنُ عُمَرَ. فَأَتَاهُ فَقَالَ إِنِّي سَائِلُكَ عَنْ شَىْءٍ أَتُحَدِّثُنِي؟ قَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ بِحُرْمَةِ هَذَا الْبَيْتِ أَتَعْلَمُ أَنَّ عُثْمَانَ بْنَ عَفَّانَ فَرَّ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَتَعْلَمُهُ تَغَيَّبَ عَنْ بَدْرٍ فَلَمْ يَشْهَدْهَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَتَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ تَخَلَّفَ عَنْ بَيْعَةِ الرُّضْوَانِ فَلَمْ يَشْهَدْهَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَكَبَّرَ. قَالَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: تَعَالَ لأُخْبِرَكَ وَلأُبَيِّنَ لَكَ عَمَّا سَأَلْتَنِي عَنْهُ، أَمَّا فِرَارُهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ فَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ الله عَفَا عَنْهُ، وَأَمَّا تَغَيُّبُهُ عَنْ بَدْرٍ فَإِنَّهُ كَانَ تَحْتَهُ بِنْتُ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَكَانَتْ مَرِيضَةً، فَقَالَ لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ لَكَ أَجْرَ رَجُلٍ مِمَّنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَسَهْمَهُ. وَأَمَّا تَغَيُّبُهُ عَنْ بَيْعَةِ الرُّضْوَانِ فَإِنَّهُ لَوْ كَانَ أَحَدٌ أَعَزَّ بِبَطْنِ مَكَّةَ مِنْ عُثْمَانَ بْنِ عَفَّانَ لَبَعَثَهُ مَكَانَهُ، فَبَعَثَ عُثْمَانَ، وَكَانَ بَيْعَةُ الرُّضْوَانِ بَعْدَ مَا ذَهَبَ عُثْمَانُ إِلَى مَكَّةَ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِيَدِهِ الْيُمْنَى: هَذِهِ يَدُ عُثْمَانَ ، فَضَرَبَ بِهَا عَلَى يَدِهِ فَقَالَ: هَذِهِ لِعُثْمَانَ، اذْهَبْ بِهَذَا الآنَ مَعَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4066) عن عبدان، أخبرنا أبو حمزة، عن عثمان بن موهب فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"مبايعة النبي ﷺ نفسه عن عثمان رضي الله عنه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (3699, 4066).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Pledges on His Own Behalf for ʿUthmān رضي الله عنه","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUthmān ibn Mawhab reported: A man came to perform pilgrimage at the Sacred House and saw a group of people sitting together. He asked, “Who are these people?” They replied, “They are Quraysh.” He asked, “Who is the elder among them?” They replied, “Ibn ʿUmar.” He approached him and said, “I wish to ask you about something. Will you answer me?” He continued, “I adjure you by the sanctity of this House: do you know that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān fled on the day of Uḥud?” Ibn ʿUmar replied, “Yes.” He asked, “Do you know that he was absent from Badr and did not witness it?” He replied, “Yes.” He asked, “Do you know that he was absent from the Pledge of al-Riḍwān and did not witness it?” He replied, “Yes.” The man exclaimed, “Allah is the Greatest!” Ibn ʿUmar said: “Come here, and I shall explain the matters about which you asked me. As for his flight on the day of Uḥud, I testify that Allah pardoned him. As for his absence from Badr, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was his wife, and she was ill. The Prophet ﷺ therefore told him: ‘You shall receive the reward and the share of a man who witnessed Badr.’ “As for his absence from the Pledge of al-Riḍwān, had there been anyone in Makkah more respected and influential than ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, the Prophet ﷺ would have sent that person in his place. Instead, he sent ʿUthmān. The Pledge of al-Riḍwān took place after ʿUthmān had departed for Makkah. The Prophet ﷺ indicated his right hand and said: ‘This is ʿUthmān’s hand.’ He then struck it against his other hand and said: ‘This pledge is for ʿUthmān.’ Now take this explanation with you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",614],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8826,13318],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4066، 3699)."},{"num":8992,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سلمة بن الأكوع قال: قَدِمْنَا الْحُدَيْبِيَةَ مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وَنَحْنُ أرْبَعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً. وَعَلَيْهَا خَمْسُونَ شَاةً لاَ تُرْوِيهَا - قَالَ - فَقَعَدَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى جَبَا الرَّكِيَّةِ فَاِمَّا دَعَا وَاِمَّا بَصقَ فِيهَا - قَالَ - فَجَاشَتْ فَسَقَيْنَا وَاسْتَقَيْنَا . قَالَ: ثُمَّ اِنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دَعَانَا لِلْبَيْعَةِ فِي أصْلِ الشَّجَرَةِ . قَالَ: فَبَايَعْتُهُ اَوَّلَ النَّاسِ ثُمَّ بَايَعَ وَبَايَعَ حَتَّى اِذَا كَانَ فِي وَسَطٍ مِنَ النَّاسِ قَالَ: بَايِعْ يَا سَلَمَةُ! . قَالَ: قُلْتُ: قَدْ بَايَعْتُكَ يَا رَسُولَ الله فِي اَوَّلِ النَّاسِ قَالَ وَأَيْضًا . قَالَ: وَرَآنِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَزِلاً - يَعْنِي لَيْسَ مَعَهُ سِلاَحٌ – قَالَ: فَاَعْطَانِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَجَفَةً أَوْ دَرَقَةً ثُمَّ بَايَعَ حَتَّى اِذَا كَانَ فِي آخِرِ النَّاسِ قَالَ: اَلاَ تُبَايِعُنِي يَا سَلَمَةُ؟. قَالَ: قُلْتُ: قَدْ بَايَعْتُكَ يَا رَسُولَ الله فِي أوَّلِ النَّاسِ وَفِي أوْسَطِ النَّاسِ قَالَ: وَأيْضًا. قَالَ: فَبَايَعْتُهُ الثَّالِثَةَ ثُمَّ قَالَ لِي:  يَا سَلَمَةُ اَيْنَ حَجَفَتُكَ اَوْ دَرَقَتُكَ الَّتِي اَعْطَيْتُكَ؟ . قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله لَقِيَنِي عَمِّي عَامِرٌ عَزِلاً فَاَعْطَيْتُهُ اِيَّاهَا – قَالَ: فَضَحِكَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَقَالَ:  اِنَّكَ كَالَّذِي قَالَ الاَوَّلُ: اللَّهُمَّ أَبْغِنِي حَبِيبًا هُوَ أَحََبُّ اِليَّ مِنْ نَفْسِي ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد (1807) من طرق عن عكرمة بن عمار، حدثني إياس بن سلمة، قال: حدثني أبي قال: فذكره في حديث طويل.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"بايع سلمة بن الأكوع ثلاث مرات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by Muslim (1807).","chapter_en":"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ Pledged Allegiance Three Times","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ reported: We arrived at al-Ḥudaybiyyah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, numbering fourteen hundred. Its well contained so little water that it could not provide enough for fifty sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat at the edge of the well and either supplicated or spat into it. The water then surged forth, so we drank and drew what we needed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then summoned us to pledge allegiance beneath the tree. I was the first person to pledge to him. He continued receiving people’s pledges until he reached the middle of the company, when he said: “Pledge to me, Salamah!” I said, “I pledged to you, Messenger of Allah, among the first people.” He said: “And again.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that I was unarmed, so he gave me a leather shield. He continued receiving pledges until he reached the last of the people, when he said: “Will you not pledge to me, Salamah?” I replied, “I pledged to you, Messenger of Allah, among the first people and again in the middle.” He said: “And again.” I therefore pledged to him a third time. He then asked me: “Salamah, where is the shield I gave you?” I replied, “Messenger of Allah, my uncle ʿĀmir met me while he was unarmed, so I gave it to him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said: “You are like the man of old who said: ‘O Allah, grant me a beloved companion who is dearer to me than my own self.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1807)."},{"num":8993,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبي الزُّبَيْرِ أَنَّه سَمِعَ جَابِرًا يَسْأَلُ: كَمْ كَانُوا يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ؟ قَالَ: كُنَّا أَرْبَعَ عَشْرَةَ مِائَةً فَبَايَعْنَاهُ وَعُمَرُ آخِذٌ بِيَدِهِ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ. وَهِيَ سَمُرَةٌ، فَبَايَعْنَاهُ غَيْرَ جَدِّ بْنِ قَيْسٍ الْأَنْصَارِيِّ اخْتَبَأَ تَحْتَ بَطْنِ بَعِيرِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإمارة (69:1856) عن محمد بن حاتم، حدثنا حجاج، عن ابن جريج، أخبرني أبو الزبير فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"ذكر المنافق الذي لم يبايع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in al-Imārah (1856:69), from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim, from Ḥajjāj, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr.","chapter_en":"The Hypocrite Who Did Not Give the Pledge","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Zubayr reported that he heard Jābir being asked, “How many were you on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah?” He replied: “We were fourteen hundred. We pledged allegiance to him beneath the tree while ʿUmar held his hand. It was an acacia tree. All of us pledged except al-Jadd ibn Qays al-Anṣārī, who hid beneath his camel.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Jadd was the son of Qays ibn Ṣakhr ibn Khansāʾ ibn Sinān ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿAdī ibn Tamīm ibn Ghanm ibn Kaʿb ibn Salimah al-Anṣārī al-Salamī. His honorific was Abū ʿAbd Allah, and he was among those suspected of hypocrisy. Ibn ʿAbd al-Barr said at the end of his biographical entry (p. 363): “It has also been said that he repented and that his repentance was sincere.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",616],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (69:1856)."},{"num":8994,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ طَارِقِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ، قَالَ انْطَلَقْتُ حَاجًّا فَمَرَرْتُ بِقَوْمٍ يُصَلُّونَ قُلْتُ: مَا هَذَا المَسْجِدُ قَالُوا: هَذِهِ الشَّجَرَةُ، حَيْثُ بَايَعَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْعَةَ الرُّضْوَانِ. فَأَتَيْتُ سَعِيدَ بْنَ المُسَيَّبِ فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ فَقَالَ سَعِيدٌ: حَدَّثَنِي أَبِي أَنَّهُ كَانَ فِيمَنْ بَايَعَ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا خَرَجْنَا مِنَ الْعَامِ المُقْبِلِ نَسِينَاهَا، فَلَمْ نَقْدِرْ عَلَيْهَا. فَقَالَ سَعِيدٌ: إِنَّ أَصْحَابَ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمْ يَعْلَمُوهَا وَعَلِمْتُمُوهَا أَنْتُمْ، فَأَنْتُمْ أَعْلَمُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4163) ومسلم في الإمارة (77:1859) كلاهما من طريق طارق بن عبد الرحمن قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أمر عمر بن الخطاب بقطع شجرة الرضوان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4163) and Muslim (1859:77).","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Orders the Tree of al-Riḍwān to Be Cut Down","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I set out to perform pilgrimage and passed by people who were praying. I asked, “What is this place of prayer?” They replied, “This is the tree beneath which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received the Pledge of al-Riḍwān.” I went to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and informed him. Saʿīd said: “My father told me that he was among those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ beneath the tree. When we returned the following year, however, we had forgotten its location and could not identify it.” Saʿīd then remarked: “The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ did not know where it was, but you know it—you must therefore know better!”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",617],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8969,13322],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4163)، ومسلم (77:1859)."},{"num":8995,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ طَارِقٍ، قَالَ: ذُكِرَتْ عِنْدَ سَعِيدِ بْنِ الْمُسَيَّبِ الشَّجَرَةُ فَضَحِكَ، فَقَالَ: أَخْبَرَنِي أَبِي وَكَانَ، شَهِدَهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4165) ومسلم في الإمارة (1859: 78) كلاهما من حديث سفيان، عن طارق فذكره، واللفظ للبخاري، وزاد مسلم: قال: فنسوها من العام المقبل.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أمر عمر بن الخطاب بقطع شجرة الرضوان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Related by al-Bukhārī (4165) and Muslim (1859:78).","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Orders the Tree of al-Riḍwān to Be Cut Down","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṭāriq reported: The tree was mentioned in the presence of Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, and he laughed. He then said: “My father, who had witnessed the pledge beneath it, informed me…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",618],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4165)، ومسلم (1859: 78)."},{"num":8996,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ نَافِعٍ قَالَ: كَانَ النَّاسُ يَأْتُونَ الشَّجَرَةَ الَّتِي يقولون لَهَا شَجَرَةُ الرِّضْوَانِ فَيُصَلُّونَ عِنْدَهَا، قَالَ: فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ فَأَوْعَدَهُمْ فِيهَا، وَأَمَرَ بقطعها فَقُطِعَتْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن سعد في طبقاته (511) عن عبد الوهاب بن عطاء، أخبرنا عبدالله بن عون، عن نافع فذكره. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أمر عمر بن الخطاب بقطع شجرة الرضوان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt (2/100).","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Orders the Tree of al-Riḍwān to Be Cut Down","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Nāfiʿ reported: People used to visit the tree they called the Tree of al-Riḍwān and pray beside it. When this reached ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, he threatened them with punishment and ordered that it be cut down, so it was cut down."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib’s statement, “The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ did not know where it was, but you know it,” expresses disapproval and sarcasm. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb had ordered the tree to be cut down, so where could it be now? Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah had known its location, but after becoming blind he was unable to point it out."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",619],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن سعد في «الطبقات» (511)."},{"num":8997,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن البراء بن عازب قال: أَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ الحُدَيْبِيَةِ أَلْفًا وَأَرْبَعَمِائَةٍ أَوْ أَكْثَرَ، فَنَزَلُوا عَلَى بِئْرٍ فَنَزَحُوهَا، فَأَتَوْا رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَتَى الْبِئْرَ، وَقَعَدَ عَلَى شَفِيرِهَا ثُمَّ قَالَ: ائْتُونِي بِدَلْوٍ مِنْ مَائِهَا فَأُتِيَ بِه،ِ فَبَصَقَ ، فَدَعَا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: دَعُوهَا سَاعَةً  فَأَرْوَوْا أَنْفُسَهُمْ وَرِكَابَهُمْ حَتَّى ارْتَحَلُوا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4151) عن فضل بن يعقوب، حدثنا الحسن بن محمد بن أعين أبو علي الحراني، حدثنا زهير، حدثنا أبو إسحاق قال: أنبأنا البراء فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر عدد الذين كانوا مع رسول الله ﷺ يوم الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Maghāzī (4151), from Faḍl ibn Yaʿqūb, from al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥarrānī, from Zuhayr, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib.","chapter_en":"The Number of Those Who Were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib reported that they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, numbering fourteen hundred or more. They stopped beside a well and drew out all its water. They went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who came to the well, sat at its edge and said: “Bring me a bucket of its water.” It was brought to him, and he spat into it and supplicated. He then said: “Leave it for a while.” Thereafter, they fully quenched themselves and their riding animals before departing."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",620],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4151)."},{"num":8998,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَلَمَةَ بْنِ الْأَكْوَعِ قَالَ: قَدِمْنَا الْحُدَيْبِيَةَ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَحْنُ أَرْبَعَ عشر مِائَةً. وَعَلَيْهَا خَمْسُونَ شَاةً لَا تُرْوِيهَا، قَالَ: فَقَعَدَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى جَبَا الرَّكِيَّةِ فَإِمَّا دَعَا، وَإِمَّا بَصَقَ فِيهَا، قَالَ: فَجَاشَتْ فَسَقَيْنَا وَاسْتَقَيْنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد والسير (1807 :132) من طرق عن عكرمة بن عمار، حدثني إياس بن سلمة، عن أبيه فذكره في حديث طويل.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر عدد الذين كانوا مع رسول الله ﷺ يوم الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in al-Jihād (1807:132) through several routes from ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār, from Iyās ibn Salamah, from his father, in a longer hadith.","chapter_en":"The Number of Those Who Were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ reported: We arrived at al-Ḥudaybiyyah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, numbering fourteen hundred. Its well contained so little water that it could not provide enough for fifty sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat at the edge of the well and either supplicated or spat into it. The water then surged forth, so we drank and drew what we needed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",621],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1807 :132)."},{"num":8999,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سالم بن أبي الجعد، عن جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الله قَالَ: قَدْ رَأَيْتُنِي مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ حَضَرَت الْعَصْرُ، وَلَيْسَ مَعَنَا مَاءٌ غَيْرَ فَضْلَةٍ، فَجُعِلَ فِي إِنَاءٍ، فَأُتِيَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِهِ، فَأَدْخَلَ يَدَهُ فِيهِ، وَفَرَّجَ أَصَابِعَهُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: حَيَّ عَلَى أَهْلِ الْوُضُوءِ، الْبَرَكَةُ مِنْ الله، فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ المَاءَ يَتَفَجَّرُ مِنْ بَيْنِ أَصَابِعِهِ، فَتَوَضَّأَ النَّاسُ، وَشَرِبُوا، فَجَعَلْتُ لَا آلُو مَا جَعَلْتُ فِي بَطْنِي مِنْهُ، فَعَلِمْتُ أَنَّهُ بَرَكَةٌ، قُلْتُ لِجَابِرٍ: كَمْ كُنْتُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ؟ قَالَ: أَلْفًا وَأَرْبَعَ مِائَةٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المرضى (5639) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا جرير، عن الأعمش قال: حدثني سالم بن أبي الجعد قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر عدد الذين كانوا مع رسول الله ﷺ يوم الحديبية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Related by al-Bukhārī (5639).","chapter_en":"The Number of Those Who Were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥudaybiyyah","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في غزوة الحديبية وغزوة ذات القَرَد","group_en":"Chapters Concerning the Campaign of al-Ḥudaybiyyah and the Campaign of Dhāt al-Qarad","part_no":48,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd reported from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah: I remember being with the Prophet ﷺ when the time for the afternoon prayer arrived. We had only a small amount of water, which was placed in a vessel and brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He placed his hand in it, spread his fingers and said: “Come, people of ablution! The blessing is from Allah.” I saw water springing from between his fingers. The people performed ablution and drank. I spared no effort in filling my stomach with it, for I knew that it was blessed. I asked Jābir, “How many were you that day?” He replied, “Fourteen hundred.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",622],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5639)."}]);